अजीर्ण <i>(I) a. (f. र्णा)</i> Undigested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=008-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्ण|अजीर्णं
अजीर्ण <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Indigestion, as in अजीर्णे भेषजं वारि; 2. vigour, absence of decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=008-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवनि|अजीवनिः
अजीवनि <i>f.</i> Non-existence (used as an imprecation, e.g. अजीवनिस्तव भूयात्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=008-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जुका
अज्जुका <i>f.</i> A courtezan (in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=008-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

