अत्रिनेत्रसूत
अत्रि-नेत्र˚ज, ˚भू, ˚प्रसूत, ˚सूत <i>m.</i> the moon. Cf. अथ नयनसमुत्थं ज्योतिरत्रेरिव द्यौः R.ii.75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ <i>(I) ind.</i> It is used as an auspicious particle, ओङ्कारश्चाथ शब्दश्च द्वावेतौ ब्रह्मणः पुरा । कण्ठं भित्वा विनिर्यातौ तेन मांगलिकावुभौ ॥ It is said that अथ does not mean auspiciousness but the very hearing of that word is auspicious. Hence at the commencement of the S.Bh., we have अर्थान्तरप्रयुक्त एवहि अथ शब्दः श्रुत्या मंगल प्रयोजनो भवति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ <i>(II) ind.</i> A particle expressing- (1) beginning, commencement, अथ योगानुशासनम् “Here begins &c.” P.Y.i.1; (2) doubt, e.g. शब्दो नित्यः अथानित्यः; (3) subsequent time (afterwards) अथ प्रजानामधिपः प्रभाते R.ii.1; (4) interrogation, अथ शक्नोषि भोक्तुम् G.M. “Are you able &c.”; (5) condition (if, in case whether) अथ (i.e. यदि) मरणमवश्यमेव जन्तोः Ve.iii.; (6) totality, entirety, अथ धर्मं व्याख्यास्यामः G.M. “we shall explain the whole Dharma”; (7) conjunction (and, also), भीमोऽथार्जुनः G.M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथापि
अथ-अपि <i>ind.</i> moreover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथकिम्
अथ-किम् <i>ind.</i> what else, certainly, assuredly (mostly found in plays).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथकिमु
अथ-किमु <i>ind.</i> how much more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथच
अथ-च <i>ind.</i> moreover, and, and likewise, R.viii.51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथतु
अथ-तु <i>ind.</i> but, on the contrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथवा
अथ-वा <i>ind.</i> or, or perhaps, दीर्ये किं न सहस्रदाऽहमथवारामेण किं दुष्करम् Ut.vi.; अथवा कृतवाग्द्वारे R.i.4; अथवा मृदु वस्तु हिंसितुम् viii.45, also 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=012-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

