अद्वैता
अद्वैत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Destitute of duality; 2. peerless, unique.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=014-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैत|अद्वैतः
अद्वैत <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Identity, sameness, अद्वैतं सुखदुःखयोः Ut.i.; 2. the Vedāntic doctrine of the identity of Brahman (n.) with the universe or with the soul; 3. Brahman (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=014-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैतवादिन्
अद्वैत-वादिन् <i>m.</i> one who maintains the identity of Brahman (n.) with the universe, a Vedāntist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=014-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
