अनामिका <i>f.</i> The ring-finger, e.g. अद्यापि तत्तुल्यकवेरभावादनामिका सार्थवती बभूव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्त|अनायत्तः
अनायत्त <i>a. (f. त्ता)</i> Independent, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्ता
अनायत्त <i>a. (f. त्ता)</i> Independent, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्तवृत्ति
अनायत्त-वृत्ति <i>a.</i> having an independent livelihood, एतावज्जन्मसाफल्यं यदनायत्तवृत्तिता Hit.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अनायास <i>(I) a. (f. सा)</i> Requiring no labour or trouble, easy, ममाप्येकस्मिन्ननायासे कर्मणि सहायेन भवता भवितव्यम् Sak.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायासा
अनायास <i>(I) a. (f. सा)</i> Requiring no labour or trouble, easy, ममाप्येकस्मिन्ननायासे कर्मणि सहायेन भवता भवितव्यम् Sak.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अनायास <i>(II) m.</i> Absence of exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारत|अनारतं
अनारत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Continual, constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारता
अनारत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Continual, constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारतम्
अनारतम् <i>ind.</i> Continually, eternally, e.g. अनारतं तेन पदेषु लम्भिताः Kir.i.15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्जव|अनार्जवं|अनार्ज्जव
अनार्जव <i>n.</i> 1. Crookedness (moral or physical); 2. disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्तवा
अनार्तवा <i>f.</i> A girl who has not arrived at puberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य|अनार्यः|अनार्य्य|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य <i>(I) m.</i> 1. Other than an Ārya; 2. a Śūdra; 3. a mleccha; 4. an ignoble person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य|अनार्यः|अनार्य्य|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य <i>(II) a.</i> Ignoble, Na.iii.57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्ष
अनार्ष <i>a. (f. र्षा)</i> 1. Not referring to a Ṛshi; 2. not relating to the Vedic hymns, अनार्षे अवैदिके S.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्षा
अनार्ष <i>a. (f. र्षा)</i> 1. Not referring to a Ṛshi; 2. not relating to the Vedic hymns, अनार्षे अवैदिके S.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्भ|अनारंभः|अनारम्भः
अनारम्भ <i>m.</i> Not undertaking, e.g. अनारम्भे मनुष्याणां प्रथमं बुद्धिलक्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्बी
अनालम्बी <i>f.</i> Śiva’s lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्भुका|अनालंभुका
अनालम्भुका <i>f.</i> A woman during menstruation (in ritual works).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृष्टि|अनावृष्टिः
अनावृष्टि <i>f.</i> Drought, considered as one of the six calamities of the season. Cf. ईति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रमिन्
अनाश्रमिन् <i>m.</i> One not belonging to any of the Āśramas, e.g. अनाश्रमी न तिष्टेत्तुक्षणमेकमपि द्विजः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रमेवास
अनाश्रमेवास <i>m.</i> Not belonging to any of the Āśramas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रव
अनाश्रव <i>a. (f. वा)</i> Not listening to the advice of, R.xix.49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रवा
अनाश्रव <i>a. (f. वा)</i> Not listening to the advice of, R.xix.49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्था
अनास्था <i>f.</i> Disrespect, indifference, पिंडेष्वनास्था खलु भौतिकेषु R.ii.57; स्त्रीपुमानित्यनास्थैषा वृत्तं हि महितं सताम् K.S.vi.12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहत|अनाहतं|अनाहतः
अनाहत <i>n.</i> A new garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार|अनाहारः
अनाहार <i>m.</i> Abstinence, starvation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहुति|अनाहुतिः
अनाहुति <i>f.</i> 1. Not sacrificing; 2. bad sacrificing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूत|अनाहूतः
अनाहूत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Uncalled, unbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूता
अनाहूत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Uncalled, unbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूतोपजल्पिन्
अनाहूत-उपजल्पिन् <i>m.</i> an uncalled-for speaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूतोपविष्ट
अनाहूत-उपविष्ट <i>a.</i> seated as an uninvited guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिकेत
अनिकेत <i>m.</i> An ascetic having no fixed abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिगीर्ण|अनिगीर्णः|अनिगीर्ण्ण
अनिगीर्ण <i>a. (f. र्णा)</i> 1. Not swallowed; 2. present, not to be supplied (in rhetoric).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिगीर्णा
अनिगीर्ण <i>a. (f. र्णा)</i> 1. Not swallowed; 2. present, not to be supplied (in rhetoric).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्य|अनित्यः
अनित्य <i>a. (f. त्या)</i> 1. Transient; 2. uncertain; 3. unstable; 4. not peremptory, not obligatory (as a rule); 5. unusual, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्या
अनित्य <i>a. (f. त्या)</i> 1. Transient; 2. uncertain; 3. unstable; 4. not peremptory, not obligatory (as a rule); 5. unusual, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यक्रिया
अनित्य-क्रिया <i>f.</i> an act of worship which is voluntary and occasional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यदत्त|अनित्यदत्तः
अनित्य-दत्त, -दत्तक, -दत्त्रिम <i>m.</i> a son given away by his parents to another temporarily (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यदत्तक|अनित्यदत्तकः
अनित्य-दत्त, -दत्तक, -दत्त्रिम <i>m.</i> a son given away by his parents to another temporarily (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यदत्त्रिम
अनित्य-दत्त, -दत्तक, -दत्त्रिम <i>m.</i> a son given away by his parents to another temporarily (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यसमास|अनित्यसमासः
अनित्य-समास <i>m.</i> a compound the sense of which may be equally expressed by using its component parts separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्द्रिय|अनिंद्रियं
अनिन्द्रिय <i>n.</i> 1. Not an organ of sense; 2. mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृत
अनिभृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Not modest, bold; 2. not private; 3. unstable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृता
अनिभृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Not modest, bold; 2. not private; 3. unstable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमक|अनिमकः
अनिमक <i>m.</i> 1. A frog; 2. a bee; 3. the Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्त
अनिमित्त <i>(I) a. (f. त्ता)</i> Causeless, groundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्ता
अनिमित्त <i>(I) a. (f. त्ता)</i> Causeless, groundless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्त
अनिमित्त <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Absence of a cause or occasion; 2. an ill omen, ममाप्यनिमित्तानि समरगमनविघ्नमुत्पादयन्ति Ve.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्तनिराक्रिया
अनिमित्त-निराक्रिया <i>f.</i> aversion of ill omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्ततस्
अनिमित्ततस् <i>ind.</i> From no cause, without a cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-39" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिष|अनिमिषं|अनिमिषः
अनिमिष <i>m.</i> 1. A god; 2. a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-40" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषाचार्य|अनिमिषाचार्यः|अनिमिषाचार्य्य|अनिमिषाचार्य्यः
अनिमिष-आचार्य <i>m.</i> Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-40" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषक्षेत्र
अनिमिष-क्षेत्र <i>f.</i> the holy place, called Viṣṇu-kṣetra, Bhag.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-40" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषीय
अनिमिषीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Relating to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-41" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषीया
अनिमिषीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Relating to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-41" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेष|अनिमेषं|अनिमेषः
अनिमेष <i>(I) a.</i> Without twinkling (as eyes), शतैस्तमक्ष्णामनिमेषवृत्तिभिः R.iii.43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-42" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेष|अनिमेषं|अनिमेषः
अनिमेष <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Absence of twinkle; 2. a god; 3. a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=020-42" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियत|अनियतं
अनियत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Uncontrolled; 2. uncertain; 3. irregular, Ut.v.; 4. transitory, perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=021-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियता
अनियत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Uncontrolled; 2. uncertain; 3. irregular, Ut.v.; 4. transitory, perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=021-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियतांक|अनियताङ्क|अनियताङ्कः
अनियत-अंक <i>m.</i> an indeterminate digit (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=021-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियतपुंस्का
अनियत-पुंस्का <i>f.</i> a woman irregular or unchaste in conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=021-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

