अन्यस्त्री
अन्य-स्त्री <i>f.</i> a woman not one’s own. In rhetoric, she is one of the three categories of the principal female characters in a poetical composition, the other two being स्वीया and साधारणस्त्री. अन्यस्त्री is either ‘another’s wife,’ or ‘a damsel.’ As ‘another’s wife,’ she is fond of festivals and the like opportunities, is a disgrace to her family, bare of modesty. The ‘damsel’ is one not yet married, bashful and arrived at the age of puberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=032-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

