अन्यतरेद्युस् <i>ind.</i> On either of two days, on the one day or or on the other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्
अन्यतस् <i>ind.</i> Used in the sense of the abl. or loc. of अन्य.(अन्यतस्-अन्यतस् or एकतस्-अन्यतस् = on the one side-on the other, तपनमण्डलदीपितमेकतः सततनैशतमोवृतमन्यतः Kir.v.2.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्र
अन्यत्र <i>ind.</i> Used in the sense of the loc. of अन्य, absolutely or with the ellipsis of a word implying ‘place,’ ‘manner’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथा
अन्यथा <i>ind.</i> 1. In a different manner, differently, भावि चेन्न तदन्यथा Hit.i.; 2. otherwise, else, e.g. अन्यथा हि विरोधः ‘otherwise there would be contradiction’; 3. on the other hand, on the contrary; 4. untruly, e.g. अन्यथावादिनो यस्य ध्रुवस्तस्य पराजयः; 5. badly, wrongly, erroneously (as in अन्यथासिद्ध). अन्यथा in combination with the root कृ, धा with वि &c. means ‘to undo,’ ‘to change.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाकारम्
अन्यथा-कारम् <i>ind.</i> doing otherwise, differently, e.g. अन्यथाकारं भुंक्ते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाख्याति|अन्यथाख्यातिः
अन्यथा-ख्याति <i>f.</i> erroneous conception of spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाभाव|अन्यथाभावः
अन्यथा-भाव <i>m.</i> alteration, difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथावादिन्
अन्यथा-वादिन् <i>a.</i> speaking differently, prevaricating (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथावृत्ति
अन्यथा-वृत्ति <i>a.</i> 1. altered; 2. disturbed by strong emotions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्ध
अन्यथा-सिद्ध <i>(I) a.</i> wrongly proved or established (referring to a cause which is not the true cause).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्ध
अन्यथा-सिद्ध <i>(II) n.</i> an unessential cause, a concomitant circumstance (in logic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथास्तोत्र
अन्यथा-स्तोत्र <i>n.</i> untrue or ironical praise (यत्र विकृताकृतिरेव दर्शनीयस्त्वमसीत्युच्यते तदन्यथास्तोत्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदा
अन्यदा <i>ind.</i> 1. At another time, on all other occasions than the one under question, e.g. अन्यदा भूषणं पुंसां क्षमा लज्जेव योषिताम् । पराक्रमः परिभवे वैयात्यं सुरतेष्विव Sis.ii.44, R.xi.73; 2. at one time, once, once upon a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदीय
अन्यदीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. Belonging to another; 2. being in another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदीया
अन्यदीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. Belonging to another; 2. being in another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यर्हि
अन्यर्हि <i>ind.</i> At another time, (the same as अन्यदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय|अन्यायः
अन्याय <i>m.</i>^1 1. An unjust or unlawful action; 2. injustice, impropriety; 3. irregularity.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: gender change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायदण्ड|अन्यायदण्डः
अन्याय-दण्ड <i>m.</i> an unjust punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायिन्
अन्यायिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Unjust, improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायिनी
अन्यायिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Unjust, improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय्य|अन्याय्यः
अन्याय्य <i>a. (f. य्या)</i> 1. Not authoritative; 2. unlawful, unjust; 3. improper, indecorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय्या
अन्याय्य <i>a. (f. य्या)</i> 1. Not authoritative; 2. unlawful, unjust; 3. improper, indecorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यून|अन्यूनः
अन्यून <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Entire, complete, not deficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूना
अन्यून <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Entire, complete, not deficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूनांग|अन्यूनाङ्ग
अन्यून-अंग <i>a. (f. गा or गी)</i> not having a limb too little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूनांगी
अन्यून-अंग <i>a. (f. गा or गी)</i> not having a limb too little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूनांगा
अन्यून-अंग <i>a. (f. गा or गी)</i> not having a limb too little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यूनाधिक
अन्यून-अधिक <i>a.</i> neither deficient nor excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युस्
अन्येद्युस् <i>ind.</i> On the other day, on the following day, अन्येद्युरात्मानुचरस्य भावम् R.ii.26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य <i>pron. (f. न्या)</i> Each other, one another, mutual (generally sing.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्या
अन्योन्य <i>pron. (f. न्या)</i> Each other, one another, mutual (generally sing.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याभाव|अन्योन्याभावः
अन्योन्य-अभाव <i>m.</i> mutual nonexistence, mutual negation, one of the four divisions of अभाव q.v. (in Vaiśeṣika phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याश्रय|अन्योन्याश्रयः
अन्योन्य-आश्रय <i>m.</i> reciprocal relation of cause and effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्योक्ति|अन्योन्योक्तिः
अन्योन्य-उक्ति <i>f.</i> conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यकलह
अन्योन्य-कलह <i>m.</i> mutual quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यघात
अन्योन्य-घात <i>m.</i> killing one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यभेद|अन्योन्यभेदः
अन्योन्य-भेद <i>m.</i> mutual dissension or enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यविभाग|अन्योन्यविभागः
अन्योन्य-विभाग <i>m.</i> mutual partition made by the sharers of an inheritance without the presence of any other persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यवृत्ति|अन्योन्यवृत्तिः
अन्योन्य-वृत्ति <i>m.</i> mutual effect of one upon another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यव्यतिकर|अन्योन्यव्यतिकरः
अन्योन्य-व्यतिकर <i>m.</i> reciprocal action or influence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यसंश्रय|अन्योन्यसंश्रयः
अन्योन्य-संश्रय <i>m.</i> reciprocal relation of cause and effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=033-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्
अन्वक् <i>ind.</i> 1. Following, after, अन्वग्ययौ मध्यमलोकपालः R.ii.16; 2. favourably, friendly disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वग्भावम्
अन्वग्भावम् <i>ind.</i> Favourably, friendly disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्षम्
अन्वक्षम् <i>ind.</i> 1. After, afterwards; 2. immediately, instantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वच्
अन्वच् <i>a. (f. अनूची)</i> Following.(The loc. sing. अनूचि is used in the sense of ‘behind,’ ‘from behind.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूची
अन्वच् <i>a. (f. अनूची)</i> Following.(The loc. sing. अनूचि is used in the sense of ‘behind,’ ‘from behind.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्वय <i>m.</i> 1. Connection, association; 2. retinue, attendants^1, का त्वमेकाकिनी भीरु निरन्वयजने वने Bt.v.66; 3. family, race, lineage, रघूणामन्वयं वक्ष्ये R.i.9, तदन्वये शुद्धिमति i.12; 4. the male descendants, ताभ्यऋतेऽन्वयः Yaj.ii.117; 5. grammatical connection of the words in a sentence, तात्पर्याख्यां वृत्तिमाहुः पदार्थान्वयबोधने S.D.ii.; 6. logical continuance, (op. to व्यतिरेक ‘logical discontinuance’ in this sense), जन्माद्यस्य यतोऽन्वयादितरतः Bhag.i.1. See T.S. under बुद्धि.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयज्ञ|अन्वयज्ञः
अन्वय-ज्ञ <i>m.</i> a geneologist, R.vi.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयव्यतिरेक
अन्वय-व्यतिरेक <i>n.</i> 1. agreement and contrariety; 2. rule and exception; 3. logical continuance and discontinuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयव्याप्ति|अन्वयव्याप्तिः
अन्वय-व्याप्ति <i>f.</i> an affirmative universal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिन्
अन्वयिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Connected with as a consequence, e.g. अन्वयिनो गुणाः (See अन्वय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिनी
अन्वयिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Connected with as a consequence, e.g. अन्वयिनो गुणाः (See अन्वय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थ
अन्वर्थ <i>a. (f. र्था)</i> Having a meaning obvious or easily to be understood from the etymon, तथैव सोऽभूदनर्थो राजा प्रकृतिरंजनात् R.iv.12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्था
अन्वर्थ <i>a. (f. र्था)</i> Having a meaning obvious or easily to be understood from the etymon, तथैव सोऽभूदनर्थो राजा प्रकृतिरंजनात् R.iv.12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थग्रहण
अन्वर्थ-ग्रहण <i>n.</i> the literal understanding of the meaning of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थसंज्ञा
अन्वर्थ-संज्ञा <i>f.</i> 1. a proper name whose meaning is intelligible; 2. a technical name which conveys its own meaning (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववकिरण|अन्ववकिरणं
अन्ववकिरण <i>n.</i> Scattering successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसर्ग|अन्ववसर्गः
अन्ववसर्ग <i>m.</i> 1. Permission to do as one likes; 2. following one’s own will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसित
अन्ववसित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसिता
अन्ववसित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववाय|अन्ववायः
अन्ववाय <i>m.</i> Race, lineage, family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववेक्षा
अन्ववेक्षा <i>f.</i> Regard, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टका
अन्वष्टका <i>f.</i> The ninth day of the latter half of पौष, माघ and फाल्गुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टक्य|अन्वष्टक्यं
अन्वष्टक्य <i>n.</i> A funeral ceremony performed on the अन्वष्टका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वहम्
अन्वहम् <i>ind.</i> Day after day, every day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाख्यान|अन्वाख्यानं
अन्वाख्यान <i>n.</i> An explanation referring to a subject mentioned before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचय|अन्वाचयः
अन्वाचय <i>m.</i> 1. Adding an object of secondary import. (The instance generally given to explain this word is- भो भिक्षो भिक्षामट गां चानय, where the going out for alms is enjoined to the beggar as his principal object and his bringing a cow when he can see one, as the matter of secondary import.); 2. such an object itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाजे
अन्वाजे <i>ind. (Only used in combination with the root कृ)</i> To support, to assist. (It is either considered as a prefix or not. Hence अन्वाजेकृत्य or अन्वाजे कृत्वा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिष्ट
अन्वादिष्ट <i>a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Mentioned after; 2. inferior, of secondary import.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिष्टा
अन्वादिष्ट <i>a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Mentioned after; 2. inferior, of secondary import.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादेश|अन्वादेशः
अन्वादेश <i>m.</i> Repeated mention (referring to what has been stated previously).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधान|अन्वाधानं
अन्वाधान <i>n.</i> Putting fuel (to the sacred fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधि|अन्वाधिः
अन्वाधि <i>m.</i> 1. A bail or deposit delivered to a third person (in civil law); 2. repentance, remorse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेय|अन्वाधेयं
अन्वाधेय <i>n.</i> Property presented to the wife after marriage by her husband’s family or by her own relatives. It is thus defined by Kat.- विवाहात्परतो यत्तु लब्धं भर्तृकुलात्स्त्रिया । अन्वाधेयं तदुक्तं तु लब्धं बन्धुकुलात्तथा ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेयक|अन्वाधेयकं
अन्वाधेयक <i>n.</i> The same as अन्वाधेय q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारम्भ|अन्वारंभः|अन्वारम्भः
अन्वारम्भ <i>m.</i> Touching, especially the touching a person who institutes a sacrifice in order to make him participate in the merits of the religious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारम्भण|अन्वारंभणं
अन्वारम्भण <i>n.</i> The same as अन्वारम्भ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहण|अन्वारोहणं
अन्वारोहण <i>n.</i> A widow’s ascending the funeral pile with the body of her husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासन|अन्वासनं
अन्वासन <i>n.</i> 1. Worship, service; 2. sorrow; 3. taking a seat after another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्य <i>n.</i> The monthly śrāddha (in ritual literature).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहिक
अन्वाहिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> Daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहिकी
अन्वाहिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> Daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित <i>n.</i> The same as अन्वाधि q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वित|अन्वितः
अन्वि(न्वी)त <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Joined or connected with; 2. possessed of; 3. understood; 4. connected grammatically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीत|अन्वीतः
अन्वि(न्वी)त <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Joined or connected with; 2. possessed of; 3. understood; 4. connected grammatically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विता
अन्वि(न्वी)त <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Joined or connected with; 2. possessed of; 3. understood; 4. connected grammatically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वितार्थ
अन्वि(न्वी)त-अर्थ <i>a.</i> having a sense which results from the context.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीतार्थ
अन्वि(न्वी)त-अर्थ <i>a.</i> having a sense which results from the context.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वितार्थवाद|अन्वितार्थवादः
अन्वि(न्वी)त-अर्थ˚वाद <i>m.</i> the doctrine of the Mīmānsākas that the words in a sentence express their meanings not generally but as connected with each other in that particular sentence, K.Pr.ii.; for further information see K.Pr.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीतार्थवाद
अन्वि(न्वी)त-अर्थ˚वाद <i>m.</i> the doctrine of the Mīmānsākas that the words in a sentence express their meanings not generally but as connected with each other in that particular sentence, K.Pr.ii.; for further information see K.Pr.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=034-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वृचम्
अन्वृचम् <i>ind.</i> Verse after verse (in Ṛgveda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीक्षण|अन्वीक्षणं
अन्वीक्षण <i>n.</i> Searching, investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीक्षा
अन्वीक्षा <i>f.</i> The same as अन्वीक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष|अन्वेषः
अन्वेष <i>m.</i> Seeking for, searching, वयं तत्वान्वेषान्मधुकर हतास्त्वं खलु कृती Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषण|अन्वेषणं
अन्वेषण <i>n.</i> See अन्वेष, R.xii.11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषणा
अन्वेषणा <i>f.</i> See अन्वेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्
अप् <i>f. (only pl. in classical language; nom. आपः)</i> Water. (According to Hindu mythology, it is the first of the five elements of creation, the other four being आकाश, वायु, अग्नि and पृथिवी. अप एव ससर्जादौ तासु बीजमवासृजन् M.i.8; however, it is the 5th object of creation in M.i.78).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्चर|अप्चरः
अप्-चर <i>m.</i> an aquatic animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पति|अप्पतिः
अप्-पति <i>m.</i> 1. the ocean; 2. a name of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पित्त|अप्पित्तं
अप्-पित्त <i>n.</i> fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
अप <i>ind.</i> As a prefix to verbs, it means- (1) ‘away,’ (e.g. अपनी ‘to take away’); (2) deterioration, (e.g. अपकृ ‘to act improperly’); (3) negation, contradiction, (e.g. अपलप् ‘to deny’).As a separable preposition, (with a noun in the abl.), it means- (1) ‘away from,’ e.g. यत्संप्रत्ययं लोकेभ्यो लंकायां वसतिर्भयाम्; (2) ‘without’ e.g. अप हरेः संसारः; (3) ‘with the exception of,’ e.g. अप त्रिगर्तेभ्यो वृष्टो देवःIn Tatpur. and Bahu. compounds with nouns, it implies the same meanings as the prefix to verbs.In adverbial compounds, it means- (1) ‘away from’ (as in अपदिशम्); (2) ‘without’ (as in अपविष्णु संसारः); (3) ‘with the exception of,’ (e.g. अपत्रिगर्तं वृष्टो देवः); (4) negation, contradiction, (e.g. अपकामम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाध्वन्
अप-अध्वन् <i>m.</i> a bad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानृत
अप-अनृत <i>a.</i> free from falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासु
अप-असु <i>a.</i> lifeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरुण
अप-करुण <i>a.</i> cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकलंक|अपकलङ्क|अपकलंकः|अपकलङ्कः
अप-कलंक <i>m.</i> an indelible disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकल्मष
अप-कल्मष <i>a.</i> sinless, faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकुक्षि
अप-कुक्षि <i>m.</i> a miserable belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकौशली
अप-कौशली <i>f.</i> news, information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगर्जित
अप-गर्जित <i>a.</i> free from the noise of a thunder (as a cloud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचरित
अप-चरित <i>n.</i> fault offence, प्रसवो ममापचरितैर्विष्टम्भितो वीरुधाम् Sak.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छत्र
अप-च्छत्र <i>a.</i> without a parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतीर्थ
अप-तीर्थ <i>m.n.</i> a bad तीर्थ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदक्षिणम्
अप-दक्षिणम् <i>ind.</i> on the left side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदम
अप-दम <i>a.</i> without self-restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदश
अप-दश <i>a.</i> far from ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिशम्
अप-दिशम् <i>ind.</i> between two regions of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेवता
अप-देवता <i>f.</i> an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्रव्य|अपद्रव्यं
अप-द्रव्य <i>n.</i> any bad thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्वार|अपद्वारं
अप-द्वार <i>n.</i> an entrance to a house other than the proper door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधूम
अप-धूम <i>a.</i> free from smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनस
अप-नस <i>a.</i> without a nose, e.g. कौक्षेयमुद्यम्य चकारापनसं मुखम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनिद्र
अप-निद्र <i>a.</i> sleepless (lit. and fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपाठ|अपपाठः
अप-पाठ <i>m.</i> a wrong reading, e.g. काशिकायां तु पञ्जराजीति क्वाचित्कः पाठः । अपपाठः स इति हरदत्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्र
अप-पात्र <i>a.</i> of low caste (lit. deprived of vessels).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभय
अप-भय <i>a.</i> fearless, undaunted, R.iii.51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभरणी
अप-भरणी <i>f.</i> the last lunar mansion, (the same as भरणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभी
अप-भी <i>a.</i> fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमन्यु
अप-मन्यु <i>a.</i> free from grief or anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्ग|अपमार्गः
अप-मार्ग <i>m.</i> a by-way, a side-way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमुख
अप-मुख <i>a.</i> 1. having a bad face; 2. having a face averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमूर्धन्
अप-मूर्धन् <i>a.</i> headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृत्यु|अपमृत्युः
अप-मृत्यु <i>m.</i> 1. accidental death; 2. a great danger or illness from which a person recovers contrary to expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्
अप-यशस् <i>n.</i> disgrace, infamy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरुष्
अप-रुष् <i>a.</i> free from anger, अपरुषा परुषाक्षरमीरिता R.ix.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूप|अपरूपं
अप-रूप <i>(I) a. (f. पा or पी)</i> deformed, ugly, odd-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूपा
अप-रूप <i>(I) a. (f. पा or पी)</i> deformed, ugly, odd-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूपी
अप-रूप <i>(I) a. (f. पा or पी)</i> deformed, ugly, odd-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूप|अपरूपं
अप-रूप <i>(II) n.</i> deformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्या
अप-विद्या <i>f.</i> Māyā or illusion, e.g. तत्वस्य संवित्तिरिवापविद्याम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवीणा
अप-वीणा <i>f.</i> a bad lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशकुन|अपशकुनं
अप-शकुन <i>n.</i> an ill-omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशंकम्|अपशङ्कम्
अप-शंकम् <i>ind.</i> fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशब्द|अपशब्दः
अप-शब्द <i>m.</i> 1. a corrupted word (either in form or in meaning), अन्यथोचारिताः शब्दा अपशब्दा इतीरिताः Bhartr., अपशब्दशतं माघे; 2. the word अप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशिरस्
अप-शिरस् <i>a.</i> headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्री
अप-श्री <i>a.</i> deprived of beauty, Sis.xi.64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्य|अपसव्यं|अपसव्यः
अप-सव्य <i>a.</i> 1. not left, right; 2. contrary, opposite (अपसव्यं कृ ‘to keep the right side towards one’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यम्
अप-सव्यम् <i>ind.</i> to the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसिद्धान्त|अपसिद्धांतः|अपसिद्धान्तः
अप-सिद्धान्त <i>m.</i> a wrong conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नान|अपस्नानं
अप-स्नान <i>n.</i> 1. funeral bathing; 2. bathing in water with which a person has previously washed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पश
अप-स्पश <i>a.</i> without spies, शब्दविद्येव नो भाति राजनीतिरपस्पशा Sis.ii.112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहसित|अपहसितं
अप-हसित <i>n.</i> silly laughter, laughter with tears in the eyes (common among low people).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहेला
अप-हेला <i>f.</i> disrespect, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरण|अपकरणं
अपकरण <i>n.</i> 1. Doing wrongs; 2. ill-treating, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्मन्|अपकर्म्मन्
अपकर्मन् <i>n.</i> 1. Discharge (as of a debt, e.g. ऋणापकर्मन्); 2. wickedness; 3. any impure or degrading act or rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्ष|अपकर्षः
अपकर्ष <i>m.</i> 1. Drawing down, pulling away, detraction, decay, (op. to उत्कर्ष); 2. decline, degradation; 3. anticipation of a word occurring later on (in Mīmānsā phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षक
अपकर्षक <i>a. (f. र्षिका)</i> detracting, making inferior, दोषा स्तस्यापकर्षकाः S.D.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षिका
अपकर्षक <i>a. (f. र्षिका)</i> detracting, making inferior, दोषा स्तस्यापकर्षकाः S.D.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=035-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षण
अपकर्षण <i>n.</i> 1. Drawing away or down; 2. making inferior; 3. superseding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकार|अपकारः
अपकार <i>m.</i> 1. Hurt, injury, उपकर्त्राऽरिणा संधिर्न मित्रेणापकारिणा । उपकारापकारौ हि लक्ष्यं लक्षणमेतयोः Sis.ii.37; 2. disservice, e.g. अपकारोऽप्युपकारायैव संवृतः; 3. a mean action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारार्थिन्
अपकार-अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारगिर्
अपकार-गिर् <i>f.</i> an offending speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारशब्द
अपकार-शब्द <i>m.</i> an offending speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारक|अपकारकः
अपकारक <i>a. (f. रिका)</i> Acting wrongly, offending, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिका
अपकारक <i>a. (f. रिका)</i> Acting wrongly, offending, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिन्
अपकारिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> See अपकारक, न मित्रेणापकारिणा Sis.ii.37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिणी
अपकारिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> See अपकारक, न मित्रेणापकारिणा Sis.ii.37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृति|अपकृतिः
अपकृति <i>f.</i> The same as अपकार q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं|अपकृष्टः
अपकृष्ट <i>(I) m.</i> A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं|अपकृष्टः
अपकृष्ट <i>(II) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Drawn down or away; 2. low, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्टा
अपकृष्ट <i>(II) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Drawn down or away; 2. low, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्टजाति
अपकृष्ट-जाति <i>a.</i> of a low tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रिया
अपक्रिया <i>f.</i> 1. Injury, hurt, disservice, Sis.ii.54; 2. acquitting (debts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ति|अपक्तिः
अपक्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Immaturity; 2. indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम|अपक्रमः
अपक्रम <i>(I) m.</i> Going away, retreating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम|अपक्रमः
अपक्रम <i>(II) a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Without any order; 2. in wrong order, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमा
अपक्रम <i>(II) a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Without any order; 2. in wrong order, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमण|अपक्रमणं
अपक्रमण <i>n.</i> See अपक्रम I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्राम|अपक्रामः
अपक्राम <i>m.</i> See अपक्रम I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रोश|अपक्रोशः
अपक्रोश <i>m.</i> Reviling, abusing. (Cf. उपक्रोश)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ष
अपक्ष <i>a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Without wings; 2. not on the same side or party; 3. adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षा
अपक्ष <i>a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Without wings; 2. not on the same side or party; 3. adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षपात|अपक्षपातः
अपक्ष-पात <i>m.</i> impartiality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षपातिन्
अपक्ष-पातिन् <i>a.</i> impartial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षय|अपक्षयः
अपक्षय <i>m.</i> Decline, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षेपण|अपक्षेपणं
अपक्षेपण <i>n.</i> 1. Casting away, throwing down; 2. throwing down, as one of the five kinds of कर्मन् in the Vaiśeṣika phil., the other four being उत्प्रेक्षण, आकुंचन, प्रसारण, and गमन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगम|अपगमः
अपगम <i>m.</i> Going off, passing away, departure (lit. and fig.), R.iii.7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगमन|अपगमनं
अपगमन <i>n.</i> The same as अपगम q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगर|अपगरः
अपगर <i>m.</i> One who blames, one who says what is disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगा
अपगा <i>f.</i> A river. (See आपगा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोपुर
अपगोपुर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Deprived of its gates (as a town).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोपुरा
अपगोपुर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Deprived of its gates (as a town).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघन|अपघनः
अपघन <i>m.</i> 1. A limb or member of the body. (The Kāśikā. says- अपघनोऽंगावयवैकदेशो न सर्वः, but other writers differ from this); 2. the body itself, लौहोद्घनघनत्कन्धां ललितापघनां स्त्रियम् Bt.vii.62 (where अपघन is rendered by the commentators by देह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघात|अपघातः
अपघात <i>m.</i> 1. Warding off, preventing; 2. any evil accident occasioning death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातिन्
अपघातिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Murderous, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातिनी
अपघातिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Murderous, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच|अपचः
अपच <i>m.</i> 1. A man who does not cook for himself, e.g. अपचो दीक्षितः; 2. a bad cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचय|अपचयः
अपचय <i>m.</i> Decrease, decline, deterioration, taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचार|अपचारः
अपचार <i>m.</i> 1. Departure, death, सिंहघोषश्च कांतकापचारं निर्भिद्य D.K.; 2. a failure, a deficiency, नापचारमगमन् क्वचित् Sis.xiv.32; 3. absence, want; 4. improper or irreligious conduct, R.xv.47; 5. injurious conduct; 6. unwholesome regimen.(In the following stanza, अपचार is used in the last two senses- कृतापचारोऽपि परैरनाविष्कृतविक्रियः । असाध्यं कुरुते कोपं प्राप्ते काले गदो यथा ॥ Sis.ii.84.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिन्
अपचारिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Wicked, bad. (Cf. अपचार)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिणी
अपचारिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Wicked, bad. (Cf. अपचार)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचिति|अपचितिः
अपचिति <i>f.</i> 1. Worship, reverence, i.e. विहितापचितिर्महीभृता; 2. loss, destruction; 3. expiation (of sin); 4. expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाय|अपच्छायः
अपच्छाय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> 1. Shadowless; 2. without brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाया
अपच्छाय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> 1. Shadowless; 2. without brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाय|अपच्छायः
अपच्छाय <i>(II) m.</i> A god. (The following stanza from Na. says that gods have no shadows- भजंतु रूपं कियदस्य देवाश्छाया नलस्यापि तथापि नैषाम् । इतीरयंतीव तथा निरैक्षि सा नैषधे न त्वमरेषु तेषु ॥ xiv.21.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छेद|अपच्छेदः
अपच्छेद <i>m.</i> 1. Cutting off; 2. interruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छेदन|अपच्छेदनं
अपच्छेदन <i>n.</i> The same as अपच्छेद q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजय|अपजयः
अपजय <i>m.</i> Defeat, overthrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजात|अपजातः
अपजात <i>m.</i> A son inferior in qualities to his parents (मातृतुल्यगुणो जातस्त्वनुजातः पितुः समः । अतिजातोऽधिकस्तस्मादपजातोऽधमाधमः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपंचीकृत|अपञ्चीकृत|अपंचीकृतं|अपञ्चीकृतं
अपंचीकृत <i>n. pl.</i> The five subtle elements (æther, air, fire, water and earth), which are not yet become the five gross elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटी
अपटी <i>f.</i> A screen or wall of cloth, especially the screen surrounding a tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटीक्षेप|अपटीक्षेपः
अपटी-क्षेप <i>m.</i> tossing aside the curtain. (अपटाक्षेपेण ‘with a toss of the curtain’ often occurs as a stage-direction in plays, when a character enters precipitately on the stage in hurry and agitation.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटु|अपटुः
अपटु <i>a. (f. टु or ट्वी)</i> 1. Awkward, uncouth; 2. diseased, sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपट्वी
अपटु <i>a. (f. टु or ट्वी)</i> 1. Awkward, uncouth; 2. diseased, sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपठ
अपठ <i>m.</i> 1. One unable to read; 2. a bad reader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्डित|अपंडित
अपण्डित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Unlearned, विभूषणं मौनमपण्डितानाम् Bhartr.ii.7; 2. wanting in skill or taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्डिता
अपण्डित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Unlearned, विभूषणं मौनमपण्डितानाम् Bhartr.ii.7; 2. wanting in skill or taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्य
अपण्य <i>a. (f. ण्या)</i> Unsaleable (as an article), जीविकार्थे चापण्ये Pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-39" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्या
अपण्य <i>a. (f. ण्या)</i> Unsaleable (as an article), जीविकार्थे चापण्ये Pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=036-39" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतर्पण|अपतर्पणं
अपतर्पण <i>n.</i> Fasting (in sickness &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतिक
अपतिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Without a husband, without a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतिका
अपतिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Without a husband, without a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्नीक
अपत्नीक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Without a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्नीका
अपत्नीक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Without a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्य|अपत्यं
अपत्य <i>n.</i> Offspring in general (whether male or female, whether sons or the later generations of a Gotra, अपत्यं पौत्रप्रभृतिगौत्रम् P.Bh. Sometimes, however, the word means only ‘children,’ R.i.50).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यकाम
अपत्य-काम <i>a.</i> desirous of offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यपथ|अपत्यपथः
अपत्य-पथ <i>m.</i> the vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यप्रत्यय|अपत्यप्रत्ययः
अपत्य-प्रत्यय <i>m.</i> a patronymic affix (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यविक्रय
अपत्य-विक्रय <i>m.</i> sale of offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यशत्रु|अपत्यशत्रुः
अपत्य-शत्रु <i>m.</i> a crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपण
अपत्रपण <i>n.</i> Bashfulness, shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपा
अपत्रपा <i>f.</i> Bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपिष्णु|अपत्रपिष्णुः
अपत्रपिष्णु <i>a.</i> Bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रस्त
अपत्रस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> Afraid of, (with the abl., e.g. तरंगादपत्रस्तः ‘afraid of a wave,’ भोजनादपत्रस्तः ‘afraid of food’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रस्ता
अपत्रस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> Afraid of, (with the abl., e.g. तरंगादपत्रस्तः ‘afraid of a wave,’ भोजनादपत्रस्तः ‘afraid of food’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ|अपथं|अपथः
अपथ <i>n.</i> 1. Absence of a road; 2. a bad or wrong road (lit. and fig.), e.g. अपथे पदमर्पयंति हि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथगामिन्
अपथ-गामिन् <i>a.</i> pursuing bad practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथिन्
अपथिन् <i>m.</i> The same as अपथ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्य|अपथ्यं
अपथ्य <i>a. (f. थ्या)</i> 1. Unwholesome, unfit (as food or drink), e.g. अपथ्यानामिवान्नानां परिणामो हि दारुणः; 2. inconsistent, obnoxious, e.g. वृद्धौ भजति चापथ्यं नरो येन विनश्यति; 3. bad, unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्या
अपथ्य <i>a. (f. थ्या)</i> 1. Unwholesome, unfit (as food or drink), e.g. अपथ्यानामिवान्नानां परिणामो हि दारुणः; 2. inconsistent, obnoxious, e.g. वृद्धौ भजति चापथ्यं नरो येन विनश्यति; 3. bad, unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद|अपदः
अपद <i>(I) m.</i> A reptile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद|अपदः
अपद <i>(II) n.</i> 1. No place; 2. a bad place; 3. a word which is not a पद or an inflected word (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान्तर|अपदान्तरः
अपद-अन्तर <i>(I) n.</i> proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान्तर|अपदान्तरः
अपद-अन्तर <i>(II) a.</i> proximate, very near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान|अपदानं
अपदान <i>n.</i> 1. Pure conduct; 2. an accomplished work; 3. an excellent work. (Cf. अवदान for which अपदान is probably a various reading.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदार्थ|अपदार्थः
अपदार्थ <i>m.</i> 1. Non-entity; 2. not the meaning of the words in a sentence, अपदार्थोऽपि वाक्यार्थः K.Pr.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेश|अपदेशः
अपदेश <i>m.</i> 1. Stating, adducing (as a reason), हेत्वपदेशात्प्रतिज्ञायाः पुनर्वचनं निगमनम् /Nyāya S./; 2. an argument, a reason (according to the Vaiśeṣikas, अपदेश is the second step in a syllogism); 3. a pretence, a pretext, a disguise, रक्षापदेशान्मुनिहोमधेनोः R.ii.8; 4. a butt, a mark; 5. place, quarter, e.g. त्यक्तापदेशो यतिः; 6. name, reputation; 7. deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यान|अपध्यानं
अपध्यान <i>n.</i> Evil thoughts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंस|अपध्वंसः
अपध्वंस <i>m.</i> Degradation, disgraceful conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्त|अपध्वस्तः
अपध्वस्त <i>(I) a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Reviled, blamed; 2. imperfectly pounded; 3. abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्ता
अपध्वस्त <i>(I) a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Reviled, blamed; 2. imperfectly pounded; 3. abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्त|अपध्वस्तः
अपध्वस्त <i>(II) m.</i> A wretch lost to all sense of right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनय|अपनयः
अपनय <i>m.</i> 1. Removing, taking away; 2. bad conduct, bad policy; 3. injury, disservice, ततः सपत्नापनयस्मरणानुशयस्फुरा Sis.ii.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयन|अपनयनं
अपनयन <i>n.</i> 1. Removing, taking away; 2. acquittance (as of a debt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनिर्वाण
अपनिर्वाण <i>a. (f. णा)</i> Not yet extinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनिर्वाणा
अपनिर्वाण <i>a. (f. णा)</i> Not yet extinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुत्ति|अपनुत्तिः
अपनुत्ति <i>f.</i> Removing, taking away, e.g. पापानामपनुत्तये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोद|अपनोदः
अपनोद <i>m.</i> See अपनुत्ति, e.g. ब्रह्महत्यापनोदाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोदन|अपनोदनं
अपनोदन <i>n.</i> See अपनुत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्रित|अपपात्रितः
अपपात्रित <i>m.</i> A person who has lost his caste through some great offence, and with whom his kindred will not eat or drink from a common vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपान|अपपानं
अपपान <i>n.</i> A bad drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपूत
अपपूत <i>m. du.</i> Badly formed buttocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रजाता
अपप्रजाता <i>f.</i> A woman who has miscarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रदान|अपप्रदानं
अपप्रदान <i>n.</i> A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंश|अपभ्रंशः
अपभ्रंश <i>m.</i> 1. Falling away or down, अत्यारूढिर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा Sak.iv.; 2. incorrect language (whether the form of the word be at variance with the rules of Sanskrit grammar or its sense not a Sanskritic one); 3. the name of the lowest class of Prākṛt dialects (in belles-lettres), any language other than Sanskrit (in Śāstra) आभीरादिगिरः काव्येष्वपभ्रंश इति स्मृताः । शास्त्रेषु संस्कृतादन्यदपभ्रंशतयोदितम् ॥ K.D.i.36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्द|अपमर्दः|अपमर्द्द
अपमर्द <i>m.</i> Dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान|अपमानं|अपमानः
अपमान <i>m.n.</i> Disrespect, disgrace, अथापमानेन पितुः प्रयुक्ता K.S.i.21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्जन|अपमार्जनं
अपमार्जन <i>n.</i> Cleaning, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृषित
अपमृषित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Obscure, unintelligible, e.g. अपमृषितं वाक्यमाह; 2. unpalatable, unbearable, विहितं मयाद्य सदसीदमपमृषितमच्युतार्चनं यस्य Sis.xv.46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृषिता
अपमृषित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Obscure, unintelligible, e.g. अपमृषितं वाक्यमाह; 2. unpalatable, unbearable, विहितं मयाद्य सदसीदमपमृषितमच्युतार्चनं यस्य Sis.xv.46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयान|अपयानं
अपयान <i>n.</i> Retreat, flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर <i>(I) a. (f. रा) (In some senses the word is treated as a pronoun except as the latter part of Dvan. and Bahu. compounds.)</i> 1. Posterior, following, later; 2. western, (op. to पूर्व), पूर्वापरौ तोयनिधी वगाह्य K.S.i.1; 3. last (in space or time), e.g. आद्योऽन्यतरकर्मजः । तथोभयक्रियाकन्यो भवेत्संयोगजोऽपरः ॥ (In this sense it may form with a noun a षष्ठीतत्पुरुष compound of which it is the former part, e.g. अपरकायः (अपरं कायस्य) ‘the hind part of the body’); 4. other, different, अन्ये कृतयुगे धर्मास्त्रेतायां द्वापरेऽपरे M.i.85; 5. low, inferior, (op. to पर); 6. than which there is nothing superior, i.e. supreme, absolute (for this sense, Cf. अनुत्तम and अनुत्तर). When अपर occurs as opposed to ‘the one’ (the one-the other) or to ‘some’ (some-others) used plurally, the correlative terms used are अपर, एक, अन्य, किंचित् &c., e.g. एको ययौ चैत्ररथप्रदेशान् सौराज्यरम्यानपरो विदर्भान् R.v.60, अन्ये त्वलंघिषुः शैलान् गुहास्वन्ये न्यलषेत । केचिदासिषत स्तब्धा भयात्केचिदघूर्णिषुः । उदतारिषुरंबोधिं वानराः सेतुनाऽपरे ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरा
अपर <i>(I) a. (f. रा) (In some senses the word is treated as a pronoun except as the latter part of Dvan. and Bahu. compounds.)</i> 1. Posterior, following, later; 2. western, (op. to पूर्व), पूर्वापरौ तोयनिधी वगाह्य K.S.i.1; 3. last (in space or time), e.g. आद्योऽन्यतरकर्मजः । तथोभयक्रियाकन्यो भवेत्संयोगजोऽपरः ॥ (In this sense it may form with a noun a षष्ठीतत्पुरुष compound of which it is the former part, e.g. अपरकायः (अपरं कायस्य) ‘the hind part of the body’); 4. other, different, अन्ये कृतयुगे धर्मास्त्रेतायां द्वापरेऽपरे M.i.85; 5. low, inferior, (op. to पर); 6. than which there is nothing superior, i.e. supreme, absolute (for this sense, Cf. अनुत्तम and अनुत्तर). When अपर occurs as opposed to ‘the one’ (the one-the other) or to ‘some’ (some-others) used plurally, the correlative terms used are अपर, एक, अन्य, किंचित् &c., e.g. एको ययौ चैत्ररथप्रदेशान् सौराज्यरम्यानपरो विदर्भान् R.v.60, अन्ये त्वलंघिषुः शैलान् गुहास्वन्ये न्यलषेत । केचिदासिषत स्तब्धा भयात्केचिदघूर्णिषुः । उदतारिषुरंबोधिं वानराः सेतुनाऽपरे ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर <i>(II) n.</i> 1. The hind quarter of an elephant; 2. the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर <i>(III) m.</i> An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराग्नि
अपर-अग्नि <i>m. du.</i> the गार्हपत्य and दक्षिण fires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरांग
अपर-अंग <i>n.</i> one of the eight divisions of गुणीभूतव्यंग्य viz., that in which the व्यंग्य (suggested sense) is subordinate to something else (अगूढमपरस्यांगम् K.Pr.v.) the example given there being- अयं स रसनोत्कर्षी पीनस्तनविमर्दनः । नाभ्यूरुजघनस्पर्शी नीविविस्रंसनः करः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्त|अपरान्तः
अपर-अन्त <i>(I) a.</i> living at the western border.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्त|अपरान्तः
अपर-अन्त <i>(II) m.</i> 1. the western border, the western shore; 2. death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्त|अपरान्तः
अपर-अन्त <i>(III) m. pl.</i> the country or the inhabitants of the western borders, R.iv.53, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरान्तक|अपरान्तकः
अपर-अन्तक <i>m. pl.</i> See अपरान्त III.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापर
अपर-अपर <i>a.</i> various. (Cf. अपरपर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरार्ध
अपर-अर्ध <i>m.</i> the second half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्ण|अपराह्णः
अपर-अह्ण <i>m.</i> afternoon, the last watch of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेतरा
अपर-इतरा <i>f.</i> the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरकाय
अपर-काय <i>m.</i> the hind part of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरजन|अपरजनः
अपर-जन <i>m.</i> an inhabitant of the west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्र
अपर-त्र <i>ind.</i> in another place.(एकत्र-अपरत्र the one place-in the other.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरदक्षिणम्
अपर-दक्षिणम् <i>ind.</i> in the south-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरपक्ष|अपरपक्षः
अपर-पक्ष <i>m.</i> 1. the latter or dark half of a month; 2. the other side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरपर
अपर-पर <i>a.</i> various, e.g. अपरपराः सार्था गच्छन्ति ‘various caravans travel.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरपाणिनीय
अपर-पाणिनीय <i>m. pl.</i> the pupils of Pāṇini who live in the west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरप्रणेय
अपर-प्रणेय <i>a.</i> easily led by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपररात्र|अपररात्रः
अपर-रात्र <i>m.</i> the latter half of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरलोक|अपरलोकः
अपर-लोक <i>m.</i> another world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवर्षा
अपर-वर्षा <i>f. pl.</i> the latter part of the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरशरद्
अपर-शरद् <i>f.</i> the latter part of autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्वस्तिक
अपर-स्वस्तिक <i>n.</i> the western point in the horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरहैमन
अपर-हैमन <i>a.</i> referring to the latter part of the cold season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=037-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरक्त
अपरक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Dissatisfied; 2. bloodless, pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरक्ता
अपरक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Dissatisfied; 2. bloodless, pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरति|अपरतिः
अपरति <i>f.</i> 1. Cessation; 2. dissatisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरव|अपरवः
अपरव <i>m.</i> Contest, dispute, especially about the enjoyment of property (अपरवो वर्जनविषयो रवः Vir.M.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Continued, uninterrupted, अपरस्पराः सार्था गच्छन्ति S.K. ‘the caravans go in uninterrupted continuation.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्परा
अपरस्पर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Continued, uninterrupted, अपरस्पराः सार्था गच्छन्ति S.K. ‘the caravans go in uninterrupted continuation.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरा
अपरा <i>f.</i> 1. The hind part of an elephant; 2. the west; 3. suppressed menstruation in pregnancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराक्
अपराक् <i>ind.</i> In front of, e.g. अलिर्मिलत्परागतः सरोरुहात्परागतः । मुखं मुदा परागतस्तदीयमापरागतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराग|अपरागः
अपराग <i>(I) m.</i> Aversion, antipathy, e.g. अपरागसमीरणेरितः क्रमशीर्णाकुलमूलसन्ततिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराग|अपरागः
अपराग <i>(II) a. (f. गा)</i> Discoloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरागा
अपराग <i>(II) a. (f. गा)</i> Discoloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराच्
अपराच् <i>a. (f. राची)</i> In front, not averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराची
अपराच् <i>a. (f. राची)</i> In front, not averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराङ्मुख|अपराङ्मुखः
अपराङ्मुख <i>a.</i> 1. with unaverted face; 2. presenting a firm front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजित|अपराजितः
अपराजित <i>m.</i> 1. A name of Viṣṇu; 2. a name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजिता
अपराजिता <i>f.</i> 1. A name of Durgā; 2. the north-east quarter; 3. a kind of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्ध
अपराद्ध <i>a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Sinned, committed (as an offence), e.g. न मया किञ्चिदपराद्धम्, (generally used with the loc. and occasionally with the gen. of the person offended, कस्मिन्नपि पूजार्हेपराद्धा शकुन्तला Sak.iv.); 2. missed (as an arrow), निमित्तादपरद्धेषोर्धानुष्कस्येव Sis.ii.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धा
अपराद्ध <i>a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Sinned, committed (as an offence), e.g. न मया किञ्चिदपराद्धम्, (generally used with the loc. and occasionally with the gen. of the person offended, कस्मिन्नपि पूजार्हेपराद्धा शकुन्तला Sak.iv.); 2. missed (as an arrow), निमित्तादपरद्धेषोर्धानुष्कस्येव Sis.ii.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धि|अपराद्धिः
अपराद्धि <i>f.</i> 1. Sin; 2. an offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध|अपराधः
अपराध <i>m.</i> Offence, transgression, fault, यथापराधदण्डानाम् R.i.6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रह|अपरिग्रहः
अपरिग्रह <i>(I) a. (f. हा)</i> Destitute of belongings (as a Yogin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रहा
अपरिग्रह <i>(I) a. (f. हा)</i> Destitute of belongings (as a Yogin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रह|अपरिग्रहः
अपरिग्रह <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Non-acceptance; 2. destitution, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छद
अपरिच्छद <i>a. (f. दा)</i> Without property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छदा
अपरिच्छद <i>a. (f. दा)</i> Without property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणीता
अपरिणीता <i>f.</i> An unmarried girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपक्व|अपरिपक्वं
अपरिपक्व <i>a. (f. क्वा)</i> Not quite mature (lit. and fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपक्वा
अपरिपक्व <i>a. (f. क्वा)</i> Not quite mature (lit. and fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपन्थिन्
अपरिपन्थिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Not antagonistic, तदस्मिन् प्रयोजने प्रियसखी मेऽपरिपन्थिनी भवतु M.M.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपन्थिनी
अपरिपन्थिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Not antagonistic, तदस्मिन् प्रयोजने प्रियसखी मेऽपरिपन्थिनी भवतु M.M.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसंख्यान|अपरिसङ्ख्यान|अपरिसंख्यानं
अपरिसंख्यान <i>n.</i> Innumerableness, infinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीक्षित
अपरीक्षित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Ill-considered, foolish; 2. untried; 3. not clearly established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीक्षिता
अपरीक्षित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Ill-considered, foolish; 2. untried; 3. not clearly established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीक्षितकारिन्
अपरीक्षित-कारिन् <i>a.</i> acting inconsiderately, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेण
अपरेण <i>ind.</i> In the west which is not far, e.g. अपरेण वसति. (with the acc. or gen., e.g. अपरेण ग्रामं or ग्रामस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेद्युस्
अपरेद्युस् <i>ind.</i> On the following day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्ष
अपरोक्ष <i>a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Not invisible, perceptible to the senses; 2. not distant, not remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्षा
अपरोक्ष <i>a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Not invisible, perceptible to the senses; 2. not distant, not remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्षम्
अपरोक्षम् <i>ind.</i> In the sight of, perceptibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=038-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोध|अपरोधः
अपरोध <i>m.</i> Exclusion, prohibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्णा|अपर्ण्णा
अपर्णा <i>f.</i> A name of Pārvatī. (Kālidāsa derives the word as follows- स्वयं विशीर्णद्रुमपर्णवृत्तिनां परा हि काष्ठा तपसस्तया पुनः । तदप्याकीर्णमतः प्रियंवदां वदन्त्यपर्णेति च तां पुराविदः ॥ K.S.v.28).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्तं
अपर्याप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> 1. Incomplete, insufficient; 2. unable, incompetent, अपर्याप्तं तदस्माकं बलं भीष्माभिरक्षितम् Bg.i.30; 3. unlimited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याप्ता
अपर्याप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> 1. Incomplete, insufficient; 2. unable, incompetent, अपर्याप्तं तदस्माकं बलं भीष्माभिरक्षितम् Bg.i.30; 3. unlimited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याय|अपर्यायः|अपर्य्याय
अपर्याय <i>m.</i> Want of order or method.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपल|अपलं
अपल <i>n.</i> A pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलपन|अपलपनं
अपलपन <i>n.</i> The same as अपलाप q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाप|अपलापः
अपलाप <i>m.</i> 1. Denial of knowledge, evasion, e.g. न च प्रत्यक्शसिद्धस्यापलापः कर्तुं शक्यते; 2. concealing, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलापदण्ड
अपलाप-दण्ड <i>m.</i> the fine inflicted on a defendant for denying a charge on which he gets convicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिका
अपलाषिका <i>f.</i> 1. Thirst; 2. ardent desire. (अपलासिका is also used in the same sense but probably wrongly.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिन्
अपलाषिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Free from desires, e.g. प्रलापिनो भविष्यन्ति कदान्वेतेऽपलाषिणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिणी
अपलाषिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Free from desires, e.g. प्रलापिनो भविष्यन्ति कदान्वेतेऽपलाषिणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवन|अपवनं
अपवन <i>n.</i> A park or forest planted in the vicinity of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरक|अपवरकः
अपवरक <i>m.</i> 1. A hole, an aperture, ततश्च एकस्मादपवरकात् Mud.i.; 2. an inner apartment, a lying-in chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरण|अपवरणं
अपवरण <i>n.</i> Covering, screening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ग|अपवर्गः
अपवर्ग <i>m.</i> 1. Completion, complete performance, क्रियापवर्गेष्वनुजोविसात्कृताः Kir.i.14, अपवर्गे तृतीया Pan., अपवर्गे तृतीयेति भणतः पाणिनेरपि Na.xvii.68; 2. final beatitude, i.e. complete delivery of the soul from the body, e.g. स्वर्गापवर्गयोर्मार्गमामनन्ति मनीषिणः; 3. a gift, a donation; 4. restriction of a general rule (according to सुश्रुत); 5. abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्जन|अपवर्जनं|अपवर्ज्जन|अपवर्ज्जनं
अपवर्जन <i>n.</i> 1. Abandoning; 2. a gift, a donation; 3. final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तन|अपवर्तनं|अपवर्त्तन
अपवर्तन <i>n.</i> 1. Removal from one place to another, as in स्थानापवर्तन; 2. taking away, depriving one of, e.g. न च दायापवर्तनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाद|अपवादः
अपवाद <i>m.</i> 1. Refutation as of an erroneous imputation, e.g. अपवदो नाम रज्जुविवर्तस्य सर्पस्य रज्जुमात्रत्ववत् &c. (in Vedānta phil.); 2. an exception, (op. to उत्सर्ग), अपवादैरिवोत्सर्गाः कृतव्यावृत्तयः परैः K.S.ii.27; 3. censure, blame, evil report, e.g. लोकापवादादपि न भीतोऽसि; 4. an order, a command, ततोऽपवादेन पताकिनीपतेः Kir.xiv.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारण|अपवारणं
अपवारण <i>n.</i> Concealment, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारित|अपवारितं
अपवारित <i>n.</i> 1. Secret manner; 2. apart, aside (in plays), तद्भवेदपवारितम् । रहस्यं तु यदन्यस्य परावृत्य प्रकाशते S.D.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारितक
अपवारितक <i>n.</i> The same as अपवारित q.v. (The inst. अपवारितकेन means ‘apart,’ ‘aside’ in theatrical language and is opposed to प्रकाशम्; it is speaking in such a way that only the addressed person may hear. अपवार्य also used in the same sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाह|अपवाहः
अपवाह <i>m.</i> Deduction, subtraction (in math.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाहन|अपवाहनं
अपवाहन <i>n.</i> The same as अपवाह q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृति|अपवृतिः
अपवृति <i>f.</i> Uncovering, opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृक्ति|अपवृक्तिः
अपवृक्ति <i>f.</i> Completion, fulfilment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्ति|अपवृत्तिः
अपवृत्ति <i>f.</i> Cessation, end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध <i>(I) a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Rejected, discarded; 2. abject, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्धा
अपविद्ध <i>(I) a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Rejected, discarded; 2. abject, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध <i>(II) m.</i> One of the twelve kinds of sons among the Hindus, viz., that rejected by his natural parents and adopted by a stranger, Yaj.ii.132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवेध|अपवेधः
अपवेध <i>m.</i> Piercing in a wrong direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्यय|अपव्ययः
अपव्यय <i>m.</i> Prodigality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशद|अपशदः
अपशद <i>m.</i> A low man, a wretch, (the same as अपसद which probably is more correct).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशुच्
अपशुच् <i>m.</i> The soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोक|अपशोकः
अपशोक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> Free from grief or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोका
अपशोक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> Free from grief or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोक|अपशोकः
अपशोक <i>(II) m.</i> The aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्चिम
अपश्चिम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Not last; 2. not having another in the rear, i.e. last, अयमपश्चिमस्ते रामस्य शिरसि पादपंकज स्पर्शः Ut.i., प्रसीदतु महारजो समानेनापश्चिमेन प्रणयेन Ve.vi.; 3. extreme, e.g. अपश्चिमामिमां कष्टामापदम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्चिमा
अपश्चिम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Not last; 2. not having another in the rear, i.e. last, अयमपश्चिमस्ते रामस्य शिरसि पादपंकज स्पर्शः Ut.i., प्रसीदतु महारजो समानेनापश्चिमेन प्रणयेन Ve.vi.; 3. extreme, e.g. अपश्चिमामिमां कष्टामापदम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्वास|अपश्वासः
अपश्वास <i>m.</i> The same as अपान q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठ|अपष्ठं
अपष्ठ <i>n.</i> The point of the hook for driving an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठु|अपष्ठुः
अपष्ठु <i>a.</i> See अपष्ठुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुर|अपष्ठुरं
अपष्ठुर(ल) <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Contrary, opposite, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुल|अपष्ठुलं
अपष्ठुर(ल) <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Contrary, opposite, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुरा
अपष्ठुर(ल) <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Contrary, opposite, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसद|अपसदः
अपसद <i>m.</i> 1. A low man, an outcaste (in this sense generally as last member of a compound, e.g. पांचालापसद); 2. the children of six degrading connections, viz., of a Brāhmaṇa with the women of the three lower classes, of a Kṣatriya with the women of the two lower, and of a Vaiśya with one of the Śūdra class, M.x.10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्जन|अपसर्जनं|अपसर्ज्जन|अपसर्ज्जनं
अपसर्जन <i>n.</i> 1. Abandonment; 2. gift, donation; 3. final deliverance or beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=039-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर|अपसरः
अपसर <i>m.</i> 1. A valid reason; 2. departure, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरण|अपसरणं
अपसरण <i>n.</i> Going away, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्प|अपसर्पः
अपसर्प <i>m.</i> A spy, a secret emissary, सर्पाधिराजोरुभुजोऽपसर्पं पप्रच्छ भद्रं विजितारिभद्रः R.xiv.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पण|अपसर्पणं
अपसर्पण <i>n.</i> Going away, retreating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसार|अपसारः
अपसार <i>m.</i> The same as अपसरण q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारण|अपसारणं
अपसारण <i>n.</i> Removing, driving away, expelling, e.g. चौरापसारणमपि कविभिर्वर्ण्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृप्ति|अपसृप्तिः
अपसृप्ति <i>f.</i> See अपसर्पण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कर|अपस्करः
अपस्कर <i>m.</i> 1. Any part of a carriage except the wheel; 2. anus; 3. vulva; 4. excrements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पर्श
अपस्पर्श <i>a. (f. र्शा)</i> Insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पर्शा
अपस्पर्श <i>a. (f. र्शा)</i> Insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मार|अपस्मारः
अपस्मार <i>m.</i> Epilepsy, falling sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह
अपह <i>a. (f. हा)</i> Destroying, removing. (This word occurs only as the last part of Tatpur. compounds, e.g. क्लेशापह, ज्वरापह &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहा
अपह <i>a. (f. हा)</i> Destroying, removing. (This word occurs only as the last part of Tatpur. compounds, e.g. क्लेशापह, ज्वरापह &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहति|अपहतिः
अपहति <i>f.</i> Removing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरण|अपहरणं
अपहरण <i>n.</i> 1. Taking away, removing; 2. stealing, robbing (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तित
अपहस्तित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Thrown off, lost, parted with, अपहस्तितबांधवो त्वया विहितं साहसमस्य तृष्णया M.M.ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तिता
अपहस्तित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Thrown off, lost, parted with, अपहस्तितबांधवो त्वया विहितं साहसमस्य तृष्णया M.M.ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहानि|अपहानिः
अपहानि <i>f.</i> 1. Abandonment; 2. exception, exclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहार|अपहारः
अपहार <i>m.</i> The same as अपहरण q.v.(The word is used figuratively also, कथं वा आत्मापहारं करोमि Sak.i., ‘or how shall I conceal myself, i.e. my name and real position.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहीन
अपहीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Left, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहीना
अपहीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Left, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नव|अपह्नवः
अपह्नव <i>m.</i> 1. Denial, concealment of knowledge, e.g. अभियुक्तोभियोगस्य यदि कुर्यादपह्नवम्; 2. dissimulation; 3. affection, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नुति|अपह्नुतिः
अपह्नुति <i>f.</i> 1. Denial, concealment of knowledge; 2. a figure of speech in which the real character of an object is denied and that of another super-imposed upon it, e.g. नेदं नभोमण्डलमम्बुराशिः. (For other instances, See K.Pr.x. under अपह्नुति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्रास|अपह्रासः
अपह्रास <i>m.</i> Diminution, lessening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्
अपाक् <i>ind.</i> Westward, southward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरण|अपाकरणं
अपाकरण <i>n.</i> 1. Driving away, removal; 2. payment, liquidation, as of a debt (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकर्मन्|अपाकर्म्मन्
अपाकर्मन् <i>n.</i> Payment, liquidation, e.g. वेतनस्यानपाकर्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृति|अपाकृतिः
अपाकृति <i>f.</i> Emotion arising from fear &c., अपाकृतीस्ततस्ततस्त्या विनियन्तुमक्षमा Kir.i.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्ष|अपाक्षं
अपाक्ष <i>(I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> Present, perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्षा
अपाक्ष <i>(I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> Present, perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्ष|अपाक्षं
अपाक्ष <i>(II) a. (f. क्षी)</i> Eyeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्षी
