अपाचीना
अपाचीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Opposite; 2. western; 3. southern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाणिनीय
अपाणिनीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. Not taught by Pāṇini (as a rule &c.); 2. one who does not study Pāṇini’s grammar, a superficial sanskritist. (पाणिनीयमधीते पाणिनीयो न पाणिनीयोऽपाणिनीयः Kāśikā.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाणिनीया
अपाणिनीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. Not taught by Pāṇini (as a rule &c.); 2. one who does not study Pāṇini’s grammar, a superficial sanskritist. (पाणिनीयमधीते पाणिनीयो न पाणिनीयोऽपाणिनीयः Kāśikā.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्र|अपात्रं
अपात्र <i>n.</i> 1. A worthless utensil, or object; 2. an undeserving or worthless person; 3. one not worthy of receiving gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रकृत्या
अपात्र-कृत्या <i>f.</i> an action which makes a man worthless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रक्रिया
अपात्र-क्रिया <i>f.</i> doing an improper act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रदायिन्
अपात्र-दायिन् <i>a.</i> giving to the undeserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रभृत्
अपात्र-भृत् <i>a.</i> cherishing the worthless, e.g. प्रायेणापात्रभृद्भवति राजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपादान|अपादानं
अपादान <i>n.</i> 1. Taking away, removal; 2. the sense expressed by the fifth case in Sanskrit (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान|अपानं|अपानः
अपान <i>m.</i> 1. The anus; 2. that of the five vital airs which goes downwards and out at the anus (the other four being प्राण, उदान, समान and व्यान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानद्वार
अपान-द्वार <i>n.</i> the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानपवन|अपानपवनः
अपान-पवन, -वायु <i>m.</i> the vital air called अपान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

