अपाय|अपायः
अपाय <i>m.</i> 1. Going away, passing away; 2. separation, जातं प्रियापाये कद्वदं हंसकोकिलम् Bt.vi.75; 3. absence, disappearance; 4. loss, injury, यत्रापायः संभवति तत्रोपायोऽप्यस्ति Hit.i.; 5. death; 6. misfortune, calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=040-39" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार|अपारं|अपारः
अपार <i>(I) a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Unbounded, shoreless, illimitable; 2. out of reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=041-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारा
अपार <i>(I) a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Unbounded, shoreless, illimitable; 2. out of reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=041-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

