अपेहि
अपेहि Imperative sing. of इ with अप q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेहिद्वितीया
अपेहि-द्वितीया <i>f.</i> a festival or ceremony where followers are denied admission; (similarly we have अपेहिप्रघसा, अपेहिवाणिजा, अपेहिविघसा, अपेहिस्वागता &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोगण्ड|अपोगंडः|अपोगण्डः
अपोगण्ड <i>a. (f. ण्डा)</i> 1. Having a limb too many or too few; 2. infant; 3. timid, fearful; 4. not under sixteen years of age, M.viii.148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोगण्डा
अपोगण्ड <i>a. (f. ण्डा)</i> 1. Having a limb too many or too few; 2. infant; 3. timid, fearful; 4. not under sixteen years of age, M.viii.148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढ
अपोढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Removed from, (with the abl., e.g. कल्पनाया अपोढः); 2. not put on, R.xvi.73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढा
अपोढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Removed from, (with the abl., e.g. कल्पनाया अपोढः); 2. not put on, R.xvi.73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह|अपोहः
अपोह <i>n.</i> 1. Removing, taking off; 2. removal of doubt by the exercise of the reasoning faculty; 3. negative reasoning, (op. to ऊह), ऊहापोहमिमं सरोजनयना यावद्वोधत्तेतराम् Bh.V.ii.74; 4. the exclusion of all things which do not come under the category in question. (अपोहः अतद्व्यावृत्तिः says Maheśvara on तद्वानपोहो वा शब्दार्थः K.Pr.ii.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहन|अपोहनं
अपोहन <i>n.</i> Reasoning faculty, (the same as अपोह q.v.), मत्तः स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनं च Bg.xv.15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह्य
अपोह्य <i>a. (f. ह्या)</i> To be removed or taken away, e.g. एतैर्व्रतैरपोह्यं स्यादेनो हिंसासमुद्भवम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह्या
अपोह्य <i>a. (f. ह्या)</i> To be removed or taken away, e.g. एतैर्व्रतैरपोह्यं स्यादेनो हिंसासमुद्भवम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुषेय
अपौरुषेय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Not being of human origin, not made by men, of divine origin, as ग्रन्थोऽपौरुषेयः पौरुषेयोऽथवा Jaim.N.M.; अपौरुषेयप्रतिष्ठः M.M.ix. (not established by man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=042-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

