अभिप्रोक्षण|अभिप्रोक्षणं
अभिप्रोक्षण <i>n.</i> Sprinkling upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लुत
अभिप्लुत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Overpowered, overrun (lit.), overwhelmed (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लुता
अभिप्लुत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Overpowered, overrun (lit.), overwhelmed (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिबुद्धि|अभिबुद्धिः
अभिबुद्धि <i>f.</i> An organ of apprehension of which there are five, viz., (1) ear; (2) skin; (3) eye; (4) tongue, and (5) nose (more usually called ज्ञानेन्द्रियाणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभव|अभिभवः
अभिभव <i>m.</i> 1. Defeat, subjugation, अभिभवः कुत एव सपत्नजः R.ix.4; 2. the being overpowered, सूर्यकान्तस्तदन्यतेजोऽभिभवाद्वमन्ति Sak.ii.; 3. humiliation, abatement of pride, अलभ्यशोकाभिभवेयमाक्तुर्विमानना सुभ्रु कुतः पितुर्गृहे K.S.v.43; 4. contempt, disrespect, निरभिभवसाराः परकथाः Bhartr.ii.64; 5. rise, spread, अधर्माभिभवान्कृष्य प्रदुष्यन्ति कुलस्त्रियः Bg.i.41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवन|अभिभवनं
