अभिभावुक <i>a. (f. का)</i> The same as अभिभाविन् q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाषण|अभिभाषणं
अभिभाषण <i>n.</i> Addressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूति|अभिभूतिः
अभिभूति <i>f.</i> 1. Defeat, discomfiture, अभिभूतिभयादसूनतः सुखमुज्झन्ति न धाम मानिनः Kir.ii.20; 2. disrespect, humiliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमत|अभिमतं|अभिमतः
अभिमत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Wished, desired, agreeable, अभिमतफलशंसी चारु पुस्फोर बाहुः Bt.i.27; 2. agreed, approved, admitted, प्रसिद्धमाहात्म्याभिमतानामपि तीर्थकाराणां कपिलकणभुक्प्रभृतीनाम् S.Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमता
अभिमत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Wished, desired, agreeable, अभिमतफलशंसी चारु पुस्फोर बाहुः Bt.i.27; 2. agreed, approved, admitted, प्रसिद्धमाहात्म्याभिमतानामपि तीर्थकाराणां कपिलकणभुक्प्रभृतीनाम् S.Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमत|अभिमतं|अभिमतः
अभिमत <i>(II) n.</i> Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनस्
अभिमनस् <i>a.</i> Wishing for, longing for, भवतोऽभिमताः समीहते सरुषः कर्तुमुपैत्य माननाम् Sis.xvi.2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रण|अभिमंत्रणं|अभिमन्त्रणं
अभिमन्त्रण <i>n.</i> 1. Calling, addressing, inviting; 2. consecrating, i.e. making sacred by reciting mantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर|अभिमरः
अभिमर <i>m.</i> 1. Killing, slaughter; 2. war, combat; 3. danger from one’s own party, treachery; 4. a binding, a tie or fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्द|अभिमर्दः|अभिमर्द्द|अभिमर्द्दः
अभिमर्द <i>n.</i> 1. Rubbing; 2. invasion, devastation of a country; 3. war, battle; 4. spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दन|अभिमर्द्दन
अभिमर्दन <i>n.</i> Oppression, devastation of a country (by an enemy &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्श|अभिमर्शः
अभिमर्श(र्ष) <i>m.</i> 1. Touch, contact; 2. sexual intercourse, कृताभिमर्शामनुमन्य्मानः सुतां त्वया Sak.v. or त्वत्कलत्राभिमर्शी वैरास्पदं धनमित्रः D.K.; 3. insult, offence, K.S.v.43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्ष|अभिमर्षः
अभिमर्श(र्ष) <i>m.</i> 1. Touch, contact; 2. sexual intercourse, कृताभिमर्शामनुमन्य्मानः सुतां त्वया Sak.v. or त्वत्कलत्राभिमर्शी वैरास्पदं धनमित्रः D.K.; 3. insult, offence, K.S.v.43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शन|अभिमर्शनं
अभिमर्श(र्ष)न <i>n.</i> The same as अभिमर्ष q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्षण|अभिमर्षणं
अभिमर्श(र्ष)न <i>n.</i> The same as अभिमर्ष q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाद|अभिमादः
अभिमाद <i>m.</i> Ebriety, intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमान|अभिमानः
अभिमान <i>m.</i> 1. Self-respect, honourable feeling, अभिमानधनस्य गत्वरैरसुभिः स्थास्नु यशश्चिचीषतः Kir.ix.19; 2. pride, arrogance, self-conceit, e.g. प्रायो मूर्खः परिभवविधौ नाभिमानं पिधत्ते; 3. affection; 4. solicitation, wish, desire; 5. misconception, conceiving objects with the notion that they refer to one’s own self (in phil.); 6. killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानशालिन्
अभिमान-शालिन् <i>a.</i> possessed of self-respect, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिन्
अभिमानिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> 1. Possessed of self respect; 2. proud, arrogant; 3. one who conceives objects with the notion that they refer to one’s own self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिनी
अभिमानिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> 1. Possessed of self respect; 2. proud, arrogant; 3. one who conceives objects with the notion that they refer to one’s own self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभिमुख <i>a. (f. खा or खी)</i> 1. With the face directed towards, facing, fronting, e.g. शार्दुलोऽभिमुखोऽभ्येति; 2. near, approaching, ready for, पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R.vii.1, प्रातः प्रयाणाभिमुखाय तस्मै R.v.29, निद्रा चिरेण नयनाभिमुखी बभूव R.v.64; 3. friendly disposed; 4. with the face upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखा
अभिमुख <i>a. (f. खा or खी)</i> 1. With the face directed towards, facing, fronting, e.g. शार्दुलोऽभिमुखोऽभ्येति; 2. near, approaching, ready for, पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R.vii.1, प्रातः प्रयाणाभिमुखाय तस्मै R.v.29, निद्रा चिरेण नयनाभिमुखी बभूव R.v.64; 3. friendly disposed; 4. with the face upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखी
अभिमुख <i>a. (f. खा or खी)</i> 1. With the face directed towards, facing, fronting, e.g. शार्दुलोऽभिमुखोऽभ्येति; 2. near, approaching, ready for, पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R.vii.1, प्रातः प्रयाणाभिमुखाय तस्मै R.v.29, निद्रा चिरेण नयनाभिमुखी बभूव R.v.64; 3. friendly disposed; 4. with the face upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखम्
अभिमुखम् <i>ind.</i> In the direction of, in front of, कर्ण ददात्यभिमुखं मयि भाषमाणे Sak.i., तिष्ठन्मुनेरभिमुखं स विकीर्णधाम्नः Kir.ii.59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृष्ट
अभिमृष्ट <i>a. (f. ष्टा)</i> Touched, rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृष्टा
अभिमृष्ट <i>a. (f. ष्टा)</i> Touched, rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिम्लान
अभिम्लान <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Quite withered, quite faded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिम्लाना
अभिम्लान <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Quite withered, quite faded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाचना
अभियाचना <i>f.</i> A solicitation, a request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाच्ञा
अभियाच्ञा <i>f.</i> See the preceding word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाति|अभियातिः
अभियाति <i>m.</i> A foe, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातिन्
अभियातिन् <i>n.</i> See अभियाति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातृ
अभियातृ <i>m.</i> See अभियाति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियान|अभियानं
अभियान <i>n.</i> 1. Coming near, approaching; 2. attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियायिन्
अभियायिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Going towards with a hostile intention, attacking, R.xii.43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियायिनी
अभियायिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Going towards with a hostile intention, attacking, R.xii.43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्त|अभियुक्तः
अभियुक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Assaulted, attacked, अभियुक्तं त्वयैनं ते (scil. नृपाः) गन्तारस्त्वायतः परे Sis.ii.101; 2. assiduous, studiously engaged in, e.g. स्वकर्मण्यभियुक्तः; 3. versed in, skilled, शास्त्रार्थेष्वभियुक्तानां पुरुषाणाम् Kumārila.; 4. learned, of acknowledged position (as an author or a language); 5. charged, prosecuted (in law), अभियुक्तोऽभियोगस्य यदि कुर्यादपह्नवम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्ता
अभियुक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Assaulted, attacked, अभियुक्तं त्वयैनं ते (scil. नृपाः) गन्तारस्त्वायतः परे Sis.ii.101; 2. assiduous, studiously engaged in, e.g. स्वकर्मण्यभियुक्तः; 3. versed in, skilled, शास्त्रार्थेष्वभियुक्तानां पुरुषाणाम् Kumārila.; 4. learned, of acknowledged position (as an author or a language); 5. charged, prosecuted (in law), अभियुक्तोऽभियोगस्य यदि कुर्यादपह्नवम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=049-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तृ
अभियोक्तृ <i>m.</i> 1. An assailant, an enemy; 2. a plaintiff, an accuser, न कश्चिदभियोक्तारं दिव्येषु विनियोजयेत् Kat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोग|अभियोगः
अभियोग <i>m.</i> 1. Attack, onset, battle, क्षुभितं वनगोचराभियोगात् Kir.xiii.10; 2. energetic effort; 3. learning, scholarship, अनभियोगश्च शब्ददेरशिष्टानाम् । अभियोगश्चेतरेषाम् Śabara.; 4. close application, connection, अद्यापि तत्कनककुंडलघृष्टगण्डमास्यं स्मरामि विपरीतरताभियोगे Ch.P.11; 5. a charge, an offence as subject of an accusation, अभियोगमनिस्तीर्य नैनं प्रत्यभियोजयेत् Yaj.ii.10, (अभियुज्यत इत्यभियोगोऽपराधः Mit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोगिन्
अभियोगिन् <i>m.</i> A plaintiff, a prosecutor (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षा
अभिरक्षा <i>f.</i> Protection in every quarter, universal or complete protection, प्रशान्तबाधं दिशतोऽभिरक्षया Kir.i.18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरति|अभिरतिः
अभिरति <i>f.</i> Pleasure, delight, attachment, न मृगयाभिरतिर्न दुरोदरम् R.ix.7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरमण|अभिरमणं
अभिरमण <i>n.</i> Delighting in, finding pleasure in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराम|अभिरामः
अभिराम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Pleasing, delightful, agreeable, मनोभिरामाः शृण्वन्तौ रथनेमिस्वनोन्मुखैः R.i.39; 2. beautiful, अभिरामेण वपुषा तस्य नोदितः R.x.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरामा
अभिराम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Pleasing, delightful, agreeable, मनोभिरामाः शृण्वन्तौ रथनेमिस्वनोन्मुखैः R.i.39; 2. beautiful, अभिरामेण वपुषा तस्य नोदितः R.x.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचि|अभिरुचिः
अभिरुचि <i>f.</i> 1. Relish or taste for, pleasure, delight, भैक्षे चाभिरुचिर्धनेषु विरतिः शश्वत्समाधौ रतिः Silhaṇa.; 2. ambition, a strong desire, यक्षसि चाभिरुचिर्व्यसनं श्रुतौ Bhartr.ii.63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुत
अभिरुत <i>n.</i> Any cry, noise, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूप|अभिरूपः
अभिरूप <i>(I) a. (f. पा)</i> 1. Pleasing, agreeable, handsome, उत्कृष्टायाभिरूपाय वराय सदृशाय च M.ix.88; 2. conformable to, काममनाभिरूपमस्यां वयसो वल्कलम् Sak.i.; 3. learned, wise, आर्ये अभिरूपभूयिष्ठा परिषदियम् Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूपा
अभिरूप <i>(I) a. (f. पा)</i> 1. Pleasing, agreeable, handsome, उत्कृष्टायाभिरूपाय वराय सदृशाय च M.ix.88; 2. conformable to, काममनाभिरूपमस्यां वयसो वल्कलम् Sak.i.; 3. learned, wise, आर्ये अभिरूपभूयिष्ठा परिषदियम् Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूप|अभिरूपः
अभिरूप <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The moon; 2. Kāmadeva; 3. Viṣṇu; 4. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूपपति|अभिरूपपतिः
अभिरूप-पति <i>m.</i> the name of a fast observed in order to obtain a desirable husband in the next world, Mrich.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलंघन|अभिलङ्घन|अभिलंघनं
अभिलंघन <i>n.</i> Jumping over or across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषण|अभिलषणं
अभिलषण <i>n.</i> Wishing, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषित
अभिलषित <i>n.</i> Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाप|अभिलापः
अभिलाप <i>m.</i> Speech, expression, वस्तुतस्तु पृथ्वीपतिदत्तनामाभिलापोऽयम् Nāgeśabhaṭṭa on R.G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाव|अभिलावः
अभिलाव <i>m.</i> Cutting, destroying, वनाभिलावान् कुर्वन्तः स्वेच्छया चारुविक्रमाः Bt.viii.87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाष|अभिलाषः
अभिलाष <i>m.</i> 1. Desire, wish, अतोऽभिलाषे प्रथमं तथाविधे R.iii.4; 2. longing especially of one in love; न खलु सत्यमेव शकुन्तलायां ममाभिलाषः Sak.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषुक|अभिलाषुकः
अभिलाषुक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Wishing, desiring, covetous, (with the acc. जयमत्रभवान्नूनमरातिष्वाभिलाषुकः Kir.xi.18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषुका
अभिलाषुक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Wishing, desiring, covetous, (with the acc. जयमत्रभवान्नूनमरातिष्वाभिलाषुकः Kir.xi.18).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलीन
अभिलीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Adhering, embracing, shrouding, Megh.i.36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलीना
अभिलीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Adhering, embracing, shrouding, Megh.i.36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलुलित
अभिलुलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Disturbed, agitated, inconvenienced, अनभिलुलितज्याघातांकम् Sak.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलुलिता
अभिलुलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Disturbed, agitated, inconvenienced, अनभिलुलितज्याघातांकम् Sak.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलूता
अभिलूता <i>f.</i> A kind of spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवदन|अभिवदनं
अभिवदन <i>n.</i> 1. Addressing, allocution; 2. salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवन्दन|अभिवंदनं
अभिवन्दन <i>n.</i> Saluting respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवर्षण|अभिवर्षणं
अभिवर्षण <i>n.</i> Raining upon, rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद|अभिवादः
अभिवाद <i>m.</i> The same as अभिवादन q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादक|अभिवादकः
अभिवादक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Respectful, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादका
अभिवादक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Respectful, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादन|अभिवादनं
अभिवादन <i>n.</i> Respectful salutation of a superior or elder by an inferior or junior for the sake of obtaining his blessing. (It consists of three acts- (1) प्रत्युत्थान or rising from the seat; (2) उपसंग्रहण or touching the feet, and (3) अभिवाद or the uttering of the formula of salutation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविधि|अभिविधिः
अभिविधि <i>m.</i> Complete pervasion, inclusion of the point of limit, e.g. आङ्मर्यादाभिविध्योः ‘आ means until exclusively’ (i.e. excluding the point of limit) and until inclusively (i.e. including the point of limit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविश्रुत
अभिविश्रुत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Widely known, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविश्रुता
अभिविश्रुत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Widely known, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवृद्धि|अभिवृद्धिः
अभिवृद्धि <i>f.</i> Growth, increase, augmentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्त
अभिव्यक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> Revealed, made manifest, distinct, apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्ता
अभिव्यक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> Revealed, made manifest, distinct, apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्ति|अभिव्यक्तिः
अभिव्यक्ति <i>f.</i> The becoming clear, manifestation, revelation, दूतीसंप्रेषणैर्नार्या भावाभिव्यक्तिरिष्यते S.D.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यञ्जन|अभिव्यंजनं
अभिव्यञ्जन <i>n.</i> The act of manifesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यापक
अभिव्यापक <i>a. (f. पिका)</i> Comprehending, including, surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यापिका
अभिव्यापक <i>a. (f. पिका)</i> Comprehending, including, surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याप्ति|अभिव्याप्तिः
अभिव्याप्ति <i>f.</i> Universal pervasion, comprehension, (the same as अभिविधि q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहरण|अभिव्याहरणं
अभिव्याहरण <i>n.</i> 1. Pronouncing, uttering, speaking; 2. an uttered word or speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहार|अभिव्याहारः
अभिव्याहार <i>m.</i> The same अभिव्याहरण q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=050-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसन|अभिशंसनं
अभिशंसन <i>n.</i> Blaming, insulting, uttering an accusation whether founded on truth or not, यदा तु ब्राह्मणः क्षत्रियादेरभिशंसनं करोति Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंका|अभिशङ्का
अभिशंका <i>f.</i> Fear, alarm, doubt, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशपन|अभिशपनं
अभिशपन <i>n.</i> The same as अभिशाप q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशब्दित
अभिशब्दित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Said, declared, named, e.g. दक्षस्य दुहिता या तु सुरभीत्याभिशब्दिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशब्दिता
अभिशब्दित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Said, declared, named, e.g. दक्षस्य दुहिता या तु सुरभीत्याभिशब्दिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्त|अभिशस्तः
अभिशस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Insulted, blamed, accused (especially wrongly), e.g. अभिशस्तो मृषा कृच्छ्रं चरेदाग्नेयमेव वा; 2. ill-famed, defamed; 3. hurt, injured, inflicted, देवि केनाभिशस्तासि केन वासि विमानिता Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्ता
अभिशस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Insulted, blamed, accused (especially wrongly), e.g. अभिशस्तो मृषा कृच्छ्रं चरेदाग्नेयमेव वा; 2. ill-famed, defamed; 3. hurt, injured, inflicted, देवि केनाभिशस्तासि केन वासि विमानिता Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्ति|अभिशस्तिः
अभिश(ष)स्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Abuse, calumny, scandal, defamation; 2. asking, begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषस्ति
अभिश(ष)स्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Abuse, calumny, scandal, defamation; 2. asking, begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशाप|अभिशापः
अभिशाप <i>m.</i> 1. Charge, accusation (अभिशापः पातकाभियोगः Mit.); 2. a curse, an imprecation; 3. calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=051-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशापज्वर
