अभीषु|अभीषुः
अभीषु <i>m.</i> 1. A ray of light; 2. a rein; 3. desire; 4. attachment, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Wished, desired; 2. dear, beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टा
अभीष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Wished, desired; 2. dear, beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट <i>(II) n.</i> Desired object, e.g. अन्यस्मै हृदयं देहि नानभीष्टे घटामहे Bt.xx.24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टा
अभीष्टा <i>f.</i> A beloved woman, a mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्न
अभुग्न <i>a. (f. ग्ना)</i> 1. Straight, not bent; 2. well, free from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्ना
अभुग्न <i>a. (f. ग्ना)</i> 1. Straight, not bent; 2. well, free from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुजिष्य
अभुजिष्य <i>a. (f. ष्या)</i> Not a servant, i.e. independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुजिष्या
अभुजिष्य <i>a. (f. ष्या)</i> Not a servant, i.e. independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभू
अभू <i>m.</i> An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूत
अभूत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Non-existent, what is not or has not been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूता
अभूत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Non-existent, what is not or has not been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूताहरण
अभूत-आहरण <i>n.</i> a covert or metaphorical expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूततद्भाव|अभूततद्भावः
अभूत-तद्भाव <i>m.</i> the becoming changed of a substance to what it has not been before. (The notion implied by this term is expressed by the affixes called च्वि; the familiar instance is पयोधरीभूतचतुःसमुद्रम् R.ii.3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतपूर्व
अभूत-पूर्व <i>a.</i> unprecedented, अयमभूतपूर्वः पुरः Ve.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतप्रादुर्भाव|अभूतप्रादुर्भावः
अभूत-प्रादुर्भाव <i>m.</i> the becoming manifest of that which has not been before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतशत्रु
अभूत-शत्रु <i>a.</i> having no enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=052-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूति|अभूतिः
अभूति <i>f.</i> Non-existence, non-entity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमि|अभूमिः
अभूमि <i>f.</i> 1. Any thing but earth; 2. no object for, स खलु मनोरथानामभूमिर्विसर्जनावसरसत्कारः Sak.vii., “the honour at the occasion of dismissing me was indeed no object for (i.e. beyond) my wishes.” or अभूदभूमिः प्रतिपक्षजन्मनां भियाम् Sis.i.42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत्रिम
अभृत्रिम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> Not supported, not hired, not paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत्रिमा
अभृत्रिम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> Not supported, not hired, not paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद|अभेदः
अभेद <i>m.</i> 1. Undividedness, close union, आशास्महे विग्रहयोरभेदम् Bhartr.i.24; 2. sameness, identity, तद्रूपकमभेदो य उपमानोपमेययोः K.Pr.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्य|अभेद्यं
अभेद्य <i>n.</i> A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्य
अभोज्य <i>a. (f. ज्या)</i> 1. Unfit for food, prohibited as food; 2. one whose food must not be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्या
अभोज्य <i>a. (f. ज्या)</i> 1. Unfit for food, prohibited as food; 2. one whose food must not be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यग्र|अभ्यग्रं
अभ्यग्र <i>(I) a. (f. ग्रा)</i> 1. Near, proximate; 2. new, fresh, e.g. इदं शोणितमभ्यग्रे संप्रहारेऽच्युतत्तयोः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यग्रा
अभ्यग्र <i>(I) a. (f. ग्रा)</i> 1. Near, proximate; 2. new, fresh, e.g. इदं शोणितमभ्यग्रे संप्रहारेऽच्युतत्तयोः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यग्र|अभ्यग्रं
अभ्यग्र <i>(II) n.</i> Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंग|अभ्यङ्ग|अभ्यंगः|अभ्यङ्गः
अभ्यंग <i>m.</i> 1. Anointing in general; 2. rubbing the body with unctuous substances, e.g. अभ्यंगनेपथ्यमलंचकार; 3. an unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंजन|अभ्यञ्जन|अभ्यंजनं|अभ्यञ्जनं
अभ्यंजन <i>n.</i> 1. Anointing in general; 2. smearing the body with unctuous substances; 3. applying collyrium to the eyelashes; 4. an unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिक
अभ्यधिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> 1. Preeminent, extraordinary, e.g. यौवनेऽभ्यधिकाः स्त्रीणां विकारा वक्त्रगात्रजाः; 2. more than, exceeding (either in quantity or quality), e.g. धान्यं दशभ्यः कुम्भेभ्यो हरतोऽभ्यधिकं वधः (in quantity), न त्वत्समोऽस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोऽन्यः (in quality).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिका
अभ्यधिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> 1. Preeminent, extraordinary, e.g. यौवनेऽभ्यधिकाः स्त्रीणां विकारा वक्त्रगात्रजाः; 2. more than, exceeding (either in quantity or quality), e.g. धान्यं दशभ्यः कुम्भेभ्यो हरतोऽभ्यधिकं वधः (in quantity), न त्वत्समोऽस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोऽन्यः (in quality).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा <i>f.</i> 1. Permission, consent, कृताभ्यनुज्ञा गुरुणा गरीयसा K.S.v.7, पपौ वसिष्ठेन कृताभ्यनुज्ञः R.ii.69; 2. command; 3. admission of an argument (in phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञान|अभ्यनुज्ञानं
अभ्यनुज्ञान <i>n.</i> The same as अभ्यनुज्ञा q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तर|अभ्यंतर|अभ्यन्तरं
अभ्यन्तर <i>(I) a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Interior, being in the middle, e.g. न बाह्याभ्यन्तरयोरुपरंज्योपरञ्जकभावोऽपि देशव्यवधानात्; 2. conversant with, familiar with, (with the loc.), e.g. कार्येष्वभ्यन्तरो यः स्यात्; 3. intimate, nearly related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरा
अभ्यन्तर <i>(I) a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Interior, being in the middle, e.g. न बाह्याभ्यन्तरयोरुपरंज्योपरञ्जकभावोऽपि देशव्यवधानात्; 2. conversant with, familiar with, (with the loc.), e.g. कार्येष्वभ्यन्तरो यः स्यात्; 3. intimate, nearly related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तर|अभ्यंतर|अभ्यन्तरं
अभ्यन्तर <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Interior, middle, the space within, शमीमिवाभ्यन्तरलीनपावकाम् R.iii.9; 2. the mind. (अभ्यन्तरीकृ is often used in the sense of- (1) ‘to initiate in,’ सजीवनिर्जीवासु च द्यूतकलास्वभ्यन्तरीकरणम् D.K. or प्रागल्भ्याद्वक्तुमिच्छन्ति मन्त्रेष्वभ्यन्तरीकृताः Ram. or (2) ‘to make a near friend of a person’ e.g. त्यक्ताश्चाभ्यन्तरा येन बाह्या अभ्यन्तरीकृताः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरकला
अभ्यन्तर-कला <i>f.</i> the art of wantonness, अभ्यन्तरकलासु वैश्वासिकजनात्प्रयत्नेन प्रयोगग्रहणम् D.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित|अभ्यमितः
अभ्यमित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Sick, diseased, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमिता
अभ्यमित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Sick, diseased, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीण|अभ्यमित्रीणः
अभ्यमित्रीण <i>m.</i> A soldier who attacks the enemy valiantly, अद्योगमभ्यमन्त्रीणो यथेष्टं त्यं च संतनु Bt.v.47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीय|अभ्यमित्रीयः
अभ्यमित्रीय <i>m.</i> The same as अभ्यमित्रीण q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्र्य|अभ्यमित्र्यः
अभ्यमित्र्य <i>m.</i> The same as अभ्यमित्रीण q.v., मरीचोऽनुनयंस्त्रासादभ्यमित्र्यो भवामि ते Bt.v.46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यय|अभ्ययः
अभ्यय <i>m.</i> 1. Arrival; 2. setting (of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्चन|अभ्यर्चनं|अभ्यर्च्चन
अभ्यर्चन <i>n.</i> Worship, reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्चा|अभ्यर्च्चा
अभ्यर्चा <i>f.</i> The same as अभ्यर्चन q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ण|अभ्यर्णं|अभ्यर्ण्ण
अभ्यर्ण <i>(I) a. (f. र्णा)</i> Near, proximate, अभ्यर्णमागस्कृतमसृशाद्भिः R.ii.32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्णा
अभ्यर्ण <i>(I) a. (f. र्णा)</i> Near, proximate, अभ्यर्णमागस्कृतमसृशाद्भिः R.ii.32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ण|अभ्यर्णं|अभ्यर्ण्ण
अभ्यर्ण <i>(II) n.</i> Proximity, अभ्यर्णे परिरभ्य निर्भरसरः प्रेमान्धया राधया Git.G.i., अन्धकारिणि वनाभ्यर्णे किमुद्भ्राम्यति vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थना
अभ्यर्थना <i>f.</i> Request, solicitation, अभ्यर्थनाभंगभयेन साधुः K.S.i.52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थिन्
अभ्यर्थिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Soliciting, requesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थिनी
अभ्यर्थिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Soliciting, requesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हणा
अभ्यर्हणा <i>f.</i> 1. Respect, honour; 2. worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हित
अभ्यर्हित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Respected, honoured; 2. fit, proper, suitable, e.g. अभ्यर्हिता बन्धुषु तुल्यरूपा वृत्तिर्विशेषणे तपोधनानाम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हिता
अभ्यर्हित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Respected, honoured; 2. fit, proper, suitable, e.g. अभ्यर्हिता बन्धुषु तुल्यरूपा वृत्तिर्विशेषणे तपोधनानाम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकर्षण|अभ्यवकर्षणं
अभ्यवकर्षण <i>n.</i> Extraction, drawing out (as a thorn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकाश|अभ्यवकाशः
अभ्यवकाश <i>n.</i> An open space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्द|अभ्यवस्कंदः|अभ्यवस्कन्दः
अभ्यवस्कन्द <i>m.</i> 1. An impetuous assault; 2. marching against an enemy; 3. disabling an enemy by blows &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्दन|अभ्यवस्कंदनं|अभ्यवस्कन्दनं
अभ्यवस्कन्दन <i>n.</i> The same as अभ्यवस्कन्द q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहरण|अभ्यवहरणं
अभ्यवहरण <i>n.</i> Taking food, eating or drinking. (Mit. thus gives the literal meaning- अभ्यवहरणं च कण्ठादधोनयनम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार|अभ्यवहारः
अभ्यवहार <i>m.</i> 1. Taking food, eating, drinking, e.g. अल्पान्नाभ्यवहारेण … … इन्द्रियाणि निवर्तयेत्; 2. food, जम्भशब्दोऽभ्यवहारार्थवाची Kāśikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार्य|अभ्यवहार्य्य
अभ्यवहार्य <i>n.</i> Food, सर्वत्रौदरिकस्याभ्यवहार्यमेव विषयः Vikr.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसन|अभ्यसनं
अभ्यसन <i>n.</i> 1. Practice, exercise; 2. study, विद्यामभ्यसनेनेव प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R.i.88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयक
अभ्यसूयक <i>a. (f. यिका)</i> detractor, calumniator, envious, spiteful, e.g. मामात्मपरदेहेषु प्रद्विषन्तोऽभ्यसूयकाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयिका
अभ्यसूयक <i>a. (f. यिका)</i> detractor, calumniator, envious, spiteful, e.g. मामात्मपरदेहेषु प्रद्विषन्तोऽभ्यसूयकाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूया
अभ्यसूया <i>f.</i> Calumny, envy, spite, शक्राभ्यसूयाविनिवृत्तये यः R.v.74, or नूनं तेषामभ्यसूयापरोऽभूत् R.ix.64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्त|अभ्यस्तं
अभ्यस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Repeated, frequently practised, नयनयोरभ्यस्तगामीलनम् Am.S.92; 2. studied, नाभ्यस्ता भुवि वादिवृन्ददमनी विद्या Bhartr.iii.89; 3. multiplied (in math.); 4. reduplicated (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्ता
अभ्यस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Repeated, frequently practised, नयनयोरभ्यस्तगामीलनम् Am.S.92; 2. studied, नाभ्यस्ता भुवि वादिवृन्ददमनी विद्या Bhartr.iii.89; 3. multiplied (in math.); 4. reduplicated (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=053-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकर्ष|अभ्याकर्षः
अभ्याकर्ष <i>m.</i> striking the flat of the hand upon the breast in defiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकांक्षित|अभ्याकाङ्क्षित|अभ्याकांक्षितं|अभ्याकाङ्क्षितं
अभ्याकांक्षित <i>n.</i> 1. A false accusation, a groundless complaint; 2. a desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यान|अभ्याख्यानं
अभ्याख्यान <i>n.</i> A false accusation, a groundless complaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागत|अभ्यागतः
अभ्यागत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Come, arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागता
अभ्यागत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Come, arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागत|अभ्यागतः
अभ्यागत <i>(II) m.</i> A guest, a visitor, e.g. सर्वत्राभ्यागतो गुरुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम|अभ्यागमः
अभ्यागम <i>m.</i> 1. Arrival, visit, उत्सिक्तस्य तपःपराक्रमनिधेरभ्यागमोदकतः Mv.ii. or तपोधनाभ्यागमसंभवा मुदः Sis.i.23; 2. neighbourhood; 3. battle; 4. enmity, hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमन|अभ्यागमनं
अभ्यागमन <i>n.</i> Arrival, visit, हेतुं तदभ्यागमने परीप्सुः Kir.iii.4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागारिक|अभ्यागारिकः
अभ्यागारिक <i>m.</i> One who takes care of his family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघात|अभ्याघातः
अभ्याघात <i>m.</i> Assault, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यादान|अभ्यादानं
अभ्यादान <i>n.</i> Beginning, commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याधान|अभ्याधानं
अभ्याधान <i>n.</i> placing upon or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यान्त|अभ्यांत
अभ्यान्त <i>a. (f. न्ता)</i> Diseased, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यान्ता
अभ्यान्त <i>a. (f. न्ता)</i> Diseased, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यामर्द|अभ्यामर्दः|अभ्यामर्द्द
अभ्यामर्द <i>m.</i> War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोह|अभ्यारोहः
अभ्यारोह <i>m.</i> 1. Ascending, mounting; 2. transition from one place to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहण|अभ्यारोहणं
अभ्यारोहण <i>n.</i> The same as अभ्यारोह q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावर्त|अभ्यावर्तः|अभ्यावर्त्त
अभ्यावर्त <i>m.</i> Repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्ति|अभ्यावृत्तिः
अभ्यावृत्ति <i>f.</i> Repetition. (See अनभ्यावृत्ति and the verse quoted there.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश <i>(I) a. (f. शा)</i> Near, proximate, तया व्याहृतसंदेशा सा बभौ निभृता प्रिये । चूतयष्टिरिवाभ्याशे मधौ K.S.vi.2. (Mall., however, does not take अभ्याश as an adjective here; we propose to translate अभ्याशे मधौ by “when the spring is approaching.”)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याशा
अभ्याश <i>(I) a. (f. शा)</i> Near, proximate, तया व्याहृतसंदेशा सा बभौ निभृता प्रिये । चूतयष्टिरिवाभ्याशे मधौ K.S.vi.2. (Mall., however, does not take अभ्याश as an adjective here; we propose to translate अभ्याशे मधौ by “when the spring is approaching.”)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश <i>(II) n.</i> Neighbourhood, vicinity, सहसाभ्यागतां भैमीमभ्याशपरिवर्तिनीम् Bh. (This word retains its ablative ending when compounded with a past pass. participle in क्त, e.g. अभ्याशादागतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याशम्
अभ्याशम् <i>ind.</i> Near, (with the abl. or gen., e.g. अभ्याशं ग्रामात् or ग्रामस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यास|अभ्यासः
अभ्यास <i>m.</i> 1. Repetition, repeated occurrence, व्याख्याता व्याख्याता इति पदाभ्यासोऽध्यायपरिसमाप्तिं द्योतयति S.Bh.i.; 2. repeated practice, habit, अमंगलाभ्यासरतिं विचिन्त्य तम् K.S.v.65; 3. study, वेदाभ्यासो हि पञ्चधा Daksha.; 4. the effort of the mind to remain in its unmodified condition of purity (in Yoga phil.), असंशयं माहाबाहो मनो दुर्निग्रहं चलम् । अभ्यासेन तु कौन्तेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते Bg.vi.35; 5. reduplication (in gram.); 6. the first syllable of the reduplicated base (in Pāṇini); 7. multiplication (in arith.); 8. neighbourhood, vicinity (also written अभ्याश in this sense), मार्गाभ्यासवर्तिनः कस्यापि क्षपणकविहारस्य D.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासयोग|अभ्यासयोगः
अभ्यास-योग <i>m.</i> deep meditation preceded by the effort to keep the mind in its unmodified condition, e.g. अभ्यासयोगेन ततो मामिच्छाप्तुं धनंजय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासलोप|अभ्यासलोपः
अभ्यास-लोप <i>m.</i> dropping of the reduplication-syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासादन|अभ्यासादनं
अभ्यासादन <i>n.</i> The same as अभ्यवस्कंद q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहनन|अभ्याहननं
अभ्याहनन <i>n.</i> 1. Hurting, killing; 2. impeding, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहार|अभ्याहारः
अभ्याहार <i>m.</i> 1. Robbery; 2. conveying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्षण|अभ्युक्षणं
अभ्युक्षण <i>n.</i> 1. Consecration by sprinkling; 2. sprinkling, wetting परस्पराभ्युक्षणतत्पराणाम् R.xvi.57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युचित
अभ्युचित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Usual, customary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युचिता
अभ्युचित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Usual, customary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युच्चय|अभ्युच्चयः
अभ्युच्चय <i>m.</i> 1. Increase, augmentation; 2. prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्क्रोशन|अभ्युत्क्रोशनं
अभ्युत्क्रोशन <i>n.</i> Loud acclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थान|अभ्युत्थानं
अभ्युत्थान <i>n.</i> 1. Rising from one’s seat to receive a guest; 2. rising (physically and morally), e.g. अभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदात्मानं सृजाम्यहम्; 3. elevation, high position, नवाभ्युत्थानदर्शिन्यो ननन्दुः सप्रजाः प्रजाः R.iv.3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पतन|अभ्युत्पतनं
अभ्युत्पतन <i>n.</i> Springing against anyone, assault, अलक्षिताभ्युत्पतनो नृपेण R.ii.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदय|अभ्युदयः
अभ्युदय <i>m.</i> 1. Rise (as of the sun or moon); 2. elevation, prosperity, भवो हि लोकाभ्युदयाय तादृशाम् R.iii.14; 3. beginning, commencing; 4. a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदाहरण|अभ्युदाहरणं
अभ्युदाहरण <i>n.</i> An illustration of a thing by its reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदित|अभ्युदितः
अभ्युदित <i>m.</i> One asleep at sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गम|अभ्युद्गमः
अभ्युद्गम <i>m.</i> 1. Rising from one’s seat to receive a guest; 2. rising, originating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यत
अभ्युद्यत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Approaching, reaching, कुलमभ्युद्यतनूतनेश्वरम् R.viii.15; 2. given without solicitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यता
अभ्युद्यत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Approaching, reaching, कुलमभ्युद्यतनूतनेश्वरम् R.viii.15; 2. given without solicitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युन्नति|अभ्युन्नतिः
अभ्युन्नति <i>f.</i> Great prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगम|अभ्युपगमः
अभ्युपगम <i>m.</i> 1. Approach, arrival; 2. a promise, an agreement, M.ix.53; 3. accepting or acknowleding to be true (as in अभ्युपगमवाद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमसिद्धान्त|अभ्युपगमसिद्धान्तः
अभ्युपगम-सिद्धान्त <i>m.</i> an admitted axiom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपत्ति|अभ्युपपत्तिः
अभ्युपपत्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Defence, protection, e.g. ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तौ च शपथे नास्ति पातकम्; 2. consolation; 3. agreement, assent; 4. impregnation of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=054-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपाय|अभ्युपायः
अभ्युपाय <i>m.</i> 1. An agreement; 2. a means, an expedient, तस्मिन् सुराणां विजयाभ्युपाये K.S.iii.19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपायन|अभ्युपायनं
अभ्युपायन <i>n.</i> A bribe, an inducement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत|अभ्युपेतं
अभ्युपेत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Come near; 2. accepted, Megh.i.38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेता
अभ्युपेत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Come near; 2. accepted, Megh.i.38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युष|अभ्युषः
अभ्यु(यू)ष <i>m.</i> A kind of bread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूष|अभ्यूषः
अभ्यु(यू)ष <i>m.</i> A kind of bread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूह|अभ्यूहः
अभ्यूह <i>m.</i> 1. Discussion, reasoning; 2. supplying an ellipsis; 3. guess, conjecture, पराभ्यूहस्थानान्यपि तनुतराणि स्थगयति M.M.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र्
अभ्र् <i>vt. 1P (pp. अभ्रित)</i> To go, to wander about, e.g. तेष्वसौ दन्दशूकारिवर्तनेष्वानभ्र निर्भयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र|अभ्रं
अभ्र <i>n.</i> 1. A cloud; 2. sky, atmosphere, परितो विपाण्डु दधदभ्रशिरः Sis.ix.3; 3. talc; 4. a cypher (in math.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाश|अभ्रावकाशः
अभ्र-अवकाश <i>m.</i> clouds as the only shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रोत्थ|अभ्रोत्थं|अभ्रोत्थः
अभ्र-उत्थ <i>m.</i> Indra’s thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंकष|अभ्रङ्कष|अभ्रंकषः|अभ्रङ्कषः
अभ्रंकष <i>(I) a.</i> touching the clouds, very high, e.g. आदायाभ्रंकषं प्रायान्मलयं फलशालिनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंकष|अभ्रङ्कष|अभ्रंकषः|अभ्रङ्कषः
अभ्रंकष <i>(II) m.</i> 1. wind; 2. a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रनाग|अभ्रनागः
अभ्र-नाग <i>m.</i> one of the elephants supporting the globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपिशाच|अभ्रपिशाचः
अभ्र-पिशाच <i>m.</i> a name of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपुष्प|अभ्रपुष्पं|अभ्रपुष्पः
अभ्र-पुष्प <i>n.</i> 1. water; 2. reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमातंग|अभ्रमातङ्ग|अभ्रमातङ्गः
अभ्र-मातंग <i>m.</i> Airāvata, Indra’s elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमाला
अभ्र-माला <i>f.</i> a series of clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिह|अभ्रंलिहः
अभ्रंलिह <i>(I) a.</i> touching the clouds, i.e. very high, अभ्रंलिहाग्राः Megh.ii.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिह|अभ्रंलिहः
अभ्रंलिह <i>(II) m.</i> wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=055-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रक|अभ्रकं
