अमूर्ति <i>(II) m.</i> A name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल
अमूल <i>a. (f. ला)</i> 1. Baseless, without support; 2. not found in the original, without authority, नामूलं लिख्यते किंचिन्नानपेक्षितमुच्यते Mall.; 3. without material cause or origin (as प्रधान according to the Sāṅkhyas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूला
अमूल <i>a. (f. ला)</i> 1. Baseless, without support; 2. not found in the original, without authority, नामूलं लिख्यते किंचिन्नानपेक्षितमुच्यते Mall.; 3. without material cause or origin (as प्रधान according to the Sāṅkhyas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल्य
अमूल्य <i>a. (f. ल्या)</i> Invaluable, price-less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल्या
अमूल्य <i>a. (f. ल्या)</i> Invaluable, price-less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृणाल|अमृणालं
अमृणाल <i>n.</i> The root of a fragrant grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Not dead; 2. imperishable, immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृता
अमृत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Not dead; 2. imperishable, immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A god; 2. Dhanvantari, the physician of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत <i>(III) n.</i> 1. Ambrosia supposed to be churned out of the Kshīrasamudra and to confer immortality on the person who tastes it, देवासुरैरमृतमम्बुनिधिर्मन्थे Kir.v.30, विषमप्यमृतं क्वचिद्गवेदमृतं वा विषमीश्वरेच्छया R.viii.46, iii.16; 2. water, e.g. अमृतोपस्तरणमसि स्वाहा (the formula repeated by a Brāhmaṇa at the time of sipping water before commencing to take food), or अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा (the formula repeated at the time of sipping water at the end of dinner); 3. clarified butter, अमृतं नाम यत्सन्तो मन्त्रजिह्वेषु जुह्वति Sis.ii.107; 4. the Soma juice; 5. quick-silver; 6. the leavings of a sacrifice (यज्ञशेषोऽमृतं स्मृतम्); 7. alms obtained without solicitation (मृतं स्याद्याचितं भैक्श्यममृतं स्यादयाचितम्), See M.iv.4, 5; 8. milk; 9. food; 10. a sweetmeat; 11. gold; 12. poison; 13. splendour; 14. final emancipation, सश्रिये चामृताय च Am.i.1; 15. the supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=057-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

