अरण्य-चटक <i>m.</i> a wild pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यचन्द्रिका
अरण्य-चन्द्रिका <i>f.</i> moonlight in a forest (lit.), any decoration which does not serve its purpose (fig.). Moonlight in a forest is not appreciated or enjoyed by people and is thus purposeless. Similarly decoration when not appreciated or enjoyed by those for whom it is intended is useless. Thus on ‘स्त्रीणां प्रियालोकफलो हि वेषः’ K.S.vii.22, Mall. observes अन्यथा अरन्यचन्द्रिका स्यात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यचर
अरण्यचर <i>a.</i> living in a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्येचर
अरण्यचर <i>a.</i> living in a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यधर्म|अरण्यधर्मः|अरण्यधर्म्म
अरण्य-धर्म <i>m.</i> 1. wild or savage state, e.g. तथारण्यधर्माद्वियोज्य ग्रामधर्मेषु नियोजितः; 2. the duties of a Vānaprastha q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यपंडित
अरण्य-पंडित <i>m.</i> a paṇḍit in a forest (lit.), a fool (fig.) (one who can show off his learning only in a forest where there are no people).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यमक्षिका
अरण्य-मक्षिका <i>f.</i> the gad-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यरक्षक|अरण्यरक्षकः
अरण्य-रक्षक <i>m.</i> a forest-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यराज्
अरण्य-राज्, -राज <i>m.</i> king of the forest, i.e. the lion or tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यराज
अरण्य-राज्, -राज <i>m.</i> king of the forest, i.e. the lion or tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यरुदित
अरण्य-रुदित <i>n.</i> weeping in a forest (lit.), doing anything to no purpose. (fig.). (Cries in a forest are useless because they are not heeded by anybody. Hence ‘अरण्ये खलु मया रुदितमासीत्’ says the Vidūṣaka to the king, in the Sak.) तदलमधुनारण्यरुदितैः Am.S.76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवायस|अरण्यवायसः
अरण्य-वायस <i>m.</i> a raven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवास|अरण्यवासः
अरण्य-वास <i>m.</i> dwelling in a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवासिन्
अरण्य-वासिन् <i>m.</i> an anchorite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यविलपित
अरण्यविलपित <i>n.</i> the same as अरण्यरुदित q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यश्वन्
अरण्य-श्वन् <i>m.</i> a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=061-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यक|अरण्यकं
अरण्यक <i>n.</i> A forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानी
अरण्यानी(नि) <i>f.</i> A large forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानि|अरण्यानिः
अरण्यानी(नि) <i>f.</i> A large forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत
अरत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Dull, apathetic; 2. not pleased with, averse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरता
अरत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Dull, apathetic; 2. not pleased with, averse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत
अरत <i>(II) n.</i> Non-copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतत्रप|अरतत्रपः
अरत-त्रप <i>m.</i> a dog (lit. without shame during copulation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
अरति <i>f.</i> 1. Dissatisfaction, discontentment; 2. absence of pleasure, want of amusement considered to be brought on by the longings of love. (It is thus defined- स्वाभीष्टवस्त्वलाभेन चेतसो याऽनवस्थितिः । अरतिः सा); 3. discomfort; 4. anxiety, agitation; 5. want of rest, uneasiness; 6. a biliary disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्नि|अरत्निः
अरत्नि <i>(I) m.</i> 1. The elbow; 2. a fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्नि|अरत्निः
अरत्नि <i>(II) m.f.</i> A cubit of the middle length extending from the elbow to the tip of the little finger. (Halāyudha says- मध्यांगुलीकुर्परयोर्मध्ये प्रामाणिकः करः । बद्धमुष्टिकरो रत्निररत्निः सकनिष्ठिकः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निक|अरत्निकः
अरत्निक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Having the length of an aratni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निका
अरत्निक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Having the length of an aratni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम्
अरम् <i>ind.</i> Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमणीय
अरमणीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Unpleasant, disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमणीया
अरमणीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Unpleasant, disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर|अररं|अररः
अरर <i>(I) n.</i> A covering, a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर|अररं|अररः
अरर <i>(II) m.n.</i> The leaf or panel of a door, चञ्चूकोटिविपाटिताररपुटो यास्यास्यहं पञ्जरात् Bh.V.i.58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर|अररं|अररः
अरर <i>(III) m.</i> An awl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररि|अररिः
अररि <i>m.n.</i> The same as अरर q.v. (Also अररी f.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररे
अररे <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle implying- (1) scorn, disdain, अररे महाराजं प्रति कुतः क्षत्रियाः G.M.; (2) emotion, haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्द|अरविंदं|अरविन्दं|अरविन्दः
अरविन्द <i>(I) n.</i> The lotus which opens its flower at sunrise, सूर्यांशुभिर्भिन्नामिवारविन्दम् K.S.i.32, 33, or अरविन्दसुरभिः कणवाही मालिनीतरंगाणाम् (पवनः) Sak.ii., R.i.43, xiii.23, xiv.50. (This flower is considered as being one of the five arrows of the god of love, which are thus enumerated- अरविन्दमशोकं च चूतं च नवमल्लिका । नीलोत्पलं च पंचैते पञ्चबाणस्य सायकाः. The word अरविन्द applies to the blue and the red variety.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्द|अरविंदं|अरविन्दं|अरविन्दः
अरविन्द <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The Indian crane; 2. copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दनाभ|अरविन्दनाभः
अरविन्द-नाभ <i>m.</i> a name of Viṣṇu, हृदये मदीये देवश्चकास्तु भगवानरविन्दनाभः Bh.V.iv.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दसद्
अरविन्द-सद् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दिनी|अरविंदिनी
अरविन्दिनी <i>f.</i> 1. An assemblage of lotus-flowers; 2. a place containing lotus flowers, e.g. प्रपीतमधुका भृंगैः सुदिवेवारविन्दिनी Bt.v.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसिक|अरसिकः
अरसिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> 1. Devoid of taste, unappreciative, insensible to the beauties and charms of, अरसिकेषु कवित्वनिवेदनं शिरसि मा लिख मलिख Ud.; 2. flavourless, tasteless, insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसिका
अरसिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> 1. Devoid of taste, unappreciative, insensible to the beauties and charms of, अरसिकेषु कवित्वनिवेदनं शिरसि मा लिख मलिख Ud.; 2. flavourless, tasteless, insipid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराग
अराग <i>a. (f. गा)</i> Cool, unimpassioned, तमहमरागमकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं वन्दे Ve.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरागा
अराग <i>a. (f. गा)</i> Cool, unimpassioned, तमहमरागमकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं वन्दे Ve.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरागिन्
अरागिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Cool, unimpassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरागिणी
अरागिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Cool, unimpassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजक|अराजकः
अराजक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Without a king, anarchical, अराजके जीवलोके दुर्बला बलवत्तरैः । पीद्यन्ते न हि वित्तेषु प्रभुत्वं कस्याचित्तद Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजका
अराजक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Without a king, anarchical, अराजके जीवलोके दुर्बला बलवत्तरैः । पीद्यन्ते न हि वित्तेषु प्रभुत्वं कस्याचित्तद Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजन्
अराजन् <i>m.</i> A no-king, one not a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजभोगीन
अराजन्-भोगीन <i>a.</i> not fit for the enjoyment of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजस्थापित
अराजन्-स्थापित <i>a.</i> not established or licensed by the king, illicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराति|अरातिः
अराति <i>m.</i> 1. An enemy, देशः सोऽयमरातिशोणितजलैर्यस्मिन् ह्रदाः पूरिताः Ve.iii., Kir.xi.18; 2. the number ‘6.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिभंग|अरातिभङ्ग|अरातिभङ्गः
अराति-भंग <i>m.</i> defeat or destruction of a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल <i>(I) a. (f. ला)</i> Crooked, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराला
अराल <i>(I) a. (f. ला)</i> Crooked, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A crooked arm; 2. an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरालकेशी
अराल-केशी <i>f.</i> a woman having curled hair, स गात्रयष्टिं भित्त्वा निराक्रामदरालकेश्याः R.vi.81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरालपक्ष्मन्
अराल-पक्ष्मन् <i>a.</i> whose eyelashes are curved, करोति लक्ष्यं चिरमस्य चक्षुषो न वक्त्रमात्मीयमरालपक्ष्मणः K.S.v.49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराला
अराला <i>f.</i> A courtezan, a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि <i>m.</i> 1. An enemy, नारीणामनुकूलमाचरसि चेज्जानासि K.Pr.x., विजितारिपुरः पुरः R.i.59, 61, iv.4; 2. the wheel of a carriage; 3. an enemy of humanity (applied to six feelings which disturb the balance of the mind. They are- (1) काम; (2) क्रोध; (3) लोभ; (4) मोह; (5) मद, and (6) मत्सर), कृतारिषड्वर्गजयेन मानवीमगम्यरूपां पदवीं प्रपित्सुना Kir.i.9; 4. the number ‘six.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिकुल
अरि-कुल <i>n.</i> 1. an enemy; 2. a host of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिघ्न|अरिघ्नः
अरि-घ्न <i>m.</i> a destroyer of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिंदम|अरिन्दम|अरिन्दमः
अरिंदम <i>m.</i> a subjugator of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिराष्ट्र
अरि-राष्ट्र <i>n.</i> an enemy’s country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषड्वर्ग
अरि-षड्वर्ग <i>m.</i> the six enemies of humanity. (See above 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिसूदन|अरिसूदनः
अरि-सूदन <i>a.</i> destroyer of foes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=062-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थभाज्
अरिक्थभाज् <i>a.</i> Not entitled to any share of ancestral property (as an heir incapacitated to inherit on account of apostacy or impotence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थीय
अरिक्थीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Not relating to रिक्थ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थीया
अरिक्थीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Not relating to रिक्थ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
अरित्र <i>n.</i> A rudder, लोलैररित्रैश्चरणैरिवाभितः Sis.xii.71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष|अरिषं|अरिषः
अरिष <i>m.</i> A stream of water from clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अरिष्ट <i>(I) m.</i> 1. A crow; 2. a heron; 3. the nimba tree; 4. garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अरिष्ट <i>(II) n.</i> 1. A woman’s lying-in chamber, R.iii.15; 2. bad luck, evil, e.g. नारिष्टशंका कर्तव्या; 3. a portent foreboding evil; 4. a symptom of approaching death (रोगिणो मरणं यस्मादवश्यंभावि लक्ष्यते । तल्लक्षणमरिष्टं स्याद्रिष्टमप्यभिधीयते.); 5. buttermilk; 6. good luck, happiness; 7. a kind of liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टगृह
अरिष्ट-गृह <i>n.</i> a lying-in chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टताति|अरिष्टतातिः
अरिष्ट-ताति <i>(I) a.</i> auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टताति|अरिष्टतातिः
अरिष्ट-ताति <i>(II) m.</i> continuous good fortune, train of happiness, तदत्रभवता निष्पन्नाशिषां काममरिष्टतातिमाशास्मेह Mv.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टमथन|अरिष्टमथनः
अरिष्ट-मथन <i>m.</i> a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टशय्या
अरिष्ट-शय्या <i>f.</i> a lying-in couch, अरिष्टशय्यां परितो विसारिणा R.iii.15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टसूदन|अरिष्टसूदनः
अरिष्ट-सूदन <i>m.</i> a name of Viṣṇu (as being the name of a demon whom Viṣṇu killed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचि|अरुचिः
अरुचि <i>f.</i> 1. Aversion, dislike; 2. want of appetite, काशाहिक्काऽरुचिप्रणुत Suśruta; 3. an unsatisfactory explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिर
अरुचिर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिरा
अरुचिर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> Disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज्
अरुज् <i>a.</i> Free from disease, healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण <i>(I) a. (f. णा or णी)</i> 1. Reddish-brown; 2. ruddy; 3. dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणा
अरुण <i>(I) a. (f. णा or णी)</i> 1. Reddish-brown; 2. ruddy; 3. dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणी
अरुण <i>(I) a. (f. णा or णी)</i> 1. Reddish-brown; 2. ruddy; 3. dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The sun, संसृज्यते सरसिजैररुणांशुभिन्नैः R.v.69; 2. the name of the charioteer of the sun, यावत्प्रतापनिधिराक्रमते न म्हानुरह्नाय तावदरुणेन तमो निरस्तम् R.v.71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण <i>(III) n.</i> 1. Red colour; 2. saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणाग्रज|अरुणाग्रजः
अरुण-अग्रज <i>m.</i> a name of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणार्चिस्
अरुण-अर्चिस् <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणावरज|अरुणावरजः
अरुण-अवरज <i>m.</i> a name of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणात्मज|अरुणात्मजः
अरुण-आत्मज <i>m.</i> a name (1) of Jaṭāyu; (2) of Karṇa; (3) of Sugrīva; (4) of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणात्मजा
अरुण-आत्मजा <i>f.</i> 1. the Narmadā; 2. the Tapatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणोदय|अरुणोदयः
अरुण-उदय <i>m.</i> break of day, dawn. (चतस्रो घटिकाः प्रातररुणोदय उच्यते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणोपल|अरुणोपलः
अरुण-उपल <i>m.</i> a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणकमल|अरुणकमलं
अरुण-कमल <i>n.</i> a red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणज्योतिस्
अरुण-ज्योतिस् <i>m.</i> a name of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणप्रिया
अरुण-प्रिया <i>f.</i> संज्ञा, the sun’s wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणलोचन|अरुणलोचनः
अरुण-लोचन <i>m.</i> a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणसारथि|अरुणसारथिः
अरुण-सारथि <i>m.</i> an epithet of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणित
अरुणित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Reddened, स्तनांगरागारुणिताच्च कन्दुकात् K.S.v.11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणिता
अरुणित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Reddened, स्तनांगरागारुणिताच्च कन्दुकात् K.S.v.11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणिमन्
अरुणिमन् <i>m.</i> Redness, अरुणिम्ना पिहितोऽपि शुक्लभावः Bh.V.ii.180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्तुद|अरुंतुद|अरुन्तुदः
अरुन्तुद <i>a. (f. दा)</i> 1. Sharp, inflicting wounds, अरुन्तुदमिवालानमनिर्वाणस्य दन्तिनः R.i.71; 2. acrimonious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्तुदा
अरुन्तुद <i>a. (f. दा)</i> 1. Sharp, inflicting wounds, अरुन्तुदमिवालानमनिर्वाणस्य दन्तिनः R.i.71; 2. acrimonious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धती|अरुंधती
अरुन्धती <i>f.</i> 1. The wife of Vasiṣṭha (See App. II.), अन्वासितमरुन्धत्या स्वाहयेव हविर्भुजम् R.i.56, K.S.vi.11, 32; 2. the morning star so personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीजानि|अरुन्धतीजानिः
अरुन्धती-जानि, -नाथ <i>m.</i> Vasiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीनाथ|अरुन्धतीनाथः
अरुन्धती-जानि, -नाथ <i>m.</i> Vasiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीदर्शनन्याय
अरुन्धती-दर्शनन्याय <i>m.</i> the maxim of the view of अरुन्धती (the star so called). The maxim is thus explained by Śankarāchārya- “यथारुन्धतीं दिदर्शयिषुस्तत्समीपस्थां स्थूलां ताराममुख्यां प्रथममरुन्धतीति ग्राहयित्वा तां प्रत्याख्याय पश्चादरुन्धतीमेव ग्राहयति.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्
अरुष् <i>a.</i> Not angry, good tempered, अरुषि नृपे स्तुतिवचनम् Panch.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुस्
अरुस् <i>m.n.</i> A sore or wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्कर|अरुष्करं|अरुष्करः
अरुष्कर <i>a.</i> causing a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूप|अरूपः
अरूप <i>(I) a. (f. पा)</i> 1. Formless; 2. ugly; 3. dissimilar, unlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपा
अरूप <i>(I) a. (f. पा)</i> 1. Formless; 2. ugly; 3. dissimilar, unlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूप|अरूपः
अरूप <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Bad figure; 2. Brahman (n.) (in the Vedānta phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपहार्य|अरूपहार्य्य
अरूप-हार्य <i>a.</i> not to be won over by beauty, अरूपहार्यं मदनस्य निग्रहात् K.S.v.53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरे
अरे <i>ind.</i> An interjection- (1) of calling (used in addressing a person inferior in position), e.g. न वा अरे पत्युः कामायास्याः पतिः प्रितो भवति (said by Yājnyavalkya to his wife); (2) of anger; (3) of envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेतस्
अरेतस् <i>a.</i> Seedless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेरे
अरेरे <i>ind.</i> An interjection- (1) of calling to inferiors, अरेरे राधागर्भभारभूत सूतापसद किमेवमाक्षिपति Ve.iii.; (2) of calling angrily, अरेरे वाचाट Ve.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोक|अरोकः
अरोक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Destitute of splendour, dim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोका
अरोक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Destitute of splendour, dim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोग|अरोगः
अरोग <i>a. (f. गा)</i> Free from disease, healthy, बन्धुशीललक्षणसम्पन्नामरोगामुपयच्छेत् Āpastamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगा
अरोग <i>a. (f. गा)</i> Free from disease, healthy, बन्धुशीललक्षणसम्पन्नामरोगामुपयच्छेत् Āpastamba.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिन्
अरोगिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> The same as अरोग q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिणी
अरोगिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> The same as अरोग q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचक|अरोचकः
अरोचक <i>a. (f. चिका)</i> 1. Not shining; 2. producing want of appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचिका
अरोचक <i>a. (f. चिका)</i> 1. Not shining; 2. producing want of appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क्
अर्क् <i>vt. 10U (pp. अर्कित)</i> 1. To heat; 2. to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क <i>m.</i> 1. The sun, आविष्कितारुणपुरःसर एकतोऽर्कः Sak.iv.; 2. a ray; 3. fire; 4. crystal; 5. copper; 6. the name of a plant, अर्कस्योपरि शिथिलं च्युतमिव नवमल्लिकाकुसुमम् Sak.ii., सोऽर्कवन्नृपतिस्त्याज्यः सदापुष्पफलोपि सन् Panch.i.; 7. the number ‘twelve’; 8. Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्काश्मन्
अर्क-अश्मन् <i>m.</i> the sunstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्केन्दुसंगम|अर्केन्दुसङ्गम|अर्केन्दुसंगमः
अर्क-इन्दुसंगम <i>m.</i> the conjunction of the sun and the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कोपल|अर्कोपलः
अर्क-उपल <i>m.</i> 1. a ruby; 2. the sun-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ककान्ता
अर्क-कान्ता, -प्रिया <i>f.</i> संज्ञा, the wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कप्रिया
अर्क-कान्ता, -प्रिया <i>f.</i> संज्ञा, the wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कचन्दन|अर्कचन्दनं|अर्कचन्दनः
अर्क-चन्दन <i>m.</i> a kind of sandal tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कनयन|अर्कनयनः
अर्क-नयन <i>m.</i> an epithet (1) of Karṇa, (2) of Yama, (3) of Śanaiścara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कजा
अर्क-जा, -तनया <i>f.</i> an epithet (1) of the Yamunā, (2) of the Tapatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कतनया
अर्क-जा, -तनया <i>f.</i> an epithet (1) of the Yamunā, (2) of the Tapatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कत्विष्
अर्क-त्विष् <i>f.</i> the light of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कनन्दन|अर्कनन्दनः
अर्क-नन्दन, -पुत्र, -सूनु <i>m.</i> the same as अर्कतनय q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपुत्र|अर्कपुत्रः
अर्क-नन्दन, -पुत्र, -सूनु <i>m.</i> the same as अर्कतनय q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कसूनु|अर्कसूनुः
अर्क-नन्दन, -पुत्र, -सूनु <i>m.</i> the same as अर्कतनय q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कमण्डल
अर्क-मण्डल <i>n.</i> the disc of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कविवाह|अर्कविवाहः
अर्क-विवाह <i>m.</i> marriage with the arka plant. (The Hindu religious law enjoins such a marriage before a man takes a third wife, चतुर्थादिविवाहार्थं तृतीयेऽर्कं समुद्वहेत् Kaśyapa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=063-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गल|अर्गलं|अर्गलः
अर्गल <i>m.n.</i> 1. A wooden bolt for fastening a door, ससंभ्रमेन्द्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव भियाऽमरावती K.Pr.i. or इदं गृहं भिन्नमनायतार्गलम् Mrich.ii.; 2. a bar; 3. a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गला
अर्गला <i>f.</i> The same as अर्गल q.v., पुरार्गलादीर्घभुजो बुभोज R.xviii.4. (This word is metaphorically used in the sense of ‘something intervening as an obstruction or bar,’ वार्यर्गलाभंग इव प्रवृत्तः Rv.45. Cf. also कण्ठे केवलमर्गलेव निहिता जीवस्य निर्गच्छतः K.Pr.viii.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलिका
अर्गलिका <i>f.</i> A small bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्
अर्घ् <i>vi. 1P (pp. अर्घित)</i> To be worth, to cost, परीक्षका यत्र न सन्ति देशे नार्घन्ति रत्नानि समुद्रजानि Panch.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ <i>m.</i> 1. Value, price, कुर्युरर्घं यथापण्यम् M.viii.898, अर्घतः पातिताः ‘caused to fall in price or depreciate in value’; 2. an offering of various ingredients to a god or a Brāhmaṇa (the ingredients of this offering are- आपः क्षीरं कुशाग्रं च दधि सर्पिः सतण्डुलम् । यव सिद्धार्थकश्चैव अष्टांगोऽर्घः प्रकीर्तितः) Megh.i.4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घार्ह
अर्घ-अर्ह <i>a.</i> worthy of respectful offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घबलाबल
अर्घ-बलाबल <i>n.</i> rate of price, proper price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घसंस्थापन
अर्घ-संस्थापन <i>n.</i> fixing the price of commodities, कुर्वीत चेषां प्रत्यक्षमर्घसंस्थापनं नृपः M.viii.402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घीश|अर्घीशः
अर्घीश <i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य <i>(I) a. (f. र्घ्या)</i> 1. Valuable; 2. venerable, तानर्घ्यानर्घ्यमादाय दूरात्प्रत्याययौ गिरिः K.S.vi.50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्या
अर्घ्य <i>(I) a. (f. र्घ्या)</i> 1. Valuable; 2. venerable, तानर्घ्यानर्घ्यमादाय दूरात्प्रत्याययौ गिरिः K.S.vi.50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य <i>(II) n.</i> A respectful offering to a god or a venerable person consisting of various ingredients, अर्घ्यमर्घ्य मिति वादिनं नृपम् R.xi.69, अनर्घ्यमर्घ्येण तमद्रिनाथः K.S.i.58, R.i.44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्
अर्च् <i>(I) vt. 1U (pp. अर्चित)</i> 1. To praise; 2. to worship, आर्चीद्द्विजातीन् परमार्थविन्दान् Bt.i.15, xiv.68, xvii.5, R.i.6, 90, ii.21, xii.89; 3. to salute.With अभि-, to worship, स्वकर्मणा तमभ्यर्च्य सिद्धिं विन्दति मानवः Bg.xviii.46, Bt.i.24.With प्र-, to worship, प्रानर्चुरर्च्या जगदर्चनीयम् Bt.ii.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्
अर्च् <i>(II) vt. 10U (pp. अर्चित)</i> To honour, to worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चक|अर्चकः|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक <i>a. (f. का)</i> A worshipper, गुरुदेवद्विजार्चकः M.xi.224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चका
अर्चक <i>a. (f. का)</i> A worshipper, गुरुदेवद्विजार्चकः M.xi.224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चन|अर्च्चनं
अर्चन <i>n.</i> Worship, the homage paid to deities and superiors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चना|अर्च्चना
अर्चना <i>f.</i> The same as अर्चन q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चा|अर्च्चा
अर्चा <i>f.</i> 1. Worship; 2. an image or idol destined to be worshipped, मौर्यौर्हिरण्यार्थिभिरर्चाः प्रकल्पिताः P.Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चि|अर्चिः|अर्च्चिः
अर्चि <i>f.</i> A flame, नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव च्छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा Vikr.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिस्|अर्च्चिस्
अर्चिस् <i>(I) n.</i> 1. A flame, प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे R.iii.14; 2. light, lustre, प्रशमादर्चिषाम् K.S.ii.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिस्|अर्च्चिस्
अर्चिस् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A ray of light; 2. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिष्मत्|अर्चिष्मन्त्
अर्चिष्मत् <i>m.</i> 1. fire; 2. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्य
अर्च्य <i>a. (f. र्च्या)</i> Fit to be worshipped, Bt.ii.20, vi.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्या
अर्च्य <i>a. (f. र्च्या)</i> Fit to be worshipped, Bt.ii.20, vi.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
अर्ज् <i>(I) vt. 1P (pp. अर्जित)</i> 1. To procure, to gain, to earn, पितृद्रव्यविरोधेन यदन्यय् स्वयमर्जितम् Yaj.ii.118, Na.v.84; 2. to take, to take up, Bt.xiv.74.With उप-, to procure, to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
अर्ज् <i>(II) vt. 10U (pp. अर्जित)</i> To obtain, to procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जक|अर्जकः|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक <i>a. (f. र्जिका)</i> Procuring, one who obtains, e.g. अर्जको द्व्यंशमाहरेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=064-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

