अर्थ्
अर्थ् <i>vt. 10Ā (pp. अर्थित)</i> 1. To request, to sue, to supplicate, to entreat, (with two accusatives, e.g. तमर्थये मोक्षम्) प्रहस्तमर्थयांचक्रे योद्धुम् Bt.xiv.88; 2. to strive to obtain, to wish.With अभि-, to beg, to request, to supplicate, इमं तावत्प्रियाप्रवृत्तये सारंगमासीनमभ्यर्थये Vikr.iv., or अवकाशं किलोदन्वान् रामायाभ्यर्थितो ददौ R.iv.58.With अभिप्र-, to request, to desire.With प्र-, 1. to desire, to wish for, to beg, to request, अवग्राहे यथा वृष्टिं प्रार्थयन्ते कृषीवलाः Bt.viii.48, R.vii.50; 2. to go in search of, to search, प्रार्थयध्वं तथा सीतां यात सुग्रीवशासनात् Bt.iii.48; 3. to attack, to fall upon, दुर्जयो लवणः शूलो विशूलः प्रार्थ्ययामिति R.xv.5, or तत्प्रार्थितं जवनवाजिगतेन राज्ञा R.ix.56.With प्रति-, 1. to make an enemy of; 2. to encounter, to meet with a hostile purpose, संख्ये प्रत्यर्थयत राघवम् Bt.vi.25 (here प्रत्यर्थयत is explained in another way also).With सम्-, 1. to consider, to believe, समर्थने वीर्यशृंगमिव भग्नमात्मनः R.xi.73; 2. to substantiate by proof, to corroborate.With संप्र-, to beg, to request, to supplicate, e.g. संप्रार्थयामास नगेन्द्रवर्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ|अर्थः
अर्थ <i>m.</i> 1. Object, purpose, e.g. ज्ञातार्थो ज्ञातसंबन्धः श्रोतुं श्रोता प्रवर्तते; (अर्थ is often used in this sense as the last member of adjectival compounds and may be rendered by ‘intended for,’ ‘for the sake of on account of’ &c., सन्तानार्थाय विधये R.i.84, ii.16, यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र लोकोऽयं कर्मबन्धनः Bg.iii.9. In ‘मशकार्थो धूमः’ and ‘आपदर्थे धनं रक्षेत्’ has the sense of “warding off” but it is derivable from the sense above given. The acc. dat. and loc. singulars of this word, viz., अर्थम्, अर्थाय and अर्थे often stand as last members of adverbial compounds in the above senses, वेलोपलक्षणार्थमादिष्टोऽस्मि भगवता काश्यपेन Sak.iv., तद्दर्शनाद्भूच्छम्भोर्भूयान् दारार्थमादरः K.S.vi.13.); 2. use, utility, profit, advantage; 3. motive, reason, ground (in these three senses, the word is generally used with the inst., e.g. को नु मे जीवितेनार्थः, नैव तस्य कृतेनार्थो नाकृतेनेह कश्चन Bg.iii.18, अचेतनग्रहणेन नार्थः, सतामर्थः शिवार्चया, कोऽर्थस्तिरश्चां गुणैः Panch.ii.); 4. meaning, sense, signification, e.g. अर्थभेदेन शब्दभेदः; 5. anything expressed by words, तददोषै शब्दार्थौ सगुणौ K.Pr.i. (According to poeticians, this अर्थ is of three kinds, viz, वाच्य or primary (i.e. expressed), लक्ष्य or secondary, and व्यंग्य or suggested.); 6. money, wealth, riches, अजरामरवत्प्राज्ञो विद्यामर्थं च साधयेत्, अर्थानामर्जने दुःखम् Panch.i.; 7. interest, concern (as in स्वार्थ ‘one’s own interest’); 8. attainment of riches or worldly prosperity (considered as one of the four ends of worldly life (पुरुषार्थ), the other three being धर्म, काम and मोक्ष), अप्यर्थकामौ तस्यास्तां धर्म एव मनीषिणः R.i.25; 9. affair, matter, concern, इक्ष्वाकूणां दुरापेऽर्थे त्वदधीना हि सिद्धयः R.i.72, or अर्थोऽयमर्थान्तरभाव्य एव K.S.iii.18; 10. an object of sense, anything which can be perceived by any of the senses, इन्द्रियेभ्यः परा ह्यर्था अर्थेभ्यश्च परं मनः Katho., (the objects of sense are five in number, vix. शब्द, स्पर्श, रूप, रस and गन्ध); 11. a request, a petition; 12. manner, kind; 13. an action, a plaint (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाधिकार|अर्थाधिकारः
अर्थ-अधिकार <i>m.</i> charge of money, office of treasurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्तर
अर्थ-अन्तर <i>n.</i> 1. another matter, a new affair, अर्थोयमर्थान्तरभाव्य एव K.S.iii.18; 2. a different meaning (as in अर्थान्तरसंक्रमितवाच्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्तरन्यास
अर्थ-अन्तर˚न्यास <i>m.</i> a figure of speech (in rhetoric). It consists in the statement of a general proposition to support a particular one or of a particular instance to support a general proposition- (1) यावदर्थपदां वाचमेवमादाय माधवः । विरराम महीयांसः प्रकृत्या मितभाषिणः Sis.ii.13; (2) बृहत्सहायः कार्यान्तं क्षोदीयानपि गच्छति । सम्भूयांभोधिमन्येति महानद्या नगापगा ii.100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थार्थिन्
अर्थ-अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> one who solicits wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थालंकार
अर्थ-अलंकार <i>m.</i> a figure of speech dependent on sense and not on sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थागम|अर्थागमः
अर्थ-आगम <i>m.</i> income, acquisition of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापत्ति|अर्थापत्तिः
अर्थ-आपत्ति <i>f.</i> 1. one of the five processes of inference of the Mīmānsākas; it is an inference by which any apparent inconsistency is explained away, e.g. पीनो देवदत्तो दिवा न भुंक्ते (where the inference of रात्रिभोजन explains the inconsistency); 2. (according to some writers on rhetoric) a figure of speech in which a relevant statement leads to an inference unconnected with the context or vice versa हारोऽयं हरिणाक्षीणां लुठति स्तनमण्डले । सक्तानामप्यववस्थेयं के वयं स्मरकिंकराः ॥ Am.S.100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोपार्जन|अर्थोपार्ज्जन
अर्थ-उपार्जन <i>n.</i> acquisition of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोष्मन्
अर्थ-उष्मन् <i>m.</i> the glow of wealth, the warmth of money, अर्थोष्मणा विरहितः पुरुषः स एव Bhartr.ii.40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थौघ|अर्थौघः
अर्थ-ओघ <i>m.</i> a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकर
अर्थ-कर, -कृत् <i>a.</i> yielding wealth, useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकृत्
अर्थ-कर, -कृत् <i>a.</i> yielding wealth, useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकाम
अर्थ-काम <i>(I) m. du.</i> wealth and pleasure, R.i.25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकाम
अर्थ-काम <i>(II) a.</i> desirous of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकृच्छ्र
अर्थ-कृच्छ्र <i>n.</i> 1. a difficulty, a difficult matter; 2. a pecuniary difficulty, e.g. न मुह्येदर्थकृच्छ्रेषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकृत्य
अर्थ-कृत्य <i>n.</i> execution of any business, अभ्युपेतार्थकृत्याः Megh.i.38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगौरव
अर्थ-गौरव <i>m.</i> depth of meaning, e.g. भारवेरर्थगौरवम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थघ्न
अर्थ-घ्न <i>a.</i> extravagant, wasteful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थजात
अर्थ-जात <i>(I) a.</i> full of meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थजात
अर्थ-जात <i>(II) n.</i> 1. a collection of things; 2. considerable wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतत्व
अर्थ-तत्व <i>n.</i> truth, the real nature or cause of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतस्
अर्थ-तस् <i>ind.</i> 1. with reference to the meaning; 2. in fact, really; 3. for the sake of money, ऐश्वर्यादनपेतमीश्वरमयं लोकोऽर्थतः सेवते Mud.i.; 4. on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतोगौरवम्
अर्थ-तस्˚गौरवम् <i>n.</i> depth of meaning, यच्चार्थतो गौरवम् M.M.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थद
अर्थ-द <i>a.</i> 1. advantageous, useful; 2. liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदूषण
अर्थ-दूषण <i>n.</i> 1. unjust seizure of property; 2. waste; 3. finding fault with the meaning of a passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदोष|अर्थदोषः
अर्थ-दोष <i>m.</i> a literary blemish in regard to sense. (The faults of composition are classed under the heads of पददोष, पदांशदोष, वाक्यदोष and अर्थदोष; for an enumeration and explanation of these, see K.Pr.vii.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थनिबन्धन
अर्थ-निबन्धन <i>a.</i> contingent on wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थनिश्चय|अर्थनिश्चयः
अर्थ-निश्चय <i>m.</i> determination, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपति|अर्थपतिः
अर्थ-पति <i>m.</i> 1. lord of riches, a king, किञ्चिद्विहस्यार्थपतिं बभाषे R.ii.46, ix.3; 2. an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपर
अर्थ-पर, -लुब्ध <i>a.</i> intent on gaining wealth, covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलुब्ध
अर्थ-पर, -लुब्ध <i>a.</i> intent on gaining wealth, covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्रकृति|अर्थप्रकृतिः
अर्थ-प्रकृति <i>f.</i> a source of the grand object in a drama. (They are five- (1) बीज; (2) बिन्दु; (3) पताका; (4) प्रकरी and (5) कार्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्रयोग|अर्थप्रयोगः
अर्थ-प्रयोग <i>m.</i> usury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थबन्ध|अर्थबन्धः
अर्थ-बन्ध <i>n.</i> composition, text, stanza.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थबुद्धि
अर्थ-बुद्धि <i>a.</i> selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थबोध|अर्थबोधः
अर्थ-बोध <i>m.</i> indication of the real meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभेद|अर्थभेदः
अर्थ-भेद <i>n.</i> difference of meaning, e.g. अर्थभेदेन शब्दभेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थमात्र
अर्थ-मात्र <i>n.</i> wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलाभ|अर्थलाभः
अर्थ-लाभ <i>m.</i> acquisition of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्|अर्थवन्त्
अर्थ-वत् <i>a.</i> 1. having meaning, अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः Pan.; 2. serving some purpose, not useless; 3. significant, e.g. अर्थवान् खलु मे राजशब्दः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवाद|अर्थवादः
अर्थ-वाद <i>m.</i> 1. an explanatory remark (it recommends a precept (विधि) by stating the good it brings on, by enumerating the evils that result from its omission, by setting up long practice &c.); 2. declaration of any purpose; 3. praise, अर्थवाद एषः । दोषं तु मे कञ्चित्कथय Ut.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविद्
अर्थ-विद् <i>a.</i> sagacious, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवृद्धि|अर्थवृद्धिः
अर्थ-वृद्धि <i>f.</i> accumulation of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविकल्प|अर्थविकल्पः
अर्थ-विकल्प <i>m.</i> 1. deviation from truth; 2. prevarication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थव्यय|अर्थव्ययः
अर्थ-व्यय <i>m.</i> expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशास्त्र|अर्थशास्त्रं
अर्थ-शास्त्र <i>n.</i> 1. science of polity or moral and political government, अर्थशास्त्रकारास्त्रिविधां सिद्धिमामनन्ति Mud.iii.; 2. science of general conduct in life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशौच
अर्थ-शौच <i>n.</i> honesty in money matters, सर्वेषामेव शौचानामर्थशौचं परं स्मृतम् M.v.106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंस्थान
अर्थ-संस्थान <i>n.</i> treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसम्बन्ध|अर्थसंबन्ध|अर्थसंबन्धः
अर्थ-सम्बन्ध <i>m.</i> connection of sense with a word or a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसिद्धि|अर्थसिद्धिः
अर्थ-सिद्धि <i>f.</i> fulfilment of desired object, success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=065-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थना
अर्थना <i>f.</i> Request, begging, entreaty, Na.v.112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थात्
अर्थात् <i>ind.</i> 1. As a matter of course, in fact, मूषकेन दण्डो भक्षित इत्यनेन तत्सहचरितमपूपभक्षणमर्थादायातं भवति S.D.x.; 2. that is to say, namely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिक|अर्थिकः
अर्थिक <i>m.</i> 1. A watchman; 2. a minstrel whose business it is to announce the different hours of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन् <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> 1. One who seeks for anything, (with the inst., e.g. भार्यया चार्थी); 2. desirous of, (with the inst., e.g. को वधेन ममार्थी स्यात्); 3. entreating anyone, (with the gen., e.g. अर्थी वररुचिर्मेस्तु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिनी
अर्थिन् <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> 1. One who seeks for anything, (with the inst., e.g. भार्यया चार्थी); 2. desirous of, (with the inst., e.g. को वधेन ममार्थी स्यात्); 3. entreating anyone, (with the gen., e.g. अर्थी वररुचिर्मेस्तु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A beggar, a suitor, कन्यारत्नमयोनिजन्म भवतामास्ते वयं चार्थिनः Mv.i., यथाकामार्चितार्थिनाम् R.i.6, ii.54, ix.27; 2. a prosecutor, a plaintiff, a complainant, स धर्मस्थसखः शश्वदर्थिप्रत्यर्थिनः स्वयम् । ददर्श संशयच्छेद्यान् व्यवहारानतन्द्रितः R.xvii.39; 3. a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिसात्
अर्थिन्-सात् <i>ind.</i> at the disposal of beggars, (with कृ, e.g. विभज्य मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात्कृतः Na.i.16).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थीय
अर्थीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Destined for, relating to (always used as the last member of a compound, कर्मचैव तदर्थीयम् Bg.xvii.27.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थीया
अर्थीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Destined for, relating to (always used as the last member of a compound, कर्मचैव तदर्थीयम् Bg.xvii.27.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य <i>(I) a. (f. र्थ्या)</i> 1. Worthy of being sought; 2. appropriate, significant, स्तुत्यं स्तुतिभिरर्थ्याभिरूपतस्थे सरस्वती R.iv.6; 3. fit, proper; 4. wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्या
अर्थ्य <i>(I) a. (f. र्थ्या)</i> 1. Worthy of being sought; 2. appropriate, significant, स्तुत्यं स्तुतिभिरर्थ्याभिरूपतस्थे सरस्वती R.iv.6; 3. fit, proper; 4. wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य <i>(II) n.</i> Red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्|अर्द्द्
अर्द् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1P (pp. अर्दित)</i> 1. To ask or beg, शरद्धनं नार्दति चातकोऽपि R.v.17; 2. to go; 3. to be hurt, to be troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्|अर्द्द्
अर्द् <i>(II) vt. 1U (pp. अर्दित)</i> To kill, to hurt, रक्षः सहस्राणि चतुर्दशार्दीत् Bt.xii.56.With अति-, 1. to kill; 2. to fall upon, अत्यार्दीद्बालिनः पुत्रं Bt.xv.115.With अभि-, to press, to afflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्|अर्द्द्
अर्द् <i>(III) vt. 10U (pp. अर्दित)</i> To hurt, to kill, येनार्दिदद्दैत्यपुरं पिनाकी Bt.ii.42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=066-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दन|अर्दनं|अर्दनः|अर्द्दन
अर्दन <i>n.</i> Pain, trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दना|अर्द्दना
अर्दना <i>f.</i> 1. Going; 2. begging; 3. killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः|अर्धः
अर्ध <i>(I) a. (f. र्धा)</i> Half, forming a half, अप्यर्धमार्गे परबाणलूना R.viii.45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धा
अर्ध <i>(I) a. (f. र्धा)</i> Half, forming a half, अप्यर्धमार्गे परबाणलूना R.viii.45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः|अर्धः
अर्ध <i>(II) m.n.</i> 1. The half, क्रोशार्धं पर्कृतिपुरःसरेण गत्वा R.xiii.79; 2. a part, यदर्धे विच्छिन्नं भवति कृतसन्धानमिव तत् Sak.i., R.iii.59; 3. half a short syllable. (अर्ध may be peculiarly compounded with an ordinal, e.g. अर्धतृतीय ‘containing the third (only) half, i.e. two and a half’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धांश|अर्धांशः
अर्ध-अंश <i>m.</i> a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धांशिन्
अर्ध-अंशिन् <i>a.</i> sharing a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धांग|अर्धाङ्ग
अर्ध-अंग <i>n.</i> half the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धार्ध|अर्धार्धः
अर्ध-अर्ध <i>m.</i> a quarter, चरोरर्धार्धभागाभ्यां तामयोजयतामुभे R.x.56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धावशेष
अर्ध-अवशेष <i>a.</i> having only one half left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धासन|अर्द्धासनं
अर्ध-आसन <i>n.</i> 1. half a seat (it is considered a mark of great respect to make room for a guest on the same seat with one’s self, उपेयुषः स्वामपि मूर्तिमग्न्यामर्धासनं गोत्रभिदोधितष्ठौ (scil. ककुत्स्थः) R.vi.73, or मम हि दिवौकसां समक्षमर्धासनोपवेशितस्य &c. Sak.vii.); 2. exemption from censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धेन्दु|अर्द्धेन्दुः|अर्धेन्दुः
अर्ध-इन्दु <i>m.</i> 1. a half moon; 2. an arrow with a crescent-shaped head; 3. a crescent-shaped nail-print.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धेन्दुमौलि
अर्ध-इन्दु˚मौलि <i>m.</i> Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धोक्त
अर्ध-उक्त <i>a.</i> half uttered, रामभद्रेत्यर्धोक्ते Ut.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धोक्ति|अर्धोक्तिः
अर्ध-उक्ति <i>f.</i> broken speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धोदय|अर्द्धोदयः|अर्धोदयः
अर्ध-उदय <i>m.</i> 1. a partial rise; 2. the rising of the half-moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धोरुक|अर्द्धोरुकं
अर्ध-उरुक <i>n.</i> a short petticoat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धकाल
अर्ध-काल, -कूट <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धकूट
अर्ध-काल, -कूट <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धकृत
अर्ध-कृत <i>a.</i> half done, incomplete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धखार
अर्ध-खार <i>n.</i> a measure of grain, half a khāri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धखारि
अर्ध-खारि <i>f.</i> a measure of grain, half a khāri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धगंगा|अर्धगङ्गा
अर्ध-गंगा <i>f.</i> a name of the river Kāverī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धगुच्छ|अर्द्धगुच्छः|अर्धगुच्छः
अर्ध-गुच्छ <i>m.</i> a necklace of 24 strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धगोल|अर्धगोलः
अर्ध-गोल <i>m.</i> the hemisphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धचन्द्र|अर्द्धचन्द्रः|अर्धचन्द्रः
अर्ध-चन्द्र <i>m.</i> 1. the half moon, शब्दमीश्वर इत्य्च्चैः सार्धचन्द्रं बिभर्ति यः K.S.vi.75; 2. a half-moon-shaped blow, e.g. अर्धचन्द्रं दत्वा निःसारितः or दीयतामेतरस्यार्धचन्द्रः; 3. the semicircular mark on the peacock’s tail; 4. an arrow the head of which is like a half-moon, अर्धचन्द्रमुखैर्बाणैश्चिच्छेद कदलीसुखम् R.xii.96; 5. a half-moon-shaped nail-print.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धचन्द्राकार|अर्धचन्द्राकारः
अर्ध-चन्द्र˚आकार <i>a.</i> half-moon-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धचोलक|अर्द्धचोलकः|अर्धचोलकः
अर्ध-चोलक <i>m.</i> a short bodice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धजाह्नवी
अर्ध-जाह्नवी <i>f.</i> See अर्धगंगा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धदिवस|अर्धदिवसः
अर्ध-दिवस <i>m.</i> 1. mid-day; 2. a day of 12 hours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धनारीश|अर्द्धनारीशः|अर्धनारीशः
अर्ध-नारीश, -नारीश्वर <i>m.</i> that form of Śiva in which he appears half male and half female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धनारीश्वर|अर्द्धनारीश्वरः|अर्धनारीश्वरः
अर्ध-नारीश, -नारीश्वर <i>m.</i> that form of Śiva in which he appears half male and half female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धनिशा
अर्ध-निशा <i>f.</i> mid-night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धपञ्चाशत्
अर्ध-पञ्चाशत् <i>f.</i> twenty-five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धपण|अर्धपणः
अर्ध-पण <i>n.</i> a particular measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धपथ
अर्ध-पथ <i>n.</i> half way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धपथे
अर्ध-पथे <i>ind.</i> mid-way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धप्रहर
अर्ध-प्रहर <i>m.</i> half a watch, i.e. one hour and a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धभाग|अर्धभागः
अर्ध-भाग <i>m.</i> a half, तदर्धभागेन लभस्व कांक्षितम् K.S.v.50, R.viii.45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धभाज्
अर्ध-भाज् <i>m.</i> 1. a sharer; 2. entitled to a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धभास्कर|अर्धभास्करः
अर्ध-भास्कर <i>m.</i> mid-day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमागधी
अर्ध-मागधी <i>f.</i> a variety of the Māgadhī dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमाणव|अर्द्धमाणवः|अर्धमाणवः
अर्ध-माणव, -माणवक <i>m.</i> a necklace of twelve strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमाणवक|अर्धमाणवकः
अर्ध-माणव, -माणवक <i>m.</i> a necklace of twelve strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमात्रा
अर्ध-मात्रा <i>f.</i> half a short syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमार्गे
अर्ध-मार्गे <i>ind.</i> mid-way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमासिक
अर्ध-मासिक <i>a.</i> 1. happening every half month; 2. lasting half a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धमुष्टि|अर्धमुष्टिः
अर्ध-मुष्टि <i>m.f.</i> a half-clenched-hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धयाम|अर्धयामः
अर्ध-याम <i>m.</i> See अर्धप्रहर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धरथ|अर्धरथः
अर्ध-रथ <i>m.</i> a warrior fighting on a car who is not as perfectly skilled as a रथी, e.g. तेन मेऽर्धरथो मतः (scil. कर्णः) Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=067-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

