अवकर|अवकरः
अवकर <i>m.</i> Dust, sweepings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकलित|अवकलितः
अवकलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Seen; 2. known; 3. received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकलिता
अवकलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Seen; 2. known; 3. received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश|अवकाशः
अवकाश <i>m.</i> 1. Space, place, room, अवकाशो विविक्तोयं महानद्योः समागमे Ram. अस्माकमस्ति न कथंचिदिहावकाशः Panch.iv.; 2. occasion, opportunity, e.g. लब्धावकाशोऽविध्यन्मां तत्र दग्धो मनोभवः; 3. footing, admission, तस्माद्देयो विपुलमतिभिर्नावकाशोऽधमानाम् Panch.iv., (छाया) शुद्धे तु दर्पणतले सुलभावकाशा Sak.vii.; 4. aperture; 5. interval, intermediate time.With the roots दा and कृ and their derivatives, अवकाश means ‘to make room for,’ ‘to give way to,’ e.g. असौ हि दत्वा तिमिरावकाशमस्तं व्रजत्युन्नतकोटिरिन्दुः.With लभ्-, it means- (1) to get a footing, लब्धावकाशो मे मनोरथः Sak.i.; शोकावेगदूषिते मे मनसि विवेक एव मावकाशं लभते; (2) to get an opportunity. (See 2 above).With रुध्-, ‘to hinder,’ ‘to impede’ (निद्राम्) नयनसलिलोत्पीडरुद्धावकाशाम् Megh.ii.28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
अवकीर्णिन् <i>m.</i> A religious student who has committed an act of incontinency contrary to his vow. (अवकीर्णी भवेद्गत्वा ब्र्हमचारी तु योषितम् Yaj.iii.280).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुंचन|अवकुञ्चन|अवकुंचनं
