अवगम|अवगमः
अवगम <i>m.</i> The same as अवगति q.v., Bg.ix.2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढ
अवगाढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Immersed, plunged into; 2. depressed, low, अभ्युन्नता पुरस्तादवगाढा जघनगौरवात्पश्चात् (पदपंक्तिः) Sak.iii.; 3. deep. (The word is sometimes written वगाढ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढा
अवगाढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Immersed, plunged into; 2. depressed, low, अभ्युन्नता पुरस्तादवगाढा जघनगौरवात्पश्चात् (पदपंक्तिः) Sak.iii.; 3. deep. (The word is sometimes written वगाढ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाह|अवगाहः
अवगाह <i>m.</i> 1. Plunging, जलावगाहक्षणमात्रशान्ता R.v.47; 2. bathing, सुभगसलिलावगाहाः (दिवसाः) Sak.i., सदावगाहक्षमवारिसंचयः Rt.i.1; 3. a bathing-place. (Written also वगाह.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=071-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहन|अवगाहनं
अवगाहन <i>n.</i> 1. Plunging; 2. bathing, दग्धानामवगाहनाय विधिना रम्यं सरो निर्मितम् Sr.T.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीत|अवगीतं|अवगीतः
अवगीत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Abused, censured; 2. wicked, vile; 3. satirized in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीता
अवगीत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Abused, censured; 2. wicked, vile; 3. satirized in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीत|अवगीतं|अवगीतः
अवगीत <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Reproach, blame; 2. an evil report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण|अवगुणः
अवगुण <i>m.</i> Fault, defect, अन्यदोषं परावगुणम् Mall. on Kir.xiii.48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठन|अवगुंठनं|अवगुण्ठनं
अवगुण्ठन <i>n.</i> 1. Veiling; 2. a veil, e.g. तिमिरावगुण्ठनपटक्षेपं विधत्ते विधुः; 3. covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठनवती
