अवगूहन|अवगूहनं
अवगूहन <i>n.</i> 1. Hiding; 2. embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगोरण|अवगोरणं
अवगोरण <i>n.</i> Assaulting with intent to kill (in criminal law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रह|अवग्रहः
अवग्रह <i>m.</i> 1. The withholding or failure of rain, नभोनभस्ययोर्वृष्टिमवग्रह इवान्तरे R.xii.29, i.62, x.48; 2. drought, कृषेव सीतां तदवग्रहक्षताम् K.S.v.61; 3. obstacle, impediment; 4. a hiatus, as in धिक् ताञ्च तञ्च मदनञ्च इमाञ्च माञ्च Bhartr.ii.2 (in gram.); 5. nature; 6. a term of abuse; 7. an elephant’s forehead; 8. a herd of elephants; 9. the sign (ऽ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रहण|अवग्रहणं
अवग्रहण <i>n.</i> 1. Obstacle, impediment; 2. disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्राह|अवग्राहः
अवग्राह <i>m.</i> The same as अवग्रह q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्ट|अवघट्टः
अवघट्ट <i>m.</i> 1. A hole in the ground, a cave; 2. a stone-mill for grinding corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघर्षण|अवघर्षणं
अवघर्षण <i>n.</i> Rubbing, rubbing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघात|अवघातः
