अवजय|अवजयः
अवजय <i>m.</i> Victory, येनेन्द्रलोकावजयाय दृप्तः संधाय … लंकाधिपतिः प्रतस्थे R.vi.62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञा
अवज्ञा <i>f.</i> Contempt, disrespect, disregard, आत्मन्यवज्ञां शिथिली चकार R.ii.41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञोपहत
अवज्ञा-उपहत <i>a.</i> treated with contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञादुःख
अवज्ञा-दुःख <i>n.</i> the pangs of humiliation, माजीवन् यः परावज्ञादुःखदग्धोपि जीवति Sis.ii.45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञान|अवज्ञानं
अवज्ञान <i>n.</i> The same as अवज्ञा q.v., R.i.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट|अवटः
अवट <i>m.</i> 1. A hole; 2. a pit, अवटे चापि मे राम प्रक्षिपेदं कलेवरम् Ram.; 3. a well; 4. any low or depressed part of the body, Yaj.iii.98; 5. a juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटकच्छप|अवटकच्छपः
अवट-कच्छप <i>m.</i> a tortoise in a hole (lit.), an inexperienced man who has seen nothing of the world (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटि|अवटिः
अवटि(टी) <i>f.</i> 1. hole, cavity; 2. a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटी
अवटि(टी) <i>f.</i> 1. hole, cavity; 2. a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=072-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटीट|अवटीटः
अवटीट <i>a. (f. टा)</i> Flat-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटीटा
अवटीट <i>a. (f. टा)</i> Flat-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटु|अवटुः
अवटु <i>m.</i> 1. A hole in the ground; 2. a well; 3. the back of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडीन|अवडीनं
अवडीन <i>m.</i> A particular flight of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंस|अवतंसं|अवतंसः
अवतंस <i>m.n.</i> 1. A garland; 2. an ear-ring, K.S.vii.38; 3. a particular ornament to be worn on the head (hence anything that prominently figures as an ornament, के वा न सन्ति भुवि तामरसावतंसाः (जलसन्निवेशाः) Chat.ii.3. Cf. कुलावतंसः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसक|अवतंसकः
अवतंसक <i>m.n.</i> The same as अवतंस q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतप्त
अवतप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> Heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतप्ता
अवतप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> Heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतप्तेनकुलस्थित
अवतप्तेनकुलस्थित <i>n.</i> an ichneumon’s standing on hot ground (metaphorically said of the inconstancy of man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतमस|अवतमसं
अवतमस <i>n.</i> 1. Slight darkness; 2. darkness in general, अवतमसभिदायौ भास्वताभ्युद्गतेन Sis.xi.57. (Mall. observes in connection with this use of the word- यद्यपि क्षीणेवतमसं तम इत्युक्तं तथाद्यपि विरोधाद्विशेषानादरेण सामान्यमेव ग्राह्यम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतर|अवतरं|अवतरः
अवतर <i>m.</i> See अवतरण, Na.iii.53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरण|अवतरणं
अवतरण <i>n.</i> 1. Descending; 2. crossing; 3. translating from one language into another; 4. an extract, a quotation; 5. a holy bathing-place; 6. an incarnation; 7. introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणिका
अवतरणिका <i>f.</i> 1. A short prayer at the beginning of a work which is supposed to cause the divinity addressed to descend from heaven; 2. an introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणी
अवतरणी <i>f.</i> The same as अवतरणिका q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवताडन|अवताडनं
अवताडन <i>n.</i> 1. Treading, M.M.i.; 2. striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतान|अवतानः
अवतान <i>m.</i> 1. Stretching; 2. the unbending of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतार|अवतारः
अवतार <i>m.</i> 1. Descent; 2. an incarnation in general, धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाणामवतार इवांगवान् R.x.84, or ऋष्यवतारोयं नृपतिः; 3. an incarnation of Viṣṇu; (they are ten in number, viz., मत्स्य, कूर्म, वराह, नृसिंह, वामन, परशुराम, राम, कृष्ण, बुद्ध and कल्कि. The first Aṣṭapadī in the Git.G. very shortly describes them all. They are alluded to in the following stanza also- वेदानुद्धरते जगन्निवहते भूगोलमुद्विभ्रते दैत्यं दारयते बलिं छलयते क्षत्रक्षयं कुर्वते । पौलस्त्यं जयते हलं कलयते कारुण्यमातन्वते म्लेच्छान् मूर्छयते दशाकृतिकृते कृष्णाय तुभ्यं नमः Git.G.i.); 4. rise, appearance, नवावतारं कमलादिवोत्पलम् R.iii.36, v.24; 5. form, मत्स्यादिभिरवतारैरवतारवता (त्वया) Śankara.; 6. a sacred bathing-place; 7. a pond; 8. a landing place; 9. translation; 10. introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारकथा
अवतार-कथा <i>f.</i> an account of an avatāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारमन्त्र|अवतारमन्त्रः
अवतार-मन्त्र <i>m.</i> a prayer causing the descent of a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारक
अवतारक <i>a. (f. रिका)</i> Making a descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारिका
अवतारक <i>a. (f. रिका)</i> Making a descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारण|अवतारणं
अवतारण <i>n.</i> 1. The causing to descend; 2. translation; 3. adoration; 4. possession by an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतोका
अवतोका <i>f.</i> A woman who has miscarried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदंश|अवदंशः
अवदंश <i>n.</i> 1. A stimulant; 2. any pungent food which excites thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदात|अवदातं|अवदातः
अवदात <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Clean, pure (as in अवदाताशयः); 2. white, कुन्दावदाताः कलहंसमालाः Bt.ii.18; 3. beautiful; 4. meritorious, अन्यस्मिञ्जग्मनि न कृतमवदातं कर्म Kad.; 5. yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाता
अवदात <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Clean, pure (as in अवदाताशयः); 2. white, कुन्दावदाताः कलहंसमालाः Bt.ii.18; 3. beautiful; 4. meritorious, अन्यस्मिञ्जग्मनि न कृतमवदातं कर्म Kad.; 5. yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदात|अवदातं|अवदातः
अवदात <i>(II) m.</i> The white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदान|अवदानं
अवदान <i>n.</i> 1. A glorious or valorous deed, प्रापदस्त्रमवदानतोषितात् R.xi.21; 2. the object of a legend; 3. a pure occupation; 4. cutting or dividing into parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदारण|अवदारणं
अवदारण <i>n.</i> 1. Tearing, cutting into pieces; 2. a spade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाह|अवदाहं|अवदाहः
अवदाह <i>m.</i> Burning down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदीर्ण|अवदीर्णं
अवदीर्ण <i>a. (f. र्णा)</i> Melted, fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदीर्णा
अवदीर्ण <i>a. (f. र्णा)</i> Melted, fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदोह|अवदोहः
अवदोह <i>m.</i> 1. Milk; 2. milking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्य|अवद्यं
अवद्य <i>(I) a. (f. द्या)</i> 1. Low, inferior; 2. faulty, defective, न चापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यम् Mal.i.; 3. disagreeable, blamable, R.vii.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्या
अवद्य <i>(I) a. (f. द्या)</i> 1. Low, inferior; 2. faulty, defective, न चापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यम् Mal.i.; 3. disagreeable, blamable, R.vii.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्य|अवद्यं
अवद्य <i>(II) n.</i> 1. A fault, a defect; 2. vice, sin, censure, reproach, उदवहदनवद्यां तामवद्यादपेतः R.vii.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधान|अवधानं
अवधान <i>n.</i> 1. Attention, attentiveness, अवधानपरे चकारा सा (विलोचने) K.S.iv.2; 2. carefulness, devotion. (अवधानात् ‘attentively,’ शृणुत जना अवधानात् क्रियामिमां कालिदासस्य Vikr.i.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधार|अवधारः
अवधार <i>m.</i> Accurate determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारण|अवधारणं
अवधारण <i>n.</i> 1. Determination; 2. affirmation, emphasis; 3. limitation (as of the sense of a word, यावदवधारणे Pan.); 4. restriction to certain instances with exclusion of others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधि|अवधिः
अवधि <i>m.</i> 1. Application, attention; 2. a period of time, दोषान् मासान् विरहदिवसस्थापितस्यावधेर्वा Megh.ii.24; 3. a division; 4. a limit (exclusive or inclusive, and either of time or space) स्मरशापावधिदां सरस्वतीम् K.S.iv.43; 5. a hole, a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरण|अवधीरणं
अवधीरण <i>n.</i> The same as अवधीरणा q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=073-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरणा
