अवरोधिक|अवरोधिकः
अवरोध(धि)क <i>(I) m.</i> A guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधक|अवरोधकः
अवरोध(धि)क <i>(II) n.</i> A barrier, a fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिक|अवरोधिकः
अवरोध(धि)क <i>(II) n.</i> A barrier, a fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधन|अवरोधनं
अवरोधन <i>n.</i> 1. A siege; 2. an impediment; 3. women’s apartments in a royal palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिका
अवरोधिका <i>f.</i> A female of the inner apartments, ययुस्तुरंगाधिरुहोऽवरोधिकाः Sis.xii.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपण|अवरोपणं
अवरोपण <i>n.</i> 1. Causing to descend; 2. taking away, depriving; 3. rooting out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोह|अवरोहः
अवरोह <i>m.</i> 1. Descent; 2. heaven; 3. the descending scale of notes in Indian music; 4. a pendent branch of the Indian fig tree; 5. a creeper encircling a tree from its bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहण|अवरोहणं
अवरोहण <i>n.</i> 1. Alighting, descending; 2. ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ण|अवर्णः
अवर्ण <i>m.</i> 1. Stain, ill-fame, सोढुं न तत्पूर्वमवर्णमीशे R.xiv.38; 2. blame, censure, न चावदद्भर्तुरवर्णमार्या R.xiv.57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्ष|अवलक्षः
अवलक्ष <i>(sometimes written वलक्ष) (I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्षा
अवलक्ष <i>(sometimes written वलक्ष) (I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्ष|अवलक्षः
अवलक्ष <i>(II) m.</i> The white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलग्न|अवलग्नः
अवलग्न <i>m.n.</i> The white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्ब|अवलंबः|अवलम्बः
अवलम्ब <i>m.</i> 1. A support, prop, सावलम्बगमना मृदुस्वना R.xix.50; 2. hanging down; 3. dependence, कुनृपतिभवनद्वारसेवावलम्बव्यासंगव्यस्तधैर्याः Bhartr.i.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बन|अवलंबनं|अवलम्बनं
अवलम्बन <i>n.</i> The same as अवलम्ब q.v., प्रस्थानविक्लवगतेरवलम्बनाय Sak.v., or अवलम्बनाय दिनभर्तुरभुत् Sis.ix.6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्त|अवलिप्तः
अवलिप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> 1. Annointed; 2. proud, arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्ता
अवलिप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> 1. Annointed; 2. proud, arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीढ|अवलीढं
अवलीढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Eaten; 2. licked; 3. surrounded, अस्त्रज्वालावलीढप्रतिबलजलधेरन्तरौर्वायमाणे Ve.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीढा
अवलीढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Eaten; 2. licked; 3. surrounded, अस्त्रज्वालावलीढप्रतिबलजलधेरन्तरौर्वायमाणे Ve.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीला
अवलीला <i>f.</i> 1. Sport, play, mirth; 2. contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुंचन|अवलुञ्चन|अवलुंचनं
अवलुंचन <i>n.</i> Pulling out, cutting off (as in केशावलुंचन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुण्ठन|अवलुंठनं|अवलुण्ठनं
अवलुण्ठन <i>n.</i> 1. Robbing; 2. wallowing on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेख|अवलेखः
अवलेख <i>m.</i> Any thing scraped off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेखा
अवलेखा <i>f.</i> 1. Rubbing; 2. adorning the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेप|अवलेपः
अवलेप <i>m.</i> 1. Smearing, anointing; 2. pride, haughtiness, व्यक्तमानावलेपाः Mud.iii., R.v.53; 3. association; 4. ornamentation; 5. assault, ददृशे पवनावलेपजं सृजती बाष्पम् R.viii.35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपन|अवलेपनं
अवलेपन <i>a.</i> The same as अवलेप q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेह|अवलेहः
अवलेह <i>m.</i> 1. Licking; 2. an extract (as of soma drug).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहिका
अवलेहिका <i>f.</i> The same as अवलेह q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोक|अवलोकः
अवलोक <i>m.</i> 1. Sight; 2. looking, beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकन|अवलोकनं
अवलोकन <i>n.</i> 1. Looking, beholding, नो बभूवुरवलोकनक्षमाः R.xi.60; 2. a look, glance, योगनिद्रान्तविशदैः पावनैरवलोकनैः R.x.14; 3. an eye; 4. looking over, commanding a view of, दीर्घिकावलोकनगवाक्षगता Mal.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकित|अवलोकितं|अवलोकितः
अवलोकित <i>n.</i> A look, a glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववाद|अववादः
अववाद <i>m.</i> 1. Evil report; 2. censure; 3. confidence; 4. dependence; 5. command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश
अवश <i>a. (f. शा)</i> 1. Independent, free; 2. not having one’s own free will, dependent, कार्यतेह्यवशः Bg.iii.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशा
अवश <i>a. (f. शा)</i> 1. Independent, free; 2. not having one’s own free will, dependent, कार्यतेह्यवशः Bg.iii.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेन्द्रिय
अवश-इन्द्रिय <i>a.</i> whose senses are not held in submission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशंगम
अवशंगम <i>a.</i> not submitting to another’s will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=075-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशातन|अवशातनं
अवशातन <i>n.</i> 1. Drying up; 2. cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेष|अवशेषः
अवशेष <i>m.</i> 1. Remainder; 2. end, termination, नामावशेष (‘having only the name left behind’), कथावशेष (‘having only the tale left behind’) are used metaphorically in the sense of “dead.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्य|अवश्यं
अवश्य <i>a. (f. श्या)</i> 1. Ungovernable; 2. necessary, inevitable, indispensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्या
अवश्य <i>a. (f. श्या)</i> 1. Ungovernable; 2. necessary, inevitable, indispensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यकरण
अवश्य-करण <i>n.</i> inevitable performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यक
अवश्यक <i>a. (f. का)</i> The same as अवश्य q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यका
अवश्यक <i>a. (f. का)</i> The same as अवश्य q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यम्
अवश्यम् <i>ind.</i> 1. Surely, certainly, by all means, at all events, तां चावश्यं दिवसगणनातत्परामेकपत्नीं (द्रक्ष्यसि) Megh.i.10, 61; 2. necessarily, inevitably, स्वामप्यस्त्रं नवजलमयं मोचयिष्यत्यवश्यम् Megh.ii.30. (If compounded with a potential pass. participle the final nasal of the particle is dropped, e.g. अवश्यकार्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यंभाविन्
अवश्यम्-भाविन् <i>a.</i> inevitable, अवश्यंभाविनो भावाः भवंति महतामपि Hit.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्या
अवश्या <i>f.</i> A fog or mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्याय|अवश्यायः
अवश्याय <i>m.</i> 1. Frost; 2. white dew, e.g. अवश्यायकणास्रावा आरुमुक्ताफलत्विषः; 3. pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्रयण|अवश्रयणं
अवश्रयण <i>n.</i> Taking any thing from off the fire, अधिश्रयणावश्रयणान्तादि पूर्वापरीभूतो व्यापारकलापः पाकादिशब्दवाच्यः S.D.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टब्ध|अवष्टब्धं
अवष्टब्ध <i>a. (f. ब्धा)</i> 1. Haughty, stubborn; 2. contiguous; 3. bound, tied; 4. supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टब्धा
अवष्टब्ध <i>a. (f. ब्धा)</i> 1. Haughty, stubborn; 2. contiguous; 3. bound, tied; 4. supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भ|अवष्टंभः|अवष्टम्भः
अवष्टम्भ <i>m.</i> 1. Leaning upon, resting; 2. resoluteness; 3. beginning, commencement; 4. impediment; 5. stupefaction, paralysis, रघोरवष्टम्भमयेन पत्रिणा R.iii.53; 6. support, prop, ख्हड्गलतावष्टंभनिश्चलः M.M.iii.; 7. gold; 8. pride, haughtiness (as in सावष्टम्भम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भन|अवष्टंभनं
अवष्टम्भन <i>n.</i> 1. Resting upon; 2. a pillar, a post; 3. supporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्थिका
अवसक्थिका <i>f.</i> 1. Cloth tied round the legs and knees of a person sitting on his hams; 2. tying a cloth round the legs and knees, कृत्वा चैवावसक्थिकाम् M.iv.112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसण्डीन|अवसंडीन|अवसंडीनं
अवसण्डीन <i>n.</i> The united downward flight of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ|अवसथः
अवसथ(थ्य) <i>m.</i> 1. Habitation; 2. a village; 3. a school. (See आवसथ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ्य|अवसथ्यः
अवसथ(थ्य) <i>m.</i> 1. Habitation; 2. a village; 3. a school. (See आवसथ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्न|अवसन्नः
अवसन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> Ended, terminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्ना
अवसन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> Ended, terminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर|अवसरः
अवसर <i>m.</i> 1. Descent; 2. rain; 3. occasion, भवद्गिरामवसरप्रदानाय वचांसि नः Sis.ii.8, R.xii.87; 4. favourable opportunity, अवसरोऽयमात्मानं प्रकाशयितुम् Sak.i., K.S.vii.40; 5. leisure, ध्रुवमनवसरग्रस्त एवार्थिभावः M.M.ix.; 6. consultation in private; 7. a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्ग|अवसर्गः
अवसर्ग <i>m.</i> 1. Permission to do as one likes^1; 2. relaxation; 3. independence.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251217. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्प|अवसर्पः
अवसर्प <i>m.</i> A spy, an emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पण|अवसर्पणं
अवसर्पण <i>n.</i> Stepping down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाद|अवसादः
अवसाद <i>m.</i> 1. Sitting down; 2. failure (as in स्वरावसाद); 3. fatigue, exhaustion; 4. end, termination; 5. badness of a cause (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादन|अवसादनं
अवसादन <i>n.</i> 1. Oppressing; 2. finishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान|अवसानं
अवसान <i>n.</i> 1. End, termination, cessation, तच्छिष्याध्ययन निवेशितावसानाम् R.i.95, ii.23, 45, xviii.10; 2. a pause; 3. death, मूलपुरुषावसाने सम्पदः परमुपतिष्ठन्ति Sak.vi.; 4. boundary, limit; 5. residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाय|अवसायः
अवसाय <i>n.</i> 1. Conclusion, end; 2. completion; 3. remainder; 4. determination, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसारण
अवसारण <i>n.</i> Removing, causing to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=076-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसित|अवसितं
