अश्रान्त <i>a. (f. न्ता)</i> 1. Unwearied; 2. incessant, continual.(अश्रान्तम् is used adverbially also in the sense of ‘continually.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=081-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रि|अश्रिः
अश्रि(श्री) <i>f.</i> 1. The sharp side of anything; 2. an angle of a room or house; 3. the edge of a weapon, वृत्रस्य हन्तुः कुलिशं कुण्ठिताश्रीव लक्ष्यते K.S.ii.20. (This word is changed into अश्र when it follows चतुर्, त्रि, षट् and some other words in a compound, e.g. चतुरश्रशोभि K.S.i.32, where is explained by Mall. to mean (fig.) ‘free from defects,’ ‘symmetrical.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=081-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्री
अश्रि(श्री) <i>f.</i> 1. The sharp side of anything; 2. an angle of a room or house; 3. the edge of a weapon, वृत्रस्य हन्तुः कुलिशं कुण्ठिताश्रीव लक्ष्यते K.S.ii.20. (This word is changed into अश्र when it follows चतुर्, त्रि, षट् and some other words in a compound, e.g. चतुरश्रशोभि K.S.i.32, where is explained by Mall. to mean (fig.) ‘free from defects,’ ‘symmetrical.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=081-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

