अष्टाह
अष्टन्-अह <i>a.</i> lasting eight days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकर्ण|अष्टकर्णः
अष्टन्-कर्ण <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकर्मन्|अष्टकर्म्मन्
अष्टन्-कर्मन् <i>m.</i> a king who has eight duties to perform (आदाने च विसर्गे च तथा प्रैषनिषेधयोः । पञ्चमे चार्थवचने व्यवहारस्य चेक्षणे । दण्डशुद्ध्योः सदा रक्तस्तेनाष्टगतिको नृपः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकृत्वस्
अष्टन्-कृत्वस् <i>ind.</i> eight times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकोण|अष्टकोणः
अष्टन्-कोण <i>n.</i> an octagon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगव
अष्टन्-गव <i>n. sing.</i> a flock of eight cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगुण
अष्टन्-गुण <i>(I) a.</i> eight-fold, M.viii.40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगुण
अष्टन्-गुण <i>(II) n. sing.</i> the eight qualities which a Brāhmaṇa ought to possess, viz., दया, क्षान्ति, अनसूया, शौच, अनायास, मंगल, अकार्पण्य and अस्पृहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगुणाश्रय
अष्टन्-गुण˚आश्रय <i>a.</i> endowed with the eight qualities above-named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टत्रिक
अष्टन्-त्रिक <i>n.</i> the number ‘24.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदल
अष्टन्-दल <i>n.</i> a lotus with eight petals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिक्पाल
अष्टन्-दिक्पाल <i>m. pl.</i> the eight regents of the cardinal points viz., इन्द्र, अग्नि, यम, निरृति, वरुण, वायु, सोम and ईशान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिग्गज
अष्टन्-दिग्गज <i>m. pl.</i> the eight elephants which guard the eight cardinal points; (they are- ऐरावतः पुंडरीको वामनः कुमुदोऽञ्जनः । पुष्पदन्तः सार्वभौमः सुप्रतीकश्च दिग्गजाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिश्
अष्टन्-दिश् <i>f.</i> the eight cardinal points of the compass, viz., पूर्वा, आग्नेयी, दक्षिणा, नैरृती, पश्चिमा, वायवी, उत्तरा and ऐशानी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधा
अष्टन्-धा <i>ind.</i> 1. eight-fold; 2. in eight parts, भिन्नोष्टधा विप्रससार वंशः R.xvi.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधातु|अष्टधातुः
अष्टन्-धातु <i>n. sing.</i> the eight metals collectively; (they are- स्वर्ण रूप्यं च ताम्रं च रंगं यशदमेव च । शीसं लौहं रसश्चेति धातवोष्टौ प्रकीर्तिताः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपाद|अष्टपादः
अष्टन्-पाद <i>(I) a.</i> having eight legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपाद|अष्टपादः
अष्टन्-पाद <i>(II) m.</i> a kind of spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमंगल|अष्टमङ्गल|अष्टमङ्गलं|अष्टमङ्गलः
अष्टन्-मंगल <i>n.</i> the collection of eight lucky things; (they are differently enumerated- (1) मृगराजो वृषो नागः कलशो व्यजनं तथा । वैजयन्ती तथा भेरी दीप इत्यष्टमंगलम्; (2) लोकोस्मिन् मंगलान्यष्टौ ब्राह्मणो गौर्हुताशनः । हिरण्यं सर्पिरादित्य आपो राजा तथाष्टमः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमासिक
अष्टन्-मासिक <i>a.</i> occurring once in eight months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्ति|अष्टमूर्तिः|अष्टमूर्त्ति|अष्टमूर्त्तिः
अष्टन्-मूर्ति <i>m.</i> the eight-formed, an epithet of Śiva; (these eight forms are thus enumerated in the opening stanza of the Sak.- या सृष्टिः स्रष्टुराद्या (i.e. water) वहति विधिहुतं या हविः (i.e. fire) या च होत्री (i.e. the sacrificer) ये द्वे कालं दिधत्तः (i.e. the Sun and the moon) श्रुतिविषयगुणा या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वम् (i.e. æther) यामाहुः सर्वभूतप्रकृतिरिति (i.e. the earth) यथा प्राणिनः प्राणवन्तः (i.e. air) प्रत्यक्षामिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्तिधर|अष्टमूर्त्तिधर
अष्टन्-मूर्ति˚धर <i>m.</i> (possessing eight forms) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टरत्न
अष्टन्-रत्न <i>n.</i> the eight jewels taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टरस
अष्टन्-रस <i>m.</i> the eight sentiments in poetry viz., शृंगारवीरकरुणाद्भुतहास्य भ्यानकाः । बीभत्सरौद्रौ च रसाः Am.; (according to some authorities, शान्त also is a rasa. निर्वेदस्थायिभावोऽस्ति शांतोऽपि नवमो रसः K.Pr.iv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टरसाश्रय
