अष्टापद्
अष्टापद् <i>m.^1</i> 1. a spider; 2. a fabulous animal called śarabha; 3. a pin or bolt; 4. the mountain Kailāsa.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251217. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: remove homonym.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापद|अष्टापदं|अष्टापदः
अष्टापद^1 <i>m.n.</i> 1. a kind of chequered cloth for dice; 2. gold, आवर्जिताष्टापद कुंभतोयैः K.S.vii.10.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251217. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=083-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

