अह्
अह् <i>(I) vt. 1Ā (pp. अंहित)</i> To go, आंहिषतां रघुव्याघ्रो शरभंगाश्रमं तत Bt.iv.4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
अह् <i>(II) vi. 10U (pp. अंहित)</i> To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह <i>ind.</i> A particle implying- (1) commendation; (2) rejecting; (3) deviation from custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयु|अहंयुः
अहंयु <i>a.</i> Proud, haughty, अहंयुनाथ क्षितिपः शुभंयूरूचे वचः Bt.i.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहत|अहतं
अहत <i>n.</i> A new garment. (ईषद्धौतं नवं श्वेतं सदशं यन्न धारितम् । अहतं तद्विजानीयात्पावनं सर्वकर्मसु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अहन् <i>n. (nom. अहः, -हनी or -ह्नी, -हानि)</i> 1. Day-time, सव्यापारामहनि न तथा पीडयेन्मद्वियोगः Megh.ii.25; 2. a day, i.e. day and night together, (as in अघाहेषु निवृत्तेषु). (As the last member of a compound, अहन् generally appears in the form of अह m. or n. and sometimes अह्न m. As the first member of a compound, अहस् and अहर् are the usual forms).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्कर|अहस्करः
अहस्कर <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरागम|अहरागमः
अहरागम <i>m.</i> the approach of day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्गण|अहर्गणः
अहर्गण <i>m.</i> 1. a series of sacrificial days; 2. a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्दिवम्
अहर्दिवम् <i>ind.</i> day by day, daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्निश|अहर्निशं
अहर्निश <i>n.</i> day and night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःपति|अहःपतिः
अहःपति <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्पति|अहर्पतिः
अहःपति <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्पति|अहस्पतिः
अहःपति <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्बान्धव|अहर्बान्धवः|अहर्ब्बान्धवः
अहःपति <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मणि|अहर्मणिः|अहर्म्मणिः
अहःपति <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मुख|अहर्मुखं
अहर्मुख <i>n.</i> commencement of the day, morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःशेष|अहःशेषः
अहःशेष <i>n.</i> evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्र|अहोरात्रः
अहोरात्र <i>n.</i> day and night, M.i.64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्
अहम् (nom. sing. of the first personal pronoun.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमग्रिका
अहम्-अग्रिका <i>f.</i> a contest for superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमहमिका
अहम्-अहमिका <i>f.</i> 1. assertion of superiority, egotism; 2. military vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंकार|अहङ्कार|अहङ्कारः
अहम्-कार <i>m.</i> 1. self-love considered as spiritual ignorance (in Vedānta phil.), Bg.ii.71, vii.4; 2. egotism, pride, haughtiness; 3. one of the 25 elements of creation (in Sāṅkhya phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंकृति|अहङ्कृति|अहङ्कृतिः
अहम्-कृति <i>f.</i> 1. self-love considered as spiritual ignorance (in Vedānta phil.), Bg.ii.71, vii.4; 2. egotism, pride, haughtiness; 3. one of the 25 elements of creation (in Sāṅkhya phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंपूर्विका|अहम्पूर्विका|अहम्पूर्व्विका
अहम्-पूर्विका, -प्रथमिका <i>f.</i> 1. the running forward of soldiers with emulation, जवादहंपुर्विका यियासुभिः Kir.xiv.82; 2. vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंप्रथमिका|अहम्प्रथमिका
अहम्-पूर्विका, -प्रथमिका <i>f.</i> 1. the running forward of soldiers with emulation, जवादहंपुर्विका यियासुभिः Kir.xiv.82; 2. vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंभद्र|अहम्भद्र
अहम्-भद्र <i>n.</i> self-conceit, a high notion of one’s superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंभाव|अहम्भाव|अहम्भावः
अहम्-भाव <i>m.</i> 1. self love considered as ignorance (in Vedānta phil.); 2. self-conceit, egotism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=089-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंमति|अहम्मति|अहम्मतिः
