आतिरेक्य <i>n.</i> Abundance, excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिशय्य|आतिशय्यं
आतिशय्य <i>n.</i> Abundance, excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतु|आतुः
आतु <i>m.</i> A raft, a float.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुर|आतुरः
आतुर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Hurt, injured; 2. influenced by, रावणावरजा तत्र राघवं मदनातुरा R.xii.32; 3. sick in body or mind, e.g. प्रपिषन्निदं जयति कुष्ठमातुरः, आकाशेशास्तु विज्ञेया बालवृद्धकृशातुराः; 4. feeble, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुरा
आतुर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Hurt, injured; 2. influenced by, रावणावरजा तत्र राघवं मदनातुरा R.xii.32; 3. sick in body or mind, e.g. प्रपिषन्निदं जयति कुष्ठमातुरः, आकाशेशास्तु विज्ञेया बालवृद्धकृशातुराः; 4. feeble, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुरशाला
आतुर-शाला <i>f.</i> hospital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोद्य|आतोद्यं
आतोद्य <i>n.</i> A musical instrument, आतोद्यविन्यासादिका विधयः Ve.i., स्रजमातोद्यशिरोनिवेशिताम् R.viii.34, xv.88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्त
आत्त <i>a. (f. त्ता)</i> 1. Taken, accepted; 2. attracted; 3. extracted, गामात्तसारां रघुरप्यवेक्ष्य R.v.26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ता
आत्त <i>a. (f. त्ता)</i> 1. Taken, accepted; 2. attracted; 3. extracted, गामात्तसारां रघुरप्यवेक्ष्य R.v.26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्तगन्ध|आत्तगन्धः
आत्त-गन्ध <i>a.</i> 1. one whose pride is humbled, one who is defeated; 2. (a flower) already smelt; नात्तगन्धमवधूय शत्रुभिः Sis.xiv.84 (where आत्त is used in both the senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्तगर्व|आत्तगर्व्व|आत्तगर्व्वः
