आत्तमनस्क
आत्त-मनस्क <i>a.</i> one whose mind is transported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्
आत्मन् <i>m.</i> 1. A soul, आत्मानं रथिनं विद्धि शरीरं रथमेव तु Katho.; 2. Brahman (n.) i.e. the supreme spirit, e.g. तस्माद्वा एतस्तमादात्मन आकाशः सम्भूतः; 3. spirit, vitality, courage; 4. the body, स्थितः सर्वोन्नतेनोर्वीं क्रान्त्वा मेरुरिवात्मना R.i.14, or भर्तृषूपसखि निक्षिपतीनामात्मनो मधुमदोद्यामितानाम् Kir.ix.66; 5. natural disposition; 6. understanding, तमात्मसम्पन्नमनिन्दितात्मा R.xviii.18 (where आत्मन् is used in senses 5 and 6); 7. the mind, आत्मानमात्मना वेत्सि K.S.ii.10; 8. the faculty of reason; 9. the sun; 10. the fire; 11. wind; 12. a son, e.g. आत्मा वै पुत्रनामासि; 13. the self; (used in this sense as a reflexive pronoun and in the singular number and masculine gender, even when it refers to two or more things, or to nouns in different genders, e.g. पुण्य श्रमदर्शनेन तावदात्मानं पुनीमहे Sak.i., गुप्तं ददृशुरात्मानं सर्वाः स्वप्नेषु वामनैः R.x.60, आत्मानं गोपायंति कुलस्त्रियः Bh. where आत्मानम् refers to a feminine noun in the plural), आत्मानं सततं रक्षेद्वारैरपि धनैरपि Hit.i.; 14. effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माधीन|आत्माधीनः
आत्मन्-अधीन <i>(I) a.</i> independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माधीन|आत्माधीनः
आत्मन्-अधीन <i>(II) m.</i> 1. a wife’s brother; 2. a son; 3. jester (in dramatic literature).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मापहार|आत्मापहारः
आत्मन्-अपहार <i>m.</i> concealing one’s self, कथं वा आत्मापहारं करोमि Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माशिन्
आत्मन्-अशिन् <i>m.</i> a fish (known to feed on the weak of its species; the Rāmāyaṇa says- मत्स्या इव जना नित्यं भक्षयन्ति परस्परम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माराम
आत्मन्-आराम <i>a.</i> finding pleasure in self, seeking spiritual knowledge, आत्मारामा विहितरतयो निर्विकल्पे समाधौ Ve.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माश्रय|आत्माश्रयः
आत्मन्-आश्रय <i>m.</i> self-dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मेश्वर
आत्मन्-ईश्वर <i>a.</i> self-possessed, आत्मेश्वराणां न हि जातु विघ्नाः समाधिभेदप्रभवो भवन्ति K.S.iii.40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोद्भव|आत्मोद्भवः
आत्मन्-उद्भव <i>m.</i> 1. a son; 2. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपजीविन्
आत्मन्-उपजीविन् <i>a.</i> 1. one who lives by his own labour; 2. one who lives by his wife; 3. a public performer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकाम
आत्मन्-काम <i>a.</i> 1. loving one’s self, possessed of self-conceit; 2. loving the supreme spirit only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगतम्
आत्मन्-गतम् <i>ind.</i> aside (used as a stage-direction in theatrical language in the sense of the English “aside”; स्वगतम् also is used in the same sense- अश्राव्यं खलु यद्वस्तु तदिह स्वगतं मतम् S.D.vi.), राजा (आत्मगतम्) अहो धिक् पौरा अस्मदन्वेषिणस्तपोवनमुपरुन्धन्ति Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगुप्ति|आत्मगुप्तिः
आत्मन्-गुप्ति <i>f.</i> a cave, the hiding place of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मग्राहिन्
आत्मन्-ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i> selfish, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघात|आत्मघातः
आत्मन्-घात <i>m.</i> 1. suicide; 2. heresy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघातिन्
आत्मन्-घातिन् <i>m.</i> 1. a suicide (व्यापादयेद् वृथात्मानं स्वयं योऽग्न्युदकादिभिः । अवैधेनैव मार्गेण आत्मघाती स उच्यते); 2. a heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघोष|आत्मघोषः
आत्मन्-घोष <i>m.</i> 1. crow; 2. a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज|आत्मजः
आत्मन्-ज <i>m.</i> 1. a son; 2. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजा
आत्मन्-जा <i>f.</i> 1. a daughter, वन्द्यं युगं चरणयोर्जनकात्मज्याः R.xiii.78; 2. the understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजन्मन्
आत्मन्-जन्मन् <i>m.</i> a son, तस्यामात्मानुरूपायामात्मजन्मसमुत्सुकः R.i.33, तमात्मजन्मानमजं चकारः v.36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजय|आत्मजयः
आत्मन्-जय <i>m.</i> self-denial, victory over one’s self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञ|आत्मज्ञः
आत्मन्-ज्ञ <i>m.</i> a sage, one who knows self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञान
आत्मन्-ज्ञान <i>n.</i> 1. knowledge of the soul or supreme spirit; 2. true wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतत्व
आत्मन्-तत्व <i>n.</i> the true nature of the soul or of the supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=097-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मत्याग|आत्मत्यागः
