आथर्वण <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> Relating to the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वण|आथर्वणः|आथर्व्वण|आथर्व्वणं|आथर्व्वणः
आथर्वण <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A Brāhmaṇa who has studied the Atharvaveda; 2. the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्वणिक|आथर्वणिकः|आथर्व्वणिक
आथर्वणिक <i>m.</i> A Brāhmaṇa who has studied the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदंश|आदंशः
आदंश <i>m.</i> 1. A bite; 2. a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर|आदरः
आदर <i>m.</i> 1. Respect, regard, reverence, अमर्षशुन्येन जनस्य जन्तुना न जातहार्देन न विद्विशादरः Kir.i.33, भूयान् दारार्थमादरः K.S.vi.13, 20; 2. commencement; 3. care, close application, K.S.vi.91; 4. love; 5. effort, अपौरादरानिर्मिता K.S.vi.41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरण|आदरणं
आदरण <i>n.</i> Respect, notice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्श|आदर्शः
आदर्श <i>m.</i> 1. A looking-glass, a mirror, आत्मानमालोक्य च शोभमानमादर्शबिम्बे K.S.v.22, R.xvii.27; (used metaphorically also, e.g. आदर्शो गुणानाम् Kad.); 2. copy of a work; 3. a commentary, gloss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शक|आदर्शकः
आदर्शक <i>m.</i> A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शन|आदर्शनं
आदर्शन <i>n.</i> 1. Showing; 2. a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदहन|आदहनं
आदहन <i>n.</i> 1. Burning; 2. injuring, killing; 3. a cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदान|आदानं
आदान <i>n.</i> 1. Taking, receiving, कुशांकुरादानपरिक्षतांगुली K.S.v.11; 2. acceptance; 3. earning, getting, आदानं हि विसर्गाय सतां वारिमुचामिव R.iv.86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदि|आदिः
आदि <i>(I) a.</i> 1. First, primary, eg. निदानं त्वादिकारणम् Am.i.4.28; 2. principal, preeminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदि|आदिः
आदि <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Commencement, beginning, अप एव ससर्जादौ तासु बीजमवासृजत् M.i.8, Bg.iii.41; 2. first in time, existing before; 3. preeminent, prime, जगदादिरनादिस्त्वम् K.S.ii.9, Bg.ix.13.(आदि is used as the last member of compounds in the sense of “such like,” “and others,” “and others of the same nature,” e.g. भावदो धातवः Pan. ‘भू and others of the same nature are called roots.’ Pāṇini uses आदि at the end of words to indicate grammatical groups (गण), e.g. तुदादि, रुधादि, चुरादि &c. आदौ and आदितः are used as indeclinables in the sense of ‘in the beginning,’ ‘at first.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्त
आदि-अन्त <i>n.</i> beginning and end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्युदात्त
आदि-उदात्त <i>a.</i> having the acute accent on the first syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर|आदिकरः
आदि-कर, -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> the creator, an epithet of Brahman (m.), Bg.xi.37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर्तृ|आदिकर्त्तृ
आदि-कर, -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> the creator, an epithet of Brahman (m.), Bg.xi.37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकवि|आदिकविः
आदि-कवि <i>m.</i> the first poet. (Brahman (m.) and Vālmīki are so called; the first because he promulgated the Vedas and the second because he is supposed to have unwittingly uttered a verse in cursing a fowler and subsequently to have composed the first poem in Sanskrit, the Rāmāyaṇa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकारण|आदिकारणं
आदि-कारण <i>n.</i> a primary cause, निदानं त्वादिकारणम् Am.i.14.28; (according to the Vedāntists, Brahman (n.) is the primary cause of the universe; according to the Sāṅkhyas it is प्रधान or प्रकृति; according to the Naiyāyikas and Vaiśeṣikas atoms are the material cause of the universe and not ईश्वर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकाव्य
आदि-काव्य <i>n.</i> the first poem; (the Rāmāyaṇa is supposed to be the first poem in Sanskrit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदेव|आदिदेवः
आदि-देव <i>m.</i> 1. the supreme God, the creator of the universe, पुरुषं शाश्वतं दिव्यमादिदेवमजं विभुम् Bg.x.12, त्वमादिदेवः पुरुषः पुराणः xi.88; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu; 3. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदैत्य|आदिदैत्यः
आदि-दैत्य <i>m.</i> an epithet of Hiraṇyakaśipu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपुरुष|आदिपुरुषः
आदि-पुरुष, -पूरुष <i>m.</i> 1. the supreme deity, the lord of the creation; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu and Kṛṣṇa, ते च प्राहुरुदन्वन्तं बुबुधे चादिपूरुषः R.x.6, तमर्घ्यमर्घादिकयादिपूरुषः Sis.i.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपूरुष|आदिपूरुषः
आदि-पुरुष, -पूरुष <i>m.</i> 1. the supreme deity, the lord of the creation; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu and Kṛṣṇa, ते च प्राहुरुदन्वन्तं बुबुधे चादिपूरुषः R.x.6, तमर्घ्यमर्घादिकयादिपूरुषः Sis.i.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिबल
आदि-बल <i>n.</i> generative power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभव|आदिभवः
आदि-भव <i>m.</i> 1. Brahman (n.), the primeval being; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu, रसातलादादादिभवेन पुंसा R.xii.8; 3. an elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिमूल
आदि-मूल <i>n.</i> primitive foundation, primeval cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवराह|आदिवराहः
आदि-वराह <i>m.</i> Viṣṇu in his third or boar incarnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिसर्ग|आदिसर्गः
आदि-सर्ग <i>m.</i> the first creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=099-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितेय|आदितेयः
आदितेय <i>m.</i> A son of Aditi, a god, a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्य|आदित्यः
आदित्य <i>m.</i> 1. A son of Aditi, a god, a divinity; 2. the sun; 3. a name of Viṣṇu in his fifth or Vāmana incarnation; 4. a collective name of 12 divinities, आदित्यानामहं विष्णुः Bg.x.21; (these twelve suns shine only at the end of the world. Cf. Ve.iii.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यसूनु|आदित्यसूनुः
आदित्य-सूनु <i>m.</i> (son of the sun) a name (1) of Sugrīva, the monkey king; (2) of Yama; (3) of Saturn; (4) of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिम|आदिमं
आदिम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> First, prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिमा
आदिम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> First, prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीनव|आदीनवं|आदीनवः
आदीनव <i>m.</i> 1. Distress; 2. fault. See Sis.ii.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपन|आदीपनं
आदीपन <i>n.</i> 1. Setting on fire; 2. whitening the walls &c. on festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत|आदृतः
आदृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Honoured, respected; 2. respectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृता
आदृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Honoured, respected; 2. respectful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवन|आदेवनं
आदेवन <i>n.</i> 1. Gambling; 2. a die used in gambling; 3. a board for gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेश|आदेशः
आदेश <i>m.</i> 1. Advice, instruction, precept, आदेशं देशकालज्ञः शिष्यः शासितुरानतः R.i.92; 2. account, information; 3. a command, आदेशो वनवासस्य प्राप्तव्यः स मया किल Ram.; 4. a prediction, राजद्विष्टादेशकृत् Yaj.ii.304; 5. a substitute (in gram.), धातोः स्थान इवादेशं सुग्रीवं संन्यवेशयत् R.xii.58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य <i>(I) a. (f. द्या)</i> 1. First in position, preeminent, आसीन्महीक्षितामाद्यः प्रणवश्चन्दसामिव R.i.11; 2. first in time. (आद्य is often used as the last member of compounds in the same sense as आदि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्या
आद्य <i>(I) a. (f. द्या)</i> 1. First in position, preeminent, आसीन्महीक्षितामाद्यः प्रणवश्चन्दसामिव R.i.11; 2. first in time. (आद्य is often used as the last member of compounds in the same sense as आदि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य <i>(II) n.</i> Grain, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यकवि|आद्यकविः
आद्य-कवि <i>m.</i> the same as आदिकवि q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यबीज
आद्य-बीज <i>n.</i> प्रधान or the inanimate principle which is the material cause of the universe according to the Sāṅkhyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्या
आद्या <i>f.</i> A name of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्योत|आद्योतः
आद्योत <i>m.</i> Light, brilliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यून|आद्यूनः
आद्यून <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Voracious, hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यूना
आद्यून <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Voracious, hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमन|आधमनं
आधमन <i>n.</i> A deposit, pledge (in law), एको ह्यनीशः सर्वत्र दानाधमनविक्रये Kat., योगाधमनविक्रीतम् M.viii.165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमर्ण्य|आधमर्ण्यं
आधमर्ण्य <i>n.</i> The state of being indebted (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षण|आधर्षणं
आधर्षण <i>n.</i> 1. Conviction of crime or error; 2. a refutation; 3. injuring, annoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधान|आधानं
आधान <i>n.</i> 1. Doing, executing, performing, providing, प्रजानां विनयाधानाद्रक्षणाद्भरणादपि R.i.24; 2. infusing, putting in, गुणो विशेषाधानहेतुः सिद्धो वस्तुधर्मः S.D.ii.; 3. creating, engendering, कौतुकाधानहेतोः Megh.i.3, गर्भाधानक्षणपरिचयात् i.9; 4. a pledge, a deposit, Yaj.ii.238; 5. keeping sacred fire, (the same as अग्न्याधान), कुर्यात्पुनराधानमेव च M.v.168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधानिक|आधानिकं|आधानिकः
आधानिक <i>m.</i> A ceremony performed after cohabitation to procure or favour conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार|आधारः
आधार <i>m.</i> 1. Support, stay; 2. aid, patronage; 3. a receptacle, चराचराणां भूतानां कुक्षिराधारतां गतः K.S.vi.67; 4. a reservoir, अपामिवाधारमनुत्तरंगम् K.S.iii.48, तिष्टन्त्याप इवाधारे Panch.i.; 5. a dam or embankment; 6. a basin round the root of a tree, आधारबन्धप्रमुखैः प्रयत्नैः R.v.6; 7. the meaning of the seventh case (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधि|आधिः
आधि <i>m.</i> 1. Mental agony, anxiety, (op. to व्याधि which is bodily pain), आधिव्याधिपराहतो यदि सदा क्षेमं निजं वाञ्छसि Bh.V.iv.11, viii.27, ix.54; 2. a bane, curse, misery, यान्त्वेवं गृहिणीपदं युवतयो वामाः कुलस्याधयः Sak.iv.; 3. a pledge, a pawn, a mortgage (in law), Yaj.ii.28, M.viii.144; 4. residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभोग|आधिभोगः
आधि-भोग <i>m.</i> enjoyment or use of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिस्तेन|आधिस्तेनः
आधि-स्तेन <i>m.</i> one who enjoys a deposit without the owner’s consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकरणिक|आधिकरणिकः
आधिकरणिक <i>m.</i> A judge, Mrich.ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिक्य|आधिक्यं
आधिक्य <i>n.</i> 1. Excess, preponderance; 2. superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिदैविक|आधिदैविकं
आधिदैविक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. Relating to a tutelary deity (as a mantra), M.vi.83; 2. brought on by fate (as pain). (According to Suśruta, pain is either आध्यात्मिक, आधिभौतिक or आधिदैविक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिदैविकी
आधिदैविक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. Relating to a tutelary deity (as a mantra), M.vi.83; 2. brought on by fate (as pain). (According to Suśruta, pain is either आध्यात्मिक, आधिभौतिक or आधिदैविक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिपत्य|आधिपत्यं
आधिपत्य <i>n.</i> 1. Supremacy, power (अवाप्य) सुराणामपि चाधिपत्यम् Bg.ii.8; 2. the duties of a king, पाण्डोः पुरं प्रकुर्रुष्वाधिपत्ये Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभौतिक|आधिभौतिकं
आधिभौतिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. Relating to beings; 2. caused by animals (as pain). See आधिदैविक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=100-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभौतिकी
