आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त <i>(III) n.</i> 1. A quotient (in math.); 2. an equation of a degree (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=103-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तकाम|आप्तकामः
आप्त-काम <i>(I) a.</i> 1. one who has obtained his desire; 2. one who has given up all worldly desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=103-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तकाम|आप्तकामः
आप्त-काम <i>(II) m.</i> the supreme soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=103-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तगर्भा
आप्त-गर्भा <i>f.</i> a woman in pregnancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=103-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवाच्
आप्त-वाच् <i>(I) a.</i> one whose word is credible and authoritative, पराभिसन्धानमधीयते यैर्विद्येति ते सन्ति किलाप्तवाचः Sak.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=103-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवाच्
आप्त-वाच् <i>(II) f.</i> 1. the advice of a friend; 2. authoritative word (Śruti and Smṛti are considered such authoritative evidence), आप्तवागनुमानाभ्यां साध्यं त्वां प्रति का कथा R.x.28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=103-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

