आश्रवा
आश्रव <i>(I) a. (f. वा)</i> Compliant, obedient, भिषजामनाश्रवः R.xix.49, Na.iii.84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=111-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रव|आश्रवं|आश्रवः
आश्रव <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Stream, river; 2. fault, transgression; 3. a promise, an engagement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=111-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रि|आश्रिः
आश्रि <i>f.</i> the edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=111-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित|आश्रितः
आश्रित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Dwelling in, inhabiting; 2. taking one’s station at or on (as in गवाक्षमाश्रितः); 3. practising, observing; 4. having recourse to. (In these senses the word is generally used with the acc.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=111-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रिता
आश्रित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Dwelling in, inhabiting; 2. taking one’s station at or on (as in गवाक्षमाश्रितः); 3. practising, observing; 4. having recourse to. (In these senses the word is generally used with the acc.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=111-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

