आश्वलक्षणिक|आश्वलक्षणिकः
आश्वलक्षणिक <i>m.</i> A farrier, a groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वास|आश्वासः
आश्वास <i>m.</i> 1. Breathing freely; 2. consolation; 3. cessation; 4. assurance of safety or protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासन|आश्वासनं
आश्वासन <i>n.</i> Consoling, cheering up, encouraging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विक|आश्विकः
आश्विक <i>m.</i> A cavalier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विन|आश्विनः
आश्विन <i>m.</i> The name of a month in the Hindu cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनेय|आश्विनेयः
आश्विनेय <i>m.</i> 1. A name of Nakula and Sahadeva, the last two Pāṇḍava princes; 2. the twin physicians of gods (du.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीन|आश्वीनं|आश्वीनः
आश्वीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Made by a horse (as journey &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीना
आश्वीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Made by a horse (as journey &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढ|आषाढः
आषाढ <i>m.</i> 1. Name of a Hindu month, आषाढस्य प्रथमदिवसे Megh.i.2; 2. a staff of the wood of पलाश carried by an ascetic, अथाजिनाषाढधरः प्रगल्भवाक् K.S.v.80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढा
आषाढा <i>f.</i> The 20th (पूर्वाषाढा) and the 21st (उत्तराषाढा) lunar mansions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढभव|आषाढभवः
आषाढ-भव <i>m.</i> the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढी
आषाढी <i>f.</i> The day of full moon in the month आषाढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्टम|आष्टमः
आष्टम <i>m.</i> The eighth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् <i>ind.</i> An interjection implying- (1) recollection; (2) anger, e.g. आः किमेतदिति क्रोधादाभाष्य महिषासुरः, or आः कथमद्यापि राक्षसत्रासः Ut.i.; (3) angry contradiction, e.g. आः क एष मयि जीवति Mud.i., आः दुरात्मन् वृथामंगलपाठक Ve.i.; (4) pain, e.g. आः शीतम्; (5) sorrow, e.g. विद्यामातरमाः प्रदर्श्य नृपशून् भिक्षामहे निस्त्रपाः Ud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् <i>vi. 2Ā (pp. आसित)</i> 1. To sit down, आस्यतामिति चोक्तः सन्नासीताभिमुखं गुरोः M.ii.193; 2. to live, to dwell, to inhabit, to make one’s abode in, तावद्वर्षाण्यासते देवलोके Bh. or कुरूनास्ते; 3. to sit quietly, to take no hostile measures, आसीतं त्वामुत्थापयति द्वयम् Sis.ii.57; 4. to be, to continue to be, गर्जमान आस्ते Panch.i., Bg.ii.61; (in this sense the root is sometimes used with a noun in the dative, when the dative denotes ‘result,’ e.g. आस्तां मानसस्तुष्टये सुकृतिनां नीतिर्नवोढेव यः); 5. to be contained in, जगन्ति यस्यां सविकाशमासत Sis.i.23; 6. to let go, to put aside (as in आस्तां तावत्), Am.S.97.With अधि-, to sit down on or in, to occupy; (in this sense it governs the acc. of the thing occupied), अध्यासामासुरुत्तुंगहेमपीठानि यान्यमी Sis.ii.5, R.ii.17, iv.74.With अनु-, 1. to sit down after, अन्वासितमरुन्धत्या R.i.56, अन्वास्यताम् R.ii.24; 2. to serve, to follow.With उद्-, to be indifferent to, to be careless, to be neglectful, विधाय वैरं सामर्षे नरोऽरौ य उदासते Sis.ii.44, Bg.ix.9, K.S.ii.13.With उप-, to wait upon, to be in attendance on, ऋतवस्तमुपासते K.S.ii.36; 2. to pass (as time), e.g. उपास्य रात्रिशेषं शोणकूले Ram.; 3. to undergo, उपासांचक्रिरे द्रष्टुं देवगन्धर्वकिन्नराः Bt.v.107; 4. to undergo, अलं ते पाण्डुपुत्राणां भक्त्या क्लेशमुपासितुम् Bh.; 5. to resort to, लक्षणोपास्यते यस्य कृते S.D.ii.; 6. to perform (as a rite); 7. to practice archery.With पर्युप-, 1. to be in attendance on, to attend respectively, भुजंगाः पर्युपासते K.S.ii.38, R.x.62; 2. to seek the patronage or protection of, अशक्ता एव सर्वत्र नरेन्स्रं पर्युपासते Panch.i.; 3. to surround; 4. to partake of.With सम्-, to sit down, प्रत्युवाच समासीनं वसिष्ठम् Ram. With समुप-, 1. to be in attendance on, to wait upon, समुपास्यत पुत्रभोग्यया R.viii.14; 2. to perform, ते सन्ध्यां समुपासत Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस|आसः
आस <i>m.</i> 1. A seat; 2. a bow, स सासिः सासुसूः सासः Kir.xv.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्त|आसक्तं|आसक्तः
आसक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Intent on, attached strongly to, generally used with loc.); 2. continuous, perpetual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्ता
आसक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Intent on, attached strongly to, generally used with loc.); 2. continuous, perpetual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचित्त
आसक्त-चित्त, -चेतस्, -मनस् <i>a.</i> having the mind fixed on any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचेतस्
आसक्त-चित्त, -चेतस्, -मनस् <i>a.</i> having the mind fixed on any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तमनस्
आसक्त-चित्त, -चेतस्, -मनस् <i>a.</i> having the mind fixed on any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्ति|आसक्तिः
आसक्ति <i>f.</i> Attachment, devotedness, application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंग|आसङ्ग|आसङ्गं|आसङ्गः
आसंग <i>m.</i> 1. Attachment to any object; 2. connection, association, त्यक्त्वा कर्म फलासङ्गम् Bg.iv.20; 3. contact (पंकजं) सशैवलासंगमपि प्रकाशते K.S.v.9; 4. fixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंगिनी|आसङ्गिनी
आसंगिनी <i>f.</i> A whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसञ्जन|आसंजनं
आसञ्जन <i>n.</i> 1. Fixing; 2. getting entangled, वृततिवलयासञ्जनात् Sak.i.; 3. attachment; 4. contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसत्ति|आसत्तिः
आसत्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Intimate union, junction, किमपि किमपि मन्दं मन्दमासत्तियोगात् Ut.i.; 2. profit, acquirement; 3. relation between two or more proximate terms and the sense they convey (in logic) (सन्निधानं तु पदस्यासत्तिरुच्यते Bh.P.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=112-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्
आसन् <i>n.</i> Mouth.(This word has no forms for the first five cases.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन|आसनं|आसनः
आसन <i>n.</i> 1. Sitting; 2. a seat, a stool, प्रयत्नमुक्तासनया गृहागतः R.iii.11, or स्वहस्तदत्ते मुनिमासने मुनिः Sis.i.14; 8. any peculiar mode of sitting; 4. any peculiar mode of sexual enjoyment; 5. maintaining a post against an enemy (one of the six modes of foreign policy which are- संधिर्ना विग्रहो यानमासनं द्वैधमाश्रयः); 6. the front part of an elephant’s body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनबन्ध
आसन-बन्ध <i>m.</i> sitting down, निषेदुषीमासनबंधधीरः R.ii.6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसना
आसना <i>f.</i> Seat, a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनी
आसनी <i>f.</i> 1. Small seat; 2. a shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्दी
आसन्दी <i>f.</i> A small couch or oblong chair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्न|आसन्नः
आसन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> 1. Near, proximate; 2. imminent, आसन्नपतने कूले S.Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्ना
आसन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> 1. Near, proximate; 2. imminent, आसन्नपतने कूले S.Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नकाल|आसन्नकालः
आसन्न-काल <i>m.</i> hour of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसम्बाध
आसम्बाध <i>a. (f. धा)</i> Blocked up, confined, आसम्बाधा भविष्यन्ति पन्थानः शरवृष्टिभिः Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसम्बाधा
आसम्बाध <i>a. (f. धा)</i> Blocked up, confined, आसम्बाधा भविष्यन्ति पन्थानः शरवृष्टिभिः Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
आसव <i>m.</i> 1. Distillation, decoction; 2. spirituous liquor, अनासवाख्यं करणं मदस्य K.S.i.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादन|आसादनं
आसादन <i>n.</i> 1. Attacking, making war upon; 2. attaining, accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसार|आसारः
आसार <i>m.</i> 1. A hard shower, आसारसिक्तक्षितिबाष्पयोगात् R.xiii.29, Megh.i.17, 43; 2. surrounding an enemy; 3. the army of an ally; 4. provision, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक|आसिकः
आसिक <i>m.</i> A swordsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिधार|आसिधारं
आसिधार <i>n.</i> A particular vow variously explained; according to some, it consists in standing on the edge of a sword; according to others, in being constantly near a youthful girl and resisting the temptation of sexual enjoyment; (the Yādava explains it thus- युवा युवत्या सार्धं यन्मुग्धभर्तृवदाचरेत् । अन्तर्निवृत्तसंगः स्यादासिधारं व्रतं हि तत्), अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारम् R.xiii.67.Figuratively the word is used in the sense of “a difficult task or undertaking.” Thus Bhartr. says- सतां केनोद्दिष्टं विषममसिधाराव्रतमिदम्. (Cf. असिधाराव्रत.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुर|आसुरं|आसुरः
आसुर <i>(I) a. (f. री) (op. to दैव)</i> 1. belonging or relating to evil spirits (as in आसुरी माया, or आसुरी रात्रिः); 2. infernal, demoniacal, आसुरं भावमाश्रिताः Bg.vii.15, xvi.6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरी
आसुर <i>(I) a. (f. री) (op. to दैव)</i> 1. belonging or relating to evil spirits (as in आसुरी माया, or आसुरी रात्रिः); 2. infernal, demoniacal, आसुरं भावमाश्रिताः Bg.vii.15, xvi.6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुर|आसुरं|आसुरः
आसुर <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A demon; 2. one of the eight forms of marriage; in it the bride-groom purchases the bride from her father; (आसुरो द्रविणादानात् Yaj.i.61, M.iii.31.) (The other seven forms are- ब्राह्म, दैव, आर्ष, प्राजापय, गान्धर्व, राक्षस, पैशाच.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरी
आसुरी <i>f.</i> 1. Surgery; 2. a female demon, सम्भ्रमादासुरीभिः Ve.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसूत्रित
आसूत्रित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Forming or wearing a garland; 2. interwoven, introduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसूत्रिता
आसूत्रित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Forming or wearing a garland; 2. interwoven, introduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेक|आसेकः
आसेक <i>m.</i> Wetting, watering, pouring in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचन|आसेचनः
आसेचन <i>n.</i> The act of pouring into, wetting, sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेध|आसेधः
आसेध <i>m.</i> Arrest, custody, legal restraint (in criminal law); it is of four kinds, viz., “स्थानासेधः कालकृतः प्रवासात् कर्मणस्तथा.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवन|आसेवनं
आसेवन <i>n.</i> 1. Assiduous practice or performance of any action; 2. frequency, repetition, आसेवनं पौनःपुन्यम् S.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवा
आसेवा <i>f.</i> The same as आसेवन q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्द|आस्कंदः|आस्कन्दः
आस्कन्द <i>m.</i> 1. Ascending, mounting; 2. an attack, R.xvii.52; 3. reproach; 4. the walk of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दन|आस्कंदनं|आस्कन्दनं
आस्कन्दन <i>n.</i> The same as आस्कन्द q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दित|आस्कंदितं|आस्कन्दितं
आस्कन्दित <i>n.</i> Galloping with full speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तर|आस्तरः
आस्तर <i>m.</i> 1. A covering; 2. a carpet; 3. a blanket thrown over the back of a horse or elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरण|आस्तरणं
आस्तरण <i>n.</i> 1. The act of spreading; 2. a carpet, तमालपत्रास्तरणास्तु रन्तुम् R.vi.64; 3. a bed; 4. an elephant’s housings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तार|आस्तारः
आस्तार <i>m.</i> Spreading, scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक|आस्तिकः
आस्तिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. One who believes in God and another world; 2. believing, pious, faithful, आस्तिकः श्रद्धधानश्च Yaj.i.268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकी
आस्तिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. One who believes in God and another world; 2. believing, pious, faithful, आस्तिकः श्रद्धधानश्च Yaj.i.268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक्य|आस्तिक्यं
आस्तिक्य <i>n.</i> 1. Belief in the existence of God and another world; 2. piety, faith; (Śankara commenting on Bg.xviii.42 says- आस्तिक्यं श्रद्धधानता परमार्थेष्वागमार्थेषु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था <i>f.</i> 1. Consideration, care, regard, मर्त्येष्वास्थापराङ्मुखः R.x.43; 2. assent, promise; 3. hope; 4. prop, support; 5. effort; 6. state, condition; 7. an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थान|आस्थानं
आस्थान <i>n.</i> 1. A place, a site; 2. an assembly, तदीयमास्थाननिकेतनाजिरम् Kir.i.16; 3. a hall of audience; 4. a recreation-ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थानगृह
आस्थान-गृह न्।, -निकेतन न्।, -मण्डप म्। <i>n.</i> an assembly-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थाननिकेतन
आस्थान-गृह न्।, -निकेतन न्।, -मण्डप म्। <i>n.</i> an assembly-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थानमण्डप|आस्थानमण्डपः
आस्थान-मण्डप <i>m.</i> an assembly-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थानी
आस्थानी <i>f.</i> An assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पद|आस्पदं
आस्पद <i>n.</i> 1. Place, site, स्तनद्वयेऽस्मिन् हरिचन्दनास्पदे K.S.v.69, also 10, 48; 2. rank; 3. dignity, authority; 4. business, affair; 5. prop, support, तदास्पदं श्रीर्युवराजसंज्ञितम् R.iii.36; 6. object, receptacle, as in दोषास्पदम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=113-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पन्दन|आस्पन्दनं
आस्पन्दन <i>n.</i> Trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्धा
आस्पर्धा <i>f.</i> Emulation, rivalry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फाल|आस्फालः
आस्फाल <i>m.</i> 1. Striking, rubbing; 2. flapping; 3. the flapping motion of an elephant’s ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालन|आस्फालनं
आस्फालन <i>n.</i> 1. Rubbing, striking against, stirring, अनवरतधनुर्ज्यास्फालनक्रूरपूर्वम् Sak.ii., or आसां जलास्फालनतत्पराणाम् R.xvi.62, iii.55, vi.73, Am.S.54; 2. arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोट|आस्फोटः
आस्फोट <i>m.</i> 1. The Arka plant; 2. the sound made by striking on the arms; 3. a kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटन|आस्फोटनं
आस्फोटन <i>n.</i> 1. Blowing, expanding; 2. contracting, closing; 3. the sound produced by striking on the arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माक
आस्माक <i>a. (f. की)</i> Ours, our, आस्माकदन्तिसन्निध्यात् Sis.ii.63, viii.50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माकी
आस्माक <i>a. (f. की)</i> Ours, our, आस्माकदन्तिसन्निध्यात् Sis.ii.63, viii.50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माकीन
आस्माकीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> The same as आस्माक q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माकीना
आस्माकीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> The same as आस्माक q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्य|आस्यं
आस्य <i>n.</i> 1. Mouth; 2. face, बाहू द्वौ च मृणालनास्यकमलम् Sr.T.1; 3. opening (as in अंकास्य ‘the opening of an act.’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यासव|आस्यासवः
आस्य-आसव <i>m.</i> spittle, saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यंधय
आस्यंधय <i>a.</i> kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यपत्र|आस्यपत्रं
आस्य-पत्र <i>n.</i> a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलांगल|आस्यलाङ्गल|आस्यलाङ्गलः
आस्य-लांगल <i>m.</i> 1. a dog; 2. a boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलोमन्
आस्य-लोमन् <i>n.</i> beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यन्दन|आस्यंदनं
आस्यन्दन <i>n.</i> Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=114-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

