इष्टम्
इष्टम् <i>ind.</i> To one’s fill or satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टि|इष्टिः
इष्टि <i>f.</i> 1. Sacrificing, sacrifice; 2. wish, desire (in this sense the word is used by Patanjali in his Bhāshya to indicate his desire that any particular form, though not sanctioned by Pāṇini, should be considered as correct; Cf. उपसंख्यान.); 3. any desired object; 4. oblation consisting of butter &c.; 5. impulse, hurry; 6. invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिपच|इष्टिपचः
इष्टि-पच <i>m.</i> a miser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिपशु
इष्टि-पशु <i>m.</i> an animal intended to be killed at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

