इष्टिका <i>f.</i> A brick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्म|इष्मः
इष्म <i>m.</i> The spring season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्य|इष्यं|इष्यः
इष्म <i>m.</i> The spring season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इस्
इस् <i>ind.</i> An interjection- (1) of anger; (2) of pain; (3) of sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इह
इह <i>ind.</i> Here (refering to time, place or direction).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहामुत्र
इह-अमुत्र <i>ind.</i> in this world and in the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहत्य
इह-त्य <i>a.</i> being here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहलोक|इहलोकः
इह-लोक <i>m.</i> this world, this life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहस्थ
इह-स्थ <i>a.</i> standing here, being here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई <i>ind.</i> An interjection- (1) of pain; (2) of sorrow; (3) of anger; (4) of perception; (5) of compassion; (6) of calling &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई <i>(I) vt. or vi. 2P (pp. ईत)</i> 1. To go; 2. to pervade; 3. to desire; 4. to throw; 5. to eat; 6. to become pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई <i>(II) vt. 4Ā (pp. ईत)</i> To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष्
ईक्ष् <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. ईक्षित)</i> 1. To look, to behold; 2. to regard, to consider; 3. to think, e.g. तदैक्षत बहु स्यां प्रजायेय; 4. to care for, न कामवृत्तिर्वचनीयमीक्षते K.S.v.82; 5. to investigate into the good or bad luck of anyone. (In this sense the person whose future is in question is put in the dat. e.g. कृष्णाय ईक्षते गर्गः ‘Garga foretells Kṛṣṇa’s future.’)With अधि-, to suspect, सत्येऽप्यपायमधीक्षते Hit.i.With अनु-, to inquire after, to investigate.With अप-, 1. to expect, किमपेक्ष्य फलम् Kir.ii.21; 2. to require, शब्दोव्यञ्जकत्वेऽर्थान्तरमपेक्षते S.D.; 3. to pay regard to, अपेक्षन्ते न च स्नेहं … उत्तमाः Ud. With अभिवि-, to look towards.With अव-, 1. to look at, to cast a glance at, योस्त्यमानानवेक्षेऽहम् Bg.i.28; 2. to consider, to think, यदवोचदवेक्ष्य मानिनी Kir.ii.2.With उद्-, 1. to look up to, सप्रणाममुदीक्षिताः K.S.vi.7; 2. to wait, त्रीणि वर्षाण्युदीक्षेत कुमार्यृतुमती सती M.ix.90.With उत्प्र-, 1. to see in prospect, e.g. तस्य विघ्नान्युत्प्रेक्षे ‘I see difficulties in his way’; 2. to conjecture, to expect, उत्प्रेक्षामो (the Par. is epic) वयं तावन्मतिमन्तं बिभीषणम् Ram. With उद्वि-, to look up.With उप-, 1. to overlook, to neglect, to look with indifference on, उपेक्षते यः श्लथलम्बिनीर्जटाः K.S.v.47; 2. to let escape, to let go, नोपेक्षेत क्षणमपि राजा साहसिकं नरम् M.viii.344.With निर्-, to view completely, यावदेतान्निरीक्षेहम् Bg.i.22; 2. to look for, निरीक्षते केलिवनं प्रविश्य क्रमेलकः कण्टकजालमेव Vikr.Ch.i.29.With परि-, to examine, to put to test, नैता (scil. स्त्रियः) रूपं परीक्षन्ते M.ix.14, परीक्षितः पुंस्त्वे ‘tested as to potency,’ मायां मयोद्भाव्य परीक्षितोऽसि R.ii.62.With प्र-, to look at, to see, R.x.44, K.S.vi.47.With प्रति-, to wait, संवत्सरं प्रतीक्षेत द्विषन्तीं योषितं पतिः M.ix.77.With प्रतिवि-, to look in return.With वि-, to see, to behold.With व्यप- to mind, to care for, न व्यपैक्षत समुत्सुकाः प्रजाः R.xix.6.With सम्-, 1. to behold; 2. to think, to consider.With समव-, 1. to inspect; 2. to consider.With समुप-, to neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=119-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षण|ईक्षणं
ईक्षण <i>n.</i> 1. A look, a sight; 2. an eye, अभिमुखे मयि संवृतमीक्षणम् Sak.i., R.ii.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिक|ईक्षणिकः
ईक्षणिक <i>m. (fem. का)</i> A fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षति|ईक्षतिः
ईक्षति <i>m.</i> Looking, sight, ईक्षतेर्नाशब्दम् Bh.4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षा
ईक्षा <i>f.</i> 1. Viewing, considering; 2. sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईख्
ईख् <i>vt. or vi. 1P (pp. इंखित)</i> To go, to vacillate.With प्र-, to tremble, प्रैंखच्च क्षुभिता क्षितिः Bt.xvii.108, Am.S.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईज्
ईज् <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. ईजित)</i> 1. To go; 2. to censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् <i>vt. 2Ā (pp. ईडित)</i> To praise, शालीनतामव्रजदीद्यमानः R.xviii.17, Bt.ix.57, xviii.15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडा
ईडा <i>f.</i> Praise, commendation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्य
ईड्य <i>a. (f. ड्या)</i> Praiseworthy, R.v.34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्या
ईड्य <i>a. (f. ड्या)</i> Praiseworthy, R.v.34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईति|ईतिः
ईति <i>f.</i> 1. A calamity of the season; they are six, viz., (1) excessive rain; (2) drought; (3) rats; (4) locusts; (5) parrots; (6) foreign invasions. (अतिवृष्टिरनावृष्टिर्मूषकाः शलभाः शुकाः । प्रत्यासन्नाश्च राजानः षडेता ईतयः स्मृताः), निरातंका निरीतयः R.i.63; 2. an infectious disease; 3. travelling; 4. an affray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ता
ईदृक्ता <i>f.</i> Quality, ईदृक्तया … इयत्तया वा ‘either by quality or by quantity^1’ R.xiii.5).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251217. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ष|ईदृक्षः
ईदृक्ष <i>a. (f. शी)</i> Such, of such a kind, of this aspect, endowed with such qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्शी
ईदृक्ष <i>a. (f. शी)</i> Such, of such a kind, of this aspect, endowed with such qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश्
ईदृश् <i>a.</i> The same as ईदृक्ष q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सा
ईप्सा <i>f.</i> 1. Desire to obtain; 2. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सिता
ईप्सित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित <i>(II) n.</i> Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु <i>a.</i> Desirous to obtain, सौरभ्यमीप्सुरिव ते मुखमारुतस्य R.v.69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्
ईर् <i>(I) vt. 1P (pp. ईरित)</i> To go, to shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्
ईर् <i>(II) vt. 2Ā (pp. ईर्ण)</i> To go, to move.With उद्-, to rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्
ईर् <i>(III) vt. 10U (pp. ईरित)</i> 1. To move; 2. to throw; 3. to pronounce, इतीरयित्वा विरचय्य वाङ्मयम् Na.i.184, Kir.i.26.With उद्-, 1. to utter, to tell, R.ii.9; 2. To put forth, कुसुमं यदन्नोकोऽवमुदीरयिष्यति R.viii.62; 3. to throw up, R.vi.18.With प्र-, to propel, to send, R.iv.24.With सम्-, 1. to move, to shake; 2. to utter.With समुत्-, to utter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरण|ईरणः
ईरण <i>n.</i> 1. Moving; 2. going; 3. See इरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण <i>(I) a. (f. णा)</i> Desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिणा
ईरिण <i>(I) a. (f. णा)</i> Desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण <i>(II) n.</i> Barren soil, आसीदीरिणसन्निभम् Ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म|ईर्मः|ईर्म्म
ईर्म <i>n.</i> A wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्या|ईर्य्या
ईर्या <i>f.</i> Wandering about as a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्वारु|ईर्वारुः|ईर्व्वारु|ईर्व्वारुः
ईर्वारु <i>m.f.</i> A cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य्
ईर्ष्य् <i>vi. 1P (pp. ईर्ष्यित)</i> To envy, to feel impatient at another’s success (this root is used with the dative of the person envied, e.g. हरवे ईर्ष्यति S.K.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यक
ईर्ष्यक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यका
ईर्ष्यक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्या
ईर्ष्या(र्षा) <i>f.</i> Envy of another’s success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्ष्या(र्षा) <i>f.</i> Envy of another’s success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यालु|ईर्ष्यालुः
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु <i>a.</i> Envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षालु|ईर्षालुः
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु <i>a.</i> Envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलि|ईलिः
ईलि(ली) <i>f.</i> A cudgel. (Also इली.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईली
ईलि(ली) <i>f.</i> A cudgel. (Also इली.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्
ईश् <i>vt. 2Ā (pp. ईशित)</i> 1. To command, to rule; 2. to own, to possess (generally used with the gen., e.g. अर्थानामीशिषे त्वं वयमपि च गिरामीश्महे Bhartr.iii.30); 3. to be powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश <i>(I) a. (f. शा)</i> Powerful, supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशा
ईश <i>(I) a. (f. शा)</i> Powerful, supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A lord, a master, K.S.ii.3; 2. an epithet of Śiva; 3. the number ‘eleven.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशपुरी
ईश-पुरी <i>f.</i> Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशसख|ईशसखः
ईश-सख <i>m.</i> a name of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशसखि
ईश-सखि <i>(nom. sing. सखा)</i> See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशा
ईशा <i>f.</i> 1. An epithet of Durgā; 2. a wealthy lady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशान|ईशानं|ईशानः
ईशान <i>m.</i> 1. A ruler, e.g. ईशानः सर्वभूतानाम्; 2. an epithet of Śiva; 3. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशानी
ईशानी <i>f.</i> An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिता
ईशिता <i>f.</i> Supremacy, considered as one of the eight siddhis or attributes of divinity; the eight siddhis are- अणिमा महिमा चैव गरिमा लघिमा तथा । प्राप्तिः प्राकाम्यमीशित्वं वशित्वं चाष्ट सिद्धयः ॥. See अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशित्व|ईशित्वं
ईशित्व <i>n.</i> Supremacy, considered as one of the eight siddhis or attributes of divinity; the eight siddhis are- अणिमा महिमा चैव गरिमा लघिमा तथा । प्राप्तिः प्राकाम्यमीशित्वं वशित्वं चाष्ट सिद्धयः ॥. See अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=120-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशी
ईशी <i>f.</i> Durgā, Śiva’s wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वर|ईश्वरं|ईश्वरः
ईश्वर <i>(I) a. (f. रा or री)</i> 1. Able, powerful; 2. wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरा
ईश्वर <i>(I) a. (f. रा or री)</i> 1. Able, powerful; 2. wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरी
ईश्वर <i>(I) a. (f. रा or री)</i> 1. Able, powerful; 2. wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वर|ईश्वरं|ईश्वरः
ईश्वर <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A husband; 2. the supreme spirit; 3. a wealthy man; 4. master, lord; 5. an epithet of Śiva; 6. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरनिषेध|ईश्वरनिषेधः
ईश्वर-निषेध <i>m.</i> atheism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरसद्मन्
ईश्वर-सद्मन् <i>n.</i> a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरसभ
ईश्वर-सभ <i>n.</i> a royal assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरा
ईश्वरा(री) <i>f.</i> An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरी
ईश्वरा(री) <i>f.</i> An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्
ईष् <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. ईषित)</i> 1. To go, to move; 2. to kill; 3. to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष|ईषः
ईष <i>m.</i> The month Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्
ईषत् <i>ind.</i> Little, a little, slightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्कर|ईषत्करः
ईषत्-कर <i>a.</i> what is easily attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पाण्डु|ईषत्पाण्डुः
ईषत्-पाण्डु <i>a.</i> whitish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पुरुष|ईषत्पुरुषः
ईषत्-पुरुष <i>m.</i> a mean man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्प्रलम्भ
ईषत्-प्रलम्भ <i>a.</i> to be gained for little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्धास|ईषद्धासः
ईषत्-हास <i>m.</i> a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषा
ईषा <i>f.</i> The pole of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिका
ईषि(षी)का <i>f.</i> 1. A painter’s brush; 2. an elephant’s eye ball; 3. an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषीका
ईषि(षी)का <i>f.</i> 1. A painter’s brush; 2. an elephant’s eye ball; 3. an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिर|ईषिरः
ईषिर <i>m.</i> Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्म|ईष्मः
ईष्म <i>m.</i> 1. Kāmadeva; 2. spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईह्
ईह् <i>vi. 1Ā (pp. ईहित)</i> 1. To aim at, to attempt; 2. to desire, शक्तस्यानीहमानस्य किञ्चिद्दत्वा पृथक्क्रिया Yaj.ii.116.With सम्-, 1. to desire; 2. to attempt to perform, प्रियाणि वांछन्त्यसभिः समीहितुम् Kir.i.19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहा
ईहा <i>f.</i> 1. Effort, exertion; 2. desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहामृग|ईहामृगः
ईहा-मृग <i>m.</i> 1. a wolf; 2. a kind of drama consisting of four acts, S.D.vi. Cf. अंक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहावृक|ईहावृकः
ईहा-वृक <i>m.</i> a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ <i>(I) ind.</i> An interjection- (1) of calling, e.g. उ मेति मात्रा तपसो निषिद्धा K.S.i.26; (2) of anger; (3) of compassion; (4) of command; (5) of acceptance; (6) of interrogation; (7) an expletive. In classics it is generally used after अथ, न and किम् with a slight modification of the sense and often only as an expletive, e.g. येन भूतान्यशेषेण द्रक्ष्यस्यात्मन्यथो मयि Bg.iv.35, नो चेत् कथं निपतनादनयोस्तदैव Bh.V.ii.92, सर्वाण्यंगानि मे यांति श्रोत्रतां किमु नेत्रताम् Am.S.63, किमु तत्र चतिष्टयम् Hit.i. (किमु here means ‘how much more’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ <i>(II) m.</i> Śiva; this word forms the second part of the mystic Syllable ओम्. See under अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त|उक्तं|उक्तः
उक्त <i>(I) a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Addressed (as a person, e.g. अनुक्तेनापि वक्तव्यं सुहृदा हितमिच्छता; 2. said, spoken; 3. said (as op. to inferred), e.g. उक्तानि प्रतिषिद्धानि पुनः संभावितानि च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ता
उक्त <i>(I) a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Addressed (as a person, e.g. अनुक्तेनापि वक्तव्यं सुहृदा हितमिच्छता; 2. said, spoken; 3. said (as op. to inferred), e.g. उक्तानि प्रतिषिद्धानि पुनः संभावितानि च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त|उक्तं|उक्तः
उक्त <i>(II) n.</i> A word, a sentence, a speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तानुक्त
उक्त-अनुक्त <i>a.</i> spoken and not spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तोपसंहार|उक्तोपसंहारः
उक्त-उपसंहार <i>m.</i> a peroration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तनिर्वाह|उक्तनिर्वाहः
उक्त-निर्वाह <i>m.</i> maintaining an assertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तपुंस्क|उक्तपुंस्कः
उक्त-पुंस्क <i>a.</i> a feminine or neuter word of which also a masculine exists and whose meaning only differs from that of the masculine by the notion of gender (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तप्रत्युक्त
उक्त-प्रत्युक्त <i>n.</i> speech and reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ति|उक्तिः
उक्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Speech, expression, M.viii.104; 2. the expressive power of a word, एकयोक्त्या पुष्पवंतौ दिवाकरनिशाकरौ Am.i.4.10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तिप्रत्युक्ति
उक्ति-प्रत्युक्ति <i>f.</i> speech and reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ|उक्थं|उक्थः
उक्थ <i>n.</i> 1. A saying, a sentence; 2. a eulogy; 3. a name of the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष्
उक्ष् <i>vt. 1P (pp. उक्षित)</i> To sprinkle, to wet, उक्षांप्रचक्रुर्नगरस्य मार्गान् Bt.iii.5, xvii.9, R.xi.5, 20.With अभि-, to sprinkle with consecrated water, शिरसि शकुंतलामभ्युक्ष्य Sak.iv.With परि-, to sprinkle around.With प्र-, to consecrate by sprinkling, प्रोक्षितं भक्षयेन्मांसम् M.v.27.With संप्र-, to hallow by sprinkling, Yaj.i.24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण|उक्षणं
उक्षण <i>n.</i> 1. Sprinkling; 2. consecration by sprinkling, वसिष्ठमंत्रोक्षणजात् प्रभावात् R.v.27, K.S.vii.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षन्
उक्षन् <i>m.</i> An ox or bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षतर|उक्षतरः
उक्षन्-तर <i>m.</i> a small bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्
उख् <i>vt. 1P (pp. ओखित or उंखित; pres. ओखति or उंखति)</i> To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखा
उखा <i>f.</i> A cooking pan or pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्य|उख्यं|उख्यः
उख्य <i>a. (f. ख्या)</i> Boiled in a pot, e.g. शून्यमुख्यं च होमवान्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्या
उख्य <i>a. (f. ख्या)</i> Boiled in a pot, e.g. शून्यमुख्यं च होमवान्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्र|उग्रं|उग्रः
उग्र <i>(I) a. (f. उग्रा; compar. उग्रतर or ओजीयस्; super. उग्रतम or ओजिष्ठ)</i> 1. Powerful; 1. mighty; 2. formidable, terrible, प्रथमविरहादुग्रंशोकाम् Megh.ii.50, सिंहनिपातमुग्रम् R.ii.60, उग्रातपा वेला Sak.iii., Bg.xi.30, M.vi.75; 3. noble; 4. ferocious; 5. pungent, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रा
उग्र <i>(I) a. (f. उग्रा; compar. उग्रतर or ओजीयस्; super. उग्रतम or ओजिष्ठ)</i> 1. Powerful; 1. mighty; 2. formidable, terrible, प्रथमविरहादुग्रंशोकाम् Megh.ii.50, सिंहनिपातमुग्रम् R.ii.60, उग्रातपा वेला Sak.iii., Bg.xi.30, M.vi.75; 3. noble; 4. ferocious; 5. pungent, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्र|उग्रं|उग्रः
उग्र <i>(II) m.</i> 1. An epithet of Rudra; 2. the poetic sentiment called रौद्र; 3. one born of a Kṣatriya father and a Śūdra mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=121-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रगंध|उग्रगन्ध|उग्रगन्धं|उग्रगन्धः
