उत्तंस|उत्तंसः
उत्तंस <i>m.n.</i> 1. An ear-ring, Bh.V.ii.55; 2. a crest, an ornament worn on the crown of the head. (Note. When preceded by the word कर्ण, उत्तंस loses part of its original meaning and expresses merely ‘an ornament’ according to some. According to Mammata, the word कर्ण expresses in such cases कर्ण स्थितत्व, this, however, being merely a device to explain away the usage of standard authors, कर्णावतंसादिपदे कर्णादिध्वनिनिर्मितिः । संनिधानादिबोधार्थं स्थितेष्वेतत्समर्थनम् K.Pr.vii.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=125-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

