उदर्क|उदर्कः
उदर्क <i>m.</i> 1. The future result of an action, consequence. नत्वयमुदर्कः प्राक्तनस्य दुष्कृतस्य D.K., M.iv.76, xi.10; 2. future time, futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्चिस्|उदर्च्चिस्
उदर्चिस् <i>(I) a.</i> Shining or blazing upwards, R.vii.24, xv.76, K.S.iii.71, vii.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्चिस्|उदर्च्चिस्
उदर्चिस् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Fire, प्रक्षिप्योदर्चिषं कक्षे शेरते तेऽभिमारुतम् Sis.ii.42; 2. god of love; 3. Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदश्रु
उदश्रु <i>a.</i> One whose tears gush up, weeping, R.xii.14, Am.S.11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदसन|उदसनं
उदसन <i>n.</i> Throwing up, raising, erecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त|उदात्तं|उदात्तः
उदात्त <i>(I) a. (f. त्ता)</i> 1. Elevated, high; 2. great, illustrious; 3. generous, bountiful; 4. dear, beloved; 5. highly or acutely accented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्ता
उदात्त <i>(I) a. (f. त्ता)</i> 1. Elevated, high; 2. great, illustrious; 3. generous, bountiful; 4. dear, beloved; 5. highly or acutely accented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त|उदात्तं|उदात्तः
उदात्त <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The acute accent (ताल्वादिषु सभागेषु स्थानेषूर्ध्वभागे निष्पन्नोऽनुदात्तः S.K.), निहंत्यरीनेकपदे य उदात्तः स्वरानिव Sis.ii.95; 2. a gift, donation; 3. a kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त|उदात्तं|उदात्तः
उदात्त <i>(III) n.</i> A figure of speech thus defined- उदात्तं वस्तुनः संपन्महतां चोपलक्षणम् K.Pr.x. (for an example, See Megh.ii.12-16.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदान|उदानः
उदान <i>m.</i> 1. Breathing upwards; 2. one of the five vital airs (the other four being प्राण, अपान, व्यान and समान); it goes up and out at the throat; 3. the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदायुध
उदायुध <i>a. (f. धा)</i> With uplifted weapon, मनुजपशुभिर्निर्भर्यादैर्भवद्धिरुदायुधैः Ve.iii., R.xii.44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदायुधा
उदायुध <i>a. (f. धा)</i> With uplifted weapon, मनुजपशुभिर्निर्भर्यादैर्भवद्धिरुदायुधैः Ve.iii., R.xii.44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदार|उदारः
उदार <i>a. (f. रा or री)</i> 1. High, lofty, illustrious, munificent, R.v.12, viii.61, Bg.vii.1; 2. honest, sincere; 3. eloquent; 4. large, wide, broad, K.S.v.36; 5. beautiful, charming, K.S.vii.14, (the acc. sing. उदारम् is sometimes used adverbially, Sis.iv.33.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारा
उदार <i>a. (f. रा or री)</i> 1. High, lofty, illustrious, munificent, R.v.12, viii.61, Bg.vii.1; 2. honest, sincere; 3. eloquent; 4. large, wide, broad, K.S.v.36; 5. beautiful, charming, K.S.vii.14, (the acc. sing. उदारम् is sometimes used adverbially, Sis.iv.33.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारी
उदार <i>a. (f. रा or री)</i> 1. High, lofty, illustrious, munificent, R.v.12, viii.61, Bg.vii.1; 2. honest, sincere; 3. eloquent; 4. large, wide, broad, K.S.v.36; 5. beautiful, charming, K.S.vii.14, (the acc. sing. उदारम् is sometimes used adverbially, Sis.iv.33.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारचरित
उदार-चरित <i>a.</i> noble-minded, उदारचरितानां तु वसुधैव कुटुंबकम् Hit.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारचेतस्
उदार-चेतस् <i>a.</i> high-minded, magnanimous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारधी
उदार-धी <i>a.</i> 1. highly intelligent, R.iii.30; 2. noble-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारसत्व
उदार-सत्व <i>a.</i> generous-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास|उदासः
उदास <i>(I) a. (f. सा)</i> Indifferent, apathetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासा
उदास <i>(I) a. (f. सा)</i> Indifferent, apathetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास|उदासः
उदास <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A stoic, a philosopher; 2. indifference, apathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीन|उदासीनः
उदासीन <i>(I) a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Indifferent, free from affection, तद्दर्शिनमुदासीनं त्वामेव पुरुषं विदुः K.S.ii.13 (पुरुष is here called उदासीन, because in the Sāṅkhya doctrine souls are not supposed to have any part in the creation of the material universe); 2. not involved in a dispute; 3. neutral (as a king or nation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीना
उदासीन <i>(I) a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Indifferent, free from affection, तद्दर्शिनमुदासीनं त्वामेव पुरुषं विदुः K.S.ii.13 (पुरुष is here called उदासीन, because in the Sāṅkhya doctrine souls are not supposed to have any part in the creation of the material universe); 2. not involved in a dispute; 3. neutral (as a king or nation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीन|उदासीनः
उदासीन <i>(II) n.</i> 1. A stranger; 2. a neutral; 3. common acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्थित|उदास्थितः
उदास्थित <i>m.</i> 1. A superintendent, a door-keeper; 2. spy, an emissary; 3. an ascetic who has given up his vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहरण|उदाहरणं
उदाहरण <i>n.</i> 1. Saying, declaring; 2. opening a discourse or conversation, K.S.vi.65; 3. an example, an illustration, समूलघातमघ्नंतः परान्नोद्यंति मानिनः । प्रध्वंसितांधरमसस्तत्रोदाहरणं रविः Sis.ii.33; 4. an illustration considered as a figure of speech by some authors; it closely resembles अर्थांतरन्यास and is very minutely distinguished from it, See R.G. under उदाहरण; 5. the third member in a five-membered syllogism (in logic); 6. a panegyric beginning with some such word as जयति and full of alliterations (it is thus defined in the Pratāparudra- येन केनापि तालेन गद्यपद्यसमन्वितम् । जयत्युपक्रमं मालिन्यादिप्रासविचित्रितम् । तदुदाहरणं नाम विभक्त्यष्टांगसंयुतम् ॥), e.g. चारणेभ्यस्त्वदीयं जयोदाहरणं श्रुत्वा Vikr.i., जयोदाहरणं बाह्वोर्गापयामास किन्नरान् R.iv.78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहार|उदाहारः
उदाहार <i>m.</i> 1. An example or illustration; 2. the beginning of a speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
उदित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Said, spoken; 2. risen, ascended, Bh.V.ii.85; 3. grown, augmented; 4. born, produced; 5. high, tall, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदिता
उदित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Said, spoken; 2. risen, ascended, Bh.V.ii.85; 3. grown, augmented; 4. born, produced; 5. high, tall, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितोदित|उदितोदितः
उदित-उदित <i>a.</i> well-acquainted with the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=130-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्षण|उदीक्षणं
उदीक्षण <i>n.</i> 1. Looking up; 2. seeing, beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीची
उदीची <i>f.</i> The north, तेनोदीचीं दिशमनुसरेः Megh.i.57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीन|उदीचीनं
उदीचीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Northern; 2. turned towards the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीना
उदीचीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Northern; 2. turned towards the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीच्य <i>(I) a. (f. च्या)</i> Being or living in the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्या
उदीच्य <i>(I) a. (f. च्या)</i> Being or living in the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीच्य <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The country to the north and west of the river Śarāvatī; 2. one who lives in the north, R.iv.66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीच्य <i>(III) n.</i> A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीप|उदीपः
उदीप <i>m.</i> High water, an inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरण|उदीरणं
उदीरण <i>n.</i> 1. Throwing, discharging (as a missile); 2. speaking, saying; 3. uttering, pronouncing, K.S.ii.12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुंबर|उदुम्बर|उदुम्बरं|उदुंबरः|उदुम्बरः
उदुंबर <i>(I) m.</i> 1. A kind of fig tree; 2. a kind of leprosy; 3. a threshold; 4. a eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुंबर|उदुम्बर|उदुम्बरं|उदुंबरः|उदुम्बरः
उदुंबर <i>(II) n.</i> Copper, brass. (See उडुंबर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूखल|उदूखलं
उदूखल <i>m.n.</i> 1. A wooden mortar used for pounding rice and separating the husk; 2. a mortar in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूढा
उदूढा <i>f.</i> A married woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेजय
उदेजय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Shaking, making to tremble, terrifying, e.g. उदेजयान् भूतगणान् न्यषेधीत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेजया
उदेजय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Shaking, making to tremble, terrifying, e.g. उदेजयान् भूतगणान् न्यषेधीत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गति|उद्गतिः
उद्गति <i>f.</i> 1. Going up, ascent; 2. rise, origin; 3. vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गंधि|उद्गन्धि
उद्गंधि <i>a.</i> 1. Fragrant, विजृंभणोद्गंधिषु कुड्मलेषु R.xvi.47; 2. having a strong smell (good or bad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गम|उद्गमः
उद्गम <i>m.</i> 1. Elevation; 2. rising, standing erect, K.S.vii.77, Am.S.36; 3. appearance, creation, production, R.iv.9, Am.S.81; 4. a shoot, हरिततृणोद्गमशंकया मृगीभिः Kir.v.38; 5. vomiting, Rt.vi.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमन|उद्गमनं
उद्गमन <i>n.</i> Rising, ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनीय|उद्गमनीयं
उद्गमनीय <i>n.</i> Bleached clothes, गृहीतपत्युद्गमनीयवस्त्रा K.S.vii.11, or धौतोद्गमनीयवासिनी (तत्स्यादुद्गमनीयं यत् धौतयोर्वस्त्रयोर्युगम् Am.ii.6.112; but not necessarily a pair. See Mall. on K.S.vii.11)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=131-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

