उपज्ञा <i>f.</i> 1. Knowledge obtained by oneself and not handed down by tradition, invention, पाणिन्युपज्ञं व्याकरणम् S.K., प्राचेतसोपज्ञं रामायणम् R.xv.63; 2. commencement of a thing not previously done, लोकेऽभूद्यदुपज्ञमेव विदुषां सौजन्यजन्यं यशः Mall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपढौकन|उपढौकनं
उपढौकन <i>n.</i> A respectful offering or present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपताप|उपतापः
उपताप <i>m.</i> 1. Heat, warmth; 2. pain, sorrow, e.g. विवक्षितं ह्यनुक्तमुपतापम् (v.l. for अनुतापम्) जनयति; 3. sickness, disease; 4. haste, hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापन|उपतापनं
उपतापन <i>n.</i> 1. Heating; 2. distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतिष्य|उपतिष्यं
उपतिष्य <i>n.</i> 1. The lunar asterism called अश्लेषा; 2. another lunar asterism, otherwise called पुनर्वसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपत्यका
उपत्यका <i>f.</i> Land at the foot of a hill or mountain, मलयाद्रेरुपत्यकाः R.ii.46, कांतातरेयं गंधपाषाणवत्युपत्यका D.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंश|उपदंशः
उपदंश <i>m.</i> 1. Anything which excites thirst or appetite अग्रमांसोपदंशं पिब नवशोणितासवम् Ve.iii.; 2. biting, stinging; 3. the venereal disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शक|उपदर्शकः
उपदर्शक <i>m.</i> 1. One who shows the way, a guide; 2. a door-keeper; 3. a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदश
उपदश <i>a. (pl.)</i> Almost ten, nearly ten, i.e. nine or eleven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा <i>f.</i> A present, an offering to a king or a great man, उपदा विविशुः शश्वत्रोत्सेकाः कोसलेश्वरम् R.iv.70, v.41, vii.30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदान|उपदानं
उपदान <i>n.</i> 1. An oblation, a present; 2. a gift for procuring favour or protection, a bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानक|उपदानकं
उपदान <i>n.</i> 1. An oblation, a present; 2. a gift for procuring favour or protection, a bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्
उपदिश् <i>f.</i> An intermediate quarter (they are four- ऐशानी, आग्नेयी, नैरृती and वायवी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिशा
उपदिश् <i>f.</i> An intermediate quarter (they are four- ऐशानी, आग्नेयी, नैरृती and वायवी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेव|उपदेवः
उपदेव <i>m.</i> An inferior deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवता
उपदेवता <i>f.</i> An inferior deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेश|उपदेशः
उपदेश <i>m.</i> 1. Instruction, advice, teaching, prescription, स्थिरोपदेशामुपदेशकाले प्रपेदिरे प्राक्तनजन्मविद्या K.S.i.30, M.viii.272, Am.S.26, R.xii.57; 2. specification; 3. plea, pretext; 4. initiation, communication of a mantra. (चंद्रसूर्यग्रहे तीर्थे सिद्धक्षेत्रे शिवालये । मंत्रमात्रप्रकथनमुपदेशः स उच्यते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशक|उपदेशकः
उपदेशक <i>m.</i> An instructor, a guide, a preceptor, e.g. उपदेशकमाहात्म्यार्थज्ञानाच्च पाणिनेः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशन|उपदेशनं
उपदेशन <i>n.</i> Advising, instructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टृ
उपदेष्टृ <i>m.</i> A teacher, a preceptor, a spiritual adviser, चत्वारो वयमृत्विजः स भगवान् कर्मोपदेष्टा हरिः Ve.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेह|उपदेहः
उपदेह <i>m.</i> 1. A cover; 2. an ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदोह|उपदोहः
उपदोह <i>m.</i> 1. A nipple of the udder of a cow; 2. a milking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रव|उपद्रवः
उपद्रव <i>m.</i> 1. An unhappy accident, misfortune, calamity; 2. injury, trouble, पुंसामसमर्थानामुपद्रवायात्मनो भवेत्कोपः Panch.i.; 3. outrage, violence; 4. national distress; 5. rebellion; 6. a symptom, a supervenient disease (in medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=137-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधर्म|उपधर्मः|उपधर्म्म|उपधर्म्मः
उपधर्म <i>m.</i> A by-law, a secondary religious precept, M.ii.237, iv.147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा <i>f.</i> 1. Imposition, forgery, fraud, M.viii.193; 2. test of honesty &c. of four kinds, (शोधयेत्) धर्मोपधाभिर्विप्रांश्च सर्वाभिः सचिवान् पुनः /Kālikā P./; 3. a means, an expedient, अयशोभिदुरा लोके कोपधा मरणादृते Sis.xix.58; 4. a penultimate letter (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाभृत|उपधाभृतः
उपधा-भृत <i>m.</i> a servant who has been guilty of dishonesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधातु|उपधातुः
उपधातु <i>m.</i> 1. A semi-metal (they are- सप्तोपधातवः स्वर्णमाक्षिकं तारमाक्षिकम् । तुत्थं कांस्यं च रीतिश्च सिंदूरं च शिलाजतु); 2. a secondary secretion of the body (six in number).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधान|उपधानं
उपधान <i>n.</i> 1. Placing or resting upon; 2. a pillow, a cushion, विपुलमुपधानं भुजलता Bhartr.iii.79; 3. peculiarity, individuality; 4. affection, kindness; 5. poison; 6. excellence, सोपधानां धियं धीराः स्थेयसीं खट्वयंति ये Sis.ii.77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानीय|उपधानीयं
उपधानीय <i>n.</i> A pillow, a cushion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधारण|उपधारणं
उपधारण <i>n.</i> 1. Consideration, reflection; 2. drawing (as by a hook).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधि|उपधिः
उपधि <i>m.</i> 1. Fraud, dishonesty, अरिषु हि विजयार्थिनः क्षितीशा विदधति सोपधिसंधिदूषणानि Kir.i.45; 2. suppression veri, suggestion falsi (in law), M.viii.165; 3. terror, threat, compulsion, false inducement, बलोपधिविनिवृत्तान् व्यवारान्निवर्तयेत् Yaj.ii.31; 4. the wheel of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिक|उपधिकः
उपधिक <i>m.</i> A cheat, a knave; (the more correct form of this word is औपधिक.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपित|उपधूपितः
उपधूपित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Fumigated; 2. being at the point of death; 3. suffering extreme pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपिता
उपधूपित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Fumigated; 2. being at the point of death; 3. suffering extreme pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपित|उपधूपितः
उपधूपित <i>(II) m.</i> Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृति|उपधृतिः
उपधृति <i>f.</i> A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मान|उपध्मानः
उपध्मान <i>(I) m.</i> A lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मान|उपध्मानः
उपध्मान <i>(II) n.</i> Blowing upon, breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानीय|उपध्मानीयः
उपध्मानीय <i>m.</i> The aspirate visarga before the letters प् and फ्. (ऊपूपध्मानीयानामोष्ठौ S.K.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनत|उपनतः
उपनत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Befallen, come, e.g. यदेवोपनतं दुःखात्सुखं तद्रसवत्तरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनता
उपनत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Befallen, come, e.g. यदेवोपनतं दुःखात्सुखं तद्रसवत्तरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनक्षत्र|उपनक्षत्रं
उपनक्षत्र <i>n.</i> A subordinate constellation (there are 729 such constellations in all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनगर|उपनगरं
उपनगर <i>n.</i> A suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनति|उपनतिः
उपनति <i>f.</i> 1. Approach; 2. bending, bow, salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनय|उपनयः
उपनय <i>n.</i> 1. Bringing near; 2. attaining, gaining; 3. investiture with the sacred thread (गृह्योक्तकर्मणा येन समीपं नीयते गुरोः । बालो वेदाय तद्योगाद् बालस्योपानयं विदुः); 4. the fourth member of the five-fold syllogism (in logic); (it is thus defined- व्याप्तिविशिष्टस्य हेतोः पक्षधर्मताप्रतिपादकं वचनमुपनयः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयन|उपनयनं
उपनयन <i>n.</i> 1. Leading to or near; 2. investiture with the sacred thread, आसमावर्तनात्कुर्यात् कृतोपनयनो द्विजः M.ii.108, 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनागरिका
उपनागरिका <i>f.</i> A kind of वृत्त्यनुप्रास. It is formed by sweet-sounding (माधुर्यव्यंजक) letters. The K.Pr. quotes the following āryā from the Kuṭṭinīmata as an example- अपसारय घनसारं कुरु हारं दूर एव किं कमलैः । अलमलमालि मृणालैरिति वदति दिवानिशं बाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाय|उपनायः
उपनाय <i>n.</i> The same as उपनयन q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायक|उपनायकः
उपनायक <i>m.</i> 1. A paramour; 2. a character in a work of art next in importance to the hero, (e.g. मकरंद in the M.M.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायन|उपनायनं
उपनायन <i>n.</i> The same as उपनयन q.v., गर्भाष्टमेऽब्दे कुर्वीत ब्राह्मणस्योपनायनम् M.ii.36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायिका
उपनायिका <i>f.</i> A character in a work of art next in importance to the heroine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाह|उपनाहः
उपनाह <i>m.</i> 1. A bundle; 2. an unguent applied to a wound or sore; 3. a peg to which the strings of a lyre are attached and by which they are tightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहन|उपनाहनं
उपनाहन <i>n.</i> Applying an unguent, anointing, plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षेप|उपनिक्षेपः
उपनिक्षेप <i>m.</i> 1. The act of depositing; 2. an open deposit, any article entrusted to one’s keeping, letting him know what it is. (उपनिक्षेपो नाम रूपसंख्याप्रदर्शनेन रक्षणार्थं परस्य हस्ते निहितं द्रव्यम् Mit. on Yaj.ii.25.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधान|उपनिधानं
उपनिधान <i>n.</i> 1. Placing near; 2. depositing; 3. a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधि|उपनिधिः
उपनिधि <i>m.</i> 1. A deposit in general; 2. a sealed deposit (यदप्रदर्शितरूपं सचिह्नवस्त्रादिना पिहितं निक्षिप्यते Medhātithi on M.viii.149), Yaj.ii.25, M.viii.145; 3. pledge, property under the care of a creditor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपात|उपनिपातः
उपनिपात <i>m.</i> 1. Approaching, coming near; 2. sudden and unexpected attack or occurrence, रंध्रोपनिपातिनोऽनर्था इति यदुच्यते तदव्यभिचारि वचः Sak.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिमंत्रण|उपनिमन्त्रण|उपनिमंत्रणं
उपनिमंत्रण <i>n.</i> Invitation, inauguration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशित
उपनिवेशित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Placed, established, colonized, R.xv.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशिता
उपनिवेशित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Placed, established, colonized, R.xv.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषद
उपनिषद <i>f.</i> 1. Certain mystical writings attached to the Brāhmaṇas (n.), the aim of which is the ascertainment of the secret sense of the Veda, यद्वेदाध्ययनं तथोपनिषदां योगस्य सांख्यस्य च ज्ञानम् M.M.i., उपनिषदः परिप्रीता गीतापि च हंत मतिपथं नीता Bh.V.ii.40 (the word is variously derived- (1) उपनीय तमात्मानं ब्रह्मापास्तद्वयं यतः । निहंत्यविद्यां तज्जं च तस्मादुपनिषद्भवेत्, (2) निहत्यानर्थमूलं स्वविद्यां प्रत्यक्तया परम् । नयत्यपास्तसंभेदमतो वोपनिषद्भवेत्, (3) प्रवृत्तिहेतून्निःशेषांस्तन्मूलोच्छेदकत्वतः । यतोऽवसादयेद्विद्या तस्मादुपनिषद्भवेत्; in the मुक्तकोपनिषद् 108 Upanishads are mentioned; but additions have been made even to this number); 2. true knowledge, knowledge regarding Brahman (n.); 3. sacred or religious lore; 4. secrecy, seclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=138-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्कर|उपनिष्करं|उपनिष्करः
उपनिष्कर <i>n.</i> A street, a principal road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्क्रमण|उपनिष्क्रमणं
उपनिष्क्रमण <i>n.</i> 1. Going out; 2. the religious rite of taking a child for the first time into the open air (generally performed in the fourth month of its age); 3. a main road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनृत्य|उपनृत्यं
उपनृत्य <i>n.</i> A place for dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतृ
उपनेतृ <i>(I) a. (f. त्री)</i> One who brings or comes, K.S.i.60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेत्री
उपनेतृ <i>(I) a. (f. त्री)</i> One who brings or comes, K.S.i.60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतृ
उपनेतृ <i>(II) m.</i> A preceptor who performs the उपनयन ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यास|उपन्यासः
उपन्यास <i>m.</i> 1. Juxtaposition; 2. statement, proposal, निर्यातः शनकैरलीकवचनोपन्यासमालीजनः Am.S.23; 3. suggestion, hint, अवसरे खलु रागोपकारयोर्गरीयसोरुपन्यासः M.M.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपति|उपपतिः
उपपति <i>m.</i> A paramour, उपपतिरिव नीचेः पश्चिमांतेन चंद्रः Sis.xi.65, M.iii.155, iv.216, 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्ति|उपपत्तिः
उपपत्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Appearance, production; 2. cause, reason; 3. reasoning (उपपत्तिमत् ‘well-reasoned’ Kir.ii.1); 4. fitness, propriety; 5. ascertainment, demonstration, an ascertained or demonstrated conclusion, उपपत्तिरुदाहृता बलात् Kir.ii.28; 6. a means, an expedient; 7. accomplishment, non-failure, स्वार्थोपपतिं प्रति दुर्बलाशः R.v.12, तात्पर्यानुपपतितः Bh.P.; 8. attainment, acquirement, R.xiv.78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपद|उपपदं
उपपद <i>n.</i> 1. A word next preceding, a word prefixed or previously uttered, तस्याः स राजोपपदं निशांतम् R.xvi.40; 2. a title, a degree, (e.g. शर्मन्, वर्मन्); 3. a secondary word of a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपन्न
उपपन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> Fit, proper (generally with the gen. or loc.) उपपन्नमिदं विशेषणं वायोः Vikr.ii., उपपन्नमेतदृषिकल्पेस्मिन्राजनि Sak.ii.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपन्ना
उपपन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> Fit, proper (generally with the gen. or loc.) उपपन्नमिदं विशेषणं वायोः Vikr.ii., उपपन्नमेतदृषिकल्पेस्मिन्राजनि Sak.ii.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपरीक्षण|उपपरीक्षणं
उपपरीक्षण <i>n.</i> Investigation, examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपरीक्षा
उपपरीक्षा <i>f.</i> Investigation, examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपात|उपपातः
उपपात <i>m.</i> 1. Unexpected occurrence; 2. accident, misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातक|उपपातकं
उपपातक <i>n.</i> A crime or sin in the second degree. (महापातकतुल्यानि पापान्युक्तानि यानि तु । तानि पातकसंज्ञानि तन्न्यूनमुपपातकम् Paiṭhinasi), Yaj.ii.210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादन|उपपादनं
उपपादन <i>n.</i> 1. Effecting, doing; 2. giving, delivering; 3. proving, establishing by argument, demonstration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपाप|उपपापं
उपपाप <i>n.</i> The same as उपपातक q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपार्श्व|उपपार्श्वं|उपपार्श्वः
उपपार्श्व <i>m.n.</i> 1. A shoulder; 2. flank; 3. the opposite side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपीडन|उपपीडनं
उपपीडन <i>n.</i> 1. Pressing down, devastating; 2. inflicting pain, व्याधिभिश्चोपपीडनम् M.vi.62; 3. agony, torture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुर|उपपुरं
उपपुर <i>n.</i> A suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुराण|उपपुराणं
उपपुराण <i>m.</i> A secondary or minor Purāṇa. (They are thus enumerated by हेमाद्रि- आद्यं सनत्कुमारोक्तं नारसिंहमतःपरम् । तृतीयं नारदप्रोक्तं कुमारेण तु भावितम् । चतुर्थं शिवधर्माख्यं साक्षान्नंदीशभाषितम् । दुर्वाससोक्तमाश्चर्यं नारदोक्तमतःपरम् । कापिलं मानवं चैव तथैवोशनसेरितम् । ब्रह्मांडं वारुणं तथा शांबं सौरं सर्वार्थसंचयम् । पराशरोक्तमवरं तथा भागवताह्वयम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुष्पिका
उपपुष्पिका <i>f.</i> Yawning, gaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रदर्शन|उपप्रदर्शनं
उपप्रदर्शन <i>n.</i> Pointing out, indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रदान|उपप्रदानं
उपप्रदान <i>n.</i> 1. Delivering over; 2. a present, a bribe; 3. a tribute, e.g. तस्योपप्रदानेन संधिरेव युक्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रलोभन|उपप्रलोभनं
उपप्रलोभन <i>n.</i> 1. Seducing, alluring; 2. a bribe, an allurement, an inducement, उच्चावचान्युपप्रलोभनानि D.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रेक्षण|उपप्रेक्षणं
उपप्रेक्षण <i>n.</i> Overlooking, disregarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रैष|उपप्रैषः
उपप्रैष <i>m.</i> Invitation, summons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लव|उपप्लवः
उपप्लव <i>m.</i> 1. Unlucky accident, injury, trouble, क्वचिन्न वाय्वादिरुपपप्लवो वः R.v.6, Megh.i.17, उपप्लवाय लोकानां धूमकेतुरिवोत्थितः K.S.ii.32; 2. a calamity, a danger, R.ii.48; 3. fear, नृपा इवोपप्लविनः R.xiii.7; 4. distress, difficulty, adversity, अथ मदनवधूरुपप्लवान्तं व्यसनकृशा परिपालयां बभूव K.S.iv.46; 5. a portent, a natural phenomenon foreboding evil; 6. anarchy; 7. an eclipse of the sun or the moon; 8. a name of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबंध|उपबन्ध|उपबंधः|उपबन्धः
उपबंध <i>m.</i> 1. Connection; 2. an affix.; 3. a particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबर्ह|उपबर्हः
उपब(व)र्ह <i>m.</i> A pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्ह|उपवर्हः
उपब(व)र्ह <i>m.</i> A pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबहु
उपबहु <i>a.</i> A few, a tolerable number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपबाहु|उपबाहुः
उपबाहु <i>m.</i> The lower arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभंग|उपभङ्ग|उपभंगः|उपभङ्गः
उपभंग <i>m.</i> 1. Fleeing away, retreat; 2. division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभाषा
उपभाषा <i>f.</i> A secondary dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभुक्ति|उपभुक्तिः
उपभुक्ति <i>f.</i> The same as उपभोग q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=139-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभृत्
उपभृत् <i>f.</i> A round cup used in sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोग|उपभोगः
उपभोग <i>m.</i> 1. Use, practice, enjoyment, न जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन शाम्यति M.ii.94; 2. usufruct; 3. pleasure, satisfaction; 4. cohabitation, R.xiv.24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपम
उपम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> Like, resembling (as the last member of compounds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमा
उपम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> Like, resembling (as the last member of compounds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमंत्रण|उपमन्त्रण|उपमंत्रणं
उपमंत्रण <i>n.</i> 1. The act of addressing or inviting; 2. of persuading, (उपमंत्रणमुपच्छंदनम् S.K.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमंथनी|उपमन्थनी
उपमंथनी <i>f.</i> A staff for stirring fire (in ritualistic works).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्द|उपमर्दः|उपमर्द्द
उपमर्द <i>m.</i> 1. Friction, rubbing down, e.g. अन्यासु तावदुपमर्दसहासु भृंग लोलं विनोदय मनः सुमनोलतासु; 2. injuring, killing, destruction; 3. unhusking; 4. reproach, abuse; 5. refutation of a charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमा
उपमा <i>f.</i> 1. Resemblance, equality, similarity, स्फुटोपमं भूतिसितेन शंभुना Sis.i.4; 2. a figure of speech (in rhetoric), corresponding to the English simile, e.g. उपमा कालिदासस्य; it is thus defined by Jagannātha- सादृश्यं सुंदरं वाक्यार्थोपस्कारकमुपमालंकृतिः R.G.; Jayadeva defines and illustrates it thus- उपमा यत्र सादृश्यलक्ष्मीरुल्लसति स्वयोः । हंसीव कृष्ण ते कीर्तिः स्वर्गंगामवगाहते Chandrāloka.v.; 3. the standard of comparison, (the same as उपमान), बुबुधे न बुधोपमः R.i.47, सर्वोपमाद्रव्यसमुच्चयेन K.S.i.50, यथा वातो निवातस्यो नेंगते सोपमा स्मृता Bg.vi.19 (where Śankara explains उपमा by उपमीयते अनेन); 4. a likeness (as a picture &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमाद्रव्य
उपमा-द्रव्य <i>n.</i> any object used for comparison, K.S.i.50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातृ
उपमातृ <i>f.</i> 1. A wet nurse; 2. a near female relative (they are- मातृष्वसा मातुलानी पितृव्यस्त्री पितृष्वसा । श्वश्रूः पूर्वजपत्नी च मातृतुल्याः प्रकीर्तिताः Bṛhaspati.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमान|उपमानं
उपमान <i>n.</i> 1. Comparison, K.S.i.36; 2. analogy, considered as one of the four kinds of proof by the Naiyāyikas; it is defined as being प्रसिद्धसाधर्म्यात् साध्यसाधनम्; 3. the standard of comparison, that with which anything is compared, (op. to उपमेय); (as such it is one of the four requisites of उपमा), K.S.iv.5, उपमानमभूद्विलासिनीनाम् K.S.iv.5, उपमानस्यापि सखे प्रत्युपमानं वपुस्तस्याः Vikr.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमिति|उपमितिः
उपमिति <i>f.</i> 1. Resemblance, comparison, similarity, तदाननस्योपमितौ दरिद्रता Na.i.24; 2. knowledge of things derived from analogy, a conclusion arrived at by (in Nyāya phil.) प्रत्यक्षमप्यनुमितिस्तथोपमितिशब्दजे Bh.P.; 3. a figure of speech, more generally known as उपमा q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेय
उपमेय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> Fit to be likened, fit to be compared, आसीदुपमेयकांतिर्मयूरपृष्ठाश्रयिणा गुहेन R.vi.4, xviii.34, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेया
उपमेय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> Fit to be likened, fit to be compared, आसीदुपमेयकांतिर्मयूरपृष्ठाश्रयिणा गुहेन R.vi.4, xviii.34, 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेय
उपमेय <i>(II) n.</i> The object of comparison (in rhetoric), उपमानोपमेययोरेव न कार्यकारणादिकयोः साधर्म्यं भवति K.Pr.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेयोपमा
उपमेय-उपमा <i>f.</i> a figure of speech consisting in the mutual comparison of the उपमान and the उपमेय, which raises an implication that the like of them does not exist. (Cf. अनन्वय); for instances, See K.Pr.x., S.D.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयंतृ|उपयन्तृ
उपयंतृ <i>m.</i> A bride-groom, a husband, R.viii.1, K.S.v.45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयंत्र|उपयन्त्र|उपयंत्रं
उपयंत्र <i>n.</i> A minor surgical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयम|उपयमः
उपय(या)म <i>m.</i> 1. Marriage, e.g. कन्या त्वजातोपयमा सलज्जा नवयौवना; 2. restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाम|उपयामः
उपय(या)म <i>m.</i> 1. Marriage, e.g. कन्या त्वजातोपयमा सलज्जा नवयौवना; 2. restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयमन|उपयमनं
उपयमन <i>n.</i> 1. Marrying, taking a wife; 2. restraining, curbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयष्टृ
उपयष्टृ <i>m.</i> One of the sixteen priests at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचक|उपयाचकः
उपयाचक <i>a. (f. का)</i> An asker, a solicitor, a suitor, a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचका
उपयाचक <i>a. (f. का)</i> An asker, a solicitor, a suitor, a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचन|उपयाचनं
उपयाचन <i>n.</i> Soliciting, approaching with a request or prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचित|उपयाचितं
उपयाचित <i>n.</i> 1. A request, a prayer; 2. a prayer or request to a deity for the fulfilment of a desire, ग्रहाणां चरितं स्वप्नो निमित्तात्युपयाचितम् । फलंति काकतालीयं तेभ्यः प्राज्ञा न बिभ्यति Ve.ii.; 3. a present promised to a deity on the fulfilment of a request made; the present generally consisted of an animal, sometimes of a human being. See M.M.v. (अद्य मया भगवत्याः करालायाः प्रागुपयाचितं स्त्रीरत्नमुपहर्तव्यम्.) उपयाचितक also is used in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाज|उपयाजः
उपयाज <i>m.</i> Additional formulæ at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयान|उपयानं
उपयान <i>n.</i> Approaching, coming near, K.S.vii.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोग|उपयोगः
उपयोग <i>m.</i> 1. Application, employment, use, utility, अनंगलेखक्रिययोपयोगम् K.S.i.7; 2. administration of medicine; 3. fitness, suitableness; 4. contact, proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्त|उपरक्तः
उपरक्त <i>(I) a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Eclipsed; 2. afflicted, overtaken by calamity; 3. tinged, coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्ता
उपरक्त <i>(I) a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Eclipsed; 2. afflicted, overtaken by calamity; 3. tinged, coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्त|उपरक्तः
उपरक्त <i>(II) m.</i> The sun or the moon in eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्ष|उपरक्षः
उपरक्ष <i>m.</i> A body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्षण|उपरक्षणं
उपरक्षण <i>n.</i> A guard, an outpost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरत|उपरतः
उपरत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Stopped, ceased, रजस्युपरते M.v.66; 2. dead, e.g. पितर्युपरते पुत्रा विभजेयुर्धनं पितुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरता
उपरत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Stopped, ceased, रजस्युपरते M.v.66; 2. dead, e.g. पितर्युपरते पुत्रा विभजेयुर्धनं पितुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतस्पृह|उपरतस्पृहः
उपरत-स्पृह <i>a.</i> indifferent to worldly belongings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=140-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरति|उपरतिः
उपरति <i>f.</i> 1. Ceasing, stopping; 2. death; 3. indifference; 4. refraining from sexual enjoyment; 5. conviction of the futility of ceremonial acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरत्न|उपरत्नं
उपरत्न <i>n.</i> A secondary or inferior gem; (उपरत्नानि काचश्च कर्पूरोऽश्मा तथैव च । मुक्ताशुक्तिस्तथा शंख इत्यादीनि बहून्यपि । गुणा यथैव रत्नानामुपरत्नेषु ते तथा । किंतु किंचित्ततो हीना विशेषोऽयमुदाहृतः Bhāvaprakāśa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरम|उपरमः
उपर(रा)म <i>m.</i> 1. Ceasing, stopping; 2. abstaining from; 3. death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराम|उपरामः
उपर(रा)म <i>m.</i> 1. Ceasing, stopping; 2. abstaining from; 3. death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरमण|उपरमणं
उपरमण <i>n.</i> 1. Abstaining from the pleasures of sense; 2. abstaining from ceremonial acts; 3. ceasing, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरस|उपरसः
उपरस <i>m.</i> 1. A secondary mineral; 2. a subordinate flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराग|उपरागः
उपराग <i>m.</i> 1. Colour; 2. an eclipse of the sun or moon, उपरागांते शशिनः समुपगता रोहिणू योगम् Sak.vii.; 3. calamity, affliction, injury, मृणालिनी हैममिवोपरागम् R.xvi.7; 4. reproach, blame, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराज|उपराजः
उपराज <i>m.</i> A viceroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरि
उपरि <i>ind.</i> As an adverb, it means- (1) high, above, upon, towards the upper side of, उपर्युपरि पश्यन्तः सर्वं एव दरिद्रति Hit.i.; (2) besides, in addition to, सहस्राण्येकविंशतिः । शतान्युपरि चैवाष्टौ तथा भूयश्च सप्ततिः Bh.; (3) afterwards, यदा पूर्वं नासीदुपरि च तथा नैव भविता Sant.S.ii.7.As a separable preposition, (with the acc. gen. or loc.), it means- (1) on, over, above, e.g. अवाङ्मुखस्योपरि पुष्पवृष्टिः पपात R.ii.60; (2) at the head, at the top, Yaj.i.819; (3) beyond, in addition to, Yaj.ii.253; (4) on, upon, in connection with, in regard to, towards, परस्परस्योपरि पर्यचीयत R.iii.24, Sant.S.xii.23; (5) after, मुहूर्तादुपरि उपाध्यायश्चेदागच्छेत्. (The double form उपर्युपरि (used either absolutely or with the acc. or gen.) means- (1) just above, e.g. उपर्युपरि लोकं हरिः, उपर्युपर्यंबुमुचां वितानैः; (2) very high, उपर्युपरि सर्वेषामादित्य इव तेजसा Bh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिचर|उपरिचरः
उपरि-चर <i>a.</i> moving above (as a bird).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरितन
उपरि-तन, -स्थ <i>a.</i> upper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिस्थ
उपरि-तन, -स्थ <i>a.</i> upper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिभाव|उपरिभावः
उपरि-भाव <i>m.</i> the being above or higher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिभूमि|उपरिभूमिः
उपरि-भूमि <i>f.</i> the ground above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्टात्
उपरिष्टात् <i>ind.</i> 1. As an adverb, it means- 1. over, above, Yaj.i.106; 2. further on, afterwards, कल्याणावतंसा हि कल्याणसंपदुपरिष्टाद्भवति M.M.vi.; 3. behind, (op. to पुरस्तात् in this sense.)As a preposition, (with the acc. or gen.), it means- (1) over, upon; (2) down upon; (3) behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरीतक|उपरीतकः
उपरीतक <i>m.</i> A mode of sexual enjoyment. (एकपादमूरौ कृत्वा द्वितीयं स्कंधसंस्थितम् । नारीं कामयते कामी बंधः स्यादुपरीतकः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरूपक|उपरूपकं
उपरूपक <i>n.</i> A drama of an inferior class of which 18 are enumerated; (they are- नाटिका, त्रोटक, गोष्ठी, सट्टक, नाट्यरासक, प्रस्थान, उल्लाप्य, काव्य, प्रेंखण, रासक, संलापक, श्रीगदित, शिल्पक, विलासिका, द्रुमेलिका, प्रकरणी, हल्लीश and भाणिका S.D.vi.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोध|उपरोधः
उपरोध <i>m.</i> 1. Covering, surrounding, blocking, R.vi.44; 2. obstruction, impediment; 3. trouble, disturbance, तपोवननिवासिनिनामुपरोधो मा भूत् Sak.i.; 4. protection, favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधन|उपरोधनं
उपरोधन <i>n.</i> 1. Covering, surrounding, blocking, R.vi.44; 2. obstruction, impediment; 3. trouble, disturbance, तपोवननिवासिनिनामुपरोधो मा भूत् Sak.i.; 4. protection, favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधक|उपरोधकं
उपरोधक <i>n.</i> An inner room, a private apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपल|उपलः
उपल <i>m.</i> 1. A rock or stone, कांते कथं घटितवानुपलेन चेतः Sr.T.3, Megh.i.19; 2. a precious stone, a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक|उपलकः
उपलक <i>m.</i> A stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षण|उपलक्षणं
उपलक्षण <i>n.</i> 1. Ascertainment, observation, वेलोपलक्षणार्थमादिष्टोऽस्मि Sak.iv.; 2. designation, mark; 3. the implication of something not expressed in addition to that which has been expressed, synecdoche of a part for the whole; (it is thus defined- स्वप्रतिपादकत्वे सति स्वेतरप्रतिपादकत्वम्), मंत्रग्रहणं ब्राह्मणस्याप्युपलक्षणम् S.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धि|उपलब्धिः
उपलब्धि <i>f.</i> 1. Obtaining, acquisition, gain, R.v.56, viii.17; 2. perception, knowledge, नान्जाव उपलब्धेः Bh.; 3. a guess; 4. perceptibility considered as a kind of proof by the Mīmānsākas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=141-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलंभ|उपलम्भ|उपलंभः|उपलम्भः
