उपवीत|उपवीतं
उपवीत <i>n.</i> 1. Investiture with the sacred thread; 2. the thread worn by the first three castes of the Hindus, पित्र्यमंशमुपवीतलक्षणं मातृकं च धनुरूर्जितं दधत् R.xi.64, M.ii.44, 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवृंहण|उपवृंहणं
उपवृंहण <i>n.</i> Increase, collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेद|उपवेदः
उपवेद <i>m.</i> A class of writings subordinate to the Vedas. (They are four, one उपवेद being attached to each of the four Vedas. Thus आयुर्वेद is attached to ऋग्वेद, धनुर्वेद to यजुर्वेद, गांधर्ववेद to सामवेद, and शस्त्रशास्त्र to अथर्ववेद; according to Suśruta and the Bhāvaprakāśa, however, आयुर्वेद is attached not to the ऋग्वेद but to the अथर्ववेद.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेश|उपवेशः
उपवेश <i>m.</i> 1. Sitting down; 2. being attached to; 3. voiding by stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेशन|उपवेशनं
उपवेशन <i>n.</i> 1. Sitting down; 2. being attached to; 3. voiding by stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

