उपशम|उपशमः
उपशम <i>m.</i> 1. The becoming quiet, assuagement, cessation, extinction, कृतोऽस्या उपशमः Ve.iii., मन्युर्दुःसह एष यात्युपशमं नो सांत्ववादैः स्फुटम् Am.S.5; 2. calmness, patience, quietude; 3. control over the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशमन|उपशमनं
उपशमन <i>n.</i> 1. Quieting, calming; 2. extinction, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशय|उपशयः
उपशय <i>m.</i> Lying by the side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशल्य|उपशल्यं|उपशल्यः
उपशल्य <i>n.</i> An open place in the vicinity of a town or village, R.xv.60, xvi.37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=142-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशाखा
