उपसूर्यक <i>n.</i> The solar halo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=143-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उपसृष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Joined, connected with, accompanied by; 2. troubled, affected, injured, R.viii.94; 3. furnished with an उपसर्ग (as a root), क्रुधद्रुहोरुपसृष्टयोः कर्म Pan.; 4. eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=143-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्टा
उपसृष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Joined, connected with, accompanied by; 2. troubled, affected, injured, R.viii.94; 3. furnished with an उपसर्ग (as a root), क्रुधद्रुहोरुपसृष्टयोः कर्म Pan.; 4. eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=143-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उपसृष्ट <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The sun or moon in eclipse; 2. a libidinous man, उपसृष्टा इव क्षुद्राधिष्ठितभवनाः Kad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=143-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उपसृष्ट <i>(III) n.</i> Copulation, coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=143-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेचन
उपसेचन <i>n.</i> 1. Pouring or sprinkling upon, watering; 2. infusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=143-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवन|उपसेवनं
