उपहत|उपहतः
उपहत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Censured, rebuked, disregarded; 2. impure; 3. doomed, destroyed, e.g. दैवेनोपहतस्य वृद्धिरथवा पूर्वं विपर्यस्यति; 4. hurt, injured; 5. vitiated, polluted, शारीरैर्मलैः सुराभिर्मद्यैर्वा यदुपहतं तदत्यन्तोपहतम् Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहता
उपहत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Censured, rebuked, disregarded; 2. impure; 3. doomed, destroyed, e.g. दैवेनोपहतस्य वृद्धिरथवा पूर्वं विपर्यस्यति; 4. hurt, injured; 5. vitiated, polluted, शारीरैर्मलैः सुराभिर्मद्यैर्वा यदुपहतं तदत्यन्तोपहतम् Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतात्मन्
उपहत-आत्मन् <i>a.</i> agitated in mind, mentally affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतदृश्
उपहत-दृश् <i>a.</i> dazzled, blinded, Kir.xii.18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतधी
उपहत-धी <i>a.</i> infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतक
उपहतक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Ill-fated, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतका
उपहतक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Ill-fated, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत्या
उपहत्या <i>f.</i> Dazzling of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरण|उपहरणं
उपहरण <i>n.</i> 1. Bringing near; 2. offering gifts to superiors; 3. presenting victims; 4. serving out food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहसित|उपहसितं
उपहसित <i>n.</i> Satirical laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्तिका
उपहस्तिका <i>f.</i> A small box containing condiments or betel, उपहस्तिकायास्तांबूलं कर्पूरसहितमुद्धृत्य मह्यं दत्वा D.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहार|उपहारः
उपहार <i>m.</i> 1. Oblation; 2. a present to a superior; 3. an offering to a deity; 4. honour; 5. indemnification; 6. food distributed to guests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारक|उपहारकः
उपहार <i>m.</i> 1. Oblation; 2. a present to a superior; 3. an offering to a deity; 4. honour; 5. indemnification; 6. food distributed to guests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहालक|उपहालकः
उपहालक <i>m.</i> A name of the Kuntala country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास|उपहासः
उपहास <i>m.</i> 1. Fun, play; 2. ridicule, R.xii.37; 3. satirical laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासक|उपहासकः
