उपह्वर|उपह्वरं|उपह्वरः
उपह्वर <i>n.</i> 1. Proximity; 2. solitary or private place, उपह्वरे पुनरित्यशिक्षयं भनमित्रम् D.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वान|उपह्वानं
उपह्वान <i>n.</i> 1. Inviting; 2. inviting with prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु <i>(I) ind.</i> 1. In a whisper; 2. secretly, in secret, privately, परिचेतुमुपांशु धीरणाम् R.viii.18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु <i>(II) m.</i> A prayer uttered in a low voice; (See M.ii.85 and Kulluka on it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकरण|उपाकरणं
उपाकरण <i>n.</i> 1. Invitation to begin; 2. preparation, beginning, commencement; 3. commencement of reading the Veda after the performance of a preparatory rite (in ritualistic literature.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकर्मन्|उपाकर्म्मन्
उपाकर्मन् <i>n.</i> 1. Preparation, beginning, commencement; 2. a ceremony performed before commencing to read the Veda after the monsoons, Yaj.i.142 (in. ritualistic works).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृत|उपाकृतं|उपाकृतः
उपाकृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Killed at a sacrifice (as an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृता
उपाकृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Killed at a sacrifice (as an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक्षम्
उपाक्षम् <i>ind.</i> Before the eyes, in presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यान|उपाख्यानं
उपाख्यान <i>n.</i> A short tale, a short narrative, उपाख्यानैर्विना तावद् भारतं प्रोच्यते बुधैः Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यानक|उपाख्यानकं
उपाख्यान <i>n.</i> A short tale, a short narrative, उपाख्यानैर्विना तावद् भारतं प्रोच्यते बुधैः Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम|उपागमः
उपागम <i>m.</i> 1. Approach, arrival; 2. occurrence; 3. agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्र|उपाग्रं
उपाग्र <i>n.</i> The part which is next to the end or top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रहण|उपाग्रहणं
उपाग्रहण <i>n.</i> Reading the Veda after initiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांग|उपाङ्ग|उपांगः|उपाङ्गः
उपांग <i>n.</i> 1. A subdivision; 2. any minor limb or member; 3. a supplement of a supplement; 4. a class of work supplementary to the Vedāṅgas. (पौराणन्यायमीमांसाधर्मशास्त्राणि चत्वार्युपांगानि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचार|उपाचारः
उपाचार <i>m.</i> 1. Position; 2. procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाजे
उपाजे <i>ind. (used only with the root कृ)</i> Supporting, infusing vigour (it considered as a prefix or not; hence उपाजेकृत्य or उपाजे कृत्वा. Cf. अन्वाजे.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांजन|उपाञ्जन|उपांजनं
उपांजन <i>n.</i> Anointing, plastering the ground with cow-dung, M.v.105 (Medhātithi explains the word by मठादेः सुधागोमयादिना संमार्जनानुलेपने.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्यय|उपात्ययः
उपात्यय <i>m.</i> Transgression, deviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादान|उपादानं
उपादान <i>n.</i> 1. Taking, receiving, acquiring, विस्रब्धं ब्राह्मणः शूद्राद्द्रव्योपार्जनमाचरेत् M.viii.417; 2. conveying some sense in addition to that actually expressed, स्वसिद्धये पराक्षेपः … उपादानम् K.Pr.ii.; 3. withdrawing the organs of sense from the outer world; 4. the material out of which anything is formed, a material cause, निमित्तमेव ब्रह्म स्यादुपादानं च वेक्षणात् Adhikaraṇaratnamālā, Sank.K.9; 5. mention, enumeration; 6. a cause, a motive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानकारण
उपादान-कारण <i>n.</i> a material cause, पारिशेष्याद् ब्रह्मणोऽन्यदुपादानकारणमशुद्धद्याधिगुणकं स्मृतिप्रसिद्धमभ्युपगंतव्यम् S.Bh.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानलक्षणा
उपादान-लक्षणा <i>f.</i> the same as अजहत्स्वार्था q.v., K.Pr.ii., S.D.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=144-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधि|उपाधिः
उपाधि <i>m.</i> 1. Fraud, deceit, deception (Cf. उपधि); 2. discriminative or distinguishing property, तदुपाधावेवसंकेतः K.Pr.ii. (उपाधि is of four kinds, viz, जाति, गुण, क्रिया and संज्ञा); 3. limitation, condition; 4. a nickname, a title, (e.g. भट्टाचार्य, महामहोपाध्याय); 5. virtuous reflection; 6. a man who is careful to support his family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिक
उपाधिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Exceeding, supernumerary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिका
उपाधिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Exceeding, supernumerary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्याय|उपाध्यायः
उपाध्याय <i>m.</i> 1. A teacher in general; 2. a spiritual teacher, a religious preceptor, किं भवानस्मदुपाध्यायादपि धर्मवित्तरः Mud.i. An उपाध्याय instructs for wages. (एकदेशं ति वेदस्य वेदांगान्यपि वा पुनः । योऽध्यापयति वृत्त्यर्थमुपाध्यायः स उच्यते M.ii.141). See अध्यापक and आचार्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्याया
उपाध्याया <i>f.</i> A female preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायानी
उपाध्यायानी <i>f.</i> The wife of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायी
उपाध्यायी <i>f.</i> 1. A female preceptor; 2. the wife of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानह
उपानह <i>f. (nom. sing. ˚नत्)</i> A shoe, e.g. उपानद्गूढपादस्य सर्वा चर्मवृत्तेव M.ii.178, 246, iii.238.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांत|उपान्त|उपान्तः
उपांत <i>m.</i> 1. Proximity, vicinity, मेरोरुपांतेष्विव वर्तमानम् R.vii.24, xvi.21, Megh.i.24; 2. skirt, border, edge, उपांतयोर्निष्कुषितं विहंगैः R.vii.50, K.S.iii.69, Am.S.23, K.S.vii.32; 8. side, slope, Megh.i.18; 4. the angle of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांतिक|उपान्तिक
उपांतिक <i>(I) m. (fem. की)</i> Near, proximate, neighbouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांतिक|उपान्तिक
उपांतिक <i>(II) n.</i> Vicinity, proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांत्य|उपान्त्य|उपान्त्यः
उपांत्य <i>(I) a. (f. त्या)</i> Last but one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांत्या
उपांत्य <i>(I) a. (f. त्या)</i> Last but one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांत्य|उपान्त्य|उपान्त्यः
उपांत्य <i>(II) m.</i> The corner of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांत्य|उपान्त्य|उपान्त्यः
उपांत्य <i>(III) n.</i> Vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाय|उपायः
उपाय <i>m.</i> 1. Approach; 2. a means, an expedient, a remedy, Am.S.23, M.viii.48; 3. beginning, commencement; 4. effort, exertion, Bg.vi.36; 5. a way, a mode, M.ix.248, x.2; 6. any of the four means of success against an enemy (in civil polity) चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सांत्वमपक्रिया Sis.ii.54, सामादीनामुपायानां चतुर्णामपि पंडिताः M.viii.109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायचतुष्टय
उपाय-चतुष्टय <i>n.</i> the four expedients against an enemy, viz, साम, दान, भेद and दंड. (According to some authorities, these expendients are seven in number. They add माया, उपेक्षा, and इंद्रजाल to the four already mentioned.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायतुरीय|उपायतुरीयः
उपाय-तुरीय <i>m.</i> the fourth means, that is, punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाययोग|उपाययोगः
उपाय-योग <i>m.</i> application of means or remedy, M.ix.10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायन|उपायनं
उपायन <i>n.</i> 1. Going near to; 2. becoming a pupil; 3. a gift or present, तस्योपायनयोग्यानि वस्तूनि सरितां पतिः K.S.ii.37, R.iv.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारंभ|उपारम्भ|उपारंभः|उपारम्भः
उपारंभ <i>m.</i> Beginning, commencement, e.g. सर्वकर्मोपारंभे विनियोगः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जन|उपार्जनं|उपार्ज्जन|उपार्ज्जनं
उपार्जन <i>n.</i> Acquiring, gaining, अर्थस्योपार्जनम् Panch.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालंभ|उपालम्भ|उपालंभः|उपालम्भः
उपालंभ <i>m.</i> 1. Taunt, reproach, abuse, censure, देवीं वसुमतीमंतरेण महदुपालंभनं गतोऽस्मि Sak.v.; 2. delaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालंभन|उपालम्भन|उपालंभनं
उपालंभन <i>n.</i> 1. Taunt, reproach, abuse, censure, देवीं वसुमतीमंतरेण महदुपालंभनं गतोऽस्मि Sak.v.; 2. delaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावर्तन|उपावर्तनं|उपावर्त्तन
उपावर्तन <i>n.</i> 1. Coming back, returning, करोति मारुतस्त्वदुपावर्तनशंकि मे मनः R.viii.53; 2. wallowing, revolving, turning round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रय|उपाश्रयः
उपाश्रय <i>m.</i> 1. Recourse, asylum, support; 2. reliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासक|उपासकः
उपासक <i>m.</i> 1. A servant; 2. worshipper, a follower; 3. a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासंग|उपासङ्ग|उपासंगः|उपासङ्गः
उपासंग <i>m.</i> 1. Proximity; 2. a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासन|उपासनं
उपासन <i>n.</i> 1. Engaging in, performing, M.ii.69; 2. practice of archery; 3. service, attendance, waiting upon, M.iii.107, Na.i.34, Bg.xiii.7, Yaj.iii.156; 4. worship, adoration; 5. religious meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासना
उपासना <i>f.</i> 1. Engaging in, performing, M.ii.69; 2. practice of archery; 3. service, attendance, waiting upon, M.iii.107, Na.i.34, Bg.xiii.7, Yaj.iii.156; 4. worship, adoption; 5. religious meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासा
