उपेक्षा <i>f.</i> 1. Leaving, abandoning; 2. over-looking, disregarding, neglecting; 3. indifference, contempt, R.xiv.65; 4. neglect considered as one of the seven expedients against an enemy. See उपाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेत
उपेत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Possessed of, सर्वगुणोपेतम् (पुत्रम्) Sak.i., (pp. of इ with उप q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेता
उपेत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Possessed of, सर्वगुणोपेतम् (पुत्रम्) Sak.i., (pp. of इ with उप q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेंद्र|उपेन्द्र|उपेंद्रः|उपेन्द्रः
उपेंद्र <i>m.</i> Name of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa as the younger brother of Indra in his fifth or Vāmana incarnation, उपेंद्रवज्रादपि दारुणोसि Git.G.v. (where there is a pun on उपेंद्रवज्रा, that being the name of the metre in which the a śloka is written.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेय|उपेयः
उपेय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. To be effected by any means; 2. to be approached; 3. to be obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेया
उपेय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. To be effected by any means; 2. to be approached; 3. to be obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=145-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
