उमा
उमा <i>f.</i> 1. A name of Pārvatī (in this sense the word is thus derived by Kālidāsa, probably on the authority of the Kālikā and Śiva Purāṇas- उ मेति मात्रा तपसो निषिद्धा पश्चादुमाख्यं सुमुखी जगाम K.S.i.26), उमावृषांकौ शरजन्मना यथा R.iii.23, K.S.iii.67; 2. light, splendour; 3. fame, reputation; 4. tranquility; 5. turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=146-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

