उशनस्
उशनस् <i>m. (nom. sing. voc. sing. उशनस्, उशन, उशनः)</i> Śukra, son of Bhṛgu and preceptor of the Asuras. He is known as a writer on civil and religious law (Yaj.i.4), as an authority on civil polity (अध्यापितस्योशनसाऽपि नीतिम् K.S.iii.6, शास्त्रमुशनसा प्रणीतम् Panch.v.), and as noted for his wisdom (कवीनामुशना कविः Bg.x.37.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=147-40" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

