औष्ट्रक <i>n.</i> A multitude of camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ
औष्ठ <i>a. (f. ष्ठी)</i> Lip-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठी
औष्ठ <i>a. (f. ष्ठी)</i> Lip-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्य
औष्ठ्य <i>a. (f. ष्ठ्या)</i> Relating to the lip, labial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्या
औष्ठ्य <i>a. (f. ष्ठ्या)</i> Relating to the lip, labial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्यवर्ण|औष्ठ्यवर्णः
औष्ठ्य-वर्ण <i>m.</i> a labial letter; they are- उ, ऊ, प्, फ्, ब्, भ्, म् and व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्यस्थान
औष्ठ्य-स्थान <i>a.</i> pronounced with the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्यस्वर|औष्ठ्यस्वरः
औष्ठ्य-स्वर <i>m.</i> a labial vowel; they are- उ and ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ण|औष्णं
औष्ण <i>n.</i> Heat, warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ण्य|औष्ण्यं
औष्ण्य <i>n.</i> See औष्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्म्य|औष्म्यं
औष्म्य <i>n.</i> See औष्ण, R.xvii.33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क <i>(I) m.</i> 1. Brahman (m.); 2. Viṣṇu; 3. Kāmadeva; 4. fire; 5. air, wind; 6. Yama, the god of death; 7. the sun; 5. the soul; 8. a king; 10. a peacock; 11. a bird; 12. the mind; 13. body; 14. time; 15. a cloud; 16. a word; 17. hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Happiness, pleasure (as in ‘heaven,’ according to Yāska); 2. water, सत्येन माभिरक्ष त्वं वरुणेत्यभिशाप्य कम् Yaj.ii.108, के शवं पतितं दृष्ट्या द्रोणो हर्षमुपागतः Vidagdhamukhamaṇḍana.; 3. head, e.g. कंधरांसमपहाय कं धरां प्राप्य संयति जहास कस्यचित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस|कंसं|कंसः
कंस <i>(I) m.n.</i> 1. A drinking-vessel, a cup; 2. a particular measure known as आढक; 3. bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस|कंसं|कंसः
कंस <i>(II) m.</i> Name of a king of Mathurā. (See App. II.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारि|कंसारिः
कंस-अरि, -कृष्, -जित्, -द्विष् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa, enemy and conqueror of Kansa, स्वयं संधिकारिणा कंसारिणा दूतेन Ve.i., Sis.i.16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकृष्
कंस-अरि, -कृष्, -जित्, -द्विष् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa, enemy and conqueror of Kansa, स्वयं संधिकारिणा कंसारिणा दूतेन Ve.i., Sis.i.16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसजित्
कंस-अरि, -कृष्, -जित्, -द्विष् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa, enemy and conqueror of Kansa, स्वयं संधिकारिणा कंसारिणा दूतेन Ve.i., Sis.i.16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसद्विष्
कंस-अरि, -कृष्, -जित्, -द्विष् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa, enemy and conqueror of Kansa, स्वयं संधिकारिणा कंसारिणा दूतेन Ve.i., Sis.i.16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसास्थि
कंस-अस्थि <i>n.</i> bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकार|कंसकारः
कंस-कार <i>m.</i> 1. a mixed tribe (कंसकारशंखकारौ ब्राह्मणात्संबभूवतुः); 2. a worker in pewter or white brass generally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसक|कंसकं
कंसक <i>n.</i> Bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्
कक् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1Ā (pp. कंकित)</i> 1. To wish; 2. to be proud; 3. to be unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्
कक् <i>(II) vt. 1Ā (pres. कंकते)</i> To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुंजल|ककुञ्जल|ककुंजलः|ककुञ्जलः
ककुंजल <i>m.</i> The Chātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्
ककुद् <i>f.</i> 1. A peak, a summit; 2. chief, head; 3. the bump on the shoulders of the Indian bull; 4. an ensign or symbol of royalty.(According to grammarians, ककुद् is the form which must be substituted for ककुद at the end of compounds, e.g. त्रिककुद् ‘three-peaked.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मत्|ककुद्मन्त्
ककुद्-मत् <i>m.</i> 1. a buffalo with a hump on his shoulders, मदोदग्राः ककुद्मन्तः सरितां कूलमुद्रुजाः R.iv.22, K.S.i.56; 2. a mountain, ककुद्मानिव चित्रकूटः R.xiii.47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मती
ककुद्-मती <i>f.</i> the hip and loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुत्स्थ|ककुत्स्थः
ककुद्-स्थ <i>m.</i> an epithet of पुरंजय, a king of the Solar race, R.vi.71. (See App. II.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद|ककुदं|ककुदः
ककुद <i>m.n.</i> 1. The hump on the shoulders of the Indian bull; 2. head, chief, इक्ष्वाकुवंश्यः ककुदं नृपाणाम् R.vi.71; ककुदं वेदविदाम् Mrich.i.; 3. a peak, a summit; 4. a symbol of royalty, R.iii.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=158-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिन्
ककुद्मिन् <i>m.</i> 1. A mountain; 2. a bull with a hump on his shoulders; 3. a name of king रैवत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिकन्या
ककुद्मिन्-कन्या, -सुता <i>f.</i> Revatī, wife of Balarāma, Sis.ii.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिसुता
ककुद्मिन्-कन्या, -सुता <i>f.</i> Revatī, wife of Balarāma, Sis.ii.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुंदर|ककुन्दर|ककुंदरं|ककुन्दरं
ककुंदर <i>n.</i> The cavities of the loins (ककुंदरे जघनकूपकौ Mit. on Yaj.iii.96).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ्
ककुभ् <i>f.</i> 1. A peak, a summit; 2. a quarter of the compass, e.g. विलोकयंती ककुभोऽतिभीता; 3. beauty, grace; 4. a wreath of Champaka flowers; 5. a sacred treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ <i>(I) m.</i> 1. A crooked piece of wood at the end of the lute; 2. the Arjuna tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ <i>(II) n.</i> A flower of the Kuṭaja tree, Megh.i.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कुल|कक्कुलः
कक्कुल <i>m.</i> The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोल|कक्कोलः
कक्कोल <i>(I) m.</i> Name of a plant bearing a berry, आकंपितकक्कोलैर्नमेरुकुसुमपांशुपातिभिः Kad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोल|कक्कोलः
कक्कोल <i>(II) n.</i> 1. A berry of this plant; 2. a perfume prepared from its berries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोली
कक्कोली <i>f.</i> See कक्कोल I, कक्कोली (v.l. for कंकोली) फलजग्धिमुग्धविकिरव्याहरिणः M.M.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खट|कक्खटः
कक्खट <i>a. (f. टा)</i> 1. Hard, solid; 2. laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटा
कक्खट <i>a. (f. टा)</i> 1. Hard, solid; 2. laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटी
कक्खटी <i>f.</i> Chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष|कक्षः
कक्ष <i>(I) m.</i> 1. A hiding place; 2. the interior of a forest, आशु निर्गत्य कक्षात् Rt.i.27; 3. a dry wood; 4. grass, यतस्तु कक्षस्तत एव वह्निः R.vii.55, M.vii.110; 5. a climbing plant; 6. the side or flank; 7. the armpit, प्रक्षिप्योदर्चिषं कक्षे शेरते तेऽभिमारुतम् Sis.ii.42; 8. a buffalo; 9. a gate; 10. the end of the lower garment, which, after the cloth is carried round the body, is brought up behind and tucked into the waistband; 11. the harem of a king; 12. marshy ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष|कक्षः
कक्ष <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Sin; 2. a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षावेक्षक|कक्षावेक्षकः
कक्ष-अवेक्षक <i>m.</i> 1. a superintendent of the harem; 2. a gardener; 3. a door-keeper; 4. a paramour; 5. an actor; 6. a debauchee; 7. eagerness of feeling, strength of sentiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षधर
कक्ष-धर <i>n.</i> the shoulder joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षप|कक्षपः
कक्ष-प <i>m.</i> a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षशाय|कक्षशायः
कक्ष-शाय, -शायु <i>m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षशायु|कक्षशायुः
कक्ष-शाय, -शायु <i>m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षा
कक्षा <i>f.</i> 1. An elephant’s rope; 2. a woman’s girdle; 3. the wrist; 4. a surrounding wall; 5. a courtyard, an enclosure; 6. a room, an apartment, कक्षांतराण्यद्रिपतेर्विवेश K.S.vii.70, गृहकलहंसकाननुसरन् कक्षांतरप्रधावितः Kad., M.vii.224; 7. similarity; 8. the armpit; 9. the end of the lower garment, which, after the cloth is carried round the body, is brought up behind and tucked into the waistband; 10. the waist; 11. tying up the waist; 12. an upper garment; 13. objection or reply in argument; 14. emulation, rivalry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षांतर|कक्षान्तर
कक्षा-अंतर <i>n.</i> 1. an inner room, a private apartment; 2. another room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षापट|कक्षापटः
कक्षा-पट <i>m.</i> a cloth passed between the legs to cover the privities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्या
कक्ष्या <i>f. (used in most of the senses of कक्षा)</i> 1. The girth of an elephant or horse; 2. a woman’s girdle; 3. similarity; 4. the inner apartment of a palace; 5. an upper garment; 6. the border of a garment; 7. an enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्या
कख्या <i>f.</i> An enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंक|कङ्क|कंकः|कङ्कः
कंक <i>m.</i> 1. A heron; 2. a kind of mango; 3. an epithet of Yama; 4. a Kṣatriya; 5. a false or pretended Brāhmaṇa, (e.g. Yudhiṣṭhira at the palace of Virāṭa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=159-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंकपत्र|कङ्कपत्र|कङ्कपत्रः
