कंटक|कण्टक|कंटकं|कंटकः|कण्टकः
कंटक <i>(I) m.n.</i> 1. A thorn; 2. a prickle, a sting, Yaj.iii.53; 3. a finger-nail; 4. horripilation; 5. any troublesome person who is, as it were, a thorn to the state and an enemy of order, राज्यकंटकविशोधनोद्यतः Vikr.Ch.v.1, M.ix.260, (कृत) त्रिदिवमुद्धृतदानवकंटकम् Sak.vii.; 6. a vexing speech; 7. any source of vexation, M.ix.253.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=162-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंटक|कण्टक|कंटकं|कंटकः|कण्टकः
कंटक <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A bamboo; 2. a workshop; 3. fault, defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=162-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंटकाशन|कण्टकाशन|कण्टकाशनः
