कंडूल <i>a. (f. ला)</i> Having or feeling the itch, itchy, कंडूलद्विपगंडपिंडकषणित्कंपेनसंपातिभिः Ut.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंडोल|कण्डोल|कंडोलः|कण्डोलः
कंडोल <i>m.</i> 1. A basket for holding grain; 2. a safe; 3. a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंडोली|कण्डोली
कंडोली <i>f.</i> The lute of the Chaṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंडोष|कण्डोष|कंडोषः|कण्डोषः
कंडोष <i>m.</i> A caterpillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्व|कण्वं|कण्वः
कण्व <i>m.</i> The name of a sage. (See App. II.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वदुहितृ
कण्व-दुहितृ, -सुता <i>f.</i> Śakuntalā, Kaṇva’s daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्वसुता
कण्व-दुहितृ, -सुता <i>f.</i> Śakuntalā, Kaṇva’s daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत|कतः
कत <i>(I) m.</i> The clearing-nut plant; (the nut of this tree clears turbid water), फलं कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यंबुप्रसादकम् । न नामग्रहाणादेव तस्य वारि प्रसीदति M.vi.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतक|कतकः
कत <i>(I) m.</i> The clearing-nut plant; (the nut of this tree clears turbid water), फलं कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यंबुप्रसादकम् । न नामग्रहाणादेव तस्य वारि प्रसीदति M.vi.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतक|कतकः
कतक <i>(II) n.</i> The nut of this tree, न कतकं पंकविशोधनाय Vāmanasūtra.i.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतम
कतम <i>pron. (f. मा, n. मत्)</i> who or which of many, अपि ज्ञायते कतमेन दिग्भागेन गतः स जाल्म इति Vikr.i., नगेभ्यो यांतीनां कथय तटिनीनां कतमया पुराणां संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G.L.22, अथ कतमं पुनर्क्रतुमधिकृत्य गास्यामि Sak.i., कतमं समयमाश्रित्य गीयताम् Ve.i. (कतम, however, is often used as a mere strengthened substitute for किम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतमा
कतम <i>pron. (f. मा, n. मत्)</i> who or which of many, अपि ज्ञायते कतमेन दिग्भागेन गतः स जाल्म इति Vikr.i., नगेभ्यो यांतीनां कथय तटिनीनां कतमया पुराणां संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G.L.22, अथ कतमं पुनर्क्रतुमधिकृत्य गास्यामि Sak.i., कतमं समयमाश्रित्य गीयताम् Ve.i. (कतम, however, is often used as a mere strengthened substitute for किम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतमत्
कतम <i>pron. (f. मा, n. मत्)</i> who or which of many, अपि ज्ञायते कतमेन दिग्भागेन गतः स जाल्म इति Vikr.i., नगेभ्यो यांतीनां कथय तटिनीनां कतमया पुराणां संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G.L.22, अथ कतमं पुनर्क्रतुमधिकृत्य गास्यामि Sak.i., कतमं समयमाश्रित्य गीयताम् Ve.i. (कतम, however, is often used as a mere strengthened substitute for किम्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतर
कतर <i>pron. (f. रा, n. रत्)</i> Who or which of two, नैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो यद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः Bg.ii.6. (It is sometimes used in the sense of कतम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतरा
कतर <i>pron. (f. रा, n. रत्)</i> Who or which of two, नैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो यद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः Bg.ii.6. (It is sometimes used in the sense of कतम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतरत्
कतर <i>pron. (f. रा, n. रत्)</i> Who or which of two, नैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो यद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः Bg.ii.6. (It is sometimes used in the sense of कतम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतमाल|कतमालः
कतमाल <i>m.</i> Fire. (Cf. खतमाल.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कति
कति <i>pron. (declined in the plural only; nom. and acc. कति)</i> 1. How many, एभिभूतैः स्मर कति कृताः स्वांत ते विप्रलंभाः Sant.S.iii.18. When followed by अपि, चन, or चित्, कति generally loses its interrogative character and means ‘several’ ‘some,’ कांते कत्यपि वासराणि गमय त्वं मीलयित्वा दृशो Am.S.25, तस्मिन्नद्रौ कतिचिदबलाविप्रयुक्तः स कामी नीत्वा मासान् Megh.i.2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिकृत्वस्
कति-कृत्वस् <i>ind.</i> how many times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिधा
कति-धा <i>ind.</i> 1. how often; 2. in how many places or parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपय|कतिपयः
कति-पय <i>pron. (f. या or यी)</i> 1. some, several, a certain number, वर्णैः कतिपयैरेव ग्रथितस्य स्वरैरिव Sis.ii.72, संपत्स्यंते कतिपयदिनस्थायिहंसा दशार्णाः Megh.i.23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपया
कति-पय <i>pron. (f. या or यी)</i> 1. some, several, a certain number, वर्णैः कतिपयैरेव ग्रथितस्य स्वरैरिव Sis.ii.72, संपत्स्यंते कतिपयदिनस्थायिहंसा दशार्णाः Megh.i.23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिविध
कति-विध <i>a.</i> of how many kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिशस्
कति-शस् <i>ind.</i> how many at a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थ्
कत्थ् <i>vi. or vt. 1Ā (pp. कत्थित)</i> 1. To boast, to swagger, कृत्वा कत्थिष्यते न कः Bt.xvi.4; 2. to praise, to celebrate; 3. to abuse.With वि-, 1. to boast; 2. to disparage, सदा भवान् फाल्गुनस्य गुणैरस्मान् विकत्थते Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थन
कत्थन <i>n.</i> Boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थना
कत्थना <i>f.</i> Boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्सवर|कत्सवरं
कत्सवर <i>n.</i> The shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्
कथ् <i>vt. or vi. 10U (pp. कथित)</i> 1. To converse, to hold conversation, कथयित्वा सुमंत्रेण चिरं सह Ram.; 2. to tell, to relate, to declare, अकीर्ति चापि भूतानि कथयिष्यंति तेऽव्ययाम् Bg.ii.34, R.xii.15; 3. to describe, कथाच्छलेन बालानां नीतिस्तदिह कथ्यते Hit.i.; 4. to inform, to give information about, M.xi.114; 5. to betray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथक|कथकः
कथक <i>(I) m. (fem. का)</i> A narrator, a relater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथक|कथकः
कथक <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A disputant; 2. a story-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन|कथनं
कथन <i>n.</i> Narration, relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम् <i>ind.</i> How, whence, in what way, in what manner, कथं मारात्मके त्वयि विश्वासः Hit.i., सानुबंधाः कथं न स्युः संपदो मे निरापदः R.i.64, iii.44.Sometimes कथम् introduces a question when the speaker doubts the propriety of what he says, कथमात्मानं निवेदयामि Sak.i.कथम् is often connected with the particles इव, वा, नाम, नु or स्विद् in order to generalize the interrogation, and may be rendered by ‘how indeed,’ कथं नाम तत्रभवान् धर्ममत्यक्षत्, कथं नु शक्योऽनुनयो महर्षेः R.ii.54, पीडयंते गृहिणः कथं नु तनयाविश्लेषदुःखैर्नवैः Sak.i., कथं वा गम्यते Ut.iii.When connected with the particle चन, it means ‘in every way,’ ‘in anyway,’ ‘on every account,’ ‘somehow,’ ‘with great difficulty,’ न लोकवृत्तं वर्तेत वृत्तिहेतोः कथंचन M.iv.11, उच्छिष्टेन तु संस्पृष्टो द्रव्यहस्तः कथंचन v.143, वृद्धेनोत्पादिताः पुत्रा मया चैते कथंचन Ram. With चित् or चिदपि or अपि, it means ‘by great effort,’ ‘on any account,’ ‘somehow,’ ‘with great difficulty,’ कथंचिदीडा मनसां बभूवुः K.S.iii.34, इत्यर्थमुक्त्वा कथंचित् Am.S.50, विशृज्य कथमप्युमाम् K.S.vi.3, Megh.i.3, 22, Am.S.12, 39, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंकथिक|कथङ्कथिक|कथङ्कथिकः
कथम्-कथिक <i>m.</i> an inquisitive person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंकारम्
कथम्-कारम् <i>ind.</i> how, in what manner, कथंकारमनालंबा कीर्तिर्व्यामाधिरोहति Sis.ii.52, स्वीचकार कथंकारमहो सा तरलं नलम् Na.xvii.126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंता|कथन्ता
कथम्-ता <i>f.</i> of what manner, what sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंप्रमाण
कथम्-प्रमाण <i>a.</i> of what measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंभूत
कथम्-भूत <i>a.</i> of what kind, of what nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथंरूप
कथम्-रूप <i>a.</i> of what shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=163-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथा
कथा <i>f.</i> 1. Mention, allusion, का कथा बाणसंधाने ज्याशब्देनैव दूरतः । हुंकारेणेव धनुषः स हि विघ्नानपोहति Sak.iii.; 2. conversation; 3. a tale, an account, कथापि खलु पापानामलमश्रेयसे यतः Sis.ii.40; 4. a fable, कथाच्छलेन बालानां नीतिस्तदिह कथ्यते Hit.i.; 5. a species of prose composition often distinguished from आख्यायिका (प्रबंधकल्पनां स्तोकसत्यां प्राज्ञाः कथां विदुः । परंपराश्रया या स्यात् सा मताख्यायिका बुधैः). See under आख्यायिका. The phrase का कथा (lit. ‘what mention’) is often used in the sense of ‘much more so,’ or ‘much less so,’ अभितप्तमयोऽपि मार्दवं भजते कैव कथाशरीरिषु R.viii.43, आतवागनुमानाभ्यां साध्यं स्वां प्रति का कथा x.28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानुराग|कथानुरागः
कथा-अनुराग <i>m.</i> taking pleasure in a discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथांतर|कथान्तर
कथा-अंतर <i>n.</i> 1. the course of conversation, स्मर्तव्योस्मि कथांतरेषु भवता Mrich.; 2. another tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथारंभ|कथारम्भ|कथारम्भः
कथा-आरंभ <i>m.</i> begining of a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोदय|कथोदयः
कथा-उदय <i>m.</i> the beginning of a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोद्घात|कथोद्घातः
कथा-उद्घात <i>m.</i> 1. the opening of a drama by the first character entering on the stage overhearing and repeating the last words of the prelude, as in the case of the Mudrārākshasa and the Veṇīsanhāra; 2. the beginning of a tale or narration, आकुमारकथोद्घातं शालिगोप्यो जगुर्यशः R.iv.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोपाख्यान
कथा-उपाख्यान <i>n.</i> narration, relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाछल|कथाच्छल
कथा-छल <i>n.</i> 1. the device of a fable; 2. giving a false account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथापीठ
कथा-पीठ <i>n.</i> the introductory part of a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रबंध|कथाप्रबन्ध|कथाप्रबन्धः
कथा-प्रबंध <i>m.</i> a tale, a fiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रसंग|कथाप्रसङ्ग|कथाप्रसङ्गः
कथा-प्रसंग <i>m.</i> 1. talking, conversation, the course of conversation, कथाप्रसंगेन मिथः सखीमुखात् Na.i.35; 2. a curer of poisons, कथाप्रसंगेन जनैरुदाहृतात् Kir.i.24 (where the word is used in both the senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्राण|कथाप्राणः
कथा-प्राण <i>m.</i> an actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथामुख
कथा-मुख <i>n.</i> the introductory part of a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाविपर्यास|कथाविपर्यासः
कथा-विपर्यास <i>m.</i> changing the course of a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाशेष
कथा-शेष <i>(I) m.</i> the remaining part of a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाशेष
कथा-शेष <i>(II) a.</i> one of whom only an account remains, i.e. dead. (कथाशेषतां गतः ‘dead,’ ‘deceased.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानक|कथानकं
कथानक <i>n.</i> A small tale; (the Vetālapanchavinśati is cited as an example).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथित|कथितः
कथित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Told, narrated; 2. expressed (वाच्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथिता
कथित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Told, narrated; 2. expressed (वाच्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथितपद
कथित-पद <i>n.</i> tautology, considered as a fault of composition, relating to a sentence. It consists in the use of a word without any purpose, K.Pr.vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1P (pres. कंदति)</i> 1. To grieve; 2. to cry, to weep; 3. to call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् <i>(II) vi. 4Ā (pres. कद्यते)</i> To be confused, to suffer mentally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्
कद् <i>ind.</i> This particle is used at the beginning of compounds and marks the uselessness, badness, littleness or defectiveness of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदक्षर|कदक्षरं
कद्-अक्षर <i>n.</i> 1. a bad letter; 2. bad writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=164-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदग्नि
