कल्क|कल्कः
कल्क <i>m.n.</i> 1. A viscous sediment deposited by oily substances when ground; 2. a kind of tenacious paste; 3. dirt, filth, ordure; 4. meanness, deceit, hypocrisy^1; 5. sin; 6. incense; 7. levigated powder, K.S.vii.9, Yaj.i.277.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260516. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=175-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

