कवल <i>m.n.</i> A mouthful, आस्वादवद्भिः कवलैस्तृणानाम् R.ii.5, ix.59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Eaten; 2. chewed; 3. taken, seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलिता
कवलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Eaten; 2. chewed; 3. taken, seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट <i>n.</i> The panel of a door, e.g. स्वर्गद्वारकवाटपाटनकरी काशीपुराधीश्वरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाटघ्न
कवाट-घ्न <i>m.</i> a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाटी
