कवि|कविः
कवि <i>(I) a.</i> 1. Omniscient, Bg.viii.9; 2. intelligent, clever; 3. wise, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A wise man, a thinker, a sage, M.vii.49, Bg.x.37; 2. a poet, मंदः कवियशः प्रार्थी R.i.3, इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो नमोवाकं प्रसास्महे Ut.i., Sis.ii.83; 3. an epithet of Śukra, the preceptor of the demons; 4. Brahman (m.); 5. Vālmīki, the first poet; 6. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि <i>(III) f.</i> The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविज्येष्ठ|कविज्येष्ठः
कवि-ज्येष्ठ <i>m.</i> an epithet of Vālmīki, the first poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=176-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविपुत्र|कविपुत्रः
