काकाक्षिगोलकन्याय
काक-अक्षिगोलकन्याय <i>m.</i> the maxim of the crow’s eye. It takes its origin from the belief that crows have but one eye, which, as occasion requires, they move from the cavity on one side into that of the other. And is applied to a word which serves two purposes in a sentence being put only once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=177-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

