कांडपात|काण्डपात|काण्डपातः
कांड-पात <i>m.</i> an arrow’s flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=179-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांडपृष्ठ|काण्डपृष्ठ|काण्डपृष्ठं|काण्डपृष्ठः
कांड-पृष्ठ <i>m.</i> 1. one of the military profession, a soldier; 2. the husband of a Vaiśya woman; 3. an adopted son, anyone other than one’s own son. (The word implies faithlessness to one’s own family, caste or religion and is often used as a term of reproach. स्वकुलं पृष्ठतः कृत्वा यो वै परकुलं व्रजेत् । तेन दुश्चरितेनासौ कांडपृष्ठं इति स्मृतः Mv.iii.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=179-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांडभंग
कांड-भंग <i>m.</i> a fracture of bones or limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=179-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांडवत्|काण्डवत्|काण्डवन्त्
कांड-वत् <i>m.</i> an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=179-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांडवीणा|काण्डवीणा
