कात्
कात् <i>ind.</i> A prefix implying insult or reproach (generally with कृ), e.g. यन्मयैश्चर्यमत्तेन गुरुः सदसि कात्कृतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=179-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर|कातरः
कातर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Cowardly, timid, afraid, discouraged, कातराः स्वांगदाने Sak.iii., Am.S.7, 30, 75, R.xi.78; 2. confused, perplexed; 3. tremulous through fear, R.ii.52, Am.S.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=179-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातरा
