कांति|कान्ति|कांतिः|कान्तिः
कांति <i>f.</i> 1. Desire, wish; 2. personal decoration or embellishment; 3. loveliness, beauty; 4. beauty enhanced by love (in rhetoric); (in this sense, the S.D. thus distinguishes it from शोभा and दीप्ति- रूपयौवनलालित्यं भोगाद्यैरंगभूषणम् । शोभा प्रोक्ता सैव कांतिर्मन्मथाप्यायिता द्युतिः । कांतिरेवातिविस्तीर्णा दीप्तिरित्यभिधीयते); 5. a lovely or desirable woman; 6. brilliancy, brightness, Megh.ii.21; 7. an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांतिकर|कान्तिकर
कांति-कर <i>a.</i> beautifying, illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांतिद|कान्तिद|कान्तिदं
कांति-द <i>n.</i> 1. bile; 2. clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांतिद|कान्तिद|कान्तिदं
कांति-द, -दायक <i>a.</i> adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांतिदायक|कान्तिदायक|कान्तिदायकं
कांति-द, -दायक <i>a.</i> adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

