कापिकी
कापिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> Shaped or behaving like a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल <i>(I) a. (f. ली)</i> 1. Belonging to Kapila; 2. taught by him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिली
कापिल <i>(I) a. (f. ली)</i> 1. Belonging to Kapila; 2. taught by him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल <i>(II) m.</i> A follower of the Sāṅkhya system of philosophy propounded by कपिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुष|कापुरुषः
कापुरुष <i>m.</i> A contemptible man, a coward, a wretch, दैवं प्रधानमिति कापुरुषा वदंति Panch.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

