कामात्मज|कामात्मजः
काम-आत्मज <i>m.</i> an epithet of Aniruddha, son of Pradyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मन्
काम-आत्मन् <i>a.</i> libidinous, enamoured, M.vii.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुध|कामायुधः
काम-आयुध <i>(I) n.</i> 1. arrow of the god of love; 2. membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुध|कामायुधः
काम-आयुध <i>(II) m.</i> the mango tree. See अरविन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुस्
काम-आयुस् <i>m.</i> 1. a vulture; 2. Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामार्त|कामार्त्त|कामार्त्तः
काम-आर्त <i>a.</i> overcome by love, कामार्ता हि प्रकृतिकृपणाश्चेतनाचेतनेषु Megh.i.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामासक्त
काम-आसक्त <i>a.</i> overcome with desire, impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामेप्सु
काम-ईप्सु <i>a.</i> striving to obtain the fulfilment of a desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामेश्वर|कामेश्वरः
काम-ईश्वर <i>m.</i> 1. an epithet of Kubera; 2. the supreme soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोदक|कामोदकं
काम-उदक <i>n.</i> a voluntary oblation of water to deceased friends who are not entitled to it by law, Yaj.iii.4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोपहत
काम-उपहत <i>a.</i> overcome with passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकला
काम-कला <i>f.</i> an epithet of Rati, the wife of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=180-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

