काम्या
काम्या <i>f.</i> Wish, desire, intention, R.i.35, Bg.x.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्ल
काम्ल <i>a. (f. म्ला)</i> Slightly acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्ला
काम्ल <i>a. (f. म्ला)</i> Slightly acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय|कायं|कायः
काय <i>(I) m.n.</i> 1. The body, वहति विकलः कायो मोहं न मुंचति चेतना M.M.ix., Bg.v.10; 2. the trunk of a tree; 3. the body of a lute (the whole lute except the wires); 4. assemblage, collection; 5. a home, a habitation; 6. principal, capital; 7. a butt, a mark; 8. natural temperament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय|कायं|कायः
काय <i>(II) n.</i> The part of the hand just below the fingers especially the little and the ring finger. It is regarded as the प्रजापतितीर्थ^1, M.ii.59.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260622. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय|कायं|कायः
काय <i>(III) m.</i> One of the eight forms of marriage, more generally known as प्राजापत्य q.v., Yaj.i.60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायाग्नि|कायाग्निः
काय-अग्नि <i>m.</i> the digestive faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक्लेश|कायक्लेशः
काय-क्लेश <i>m.</i> bodily suffering or pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायचिकित्सा
काय-चिकित्सा <i>f.</i> treatment of the diseases which affect the whole body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायमान|कायमानं
काय-मान <i>n.</i> measurement of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायवलन|कायवलनं
काय-वलन <i>n.</i> an armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थ|कायस्थः
काय-स्थ <i>m.</i> 1. the supreme spirit; 2. the writer-caste proceeding from a क्षत्रिय father and a शूद्र mother; 3. a man of that caste, Yaj.i.336, Mrich.ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्था
काय-स्था <i>f.</i> 1. a woman of this caste; 2. the myrobalan tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थी
काय-स्थी <i>f.</i> the wife of a कायस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थित
काय-स्थित <i>a.</i> corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक
कायक <i>a. (f. यिका)</i> Relating to the body, bodily, corporeal, M.xii.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=182-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

