काव्य <i>(I) a. (f. व्या)</i> 1. Endowed with the qualities of a sage or a poet; 2. prophetic, inspired, poetical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्या
काव्य <i>(I) a. (f. व्या)</i> 1. Endowed with the qualities of a sage or a poet; 2. prophetic, inspired, poetical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य <i>(II) m.</i> An epithet of Śukra, the teacher of Rākṣasas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य <i>(III) n.</i> 1. poetry, poetical composition (काव्य is variously defined by writers on rhetoric- (1) शरीरं तावदिष्टार्थव्यवच्छिन्ना पदावली Danḍin; (2) तददोषौ शब्दार्थौ सगुणावनलंकृती पुनः क्वापि Mammata; (3) वाक्यं रसात्मकं काव्यम् Viśvanātha; (4) रमणीयार्थप्रतिपादकः शब्दः Jagannātha); 2. a poem; 3. happiness, welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यार्थ|काव्यार्थः
काव्य-अर्थ <i>m.</i> poetic thought, poetic idea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यार्थचौर
काव्य-अर्थ˚चौर <i>m.</i> a robber of the ideas of another poet, यदस्य दैत्या इव लुंठनाय काव्यार्थचौराः प्रगुणीभवंति Vikr.Ch.i.11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यचौर|काव्यचौरः
काव्य-चौर <i>m.</i> a stealer of other poems, a plagiarist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यमीमांसक|काव्यमीमांसकः
काव्य-मीमांसक <i>m.</i> a rhetorician, a critic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यरसिक
काव्य-रसिक <i>a.</i> one who has a taste for poetical composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यलिंग|काव्यलिङ्ग
काव्य-लिंग <i>n.</i> a figure of speech thus defined by Mammata- काव्यलिंगं हेतोर्वाक्यपदार्थता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यशास्त्र
काव्य-शास्त्र <i>n.</i> the science and art of rhetoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=186-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्या
काव्या <i>f.</i> Understanding, intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्
काश् <i>(I) vi. 1Ā (pp. काशित)</i> 1. To be visible, नैवं भूमिर्न च दिशः प्रदिशो वा चकाशिरे Bh.iii.; 2. to shine, to look brilliant or beautiful, R.x.86, vii.24, K.S.i.24, Bt.ii.25; (hence) 3. to appear or look like.With प्र-, 1. to be visible; 2. to shine, to look brilliant; (hence) 3. to appear or look like.With प्रति-, 1. to appear like; 2. to shine in opposition.With वि-, 1. to open up as a flower; 2. to shine.With सम्-, to appear like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्
काश् <i>(Caus. काशयति-ते)</i> With निस्-, 1. to open; 2. to take out, to present to the sight; 3. to turn out, to banish, e.g. गृहान्निष्काशयेत्.With प्र-, 1. to show, to discover, to disclose, to reveal, अवसरोऽयमानात्मानं प्रकाशयितुम् Sak.i.; 2. to lighten, to illumine, यथा प्रकाशयत्येकः कृत्स्नं लोकमिमं रविः Bg.xiii.33; 3. to bring to light, to make public, to communicate, to proclaim, कदाचित्कुपितं मित्रं सर्वदोषं प्रकाशयेत् Cāṇakya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्
काश् <i>(II) vi. 4Ā (pp. काशित)</i> 1. To shine, to appear like; 2. to be visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश(स) <i>(I) m.n.</i> A species of grass used for mats, roofs &c., Rt.iii.1, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
काश(स) <i>(I) m.n.</i> A species of grass used for mats, roofs &c., Rt.iii.1, 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश(स) <i>(II) n.</i> A flower of that grass, K.S.vii.11, R.iv.17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
काश(स) <i>(II) n.</i> A flower of that grass, K.S.vii.11, R.iv.17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश(स) <i>(III) m.</i> 1. Cough, catarrh, काशाश्रुलालाविलः Sant.S.ii.29; 2. sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
काश(स) <i>(III) m.</i> 1. Cough, catarrh, काशाश्रुलालाविलः Sant.S.ii.29; 2. sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशि|काशिः
काशि <i>(I) m. pl.</i> The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशि|काशिः
काशि <i>(II) f.</i> Name of a celebrated city on the Ganges, the modern Benares. It is one of the seven sacred cities. See कांची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिप|काशिपः
काशि-प <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिन्
काशिन् <i>a. (f. नी) (generally at the end of compounds)</i> Shining, appearing like, having the semblance of, e.g. जितकाशिन् ‘one who deports himself like a conqueror,’ जितकाशी राजसेवकः Mud.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिनी
काशिन् <i>a. (f. नी) (generally at the end of compounds)</i> Shining, appearing like, having the semblance of, e.g. जितकाशिन् ‘one who deports himself like a conqueror,’ जितकाशी राजसेवकः Mud.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=187-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

