कुंडिर <i>m.</i> A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतप|कुतपः
कुतप <i>(I) m.</i> 1. The sun; 2. fire; 3. a guest; 4. an ox, a bull; 5. a daughter’s son; 6. a sister’s son; 7. a twice-born man; 8. the eighth muhūrta of the day, अह्णो मुहूर्ता विख्याता दश पंच च सर्वदा । तत्राष्टमो मुहूर्तो यः स कालः कुतपः स्मृतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतप|कुतपः
कुतप <i>(II) n.</i> 1. The Kuśa grass; 2. a sort of blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्
कुतस् <i>ind.</i> 1. From where, e.g. कुतस्त्वमसि संप्रातः; 2. where, where else, ईदृग्विनोदः कुतः Sak.ii.; 3. how, e.g. मदमूढबुद्धिषु विवेकिता कुतः; 4. much more, much less, e.g. न मे स्तेनो जनपदे … न स्वैरी स्वैरिणी कुतः. (कुतस् is often used in the sense of the ablative of किम्, कुतश्चित् संलपतो जनसमाजात् D.K.)अपि, चित् and चन often follow कुतस् and render its sense indefinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्त्य
कुतस्-त्य <i>ind.</i> 1. Whence come; 2. how happened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुक|कुतुकं
कुतुक <i>n.</i> 1. Desire, curiosity, inclination; 2. eagerness, vehemence, केलिकलाकुतुकेन च काचिदमुं यमुनाजलकूले । मंजुलवंजुलकुंजगतं विचकर्ष करेन दुकूले Git.G.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुप|कुतुपं|कुतुपः
कुतुप <i>m.</i> A small leathern oil-bottle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतू
कुतू <i>f.</i> A small leathern oil-bottle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहल|कुतूहलं|कुतूहलः
कुतूहल <i>(I) a. (f. ला)</i> 1. Wonderful; 2. excellent, praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहला
कुतूहल <i>(I) a. (f. ला)</i> 1. Wonderful; 2. excellent, praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहल|कुतूहलं|कुतूहलः
कुतूहल <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Desire, curiosity, (पपौ) कुतूहलेनेव मनुष्यशोणितम् R.iii.14, xiii.2, xv.65; 2. eagerness; 3. what excites curiosity, any thing interesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्र
कुत्र <i>ind.</i> 1. Where, in which place, प्रवृत्तिः कुत्र कर्तव्या Hit.i.; 2. in which case, तेजसां सहजातानां वयः कुत्रोपयुज्यते. (कुत्र is sometimes used for the loc. sing. of किम्).When followed by अपि or चित्, it becomes indefinite in sense. कुत्रचित् ‘one place-in another’ M.ix.34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रत्य
कुत्र-त्य <i>a.</i> where living or residing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स्
कुत्स् <i>vt. 10Ā (pp. कुत्सित; pres. कुत्सयते)</i> To abuse, to censure, to condemn, M.ii.54, Yaj.i.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सन|कुत्सनं
कुत्सन <i>n.</i> Abuse, contempt, abusive language, देवतानां च कुत्सनम् M.iv.163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सा
कुत्सा <i>f.</i> Abuse, contempt, abusive language, देवतानां च कुत्सनम् M.iv.163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सित|कुत्सितं|कुत्सितः
कुत्सित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Despised, contemptible, mean, hateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सिता
कुत्सित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Despised, contemptible, mean, hateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
कुथ <i>m.</i> The kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=194-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
