कृ
कृ <i>(I) vt. 5U (pres. कृणोति, कृणुते)</i> To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=201-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृ
कृ <i>(II) vt. 8U [The root is generally Atm. (with prepositions) when used in the sense of- (1) injury, (2) censure, (3) serving, (4) doing a rash act, (5) changing the condition, (6) reciting, (7) use, Pan.i.3.32.] (pp. कृत; caus. कारयति-ते; desid. चिकीर्षति) (the senses of कृ are almost infinitely modified according to the noun it is joined with.)</i> 1. to do, as in करिष्यामि प्रियं तव; 2. to manufacture, to prepare, to shape, as in कटंकरोति or यथा मृत्पिंडतः कर्ता कुरुते यद्यदिच्छति; 3. to make, as in नृपेण चक्रे युवराजशब्दभाक् R.iii.35; 4. to let out, to make, as in न मूत्रं पथि कुर्वीत M.iv.45; 5. to build, as in गृहं करोति; 6. to compose, as in इदं शास्त्रं तु कृत्वा M.i.58; 7. to form, as in अंजलिं करोति; 8. to create, to engender, as in रतिमुभयप्रार्थना कुरुते Sak.ii.; 9. to perform, as in पूजां करोति; 10. to tell, to narrate, as in कथां करोति; 11. to assume, as in नानारूपाणि कुर्वाणः Yaj.iii.162 or as in स चक्रे सुमहत्कायम् or स माणुषीं गिरं कृत्वा; 12. to execute, to carry out, to obey, as in करुष्व मम शासनम् or न तदाज्ञां चकार सा or करिष्ये वचनं तव Bg.xviii.73; 13. to cook, as in कृतान्न; 14. to effect, to accomplish, as in किं नाम खलसंसर्गः कुरुते नाश्रयाशवत् Hit.ii.; 15. to make a sound, as in फट्कृत्य, फुत्कृत्य, स्वधाकृत्य, स्वाहाकृत्य; 16. to spend, as in कालं करोति; 17. to appoint, as in अध्यक्षान् विविधान्कुर्यात् तत्र तत्र विपश्चितः M.vii.81; 18. to put, to place, (with a loc.), as in उत्संगे शिरः कृत्वा or उरसि हस्तं कृत्वा; 19. to think, to regard, as in राज्यं तृणवत्कृत्वा; 20. to do anything for the advantage or injury of another, (with gen. or loc. of the person), as in असौ किं मे करिष्यति or यदनेन कृतं मयि; 21. to direct towards, to turn the attention to, as in मा शोके मनः कृथा.With adverbs ending in सात्, कृ means ‘to reduce wholly to,’ ‘to cause to become,’ ‘to make subject,’ e.g. आत्मसात् कृ ‘to subject to one’s self’; भस्मसात् कृ ‘to reduce to ashes’; अस्त्राणि कृ ‘to practice the use of weapons’; उदकं कृ ‘to offer a libation of water to the dead’; कन्यां कृ ‘to violate a maiden’; कालं कृ ‘to die’; चिरं कृ ‘to be long in doing anything, to delay’; दर्दुरं कृ ‘to play on the the lute’; नखानि कृ ‘to clean one’s nails’; पदं कृ ‘to set foot on’ (lit. and fig.), e.g. करिष्यसि पदं पुनराश्रमेऽस्मिन् Sak.iv., क्रमेण च कृतं मे वपुषि नवयौवनेन पदम् Kad.; मनसां कृ ‘to think of, to meditate’; मनसि कृ 1. to determine, to resolve upon; 2. ‘to think’ आलोकमात्रेणैव अपगतश्रमो दृष्ट्वा मनस्येवमकरोत् Kad.; मतिं कृ, बुद्धिं कृ ‘to think of, to intend, to mean’; मध्ये कृ ‘to have reference to,’ मध्येकृत्य स्थितं क्रथकैशिकान् Mal.v.; वशे कृ ‘to place in subjection’; विना कृ ‘to separate from, to be abandoned by’; सख्यं कृ ‘to contract friendship with.’With nouns, adjectives and indeclinables, कृ is often used to form verbs, somewhat like the affix ‘en’ or ‘fy’ in English. The usual meaning is ‘to make a person or thing to be what it is not previously,’ but sometiuies other modifications (some of which are given above) of the sense also take place. Thus कृष्णी कृ means ‘to make that (which is not black) black,’ ‘to blacken’; उच्चक्षू कृ ‘to make one (who has not done so before) to raise his eyes (eager)’; क्रोडीकृ ‘to embrace’; तृणीकृ ‘to value (as little) as grass’; प्रवणीकृ ‘to incline, to induce’; भस्मीकृ ‘to reduce to ashes’; मंदीकृ ‘to make slow, to slaken’; शूलाकृ ‘to roast on the end of a pointed poker’; समयाकृ ‘to ‘pass time’; सुखाकृ ‘to please, to satisfy.’ Some of these are given below, but the number of verbs that can be so formed is practically unlimited.With अंगी-, 1. to favour, यस्ताद्यते दयितया प्रणयापराधात् सोऽंगीकृतो भगवता मकरध्वजेन Am.S.52; 2. to accept; 3. to confess, to acknowledge; 4. to promise, to undertake, e.g. किं त्वंगीकृतमुत्सृजन्कृपणववछ्लाघ्यो जनो लज्जते Mud.ii.With अति-, to exceed, to surpass.With अधि-, 1. to be entitled, to have a right, to be invested with authority, नैवाध्यकारिष्महि वेदवृत्ते Bt.ii.34, Yaj.ii.30; 2. to have reference to. (अधिकृत्य is often used in the sense of ‘with reference to,’ ‘referring to,’ ‘with regard to,’ ‘on the subject of,’ ग्रीष्मसमयमधिकृत्य गीयताम् Sak.i., R.xi.62); 3. to bear, अधिचक्रे न यं हरिः Bt.viii.20; 4. to overcome, [in (3) and (4) the root is Atm.]; 5. to refrain from.With अनु-, (Par.) 1. to imitate, to follow, M.ii.199; 2. to look like, to be like (often with the gen.), अनुकरोति भगवतो नारायणस्य Kad. With अप-, 1. to wrong, to insult, योपचक्रे वनात् सीताम् Bt.viii.20; 2. to injure, to inflict injury on, (with the gen. of the person injured), यस्य किंचिदपकर्तुमक्षमः Māgha quoted in K.Pr.x.With अपा-, 1. to remove, न पुत्रवात्सल्यमपाकरिष्यति K.S.v.14; 2. to put aside, to give up, शिवा भुजच्छेदमपाचकार R.vii.50.With अभ्यंतरी-, 1. to initiate in; 2. to make a friend of. (See under अभ्यंतर)With अलं-, to adorn, उभावलंचक्रतुरंचिताभ्यां तपोवनावृत्तिपथं गताभ्याम् R.ii.18.With आविस्-, to make manifest, to make visible, to show (See under आविस्).With उप-, (pres. उपकरोति) 1. to befriend, to serve, to assist, to oblige (often with the gen. or loc. of the person obliged, M.ii.149), Bt.viii.18. In Megh.ii.38 (आत्मनश्चोपकर्तुम्) Mall. renders उपकर्तुम् by “परोपकारेण कृतार्थयितुम्”; 2. to attend on, to wait upon; (pres. उप्स्करोति); 3. to adorn, to decorate; 4. to make efforts, (with a gen.), Bt.vii.119; 5. to prepare, to elaborate, to perfect.With उपा-, 1. to deliver; 2. to perform a preparatory rite, M.iv.95; See उपाकर्मन्; 3. to consecrate by hymns.With उरी, उररी, उरुरी, ऊरी or ऊररी used in all the senses of अंगीकृ, R.xv.70; See under उरी.With कात्-, to contemn. See under कात्.With खली-, See under खल.With तिरस्-, 1. to abuse, to revile, to contemn; 2. to conquer. See under तिरस्.With स्वं-, to thou anybody as an insult.With दक्षिणी or प्रदक्षिणी-, to walk round something keeping the right side towards it, e.g. प्रदक्षिणीकृत्य हुतं हुताशमनंतरं भर्तुररुंधतीं च R.ii.71.With दुष्-, to act wrongly.With धिक्-, to reproach, to condemn. (See under धिक्.)With नमस्-, to salute, to adore, मुनित्रयं नमस्कृत्य S.K. See under नमस्.With नि-, to injure to wrong.With निस्-, to remove, to break, to frustrate, Bt.xv.54.With निरा-, 1. to make light of, to condemn; 2. to expel, R.xiv.57, Bt.v.100; 3. to refute, to give up; 4. to annihilate.With न्यक्-, to insult, to contemn.With परा-, (Par.) to reject, to disregard, to take no notice of, तां हनूमान् पराकुर्वन्नगमत् पुष्यकं प्रति Bt.viii.50.With परि-, (pres. परिकरोति) 1. to surround; (pres. परिष्करोति); 2. to polish, to refine, to adorn, परिष्कुर्वंत्यर्थान् सहृदयधुरीणाः कतिपये R.G. With पुरस्-, to place in front, हते जरति गांगेये पुरस्कृत्य शिखंडिनम् Ve.ii. See under पुरस्.With प्र-, to commence (it is also used in many senses of कृ without any change of meaning). See Am.S.13, M.viii.239, R.i.6, M.vii.54, 60. In Bt.viii.19, it has the sense of ‘to assault, to insult’).With प्रति-, to requite, to repay, पूर्वं कृतार्थो मित्राणां नार्थं प्रतिकरोति यः Ram.iv.; 2. to remedy, व्याधिमिच्छामि ते ज्ञातुं प्रतिकुर्यां हि तत्र वै Bh.; 3. to retaliate, R.xii.94; 4. to restore, to replace, M.ix.285.With प्रमाणी-, 1. to mete out, e.g. दैवेन प्रभुणा स्वयं जगति यद्यस्य प्रमाणीकृतम् Bhartr.ii.(misc.)11; 2. to believe, to confide.With प्रादुस्-, to make manifest, to make visible, to show. See under प्रादुस्.With प्रत्युप-, to requite, to return (an obligation).With वि-, 1. to alter, to change, विकारहेतो सति विक्रियंते येषं न चेतांसि त एव धीराः K.S.i.59, R.xiii.42; 2. to disfigure, M.xi.52; 3. to create, to effect, M.i.75; 4. to utter (Atm.), Bt.viii.20; 5. to injure, to disturb, हीनान्यनुपकर्तॄणि प्रवृद्धानि विकुर्वते R.xvii.58.With विप्र-, 1. to trouble, to harass, K.S.ii.1; 2. to affect, to cause change in, कं न विप्रकुर्युः K.S.vi.95.With व्या-, 1. to make manifest, नामरूपे व्याकरवाणि Chando.U.; 2. to explain; 3. to tell, to narrate, तन्मे सर्वं भगवान् व्याकरोतु Bh.iii.With सम्-, (pres. संकुरुते) 1. to commit, ये … … पापानि संकुर्वते Mrich.ix.; 2. to perform; 3. to manufacture; (pres. संस्कुरुते); 4. to consecrate by the recital of mantras, M.v.36; 5. to perform purificatory ceremonies over (a person), संचस्करोभयप्रीत्या मैथिलेयौ यथाविधि R.xv.31; 6. to adorn, ककुभं समस्कुरुत माधवनीम् Sis.ix.25; 7. to polish, to refine, to train, वाण्येका समलंकरोति पुरुषं या संस्कृता धार्यते Bhartr.ii.19.With साची-, to turn aside, साचीकृतचारुवक्त्रR.vi.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=201-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृक|कृकः
कृक <i>m.</i> The throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकण|कृकणः
कृकण(र) <i>m.</i> A kind of partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकर|कृकरः
कृकण(र) <i>m.</i> A kind of partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलास|कृकलासः
कृक(कु)लास <i>m.</i> A lizard, a chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकुलास
कृक(कु)लास <i>m.</i> A lizard, a chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकु|कृकवाकुः
कृकवाकु <i>m.</i> 1. A cock; 2. a peacock; 3. a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकुध्वज|कृकवाकुध्वजः
कृकवाकु-ध्वज <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकाटिका
कृकाटिका <i>f.</i> The raised and straight part of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृच्छ्रः|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र <i>(I) a. (f. च्छ्रा)</i> 1. Causing trouble, painful; 2. bad, miserable, wicked; 3. being in a painful situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रा
कृच्छ्र <i>(I) a. (f. च्छ्रा)</i> 1. Causing trouble, painful; 2. bad, miserable, wicked; 3. being in a painful situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृच्छ्रः|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र <i>(II) m.n.</i> 1. Difficulty, trouble, hardship, calamity, danger, कृच्छ्रं महत्तीर्णः R.xiv.6, M.vi.78; 2. bodily mortification, penance, expation, M.iv.222, xi.191.(कृच्छ्रम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘miserably,’ ‘painfully,’ ‘with difficulty.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रप्राण
कृच्छ्र-प्राण <i>a.</i> 1. one whose life is in danger; 2. breathing with difficulty; 3. hardly supporting life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रसाध्य
कृच्छ्र-साध्य <i>a.</i> 1. curable with difficulty (as a disease); 2. accomplished with difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् <i>(I) vt. 6P (pp. कृत्त; pres. कृंतति)</i> 1. To cut, to cut off, to divide, to tear asunder, to destroy, प्रहरति विधिर्मर्मच्छेदी न कृंतति जीवितम् M.M.ix., M.viii.12, Bt.xvi.15, ix.42, xv.97.With अव-, to cut off, to tear asunder, to divide.With उद्-, 1. to tear out, उत्क्रियोत्कृत्य कृतिम् M.M.v.; 2. to cut off, R.xii.49.With नि-, to cut off, to tear off, निकृंतान्निव मानसम् Bt.vii.11, भल्लनिकृत्तकंठैः R.vi.58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् <i>(II) vt. 7P (pp. कृत्त)</i> 1. To surround; 2. to spin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् <i>(I) a. (generally at the end of compounds)</i> doer, maker, performer, manufacturer, composer &c. See Bg.xv.15, M.i.18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्
कृत् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. An affix used to form nouns from roots; 2. a noun formed by a Kṛt affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Done, performed, made, manufactured, (pp. of कृत् q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृता
कृत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Done, performed, made, manufactured, (pp. of कृत् q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Work, deed, movement, M.vii.197; 2. service, benefit; 3. consequence, result; 4. name of that side of a die which is marked with four points; 5. name of the first of the four Yugas of the world extending over 17,28,000 years of men, See M.i.69, and Kull. on it; 6. the number ‘4.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताकृत|कृताकृतः
कृत-अकृत <i>a.</i> done and not done, i.e. done in part but not completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतांक|कृताङ्क|कृताङ्कः
कृत-अंक <i>(I) a.</i> 1. marked, branded, M.viii.281; 2. numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतांक|कृताङ्क|कृताङ्कः
कृत-अंक <i>(II) m.</i> that side of a die which is marked with four points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतांजलि|कृताञ्जलि|कृताञ्जलिः
कृत-अंजलि <i>a.</i> one who joins the hands in reverence, Bg.xi.14, M.iv.154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुकर
कृत-अनुकर <i>a.</i> following another’s example, subservient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुसार|कृतानुसारः
कृत-अनुसार <i>m.</i> custom, usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतांत|कृतान्त|कृतान्तः
कृत-अंत <i>(I) a.</i> causing an end, terminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतांत|कृतान्त|कृतान्तः
कृत-अंत <i>(II) m.</i> 1. fate, destiny, न सहते संगमं नौकृतांतः Megh.ii.42; 2. Yama, the god of death, द्वितीयं कृतांतमिवाटंतं व्याधमपश्यत् Hit.i.); 3. a demonstrated conclusion, a dogma, a proved doctrine; 4. a sinful or inauspicious action; 5. an epithet of Saturn; 6. Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतांतजनक|कृतान्तजनक|कृतान्तजनकः
कृत-अंत˚जनक <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्न
कृत-अन्न <i>n.</i> 1. cooked food, कृतान्नमुदकं स्त्रियः M.iv.219, xi.3; 2. digested food, excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापराध
कृत-अपराध <i>a.</i> guilty, criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभय
कृत-अभय <i>a.</i> saved from fear or danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभिषेक|कृताभिषेकः
कृत-अभिषेक <i>a.</i> crowned, inaugurated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभ्यास
कृत-अभ्यास <i>a.</i> practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थ|कृतार्थः
कृत-अर्थ <i>a.</i> 1. successful; 2. satisfied, contented, कृतः कृतार्थोऽस्मि निबर्हितांहसा Sis.i.29, R.viii.3; 3. clever. (कृतार्थीकृ ‘to maintain,’ कांतं प्रत्युपचारतश्चतुरया कोपः Am.S.15).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधान
कृत-अवधान <i>a.</i> 1. careful, cautious; 2. attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधि
कृत-अवधि <i>a.</i> fixed, appointed, bounded, limited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावस्थ
कृत-अवस्थ <i>a.</i> 1. summoned, made present; 2. fixed, settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्त्र
कृत-अस्त्र <i>a.</i> 1. armed; 2. skilled in the practice of arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागम
कृत-आगम <i>(I) a.</i> advanced, proficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागम
कृत-आगम <i>(II) m.</i> the supreme soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागस्
कृत-आगस् <i>a.</i> offending, criminal, sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतात्मन्
कृत-आत्मन् <i>a.</i> 1. having control over himself, of a self-governed spirit; 2. purified in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभरण
कृत-आभरण <i>a.</i> adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतायास
कृत-आयास <i>a.</i> labouring, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताह्वान
कृत-आह्वान <i>a.</i> challenged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोत्साह
कृत-उत्साह <i>a.</i> making effort, striving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोद्वाह
कृत-उद्वाह <i>a.</i> 1. making penance by standing with up-lifted hands; 2. married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपकार
कृत-उपकार <i>a.</i> 1. befriended, assisted; 2. friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपभोग
कृत-उपभोग <i>a.</i> used, enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर्मन्|कृतकर्म्मन्
कृत-कर्मन् <i>(I) a.</i> 1. one who has done his work, R.ix.3; 2. skilful, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर्मन्|कृतकर्म्मन्
कृत-कर्मन् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. the supreme spirit; 2. a sannyāsin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकाम
कृत-काम <i>a.</i> one whose desire is attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकाल|कृतकालः
कृत-काल <i>(I) a.</i> fixed or settled as to time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकाल|कृतकालः
कृत-काल <i>(II) m.</i> appointed time, Yaj.ii.184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकृत्य|कृतकृत्यः
कृत-कृत्य <i>a.</i> 1. who has accomplished or attained his object, Bg.xv.20; 2. satisfied, contented, Sant.S.iii.19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रय|कृतक्रयः
कृत-क्रय <i>m.</i> a purchaser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्षण
कृत-क्षण <i>a.</i> 1. one who is waiting impatiently for the exact moment, e.g. कृतक्षणोहं ते गमनं प्रति; 2. one who has got an opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघ्न|कृतघ्नः
कृत-घ्न <i>a.</i> 1. ungrateful, M.iv.214; 2. defeating all previous measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतचूड|कृतचूडः
कृत-चूड <i>m.</i> a boy on whom the ceremony of tonsure has been performed, M.v.58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञ|कृतज्ञः
कृत-ज्ञ <i>(I) a.</i> 1. grateful, M.vii.209, 210; 2. correct in conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञ|कृतज्ञः
कृत-ज्ञ <i>(II) m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृततीर्थ
कृत-तीर्थ <i>a.</i> 1. one who has visited holy places; 2. one who has studied with a professional teacher; 3. fertile in expedients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदास|कृतदासः
कृत-दास <i>m.</i> a servant hired for a stated period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतधी
कृत-धी <i>a.</i> 1. prudent, considerate; 2. learned, educated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिर्णेजन|कृतनिर्णेजनः
कृत-निर्णेजन <i>m.</i> a penitent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिश्चय
कृत-निश्चय <i>a.</i> resolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपुंख|कृतपुङ्ख|कृतपुङ्खः
कृत-पुंख <i>a.</i> skilled in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्व|कृतपूर्व्व
कृत-पूर्व <i>a.</i> done formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रतिकृत
कृत-प्रतिकृत <i>n.</i> assault and counter-assault, R.xii.94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रतिज्ञ
कृत-प्रतिज्ञ <i>a.</i> 1. one who has taken a vow; 2. one who has fulfilled his promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतबुद्धि
कृत-बुद्धि <i>a.</i> learned, educated, wise, M.i.97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमुख|कृतमुखः
कृत-मुख <i>a.</i> learned, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतलक्षण|कृतलक्षणः
कृत-लक्षण <i>a.</i> 1. stamped, branded, M.ix.239; 2. excellent, amiable; 3. defined, discriminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविद्य
कृत-विद्य <i>a.</i> learned, सुवर्णपुष्पितां पृथ्वीं विचिन्वंति त्रयो जनाः । शूरश्च कृतविद्यश्च यश्च जानाति सेवितुम् Panch.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेतन|कृतवेतनः
कृत-वेतन <i>a.</i> hired, paid, (as a servant), Yaj.ii.164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेदिन्
कृत-वेदिन् <i>a.</i> See कृतज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेश
कृत-वेश <i>a.</i> attired, decorated, गतवति कृतवेशे केशवे कुंजशय्याम् Git.G.xi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशोभ
कृत-शोभ <i>a.</i> 1. splendid; 2. beautiful; 3. dexterous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशौच
कृत-शौच <i>a.</i> purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतश्रम|कृतश्रमः
कृत-श्रम <i>a.</i> studied, e.g. पुराणे कृतश्रमः ‘who has spent his labours over Purāṇa, i.e. who has studied that branch of literature.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंकल्प
कृत-संकल्प <i>a.</i> resolved, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंकेत|कृतसङ्केत
कृत-संकेत <i>a.</i> making an appointment, नामसमेतं कृतसंकेतं वादयते मृदुवेणुम् Git.G.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंज्ञ
कृत-संज्ञ <i>a.</i> restored to consciousness or animation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंनाह
कृत-संनाह <i>a.</i> cased in armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसापत्निका
कृत-सापत्निका <i>f.</i> a woman whose husband has married another wife, a married woman having a co-wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्त|कृतहस्तः
कृत-हस्त, -हस्तक <i>a.</i> 1. dexterous, clever, skilful; 2. skilled in archry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्तक
कृत-हस्त, -हस्तक <i>a.</i> 1. dexterous, clever, skilful; 2. skilled in archry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्तता
कृत-हस्तता <i>f.</i> 1. skill, dexterity; 2. skill in handling arms, कौरव्ये कृतहस्तता पुनरियं देवे यथा सीरिनि Ve.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=203-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक|कृतकं|कृतकः
कृतक <i>a. (f. का)</i> 1. Done, created, e.g. यद्यत्कृतं तत्तदनित्यम्; 2. artificial, कृतकविधिसर्वांगीणमाकल्पजातम् R.xviii.52; 3. adopted (as a son), यस्योपेतं कृतकतनयः कांतया वर्धितो मे (बालमंदारवृक्षः) Megh.ii.12; 4. assumed, simulated, false, कृतककलहं कृत्वा स्वतंत्रेन किंचित् कालांतर व्यवहर्तव्यमित्यार्यादेशः Mud.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतका
कृतक <i>a. (f. का)</i> 1. Done, created, e.g. यद्यत्कृतं तत्तदनित्यम्; 2. artificial, कृतकविधिसर्वांगीणमाकल्पजातम् R.xviii.52; 3. adopted (as a son), यस्योपेतं कृतकतनयः कांतया वर्धितो मे (बालमंदारवृक्षः) Megh.ii.12; 4. assumed, simulated, false, कृतककलहं कृत्वा स्वतंत्रेन किंचित् कालांतर व्यवहर्तव्यमित्यार्यादेशः Mud.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतम्
कृतम् <i>ind.</i> Enough, no more of, (with the inst.), अथवा कृतं संदेहेन Sak.i., अथवा गिरा कृतम् R.xi.41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृति|कृतिः
कृति <i>f.</i> 1. Doing, manufacturing; 2. action; 3. creation, work, composition, श्रीश्रीहर्षकवेः कृतिः कृतिमुदे तस्याभ्युदीयादियम् Na.xxii.155, R.xv.33, 64, 69; 4. magic, enchantment; 5. injuring, killing; 6. the number ‘20’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिकर|कृतिकरः
कृति-कर <i>m.</i> an epithet of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिन्
कृतिन् <i>a. (f. नी) (often used as a noun)</i> 1. Expert, clever, wise, learned, तं क्षुरप्रशकलीकृतं कृती R.xi.29, Kir.ii.9; 2. good, virtuous, pious, तावदेवकृतिनामपि स्फुरस्येव निर्मलविवेकदीपकः Bhartr.i.56; 3. fortunate, lucky; 4. obeying, doing what is enjoined; 5. one who has done his work or obtained his desire, satisfied, contented, न खल्वनिर्जित्य रघुं कृती भवान् R.iii.51, xii.64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिनी
कृतिन् <i>a. (f. नी) (often used as a noun)</i> 1. Expert, clever, wise, learned, तं क्षुरप्रशकलीकृतं कृती R.xi.29, Kir.ii.9; 2. good, virtuous, pious, तावदेवकृतिनामपि स्फुरस्येव निर्मलविवेकदीपकः Bhartr.i.56; 3. fortunate, lucky; 4. obeying, doing what is enjoined; 5. one who has done his work or obtained his desire, satisfied, contented, न खल्वनिर्जित्य रघुं कृती भवान् R.iii.51, xii.64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृते
कृते <i>ind. (with a gen. if not compounded)</i> For, for the sake of, on account of, अपि त्रैलोक्यराज्यस्य हेतोः किं नु महीकृते Bg.i.35, Yaj.i.216, विधिना कस्य कृते विनिर्मिता R.G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतेन
कृते <i>ind. (with a gen. if not compounded)</i> For, for the sake of, on account of, अपि त्रैलोक्यराज्यस्य हेतोः किं नु महीकृते Bg.i.35, Yaj.i.216, विधिना कस्य कृते विनिर्मिता R.G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=204-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्ति|कृत्तिः
कृत्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Skin, hide, especially the hide of an antelope on which a religious student sits; 2. the bark of the birch tree used for writing; 3. one of the lunar mansions, Pleiades.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवास|कृत्तिवासः
कृत्ति-वास, -वासस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva, स कृत्तिवासास्तपसे यतात्मा K.S.i.54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवासस्
कृत्ति-वास, -वासस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva, स कृत्तिवासास्तपसे यतात्मा K.S.i.54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिका
कृत्तिका <i>f. pl.</i> 1. The third of the 27 constellations consisting of 6 stars, the Pleiades; 2. those six stars represented as six nymphs nursing Kārtikeya, the god of war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकातनय|कृत्तिकातनयः
कृत्तिका-तनय, -पुत्र, -सुत <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकापुत्र|कृत्तिकापुत्रः
कृत्तिका-तनय, -पुत्र, -सुत <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकासुत|कृत्तिकासुतः
कृत्तिका-तनय, -पुत्र, -सुत <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकाभव|कृत्तिकाभवः
कृत्तिका-भव <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्नु|कृत्नुः
कृत्नु <i>(I) a.</i> 1. Working well, able to work powerful; 2. skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्नु|कृत्नुः
कृत्नु <i>(II) m.</i> A mechanic, an artist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्य|कृत्यं|कृत्यः
कृत्य <i>(I) a. (f. त्या)</i> 1. What ought to be done, right, proper; 2. practicable; 3. who may be seduced from allegiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्या
कृत्य <i>(I) a. (f. त्या)</i> 1. What ought to be done, right, proper; 2. practicable; 3. who may be seduced from allegiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्य|कृत्यं|कृत्यः
कृत्य <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Work, deed, action, commission, कूजद्भिरापादितवंशकृत्यम् R.ii.12, 51; 2. duty, M.ii.237; 3. purpose, end; 4. motive, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्य|कृत्यं|कृत्यः
कृत्य <i>(III) m.</i> A class of affixes forming future passive participles &c., (e.g. तव्य, अनीय, य, एलिम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्या
कृत्या <i>f.</i> 1. Action, deed; 2. magic; 3. a female deity to whom sacrifices are offered for destructive purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम <i>(I) a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Artificial, not spontaneous, R.xiii.75, xix.37; 2. adopted (as a child).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमा
कृत्रिम <i>(I) a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Artificial, not spontaneous, R.xiii.75, xix.37; 2. adopted (as a child).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम <i>(II) m.</i> A grown up boy who is adopted without the consent of his natural parents (कृत्रिमः स्यात् स्वयंकृतः Yaj.ii.131, M.ix.159, 169.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम <i>(III) n.</i> 1. A kind of salt; 2. a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

