कृष्
कृष् <i>(I) vt. 1P (pp. कृष्ट)</i> 1. To draw, to drag, to pull, to tear, प्रसह्य सिंहः किल तां चकर्षR.ii.27; 2. to attract, Bg.xv.7; 3. to lead or conduct, as an army, e.g. स सेनां महतीं कर्षन् R.iv.32; 4. to bond (as a bow), नात्यायतकृष्टशार्ङ्गः R.v.50; 5. to become master of, to overpower, to subdue, बलवानिंद्रियग्रामो विद्वांसमपि कर्षति M.ii.215; 6. to plough, e.g. अनुलोमकृष्टं क्षेत्रं प्रतिलोमं कर्षति; 7. to obtain, e.g. कर्षति च महद्यशः.With अप-, 1. to draw back or away, to pull off, to take away, to drag away, दंतच्छदं प्रियतमेन निपीतसारं दंताग्रभिन्नमपकृष्य निरीक्षते च Rt.iv.14, R.xvi.55; 2. to lessen, to diminish.With अव-, to draw, to draw away from.With आ-, 1. to draw, to draw towards, to pull, to attract, दूरममुना सारंगेण वयमाकृष्टाः Sak.i., नाकस्माद् युवती वृद्धं केशेष्वाकृष्य चुंबति Hit.i., Am.S.72, K.S.ii.59, R.i.23; 2. to bend, as a bow, Sis.ix.40; 3. to snatch, to take by force, Bt.xvi.30; 4. to supply a word or words from a previous sentence.With उद्-, 1. to draw up, to pull up, to extricate, अंगदकोटिलग्नं प्रालंबमुत्कृष्य R.vi.14; 2. to enhance, to increase.With नि-, to sink down, to diminish.With निस्-, 1. to draw out, to pull out; 2. to exact, to snatch, to take by force, निष्क्रष्टुमर्थं चकमे कुबेरात् R.v.26.With परि-, to draw, to pull, to drag.With प्र-, 1. to draw away, to pull, to attract; 2. to lead, as an army; 3. to bend, as a bow.With वि-, 1. to draw, to pull; 2. to bend, as a bow, करासनं तेषु विकृष्यतामिदम् Sak.vi.With विप्र-, to remove.With संनि-, to make near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=205-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

