क्लद् <i>(I) vt. 1P (pp. क्लंदित)</i> 1. To call, to call out; 2. to cry, to lament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लद्
क्लद् <i>(II) vt. 4Ā (pres. क्लद्यते)</i> To be confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम्
क्लम् <i>vi. 1P, 4P (pp. क्लांत)</i> To be fatigued or tired, to be depressed, न चक्लाम न विव्यथे Bt.v.102, xiv.101.With वि-, to be fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम|क्लमः
क्लम <i>m.</i> Fatigue, languor, exhaustion, विनोदितदिनक्लमाः कृतरुचश्च जांबूनदैः Sis.iv.66, M.vii.151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमथ|क्लमथः
