क्लिशिता
क्लिशित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Distressed, suffering pain or misery; 2. tormented; 3. faded; 4. self contradictory speech, e.g. माता मे वंध्या, (pp. of क्लिश् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्टि|क्लिष्टिः
क्लिष्टि <i>f.</i> 1. Affliction, anguish, pain; 2. service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीब|क्लीबः
क्लीब(व) <i>(I) a. (f. बा)</i> 1. Impotent, emasculated, M.iii.150; 2. unmanly, timid, weak-minded, R.viii.84; 3. base, idle; 4. of the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
