क्लीबा
क्लीब(व) <i>(I) a. (f. बा)</i> 1. Impotent, emasculated, M.iii.150; 2. unmanly, timid, weak-minded, R.viii.84; 3. base, idle; 4. of the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीब|क्लीबः
क्लीब(व) <i>(II) m.n.</i> 1. An impotent man, a eunuch; (he is thus described by Kat.- न मूत्रं फेनिलं यस्य विष्ठा चाप्सु निमज्जति । मेढ्रंचोन्मादशुक्राभ्यां हीनं क्लीबः स उच्यते); 2. the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीब(व) <i>(II) m.n.</i> 1. An impotent man, a eunuch; (he is thus described by Kat.- न मूत्रं फेनिलं यस्य विष्ठा चाप्सु निमज्जति । मेढ्रंचोन्मादशुक्राभ्यां हीनं क्लीबः स उच्यते); 2. the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेद|क्लेदः
क्लेद <i>m.</i> 1. Wetness, moisture, R.vii.27; 2. running, discharge from a sore; 3. distress, pain, suffering, R.xv.32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश|क्लेशः
क्लेश <i>m.</i> 1. Pain, anguish, trouble, suffering, क्लेशः फलेन हि पुनर्नवतां विधत्ते K.S.v.86, Bg.xii.5, xviii.8; 2. wrath, anger; 3. worldly occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=217-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशक्षम
