क्षपण|क्षपणः
क्षपण <i>(I) m.</i> a Bauddha mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण|क्षपणः
क्षपण <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Defilement, impurity; 2. destroying, suppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणक|क्षपणकः
क्षपणक <i>m.</i> A Bauddha or Jaina mendicant, नग्नक्षपणके देशे रजकः किं करिष्यति Cāṇakya.110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणी
क्षपणी <i>f.</i> 1. An oar; 2. a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण्यु|क्षपण्युः
क्षपण्यु <i>m.</i> An offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपा
क्षपा <i>f.</i> 1. A night, विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः Sak.vi., R.ii.20; 2. turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाट|क्षपाटः
क्षपा-अट <i>m.</i> a demon, a goblin, ततः क्षपाटैः पृथुपिंगलाक्षैः Bt.ii.30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाकर|क्षपाकरः
क्षपा-कर, -नाथ <i>m.</i> 1. the moon; 2. camphire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपानाथ|क्षपानाथः
क्षपा-कर, -नाथ <i>m.</i> 1. the moon; 2. camphire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाघन|क्षपाघनः
क्षपा-घन <i>m.</i> a dark cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाचर|क्षपाचरः
क्षपा-चर <i>m.</i> a demon, a goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्
क्षम् <i>vt. 1Ā, 4P (pp. क्षांत or क्षमित; pres. क्षमते, क्षाम्यति)</i> 1. To be patient or quiet; 2. to allow, to suffer, अतो नृपाश्चक्षमिरे समेताः स्त्रीरत्नलाभं न तदात्मजस्य R.vii.34; 3. to pardon, to forgive, निघ्नस्य मे भर्तृनिदेशरौक्ष्यं देवि क्षमस्वेति बभूवः नम्रः R.xiv.58; 4. to endure, to put up with, आज्ञाभंगकरान्राजा न क्षमेत सुतानपि Hit.ii.; 5. to resist; 6. to be competent or able to do anything, ऋते रवेः क्षालयितुं क्षमेत कः क्षपातमस्कांडमलीमसं नभः Sis.i.38, ix.65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम <i>a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Patient, enduring, submissive; 2. adequate, competent, able, (with loc. or inf.), e.g. मलिनो हि यथादर्शो रूपालोकस्य न क्षमः Yaj.iii.141, हृदयं न त्ववलंबितुं क्षमाः R.viii.59, xi.6, K.S.iii.16; 3. friendly, favourable; 4. bearble, tolerable; 5. appropriate, suitable, आत्मकर्मक्षमं देहं क्षात्रो धर्म इवाश्रितः R.i.13; 6. fit for, इदं वपुस्तपःक्षमं साधयितुं य इच्छति Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=219-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमा
