क्षिप्
क्षिप् <i>vt. 6U (but Par. when preceded by अभि, प्रति and अति) 4P (pp. क्षिप्त; pres. क्षिपति-ते, क्षिप्यति)</i> 1. To throw, to cast, to send, to let go, यथा महाह्रदं प्राप्य क्षिप्तं लोहं विनश्यति M.xi.263, Sant.S.iii.16, Bhartr.iii.67; 2. to put on or into, स्रजमपि शिरस्यंधः क्षिप्तां धुनोत्यहिशंकया Sak.vii.; 3. to cast away, to get rid of, किं कूर्मस्य भरव्यथा न वपुषि क्ष्मां न क्षिपत्येष यत् Mud.ii.; 4. to fix, to attach to, तदा भृत्ये दोषान् क्षिपति Hit.ii.; 5. to reject, to disdain; 6. to insult, to revile, to abuse, M.viii.270, Sant.S.iii.10.With अधि-, 1. to offend, to abuse; 2. to surpass.With अव-, 1. to cast down, to abandon; 2. to slander.With आ-, 1. to hit, to pull down; 2. to pull off, to throw off, to take off, to snatch, प्रसाधिकालंबितमग्रपादमाक्षिप्य R.vii.7; 3. to neglect; 4. to insult; 5. to object to (as an argument); 6. to infer from circumstances.With उद्-, to throw up, Rt.i.22.With उप-, 1. to cast on, वपुषि वधाय तवं शस्त्रमुपक्षिपतः M.M.v.; 2. to insult; 3. to hint, छत्रं कार्यमुपक्षिपंति Mrich.ix.With नि-, 1. to put down, to throw down, Yaj.i.103, Am.S.80; 2. to entrust, to put in the hands of, to consign to the care of, M.viii.179, 180, vi.3; 3. to encamp; 4. to cast off.With परि-, 1. to surround, गंगास्रोतः परिक्षिप्तम् K.S.vi.38; 2. to embrace.With पर्या-, to bind up, to collect, (केशांतं) पर्याक्षिपन् काचिदुदारबंधं K.S.vii.14.With प्र-, 1. to throw at or in, क्षेत्रपतिना लगुडः प्रक्षिप्तः Hit.i., नामेध्यं प्रक्षिपेदग्नौ M.iv.53; 2. to interpolate, e.g. इदं पद्यं प्रक्षिप्तम्.With वि-, 1. to throw, to cast, Am.S.54; 2. to divert; 3. to distract.With सम्-, 1. to heap, to gather, आतपात्ययसंक्षिप्तनीवारासु निषादिभिः R.i.52; 2. to with-draw, to destroy; 3. to shorten, to abridge, संक्षिप्येत क्षणं इव कथं दीर्घयामा त्रियामा Megh.ii.45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=220-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपा
