घोल|घोलं|घोलः
घोल <i>m.n.</i> Buttermilk without any quantity of water in it (तत्तु सस्नेहमजलं मथितं घोलमुच्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोष|घोषं|घोषः
घोष <i>(I) m.</i> 1. Noise, tumult, स घोषो धार्तराष्ट्राणां हृदयानि व्यदारयत् Bg.i.19; 2. the thundering of clouds, स्निग्धगंभीरघोषम् Megh.ii.1; 3. a proclamation; 4. the soft sound heard in the articulation of certain letters (in gram.); 5. a herdsman, हैयंगवीनमादाय घोषवृद्धानुपस्थितान् R.i.45; 6. a hamlet, a station of cowherds, गंगायां घोषः K.Pr.ii.; 7. a Kāyastha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोष|घोषं|घोषः
घोष <i>(II) n.</i> Bellmetal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषवती
घोष-वती <i>f.</i> a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषण|घोषणं
घोषण <i>n.</i> Declaring publicly, speaking aloud, proclamation, दिग्विजृंभितकाकुत्स्थपौलस्त्यजयघोषणः R.xii.72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषणा
घोषणा <i>f.</i> Declaring publicly, speaking aloud, proclamation, दिग्विजृंभितकाकुत्स्थपौलस्त्यजयघोषणः R.xii.72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषयित्नु|घोषयित्नुः
घोषयित्नु <i>m.</i> 1. A Brāhmaṇa; 2. the Indian cuckoo; 3. a bard, a herald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्न
घ्न <i>a. (f. घ्ना) (used only as the last member of compounds)</i> 1. Killing, destroying, (e.g. राक्षसघ्न); 2. taking away from, (e.g. धर्मघ्न Yaj.i.138); 3. curing, (e.g. वातघ्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्ना
घ्न <i>a. (f. घ्ना) (used only as the last member of compounds)</i> 1. Killing, destroying, (e.g. राक्षसघ्न); 2. taking away from, (e.g. धर्मघ्न Yaj.i.138); 3. curing, (e.g. वातघ्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रा
घ्रा <i>vt. 1P (pp. घ्रात or घ्राण; pres. जिघ्रति)</i> To smell, to perceive by odour, to smell at, लेढि जिघ्रति संक्षिप्य करोत्युन्नतमासनम् Bh.V.i.99, Bt.xv.109.(This verb is used with several prepositions without any material difference in meaning, Bt.ii.10, xiv.12, R.iii.3, i.43, xiii.70.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=260-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राण|घ्राणं|घ्राणः
घ्राण <i>(I) a. (f. णा)</i> Smelt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणा
घ्राण <i>(I) a. (f. णा)</i> Smelt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राण|घ्राणं|घ्राणः
घ्राण <i>(II) n.</i> 1. The act of smelling, घ्राणेन सूकरो हंति M.iii.241; 2. odour; 3. the nose, घ्राणं करेण विरुणद्धि Rt.vi.27, M.v.135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणेंद्रिय|घ्राणेन्द्रिय
घ्राण-इंद्रिय <i>n.</i> the organ or sense of smell; (नासाग्रवर्ति according to Vaiśeṣikas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणचक्षुस्
घ्राण-चक्षुस् <i>a.</i> using the nose for eyes, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणतर्पण|घ्राणतर्पणः
घ्राण-तर्पण <i>a.</i> pleasant to the nose, fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राति|घ्रातिः
घ्राति <i>f.</i> 1. The nose; 2. the act of smelling, घ्रातिरघ्रेयमद्ययोः M.xi.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च <i>(I) ind.</i> A particle- (1) of copulation (and, also, moreover, as well as); (in this sense च is either repeated after each of the words or assertions which it joins together, or it is put only after the last of the words or assertion so joined), अधृष्यश्चाभिगम्यश्च यादोरत्नैरिवार्णवः R.i.16, 68, M.i.57, 64, iii.5, कुलेन कांस्या वयसा नवेन गुणैश्च तैस्तैर्विनयप्रधानैः R.vi.79, M.i.105, iii.116 (it is sometimes used to join a subordinate fact with a principal one, e.g. भिक्षामट गां चानय; and sometimes to express ‘combination,’ ‘mutual connection’ or ‘aggregation’); (2) of disjunction (yet, nevertheless), शांतमिदमाश्रमपदं स्फुरति च बाहुः Sak.i.; (3) of certainty, determination (exactly, indeed, certainly), ते तु यावंत एवाजौ तावांश्च ददृशे स तैः R.xii.45; (4) of condition (if), e.g. लोभश्चास्ति (i.e. चेदस्ति) गुणेन किम्, or जीवितुं चेच्छसे (i.e. चेदिच्छसे) मूढ हेतुं मे गदतः शृणु.च is sometimes used as an expletive (निरर्थकं चादि पादपूरणैकप्रयोजनम्), e.g. अन्यैश्च क्रतुभिश्च ‘and with other sacrifices.’When repeated in a co-ordinate sentence, it expresses- (1) simultaneous action, ते च प्रापुरुदन्वंतं बुबुधे चादिपूरुषः R.x.6, iii.40, K.S.iii.58, 66; (2) anti-thesis, अयमेकपदे तया वियोगः प्रियया चोपनतः सुदुःसहो मे । नववारिधरोदयादहोभिर्भवितव्यं च निरातपत्चरम्यैः Vikr.iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The moon; 2. a tortoise; 3. a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्
चक् <i>vi. 1Ā (pp. चकित; pres. चकते)</i> 1. To be satiated, to be satisfied; 2. to repel, to resist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकास्
चकास् <i>vi. 2U (pp. चकासित; pres. चकास्ति-स्ते)</i> 1. To shine, to be bright, चकासतं चारुचमूरुचर्मणा Sis.i.8, iii.6, Bt.iii.37; 2. to be prosperous, वितन्वति क्षेममदेवमातृकाश्चिराय तस्मिन्कुरवश्चकासते Kir.i.17.With वि-, to shine, to be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकित|चकितं
चकित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Trembling or shaking through fear, Megh.i.27; 2. fearful, timid पौलस्त्यचकितेश्वराः (दिशः) R.x.73; 3. startled, frightened, व्याधानुसारचकिता हरिणीव यासि Mrich.i.(चकितम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘alarmingly,’ ‘with fear,’ ‘in a frightened manner,’ सभयचकितं विन्यस्यंतीं दृशौ तिमिरे पथि Git.G.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकिता
चकित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Trembling or shaking through fear, Megh.i.27; 2. fearful, timid पौलस्त्यचकितेश्वराः (दिशः) R.x.73; 3. startled, frightened, व्याधानुसारचकिता हरिणीव यासि Mrich.i.(चकितम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘alarmingly,’ ‘with fear,’ ‘in a frightened manner,’ सभयचकितं विन्यस्यंतीं दृशौ तिमिरे पथि Git.G.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोर|चकोरः
चकोर <i>m.</i> A kind of bird, the Greek partridge, श्रीमुखचंद्रचकोर Git.G.ix., स्फुरदधरसीधवे तव वदनचंद्रमा रोचयति लोचनचकोरम् x., R.vi.59, vii.25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्र|चक्रं|चक्रः
चक्र <i>(I) n.</i> 1. The wheel of a carriage, Yaj.i.351; 2. a potter’s wheel; 3. a sharp circular missile weapon, a disc (especially applied to the disc of Viṣṇu); 4. an oil-mill; 5. a circle, a ring, कलापचक्रेषु निवेशिताननम् Bt.i.16; 6. a form of military array in a circle; 7. a circle or depression of the body; 8. a cycle, a cycle of years; 9. the horizon; 10. a troop, a multitude; 11. an army, a host; 12. a group of villages, a province, a district; 13. section of a book; 14. realm, sovereignty; 15. a whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्र|चक्रं|चक्रः
चक्र <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The ruddy goose (also called चक्रवाक); 2. a multitude, a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=261-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

