चांद्रायण|चान्द्रायण|चांद्रायणं|चान्द्रायणं
चांद्रायण <i>n.</i> A religious observance or expiatory penance regulated by the waxing and waning of the moon; in it, the daily consumption of food is reduced from fifteen mouthfuls to nothing during the dark fortnight of a month, and then increased in the same manner during the bright fortnight. See Yaj.iii.324.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=270-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

