चित्र <i>(I) a. (f. त्रा)</i> 1. Variegated, spotted; 2. various, different, manifold, Yaj.i.288, M.ix.248; 3. wonderful, surprising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=273-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रा
चित्र <i>(I) a. (f. त्रा)</i> 1. Variegated, spotted; 2. various, different, manifold, Yaj.i.288, M.ix.248; 3. wonderful, surprising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=273-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The variegated colour; 2. the Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=273-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र <i>(III) n.</i> 1. A picture, a painting, सेंद्रचापं सचित्राः Megh.ii.1, चित्रस्थानपि रोदयंति शतधा कुर्वंति भित्तीरपि K.Pr.iv.; 2. an extraordinary appearance, a wonder; 3. a sectarial mark on the forehead; 4. the sky; 5. a spot; 6. the white or spotted leprosy; 7. the last of the three divisions of poetry (in rhetoric). In it, the charm consists chiefly in the use of figures of speech (either of sense or of sound). It is of two kinds- 1. शब्दचित्र, 2. अर्थचित्र (शब्दचित्रं वाच्यचित्रमव्ययं त्ववरं स्मृतम् K.Pr.i.).(चित्रम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘oh! what a wonder,’ e.g. चित्रं महानेष बतावतारः K.Pr.iv.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=273-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

