जाति|जातिः
जाति <i>f.</i> 1. Birth, production, Bhartr.i.90; 2. family, race, lineage; 3. caste, high caste, जातिर्यातु रसातलं गुणगणस्तस्याप्यधस्तिष्ठतु Bhartr.ii.39; (there are four primary castes of the Hindus- ब्राह्मण, क्षत्रिय, वैश्य and शूद्र); 4. class, genus, species; 5. properties which are peculiar to a class and distinguish it from all others, K.Pr.ii., Sis.ii.47; 6. futile answer (in Nyāya Phil.); 7. a fireplace; 8. seven primary notes in Hindu music; 9. the jasmine plant or its flower, पुष्पाणां प्रकरः स्मितेन रचितो ना कुंदजात्यादिभिः Am.S.40; 10. mace, nutmeg; (written also जाती in the last two senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=288-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

