जाबाल <i>m.</i> A goat-herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न्य|जामदग्न्यः
जामदग्न्य <i>m.</i> A name of Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामा
जामा <i>f.</i> a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृ
जामातृ <i>m.</i> 1. A son-in-law, K.S.vii.55; 2. a lord, a master; 3. the sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामि|जामिः
जामि <i>f.</i> 1. A sister; 2. a daughter; 3. a daughter-in-law; 4. a virtuous and respectable woman; 5. a near female relative, M.iii.57, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामित्र|जामित्रं
जामित्र <i>n.</i> The seventh zodiacal sign from the natal one. In astrology, the sign is indicatory of the welfare, or otherwise of one’s wife; hence some derive the word from जाया, but it is found to be of Greek origin (Gr. diametron). See K.S.vii.1 and Mall. on it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामेय|जामेयः
जामेय <i>m.</i> A sister’s son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबव|जाम्बव|जांबवं|जाम्बवं
जांबव <i>n.</i> 1. the fruit of the jambu tree; 2. gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबीर|जाम्बीर|जांबीरं
जांबीर(ल) <i>n.</i> A citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबील|जाम्बील|जांबीलं
जांबीर(ल) <i>n.</i> A citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबूनद|जाम्बूनद|जांबूनदं|जाम्बूनदं
जांबूनद <i>n.</i> 1. Gold; 2. a golden ornament, कृतरुचश्च जांबूनदैः Sis.iv.66; 3. the dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया <i>f.</i> A wife, R.ii.1, Megh.i.8, 10. The word is thus derived- पतिर्भार्यां संप्रविश्य गर्भो भूत्वेह जायते । जयायास्तद्धि जायार्वं यदस्यां जायते पुनः M.ix.8. See also Mall. on R.ii.1. As the last member of a Bahu. compound, जाया is changed to जानि, e.g. युवजानि ‘one who has a young wife,’ नमो वामार्धजानये Mall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायानुजीविन्
जाया-अनुजीविन्, -आजीव <i>m.</i> 1. an actor, a dancer; 2. the husband of a harlot; 3. a needy man, a pauper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाजीव|जायाजीवः
जाया-अनुजीविन्, -आजीव <i>m.</i> 1. an actor, a dancer; 2. the husband of a harlot; 3. a needy man, a pauper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायापती
जायापती <i>m. du.</i> husband and wife. Cf. जंपती and दंपती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

