जालक|जालकं|जालकः
जालक <i>n.</i> 1. A net; 2. a multitude, a collection, समुद्धृताशेषमृणालजालकम् Rt.i.19; 3. a window; 4. a nest; 5. an unblown flower, नवजलकणैर्यूथिकाजालकानि Megh.i.26; 6. illusion; 7. a particular ornament worn in the hair, R.ix.44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकमालिन्
जालक-मालिन् <i>a.</i> veiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिन्
जालकिन् <i>m.</i> A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिनी
जालकिनी <i>f.</i> An ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिक|जालिकः
जालिक <i>m.</i> 1. A fisherman; 2. a fowler, a bird-catcher; 3. a spider; 4. the governor of a province; 5. a rogue, a cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिका
जालिका <i>f.</i> 1. A net; 2. a chain-armour; 3. a spider; 4. a leech; 5. a veil; 6. a widow; 7. iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिनी
जालिनी <i>f.</i> A room ornamented with pictures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म <i>(I) a. (f. ल्मी)</i> 1. Cruel, harsh; 2. rash, inconsiderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मी
जाल्म <i>(I) a. (f. ल्मी)</i> 1. Cruel, harsh; 2. rash, inconsiderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म <i>(II) m. (fem. ˚ल्मी)</i> 1. A low or degraded man, a poor man, क्षणं विश्राम्यतां जाल्म स्कंधस्ते यदि बाधति । न तथा बाधते स्कंधो यथा बाधति बाधते Ud.; 2. a miscreant, a rogue, a rascal, M.M.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=289-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मक
जाल्मक <i>a. (f. ल्मिका)</i> Despised, base, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=290-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मिका
जाल्मक <i>a. (f. ल्मिका)</i> Despised, base, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=290-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जावन्य|जावन्यं
जावन्य <i>n.</i> Speed, swiftness, haste, hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=290-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नवी
जाह्नवी <i>f.</i> An epithet of the river Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=290-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि <i>vt. or vi. 1P (but with the prepositions वि and परा Atm.) (pp. जित; caus. जापयति-ते; desid. जिगीषति.)</i> 1. To conquer, to defeat, to overcome, to subjugate, Bt.xv.76, Ghat.22; 2. to win, to acquire by conquest, यो यज्जयति तस्य तत् M.vii.96, R.xi.65; 3. to excel, to surpass, वपुःप्रकर्षादजयद् गुरुं रघुः R.iii.34, K.S.ii.53; 4. to be victorious or preeminent, राधामाधवयोर्जयंति यमुनाकूले रहःकेलयः Git.G.i., जयंति ते सुकृतिनो रससिद्धाः कवीश्वराः Bhartr.ii.24.With अधि-, to subjugate, to conquer, to kill, Bt.xix.2.With निस्-, 1. to conquer, to defeat, Bt.ii.52, vii.94; 2. to win, to acquire by conquest.With परा-, 1. to defeat, to overcome, to subjugate, e.g. नैते पराजेतुं शक्या देवगणैरपि; 2. to loose, to be deprived of; 3. to be overcome by, (with an abl., e.g. अध्ययनात् पराजयते).With वि-, 1. to conquer, to subjugate, एष व्यजेष्ट देवेंद्रम् Bt.xv.39, i.2, ii.39; 2. to win, to acquire by conquest, R.i.59, xii.104; 3. to be victorious, to be preeminent, e.g. विजिगीषोश्च चेष्टितम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=290-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि <i>m.</i> A piśācha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=290-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगत्नु|जिगत्नुः
जिगत्नु <i>m.</i> Breath, life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=290-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
