जुष्
जुष् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 6Ā (pp. जुष्ट; pres. जुषते)</i> 1. To be pleased or satisfied; 2. to be favourable or propitious; 3. to like, to take delight in; 4. to practise, to undergo, to suffer, पौलस्त्योऽजुषत शुचं विपन्नबंधुः Bt.xvii.112; 5. to visit, to inhabit, to enter, to seat oneself in, रथं च जुजुषे शुभम् Bt.xiv.95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् <i>(II) vt. or vi. 1P, 10U (pres. जोषति, जोषयति-ते)</i> 1. To reason, to think, to examine; 2. to be satiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् <i>a. (generally at the end of compounds)</i> 1. Visiting, approaching, assuming, taking, रजोजुषे जन्मनि Kad.; 2. liking, taking pleasure in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्ट|जुष्टं
जुष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Gratified, pleased; 2. practised, suffered; 3. furnished with, possessed of, (pp. of जुष् q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्टा
जुष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Gratified, pleased; 2. practised, suffered; 3. furnished with, possessed of, (pp. of जुष् q.v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहू
जुहू <i>f.</i> A wooden ladle used for pouring the sacrificial butter into the fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहोति|जुहोतिः
जुहोति <i>m.</i> A term for those sacrificial ceremonies to which the verb जुहोति is applied (Cf. यजति), यहतिजुहोतीनां को विशेषः Kātyāyana, क्षरंति सरा वैदिक्यो जुहोतियजतिक्रियाः M.ii.84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू <i>f.</i> 1. Speed; 2. a female demon; 3. an epithet of Sarasvatī; 4. the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूक|जूकः
जूक <i>m.</i> The sign Libra of the Zodiac (a word of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=292-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूट|जूटः
जूट <i>m.</i> Matted hair, भूतेशस्य भुजंगवल्लिवलयस्रङ्नद्धजूटा जटाः M.M.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूति|जूतिः
जूति <i>f.</i> Speed, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्
जूर् <i>vt. or vi. 4Ā (pp. जूर्ण; pres. जूर्यते)</i> 1. To hurt, to kill; 2. to be angry with, (with a dat.), भर्त्रे नखेभ्यश्च चिरं जुजूरे Bt.xi.8; 3. to become old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्ति|जूर्तिः|जूर्त्ति|जूर्त्तिः
जूर्ति <i>f.</i> Fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृ
जृ <i>vt. 1P (pres. जरति)</i> To make low, to humiliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृभ्
जृभ् <i>vi. 1Ā (pp. जृंभित, जृब्ध; pres. जृभते, जृंभते)</i> 1. To yawn, to gape; 2. to burst open (as a flower), वरयुवातिमुखाभं पंकजं जृंभतेऽद्य Rt.iii.22; 3. to fly back or recoil (as a bow); 4. to increase, to spread everywhere, तृष्णे जृंभसि (here used in the Par.) पापकर्मविरते Bhartr.iii.5; 5. to rise, to appear, to be visible or manifest, संकल्पयोनेरभिमान भूतमात्मानमादाय मधुर्जजृंभे K.S.iii.24; 6. to be preeminent, भिगः कोपि स एक एव परमो नित्योदितो जृंभते Bhartr.iii.80.With उद्-, to rise, to arise, to appear.With वि-, 1. to open the mouth, to yawn, to gape, व्यजृंभिषत चापरे Bt.xv.108; 2. to open, to expand (as a flower); 3. to spread, रजोंधकारस्य विजृंभितस्य R.vii.42 (मंगलतूर्यनिस्वनाः) पथि व्यजृंभंत दिवौकसामपि R.iii.19; 3. to pervade, to appear.With समुद्-, to endeavour, to strive, व्यालं बालमृणालतंतुभिरसौ रोद्धुं समुज्जृंभते Bhartr.ii.6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभ|जृम्भ|जृंभं|जृंभः|जृम्भः
जृंभ <i>m.n.</i> 1. Yawning; 2. opening, blossoming, मालती शिरसि जृंभणोन्मुखी Bhartr.i.25 or जृंभारंभप्रविततदलोपांतजालप्रविषैरुस्रैर्भानोः Ve.ii.; 3. stretching (the limbs), मुहुर्मुहुर्जृंभणतत्पराणि (अंगानि) Rt.vi.10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

