जैमिनि|जैमिनिः
जैमिनि <i>m.</i> A celebrated sage and philosopher, the founder of the Mīmānsā school of philosophy, मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ सहसा हस्ती मुनिं जैमिनीम् Panch.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृक|जैवातृकः
जैवातृक <i>(I) a. (f. की)</i> 1. Long-lived, one for whom long life is desired, e.g. जैवातृक ननु श्रूयते पतिरस्याः &c. D.K.; 2. thin, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृकी
जैवातृक <i>(I) a. (f. की)</i> 1. Long-lived, one for whom long life is desired, e.g. जैवातृक ननु श्रूयते पतिरस्याः &c. D.K.; 2. thin, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृक|जैवातृकः
जैवातृक <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The moon, राजानं जनयांबभुव सहसा जैवातृक त्वां तु यः Bh.V.ii.78; 2. camphor; 3. a son; 4. a drug, a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवेय|जैवेयः
जैवेय <i>m.</i> An epithet of Kacha, son of Brishaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्म्य|जैह्म्यं
जैह्म्य <i>n.</i> Crookedness, deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=293-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोंगट|जोङ्गट|जोंगटः|जोङ्गटः
