ज्ञानात्मन्
ज्ञान-आत्मन् <i>a.</i> all-wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=294-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानेंद्रिय|ज्ञानेन्द्रिय|ज्ञानेन्द्रियं
ज्ञान-इंद्रिय <i>n.</i> an organ of perception, [of which there are five, viz., त्वच्, रसना, चक्षुस्, कर्ण and प्राण the skin, tongue, eye, ear and nose].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=294-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानकांड|ज्ञानकाण्ड
ज्ञान-कांड <i>m.</i> the esoteric portion of the Veda which treats of the knowledge of the supreme spirit, (op. to कर्मकांड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=294-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

