डब् <i>vt. 10U (pres. डंबयति-ते)</i> 1. To throw, to send; 2. to behold.With वि-, 1. to imitate, to copy, (तं) ऋतुर्विडिडंबयामास न पुनः प्राप तच्छ्रियम् R.iv.17, iii.52, xiii.29, xvi.11, Sis.i.6, Kir.v.46; 2. to ridicule, to deride, to mock, (वामनयनाः) संमोहयंति मदयंति विडंबयंति निर्भर्त्सयंति रमयंति विषादयंति Bhartr.i.22; 3. to cheat, to deceive, एवमात्माभिप्रायसंभावितेष्टजनचित्तवृत्तिः प्रार्थयिता विडंब्यते Sak.ii.; 4. to afflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=297-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डभ्
डभ् <i>vt. 10U (pres. डंभयति-ते)</i> To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=297-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम|डमः
डम <i>m.</i> A despised mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=297-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमर|डमरं|डमरः
डमर <i>(I) m.</i> 1. Riot, tumult; 2. terrifying an enemy by shouts and jestures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=297-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमर|डमरं|डमरः
डमर <i>(II) n.</i> Running away through fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=297-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरु|डमरुः
डमरु <i>m. (according to some n.)</i> A sort of small drum, shaped like an hour-glass usually carried about by Kāpālikas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=297-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डंबर|डम्बर|डम्बरः
