तम्
तम् <i>vi. 4P (pp. तांत; pres. ताम्यति)</i> 1. To choke, to be suffocated; 2. to be exhausted, to be fatigued, ललितशिरीषपुष्पहननैरपि ताम्यति यत् M.M.v.; 3. to be distressed in body or mind, तत्किं ताम्यसि किं च रोदिषि मुधा Am.S.7.With उद्-, to be impatient, e.g. हृदय किमेवमुत्ताम्यसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=304-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम <i>(I) n.</i> 1. Darkness; 2. the tip of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=304-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम <i>(II) m.</i> 1. An epithet of Rāhu; 2. the tamāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=304-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
तमस् <i>(I) n.</i> 1. Darkness, आविर्भूते शशिनि तमसा रिच्यमानेव रात्रिः Vikr.i., Megh.i.37; 2. illusion, error, मुनिसुताप्रणयस्मृतिरोधिना मम च मुक्तमिदं तमसा मनः Sak.vi.; 3. ignorance as one of the three qualities or constituents of nature (the other two being सत्व and रजस्), M.xii.24; 4. grief, sorrow; 5. sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=304-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
