तात|तातः
तात <i>m.</i> 1. A father, हा तातेति क्रंदितमाकर्ण्य विषण्णः R.ix.75; 2. a term of endearment applied to pupils, younger relatives, or other persons of inferior position, न्यस्यतां कलशस्तात दीयतां कल्कलं मम Ram.; 3. a term of reverence applied to elders and venerable persons, तस्मान्मुच्ये यथा तात संविधातुं तथार्हसि R.i.72, ह्रेपिता हि बहवो नरेश्वरास्तेन तात धनुषा धनुर्भृतः R.xi.40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=306-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातगु|तातगुः
तात-गु <i>(I) a.</i> agreeable to a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=306-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातगु|तातगुः
तात-गु <i>(II) m.</i> a paternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=306-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातन|तातनः
