तृणराज|तृणराजः
तृण-राज <i>m.</i> 1. the cocoanut tree; 2. the bamboo; 3. the palmyra tree; 4. the sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणवृक्ष|तृणवृक्षः
तृण-वृक्ष <i>m.</i> 1. the palm tree; 2. the date tree; 3. the cocoanut tree; 4. the areca-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणशीत|तृणशीतं
तृण-शीत <i>n.</i> a kind of fragrant grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणसारा
तृण-सारा <i>f.</i> the plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणसिंह|तृणसिंहः
तृण-सिंह <i>m.</i> an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणहर्म्य|तृणहर्म्म्यः|तृणहर्म्यः
तृण-हर्म्य <i>m.</i> a house of straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण्या
तृण्या <i>f.</i> A heap of grass or straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीय|तृतीयः
तृतीय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> the third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीया
तृतीय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> the third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीय|तृतीयः
तृतीय <i>(II) n.</i> A third part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयप्रकृति|तृतीयप्रकृतिः
तृतीय-प्रकृति <i>m. or f.</i> a eunuch. (Also तृतीयाप्रकृति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयक
तृतीयक <i>m.</i> A fever returning every third day (in medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीया
तृतीया <i>f.</i> 1. The third day of a lunar fortnight; 2. the instrumental case (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयाकृत|तृतीयाकृतं
तृतीयाकृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Thrice ploughed (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयाकृता
तृतीयाकृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Thrice ploughed (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयिन्
तृतीयिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Entitled to a third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयिनी
तृतीयिन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> Entitled to a third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृह्
तृह् <i>vt. 1P, 7U (pp. तृण्ण; pres. तर्दति, तृणाति, तृंत्ते)</i> 1. To split, to pierce; 2. to kill, to destroy, to annihilate, Bt.xiv.33, 108, vi.38; 3. to disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्
तृप् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 4P, 5P, 6P (pp. तृप्त; pres. तृप्यति, तृप्नोति, तृपति; desid. तितर्पिषति, तितृप्सति)</i> 1. To become satisfied, to be contented, प्राशीन्न चातृपत् Bt.xv.29, xvi.29; (used with the inst. gen. or loc., e.g. को न तृप्यति वित्तेन, or नाग्निस्तृप्यति काष्ठानां नापगानां महोदधिः । नांतकः सर्वभूतानां न पुंसां वामलोचनाः, or तस्मिन् हि ततृपुर्देवास्तते यज्ञे); 2. to please, to satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्
तृप् <i>(II) vt. 1P, 10U (pres. तर्पति, तर्पयति-ते)</i> To light up, to kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=314-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्त|तृप्तः
तृप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> Satiated, satiated, contented, (pp. of तृप् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्ता
तृप्त <i>a. (f. प्ता)</i> Satiated, satiated, contented, (pp. of तृप् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्ति|तृप्तिः
तृप्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Satisfaction, contentment, R.ii.39, iii.3, Bg.x.18; 2. satiety, disgust; 3. pleasure, gratification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
तृष् <i>vt. 4P (pp. तृषित; pres. तृष्यति)</i> 1. To be thirsty, Bt.vii.106; 2. to wish, to wish excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
तृष् <i>f. (nom. sing. तृट्-ड्)</i> 1. Thirst, तृषां महत्या परिशुष्कतालवः Rt.i.11; 2. strong desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषा
तृषा <i>f.</i> The same as तृष् q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषार्त|तृषार्त्त
तृषा-आर्त <i>a.</i> suffering from thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषाह|तृषाहं
तृषा-ह <i>n.</i> water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषित|तृषितः
तृषित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Thirsty, Ghat.9, Rt.i.18; 2. greedy, desirous of gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषिता
तृषित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Thirsty, Ghat.9, Rt.i.18; 2. greedy, desirous of gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णज्
तृष्णज् <i>a.</i> Covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णा
तृष्णा <i>f.</i> 1. Thirst, Rt.i.15; 2. strong desire, avidity, R.viii.2; 3. desire of gain, Bhartr.iii.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णाक्षय|तृष्णाक्षयः
तृष्णा-क्षय <i>m.</i> cessation of desire, tranquility of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णालु
तृष्णालु <i>a.</i> Very thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृह्
तृह् <i>vt. 7P, 10U (pp. तृढ; pres. तृणेढि, तर्हयति-ते; desid. तितृक्षति, तितृंहिषति)</i> To injure, to hurt, to kill, (तानि) तृनेद्रु रामः सह लक्ष्मणेन Bt.i.19, vi.39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तॄ
तॄ <i>vt. 1P (pp. तीर्ण; pres. तरति; pass. तीर्यते; desid. तितीर्षति, तितिरिषति, तितिरीषति)</i> 1. To cross over, न बाहुभ्यां नदीं तरेत् M.iv.77, केनोडुपेन परलोकनदीं तरिष्ये Mrich.viii.; 2. to float, to swim, शिला तरिष्यत्युदके न पर्णम् Bt.xii.77; 3. to come to the end of, to get over, सर्वदुर्गाणि मत्प्रसादात्तरिष्यति Bg.xviii.58, R.xiv.6, M.xi.34; 4. to accomplish, to attain, e.g. प्रतिज्ञेयं मया तीर्णा; 5. to be saved, to escape from, e.g. तपोभिः क्रतुभिश्चैव … तरंति नित्यं पुरुषा ये स्म पापानि कुर्वते.With अति-, 1. to cross over; 2. to overcome, Bg.xiii.25.With अव-, 1. to descend, शैलराजावतीर्णां जह्नोः कन्याम् Megh.i.50, R.i.54, xiii.68; 2. to enter, to enter into, to come to, Sis.ix.32; 3. to overcome; 4. to descend into the world of mortals in the shape of a mortal.With उद्-, 1. to get out of, to rise from, R.ii.17; 2. to overcome, e.g. रोगोत्तीर्ण, विरहोत्तीर्ण; 3. to cross over, उदतारीदुदन्वंतम् Bt.xv.10, R.xii.71, xvi.33.With निस्-, 1. to cross over; 2. to accomplish, to attain; 3. to get over, to pass over, to go to the end of, R.iii.7.With प्र-, to cross over.With वि-, 1. to cross over, to go beyond, R.vi.77; 2. to give, to grant, to bestow on, to favour with, निवासहेतोरुटजं वितेरुः R.xiv.81, वितरति गुरुः प्राज्ञे विद्यां यथैव तथा जडे Ut.ii.; 3. to cause, ज्योत्स्नाशंकामिह वितरंति हंसश्येनी Kir.v.31.With व्यति-, to overcome.With सम्-, 1. to cross over; 2. to float; 3. to get over, to go to the end of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तॄ
तॄ <i>Caus. (तारयति-ते)</i> 1. to carry or lead over; 2. to cause to arrive at; 3. to rescue, to liberate.With अव-, to bend, to bring down.With प्र-, to cheat, to deceive, किंत्वेवं कविभिः प्रतारितमनास्तत्वं विजानन्नपि Bhartr.i.78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजन|तेजनं|तेजनः
तेजन <i>(I) m.</i> A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजन|तेजनं|तेजनः
तेजन <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Sharpening, whetting; 2. kindling; 3. rendering bright, polishing; 4. the point of an arrow, the edge of a weapon, M.vii.90; 5. a reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजल|तेजलः
तेजल <i>m.</i> The francoline partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्
तेजस् <i>n.</i> 1. Heat, light, lustre, R.iv.1; 2. heat or light as the third of the five elements of creation (the other four being पृथिवी, अप्, वायु and आकाश); 3. the bright appearance of the human body, beauty, R.iii.15; 4. might, power; (also used for ‘one possessed of might,’ तेजसां हि न वयः समीक्ष्यते R.xi.1); 5. spirit, energy; 6. semen, virile, दुष्यंतेनाहितं तेजो दधानां भूतये भुवः Sak.iv.; 7. marrow; 8. the essential nature of anything; 9. essence, quintessence; 10. spiritual, moral or magical power; 11. majesty, dignity, राजलक्ष्मीं तेजोविशेषानुमितां दधानः R.ii.7; 12. the not putting up with insult or ill-treatment (as a qualification of a hero in poetic composition); 13. the speed of a horse; 14. fresh butter; 15. gold; 16. fire; 17. bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्कर|तेजस्करं
तेजस्-कर <i>a.</i> 1. illuminating; 2. granting strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोभंग|तेजोभङ्ग|तेजोभङ्गः
तेजोभंग <i>m.</i> 1. discouragement; 2. disgrace, destruction of dignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोमंडल|तेजोमण्डल
तेजोमंडल <i>n.</i> a halo of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=315-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

