त्रिदंड|त्रिदण्ड|त्रिदण्डः
त्रि-दंड <i>(II) m.</i> the state of a religious ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=318-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदंडिन्|त्रिदण्डिन्
त्रि-दंडिन् <i>xxx</i> 1. a religious mendicant who has renounced the world and carries three long staves tied together in his right hand; 2. a religious man who has obtained command over his mind, body and speech, (वाग्दंडोऽथ मनोदंडः कायदंडस्तथैव च । यस्यैते निहिता बुद्धौ त्रिदंडीति स उच्यते M.xii.10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=318-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
त्रि-दश <i>(I) m. pl.</i> 1. thirty; 2. the thirty-three gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=318-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
