त्वरित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Quick, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरित|त्वरितं
त्वरित <i>(II) n.</i> Despatch, haste.(त्वरितम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘quickly, fast, hastily.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टृ
त्वष्टृ <i>m.</i> 1. A carpenter, a workman; 2. Viśvakarman, the carpenter of gods, आरोप्य चक्रभ्रमिमुष्णतेजास्त्वष्ट्रेव यत्नोल्लिखितो विभाति R.vi.32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वादृश्
त्वादृश् <i>a.</i> Similar to thee, one of thy kind, Megh.ii.6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
त्विष् <i>vi. 1U (pres. त्विषति-ते)</i> To shine, to glitter, to sparkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
त्विष् <i>f.</i> 1. Light, lustre, brilliancy, splendour, विविशुर्ज्वलनं त्विषः Sis.ix.13, R.iv.75, Sis.i.3; 2. beauty; 3. authority, weight; 4. wish, desire; 5. custom, practice; 6. speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषामीश
त्विषामीश <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषांपति|त्विषाम्पति|त्विषाम्पतिः
त्विषामीश <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषि|त्विषिः
त्विषि <i>m.</i> A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सरु|त्सरुः
त्सरु <i>m.</i> 1. Any creeping animal; 2. the hilt or handle of a sword or any other weapon, सुप्रग्रहविमलकलधौतत्सरुणा खड्गेन Ve.iii., R.xviii.48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
थ <i>(I) m.</i> A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
थ <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Protection, preservation; 2. fear; 3. auspiciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुड्
थुड् <i>vt. 6P (pres. थुडति)</i> 1. To cover, to screen; 2. to hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुडन
थुडन <i>n.</i> Covering, wrapping up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुत्कार|थुत्कारः
थुत्कार <i>m.</i> The sound थुत् made in spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुर्व्
थुर्व् <i>vt. 1P (pres. थूर्वति)</i> To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थूत्कार|थूत्कारः
थूत्कार <i>m.</i> The sound थूत् made in spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थूत्कृत|थूत्कृतं
थूत्कृत <i>n.</i> The sound थूत् made in spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थैथै
थैथै <i>ind.</i> The imitative sound of a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द <i>(I) a. (f. दा) (at the end of compounds only)</i> Giving, granting, administering, causing, cutting off, destroying, e.g. अन्नद, गरद, वारिद, अवधिद, अनलद &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
द <i>(I) a. (f. दा) (at the end of compounds only)</i> Giving, granting, administering, causing, cutting off, destroying, e.g. अन्नद, गरद, वारिद, अवधिद, अनलद &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A gift, a donation; 2. a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द <i>(III) n.</i> A wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्
दंश् <i>vt. 1P (pp. दष्ट; pres. दशति; desid. दिदङ्क्षति)</i> To bite, to sting, Bt.xv.4, xvi.19.With उप-, to eat anything as a relish.With सम्-, 1. to bite, Am.S.32; 2. to stick, सदंष्टवस्त्रेष्वबलनितंबेषु R.xvi.65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्
दंश् <i>(II) vt. 10Ā (pres. दंक्षयते)</i> To bite, to sting, e.g. नाहिर्दंशयते कंचित्तद्देशे गरुडाज्ञया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश <i>m.</i> 1. Biting, stinging, मुग्धे विधेहि मयि निर्दयदंतदंशम् Git.G.x.; 2. the sting of a snake; 3. a gadfly, R.ii.5; 4. fault, defect (in a jewel); 5. a tooth; 6. pungency; 7. an armour; 8. a joint, a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशभीरु|दंशभीरुः
दंश-भीरु <i>m.</i> a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=321-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशक|दंशकः
दंशक <i>m.</i> 1. A dog; 2. a gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशन|दंशनं
दंशन <i>n.</i> 1. The act of biting, e.g. दष्टाश्च दंशनैः कांतं दासीकुर्वति योषितः; 2. an armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशित|दंशितः
दंशित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Bitten; 2. mailed, furnished with an armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशिता
दंशित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Bitten; 2. mailed, furnished with an armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशिन्
दंशिन् <i>m.</i> The same as दंशक q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशी
दंशी <i>f.</i> A small gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रा
दंष्ट्रा <i>f.</i> A large tooth, a tusk, a fang, दंष्ट्राभंगं मृगाणामधिपतय इव … … नाज्ञाभंगं सहंते नृवर नृपतयस्त्वादृशाः सार्वभौमाः Mud.iii., R.ii.46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रास्त्र|दंष्ट्रास्त्रः
दंष्ट्रा-अस्त्र, -आयुध <i>m.</i> a wild boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रायुध|दंष्ट्रायुधः
दंष्ट्रा-अस्त्र, -आयुध <i>m.</i> a wild boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्राकराल
दंष्ट्रा-कराल <i>a.</i> having terrible tusks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्राविष|दंष्ट्राविषः
दंष्ट्रा-विष <i>m.</i> a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्राल
दंष्ट्राल <i>a. (f. ला)</i> Having large tusks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्राला
दंष्ट्राल <i>a. (f. ला)</i> Having large tusks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिका
दंष्ट्रिका <i>f.</i> the same as दंष्ट्रा q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिन्
दंष्ट्रिन् <i>m.</i> 1. A boar; 2. a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष <i>(I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Able, competent, expert, clever, दोग्धरि दोहदक्षे K.S.i.2, R.xii.11, Bhartr.i.88; 2. fit, suitable; 3. ready, careful, M.v.150; 4. honest, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षा
दक्ष <i>(I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Able, competent, expert, clever, दोग्धरि दोहदक्षे K.S.i.2, R.xii.11, Bhartr.i.88; 2. fit, suitable; 3. ready, careful, M.v.150; 4. honest, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Name of a son of Brahman (m.), the father of Pārvatī in her former birth, दक्षस्य कन्या भवपूर्वपत्नी K.S.i.21; 2. a cock; 3. fire; 4. the bull of Śiva; 5. a lover attached to many mistresses; 6. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाध्वरध्वंसक|दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकः
दक्ष-अध्वरध्वंसक, -क्रतुध्वंसिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षक्रतुध्वंसिन्
दक्ष-अध्वरध्वंसक, -क्रतुध्वंसिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षकन्या
दक्ष-कन्या, -जा, -तनया <i>f.</i> 1. an epithet of Durgā; 2. any lunar mansion (the 27 lunar mansions being considered to be so many daughters of Daksha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षजा
दक्ष-कन्या, -जा, -तनया <i>f.</i> 1. an epithet of Durgā; 2. any lunar mansion (the 27 lunar mansions being considered to be so many daughters of Daksha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षतनया
दक्ष-कन्या, -जा, -तनया <i>f.</i> 1. an epithet of Durgā; 2. any lunar mansion (the 27 lunar mansions being considered to be so many daughters of Daksha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षसुत|दक्षसुतः
दक्ष-सुत <i>m.</i> a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाय्य|दक्षाय्यः
दक्षाय्य <i>m.</i> 1. A vulture; 2. an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण <i>(I) a. (f. णा)</i> 1. Able, competent, clever; 2. right, (op. to वाम); 3. southern; 4. straightforward, honest, impartial; 5. pleasing, amiable, agreeable; 6. liberal, courteous; 7. submissive; 8. situated on the right side; 9. situated to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणा
दक्षिण <i>(I) a. (f. णा)</i> 1. Able, competent, clever; 2. right, (op. to वाम); 3. southern; 4. straightforward, honest, impartial; 5. pleasing, amiable, agreeable; 6. liberal, courteous; 7. submissive; 8. situated on the right side; 9. situated to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The right hand; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu; 3. a lover who is equally courteous to several mistresses (in poetic composition).(The inst. sing. दक्षिणेन is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘on the right side of,’ ‘on the south of,’ (with an acc. or gen.), अयि दक्षिणेन वृक्षवाटिकामालाप इव श्रूयते Sak.i.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाग्नि|दक्षिणाग्निः
दक्षिण-अग्नि <i>m.</i> the sacred fire in the household of a Brāhmaṇa, which is otherwise called अन्वाहार्यपचन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाग्र
दक्षिण-अग्र <i>a.</i> pointing to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाचल|दक्षिणाचलः
दक्षिण-अचल <i>m.</i> the southern mountain, i.e. Malaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाभिमुख
दक्षिण-अभिमुख <i>a.</i> facing the south, directed southward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणायन|दक्षिणायनं
दक्षिण-अयन <i>n.</i> the sun’s progress south of the equator, the half year in which the sun moves from north to south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

