दक्षिणा
दक्षिणा <i>(I) ind.</i> To the south, in the southern direction, (with an abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणा
दक्षिणा <i>(II) f.</i> 1. A prolific cow; 2. a present or gift to Brāhmaṇas on the performance of religious rites; 3. दक्षिणा considered (originally only in a figure) as the wife of a sacrifice, R.i.31; 4. gift, offering in general; 5. the south; 6. the Dekkan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणार्ह|दक्षिणार्हः
दक्षिणा-अर्ह <i>a.</i> deserving a fee, worthy of a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त|दक्षिणावर्तः|दक्षिणावर्त्त
दक्षिणा-आवर्त <i>a.</i> 1. curved to the right; 2. turned towards the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाकाल|दक्षिणाकालः
