दक्षिणापथ|दक्षिणापथः
दक्षिणा-पथ <i>m.</i> the southern portion of India, the Dekkan, अस्ति दक्षिणापथे विदर्भेषु पद्मपुरं नाम नगरम् M.M.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रवण
दक्षिणा-प्रवण <i>a.</i> inclining to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाहि
दक्षिणाहि <i>ind.</i> 1. Far on the right; 2. far in the south, (with an abl., e.g. दक्षिणाहि ग्रामात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीय|दक्षिणीयः
दक्षिणीय <i>m.</i> A Brāhmaṇa fit for a sacrificial fee. (Also दाक्षिण्य and दाक्षिण्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध|दग्धं|दग्धः
दग्ध <i>a. (f. ग्धा)</i> 1. Burnt, consumed by fire; 2. tortured, pained, consumed by grief; 3. tasteless, insipid; 4. inauspicious; 5. a term of abuse usually prefixed to the word it vilifies, को देहीति वदेत्स्वदग्धजठरस्यार्थे मनस्वी जनः Bhartr.iii.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धा
दग्ध <i>a. (f. ग्धा)</i> 1. Burnt, consumed by fire; 2. tortured, pained, consumed by grief; 3. tasteless, insipid; 4. inauspicious; 5. a term of abuse usually prefixed to the word it vilifies, को देहीति वदेत्स्वदग्धजठरस्यार्थे मनस्वी जनः Bhartr.iii.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धिका
दग्धिका <i>f.</i> Scorched rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्न
दघ्न <i>a. (f. घ्ना)</i> A termination affixed to nouns to denote ‘reaching to,’ ‘as high as,’ नाभिदघ्नोदकस्थस्य गृहीत्वोरू जलं विशेत् Yaj.ii.108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ्ना
दघ्न <i>a. (f. घ्ना)</i> A termination affixed to nouns to denote ‘reaching to,’ ‘as high as,’ नाभिदघ्नोदकस्थस्य गृहीत्वोरू जलं विशेत् Yaj.ii.108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंड्|दण्ड्
दंड् <i>vi. 10U (pp. दंडित; pres. दंडयति-ते) (This is one of those verbs which take two accusatives, e.g. प्रजाः शतं दंडयति राजा.)</i> To fine, to punish, स्थित्यै दंडयतो दंडश्चान् R.i.25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=322-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंड|दण्ड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दंड <i>(I) m.n.</i> 1. A stick, a staff, a cudgel, a mace, परस्य दंडं नोद्यच्छेत् M.iv.164; 2. the sceptre of a king; 3. the staff given to a twice-born man at the time of investiture with the sacred thread; 4. the staff carried by a Sannyāsin; 5. the trunk of an elephant; 6. a stalk, the stem of a tree, the handle of anything, ब्रह्मांडच्छत्रदंडः … भुवनांभोरुहो नालदंडः D.K., राज्यं स्वहस्तधृतदंडमिवातपत्रम् Sak.v., K.S.vii.89; 7. the oar of a boat; 8. a churning stick; 9. a measure of length equal to four hands, a rod of that length used for the purpose of taking measurements; 10. the penis; 11. a form of military array; 12. an army, तस्य दंडवतो दंडः स्वदेहान्न व्यशिष्यत R.xvii.62, Kir.ii.12; 13. control, restraint, वाग्दंडोऽथ मनोदंडः कायदंडस्तथैव च । यस्यैते निहिता बुद्धौ त्रिदंडीति स उच्यते M.xii.10; 14. punishment, corporal chastisement (as राजदंड, धर्मदंड), R.i.6, M.vii.103; 15. imprisonment; 16. the last of the four ways of dealing with an enemy, viz., violence, war, punishment; See उपायचतुष्टय, Sis.ii.54, M.vii.109; 17. pride; 18. the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंड|दण्ड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दंड <i>(II) m.</i> 1. An epithet of Yama; 2. of Viṣṇu; 3. of Śiva; 4. an attendant on the sun; 5. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडाजिन|दण्डाजिन|दण्डाजिनं
दंड-अजिन <i>n.</i> 1. staff and skin (collectively), 2. hypocrisy^1, deceit.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260516. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/224.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडाधिप|दण्डाधिप|दण्डाधिपः
दंड-अधिप <i>m.</i> chief magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडानीक|दण्डानीक
दंड-अनीक <i>n.</i> a division of an army, a detachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडापूपन्याय|दण्डापूपन्याय|दण्डापूपन्यायः
दंड-अपूपन्याय <i>m.</i> the maxim of the staff and cakes. It denotes that when one thing is connected with another in a particular way, what is predicable of the one is, as a matter of course, predicable of the other also; as when a staff and cakes are kept together the pulling of the staff by a cat naturally leads one to expect the pulling of the cakes also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडार्ह|दण्डार्ह
दंड-अर्ह <i>a.</i> deserving punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडालसिका|दण्डालसिका
दंड-अलसिका <i>f.</i> cholera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडाज्ञा|दण्डाज्ञा
दंड-आज्ञा <i>f.</i> judicial sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडाहत|दण्डाहत|दण्डाहतं
दंड-आहत <i>n.</i> butter-milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडकर्मन्|दण्डकर्मन्
दंड-कर्मन् <i>n.</i> infliction of punishment, chastisement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडकाक|दण्डकाक|दण्डकाकः
दंड-काक <i>m.</i> a raven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडकाष्ठ|दण्डकाष्ठ
दंड-काष्ठ <i>n.</i> a wooden staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडग्रहण|दण्डग्रहण
दंड-ग्रहण <i>n.</i> assumption of the staff of a yati, becoming a mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडच्छदन|दण्डच्छदन
दंड-च्छदन <i>n.</i> a room in which utensils of various kinds are kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडढक्का|दण्डढक्का
दंड-ढक्का <i>f.</i> a kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडादंडि|दण्डादण्डि
दंडादंडि <i>ind.</i> (fighting) with sticks and staves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडदास|दण्डदास|दण्डदासः
दंड-दास <i>m.</i> one who has become a slave from non-payment of a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडदेवकुल|दण्डदेवकुल
दंड-देवकुल <i>n.</i> a court of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडधर|दण्डधर|दण्डधरः
दंड-धर, -धार <i>(I) a.</i> carrying a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडधार|दण्डधार|दण्डधारः
दंड-धर, -धार <i>(I) a.</i> carrying a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडधार|दण्डधार|दण्डधारः
दंड-धार <i>(II) m.</i> 1. an epithet of Yama; 2. a king, श्रमनुदं मनुदंडधरान्वयम् R.ix.3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडनायक|दण्डनायक|दण्डनायकः
