दंडन|दण्डन|दंडनं
दंडन <i>n.</i> Punishing, chastising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडार|दण्डार|दंडारः|दण्डारः
दंडार <i>m.</i> 1. A furious elephant; 2. a potter’s wheel; 3. a raft, a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडिक|दण्डिक|दंडिकः|दण्डिकः
दंडिक <i>m.</i> A staff-bearer, a mace-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडिका|दण्डिका
दंडिका <i>f.</i> 1. A stick; 2. a row, a line; 3. a string of pearls, a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडिन्|दण्डिन्
दंडिन् <i>m.</i> 1. A Brāhmaṇa of the fourth order, a Sannyāsin; 2. a door-keeper; 3. an epithet of Yama; 4. a king; 5. name of a poet, author of Kāvyādarsa and Daśakumāracharita, e.g. जाते जगति वाल्मीके कविरित्यभिधाऽभवत् । कवी इति ततो व्यासे कवयस्त्वयि दंडिनि ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=323-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्|दन्त्
दत् <i>m. (This word has no forms for the first five cases and is rarely used by itself. According to some authorities, it is not a separate word but a substitute for दंत in certain cases.)</i> A tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दच्छद|दच्छदः
