दत्ताप्रदानिक|दत्ताप्रदानिकं
दत्त-अनपाकर्मन्, -अप्रदानिक <i>n.</i> non-delivery or resumption of gifts (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तावधान
दत्त-अवधान <i>a.</i> attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्रेय|दत्तात्रेयः
दत्त-आत्रेय <i>m.</i> name of a sage, son of Atri and Anasūyā, considered as an incarnation of Brahman (m.), Viṣṇu and Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादर
दत्त-आदर <i>a.</i> 1. showing respect, respectful; 2. treated with respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तशुल्का
दत्त-शुल्का <i>f.</i> a bride for whom a dowry has been paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तहस्त
दत्त-हस्त <i>a.</i> 1. having a hand given for upport, supported by the hand, स कामरूपेश्वरदत्तहस्तः R.vii.17; (hence) 2. supported, encouraged, assisted, दैवेनेत्थं दत्तहस्तावलंबे Rat.i, or वात्या खेदं कृशांग्याः सुचिरमवयवैर्दत्तहस्ता करोति Ve.ii. (In this phrase, हस्त is rendered by some scholars by ‘writing, autograph’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तक|दत्तकः
दत्तक <i>m.</i> An adopted son, Yaj.ii.130. See दत्त II.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=324-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ति|दत्तिः
