दंतिन्|दन्तिन्
दंतावल <i>m.</i> An elephant, Bh.V.i.60, R.i.71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंतुर|दन्तुर|दन्तुरः
दंतुर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Having long or projecting teeth, e.g. शूकरे निहते चैव दंतुरो जायते नरः; 2. notched, serrated, uneven; 3. undulatory; 4. rising, bristling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंतुरा|दन्तुरा
दंतुर <i>a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Having long or projecting teeth, e.g. शूकरे निहते चैव दंतुरो जायते नरः; 2. notched, serrated, uneven; 3. undulatory; 4. rising, bristling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंतुरच्छद|दन्तुरच्छद|दन्तुरच्छदः
