दभ्र|दभ्रं|दभ्रः
दभ्र <i>(I) a. (f. भ्रा)</i> Little, small, अदभ्रदर्भामधिशय्य स स्थलीम् Kir.i.38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्रा
दभ्र <i>(I) a. (f. भ्रा)</i> Little, small, अदभ्रदर्भामधिशय्य स स्थलीम् Kir.i.38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्र|दभ्रं|दभ्रः
दभ्र <i>(II) m.</i> The ocean.(दभ्रम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘a little, slightly.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्
दम् <i>vt. or vi. 4P (pp. दमित or दांत; pres. दाम्यति; caus. दमयति)</i> 1. To be tamed, to be tranquilised, M.iv.35, vi.8; 2. to subdue, to conquer, to restrain, यमो दाम्यति राक्षसान् Bt.xviii.20, xv.37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम|दमः
दम <i>m.</i> 1. Taming, subduing; 2. self-command, subduing the passions, curbing the senses (निग्रहो बाह्यवृत्तीनां दम इत्यभिधीयते) Bg.x.4; 3. curbing the evil propensities of the mind, turning the mind from bad deeds (कुत्सितात्कर्मणो विप्र यच्च चित्तनिवारणं स कीर्तितो दमः); 4. firmness of the mind; 5. punishment, fine, M.ix.284; 6. mud, mire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथ|दमथः
दमथ <i>m.</i> 1. Suppressing the passions, self-restraint; 2. punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथु|दमथुः
दमथ <i>m.</i> 1. Suppressing the passions, self-restraint; 2. punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन|दमनं|दमनः
दमन <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> 1. Taming, subduing, overpowering, defeating, e.g. सर्वदमन, शत्रुदमन; 2. tranquil, passionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनी
दमन <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> 1. Taming, subduing, overpowering, defeating, e.g. सर्वदमन, शत्रुदमन; 2. tranquil, passionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन|दमनं|दमनः
दमन <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Taming, subjugation; 2. punishing, chastising, दुर्दांतानां दमनविधयः क्षत्रियेष्वायतंते Mv.iii.; 3. self-restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयितृ
दमयितृ <i>m.</i> 1. A chasister, a punisher; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमित|दमितः
दमित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Tamed, tranquilized; 2. conquered, subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमिता
दमित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Tamed, tranquilized; 2. conquered, subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमुनस्
दमु(मू)नस् <i>m.</i> Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमूनस्
दमु(मू)नस् <i>m.</i> Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंपती
दंपती <i>m. du.</i> Man and wife, R.i.35, ii.70, M.iii.116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंभ|दम्भ|दंभः|दम्भः
दंभ <i>m.</i> 1. Deceit, fraud, roguery; 2. religious hypocrisy, Bg.xvi.4; 3. arrogance, ostentation; 4. sin, wickedness; 5. the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंभन|दम्भन|दंभनं
दंभन <i>n.</i> Cheating, deceiving, deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंभिन्|दम्भिन्
दंभिन् <i>m.</i> A hypocrite, an impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंभोलि|दम्भोलि|दंभोलिः|दम्भोलिः
दंभोलि <i>m.</i> Indra’s thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
दम्य <i>(I) a. (f. म्या)</i> 1. To be trained, R.vi.78; 2. to be subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्या
दम्य <i>(I) a. (f. म्या)</i> 1. To be trained, R.vi.78; 2. to be subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
दम्य <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A young bullock, नार्हति तातः पुंगाधारितायां धुरि दम्यं नियोजयितुम् Vikr.v.; 2. a steer that has to be tamed or trained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय्
दय् <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. दयित; pres. दयते)</i> 1. To pity, to have compassion for, to sympathise with, (with a gen.), रामस्य दयमानोऽप्तावध्येति तव लक्ष्मणः Bt.viii.119, ii.33, xv.63; 2. to protect, नगजा न गजा दयिता दयिताः Bt.x.9; 3. to love, to like, Bt.x.9 (the first दयित); 4. to go, to move; 5. to give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दया
दया <i>f.</i> Sympathy, compassion, pity, mercy, tenderness, R.ii.11, Bg.xvi.2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकूट|दयाकूटः
दया-कूट <i>m.</i> an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयावीर|दयावीरः
दया-वीर <i>m.</i> the sentiment of heroism based on compassion, i.e. the sentiment of chivalrous compassion (in rhetoric). The following is an instance of दयावीर- न कपोत भवंतमंतरा स्पृशतु श्येनसमुद्भवं भयम् । इदमद्य मया तृणीकृतं भवदायुःकुशले कलेवरम् R.G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=325-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालु|दयालुः
