दान्
दान् <i>vt. 1U (pres. दीदांसति-ते in the first sense; दानति-ते in the second)</i> 1. To make straight; 2. to cut, to divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
दान <i>n.</i> 1. Giving, delivering, K.S.v.15; 2. a gift, a present, Bg.xvii.20; 3. liberality, charity, R.i.69; 4. bribery as one of the four means by which a king overpowers his enemies (in civil polity) See उपायचतुष्टय; 5. the juice flowing from the temples of an elephant, rut, ichor, R.ii.7, iv.45, v.43; 6. cutting, dividing; 7. purification; 8. protection; 9. pasture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानकुल्या
दान-कुल्या <i>f.</i> the flow of fluid from an elephant’s temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानधर्म|दानधर्मः|दानधर्म्म|दानधर्म्मः
दान-धर्म <i>m.</i> alms-giving, charity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपति|दानपतिः
दान-पति <i>m.</i> 1. an exceedingly munificent man; 2. Akrūra, a friend of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपत्र
दान-पत्र <i>n.</i> a deed of gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपात्र
दान-पात्र <i>n.</i> a Brāhmaṇa fit to receive gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानप्रतिभाव्य
दान-प्रतिभाव्य <i>n.</i> security for payment of a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानभिन्न
दान-भिन्न <i>a.</i> made hostile by bribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवीर|दानवीरः
दान-वीर <i>m.</i> 1. an exceedingly liberal man; 2. the sentiment of heroism based on liberality, i.e. the sentiment of enthusiastic liberality (in rhetoric). The following is an instance- कियदिदमधिकं मे यद्द्विजायार्थायित्रे कवचमरमणीयं कुंडले चार्पयामि । अकरुणमवकृत्य द्राक्कृपाणेन निर्यद्बहलरुधिरधारं मौलिमावेदयामि R.G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशूर
दान-शूर, -शौंड <i>m.</i> an exceedingly liberal man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशौंड|दानशौण्ड|दानशौण्डः
दान-शूर, -शौंड <i>m.</i> an exceedingly liberal man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=329-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानक|दानकं
दानक <i>n.</i> A mean gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=330-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव|दानवः
दानव <i>m.</i> A demon, a Rākṣasa, Bg.x.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=330-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवारि|दानवारिः
दानव-अरि <i>m.</i> 1. a god; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=330-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवगुरु|दानवगुरुः
