दिश्य|दिश्यं
दिश्य <i>a. (f. श्या)</i> Belonging to or born in any quarter of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्या
दिश्य <i>a. (f. श्या)</i> Belonging to or born in any quarter of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट|दिष्टं|दिष्टः
दिष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Shown, pointed out; 2. described, referred to; 3. fixed, settled, (pp. of दिश् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टा
दिष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Shown, pointed out; 2. described, referred to; 3. fixed, settled, (pp. of दिश् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट|दिष्टं|दिष्टः
दिष्ट <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Fate, destiny; 2. order, direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट|दिष्टं|दिष्टः
दिष्ट <i>(III) m.</i> Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टांत|दिष्टान्त|दिष्टान्तः
दिष्ट-अंत <i>m.</i> death, दिष्टांतमाप्स्यति भवानपि पुत्रशोकात् R.ix.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टि|दिष्टिः
दिष्टि <i>f.</i> 1. Direction, instruction, rule, precept; 2. a kind of measure; 3. fate, destiny, fortune; 4. good fortune, happiness, राजकुले दिष्टिवृद्धिसंभ्रमो महानभूत् Kad.; 5. joy.(The inst. sing. दिष्ट्या is used as an indeclinable in the sense of, ‘fortunately,’ ‘how glad I am,’ दिष्ट्याऽर्धश्रुतविप्रलंभजनितक्रोधादहं नो गतो दिष्ट्या नो परुषं रुषार्धकथने किंचिन्मया व्याहृतम् । मां प्रत्याययितुं विमूढहृदयं दिष्ट्या कथांतं गता मिथ्यादूषितयाऽनया विरहितं दिष्ट्या न जातं जगत् ॥ Ve.ii.)(दिष्ट्या वृध् ‘to congratulate anyone upon.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=333-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिह्
दिह् <i>vt. 2U (pp. दिग्ध; pres. देग्धि, दिग्धे; desid. दिधिक्षति)</i> 1. To anoint, to plaster, to smear, Bt.xvii.54; 2. to pollute, to soil, R.xvi.15.With सम्-, 1. to doubt, to be uncertain about, संदिग्धसाध्यवा पक्षः T.S.; 2. to raise an objection; 3. to mistake for, धूपैर्जालविनिःसृतैर्वलभयः संदिग्धपारावताः Vikr.iii., K.S.vi.40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=334-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
दी <i>vi. 4Ā (pp. दीन; pres. दीयते)</i> To perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=334-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्ष्
दीक्ष् <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. दीक्षित; pres. दीक्षते)</i> 1. To consecrate anyone for the performance of a sacred rite; 2. to dedicate oneself to; 3. to initiate a pupil; 4. to invest with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=334-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षक|दीक्षकः
दीक्षक <i>m.</i> A spiritual guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=334-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षण|दीक्षणं
दीक्षण <i>n.</i> Initiation, consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=334-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षा
दीक्षा <i>f.</i> 1. Consecration for a religious ceremony, R.iii.44, 65; 2. a ceremony preliminary to a sacrifice; 3. investiture with the sacred thread; 4. a ceremony in general, R.iii.33, K.S.viii.24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=334-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षांत|दीक्षान्त|दीक्षान्तः
