दृश्
दृश् <i>vt. 1P (pp. दृष्ट; pres. पश्यति)</i> 1. To see, to look at, to view, to behold, R.iii.42, M.ii.54; 2. to visit, to wait upon, e.g. प्रत्युद्ययौ मुनिं द्रष्टुं ब्रह्माणमिव वासवः; 3. to see with the mind, to learn, to know, to understand, M.xii.23; 4. to inspect, to search, to investigate, to decide, Yaj.i.327, ii.305; 5. to see by divine intuition, e.g. ददर्शादौ मधुच्छंदा द्व्यधिकं यदृचां शतम्; 6. to look on while anything occurs which cannot be prevented.With उद्-, to expect, to foresee, to see in prospect, उत्पश्यामि द्रुतमपि सखे मत्प्रियार्थं यियासोः कालक्षेपं ककुभसुरभौ पर्वते पर्वते ते Megh.i.22.With सम्-, to see, to behold, to see well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=340-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् <i>Caus. (दर्शयति-ते)</i> 1. to show, to point out, न दिवीद्रायुधं दृष्ट्वा कस्यचिदर्शयेद्बुधः M.iv.57, R.i.47; 2. to prove, to demonstrate, Bt.xv.12; 3. to make visible, तदेव मे दर्शय देव रूपम् Bg.xi.45; 4. to produce, to adduce, e.g. अत्र श्रुतिं दर्शयति; 5. (Atm.) to show oneself, to appear, e.g. दर्शयते भृत्यान् राजा स्वयमेव, or स संततं दर्शयते गतस्मयः कृताधिपत्यामिव साधु बंधुताम् Kir.i.10.With अनु-, to show, to exhibit, to make clear.With आ-, to point out, to show, उत्कलादर्शितपथः कलिंगाभिमुखो ययौ R.iv.38.With उप-, to point out, to show, to communicate to, to make acquainted with, नयविद्भिर्नवे राज्ञि सदसच्चोपदर्शितम् R.iv.10.With नि-, 1. to show, to point out, R.vi.31; 2. to treat of (in a book); 3. to prove, to demonstrate; 4. to illustrate by an example.With प्र-, 1. to show, to discover; 2. to prove, to demonstrate.With सम्-, 1. to show, to exhibit, to discover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=340-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् <i>Pass. (दृश्यते)</i> 1. to be seen, to become visible, to be manifested, Bt.iii.19, M.viii.152, R.iii.40; 2. to be found, to occur (as in a book), e.g. विंदतिः भाव्येऽपि दृश्यते; 3. to be regarded or considered, सामान्यप्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकमियं दारेषु दृश्या त्वया Sak.iv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=340-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् <i>Desid. (दिदृक्षते)</i> to wish to see, to desire to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=340-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् <i>(I) a. (at the end of compounds)</i> 1. Seeing, superintending, viewing; 2. discerning, knowing; 3. looking like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=341-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश् <i>(II) f.</i> 1. Seeing, viewing, perceiving; 2. the eye, sight, e.g. संदधे दृशमुदग्रतारकाम् R.xi.69; 3. knowledge; 4. the number ‘two.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=341-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

