द्योतिस् <i>n.</i> 1. Light, brightness; 2. a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतिरिंगण|द्योतिरिङ्गण|द्योतिरिङ्गणः
द्योतिरिंगण <i>m.</i> the firefly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रंक्षण|द्रङ्क्षण|द्रङ्क्षणं
द्रंक्षण <i>n.</i> A measure of weight, a tolā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रढय्
द्रढय् <i>vt. (denom. pres. द्रढयति)</i> 1. To fasten, to tighten, to strengthen, विशुद्धेरुत्कर्षस्त्वयि तु मम भक्तिं द्रढयति Ut.iv.; 2. to confirm, to corroborate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रढिमन्
द्रढिमन् <i>m.</i> 1. Firmness, tightness, बधान द्रागेव द्रढिमरमणीयं परिकरम् G.L.47; 2. heaviness; 3. affirmation, assertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रप्स|द्रप्सः
द्रप्स <i>n.</i> Diluted sour milk, diluted curds. (Also द्रप्स्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रम्
द्रम् <i>vt. 1P (pres. द्रमति)</i> To run, to run about, Bt.xiv.70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रम्म|द्रम्मं
द्रम्म <i>m.</i> A drachma (a word of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव|द्रवः
द्रव <i>(I) a. (f. वा)</i> 1. Running (as a horse); 2. dropping, oozing, wet, R.vii.7; 3. liquid, K.S.ii.11; 4. melted.(द्रवीभू ‘to melt,’ द्रवीभूतं प्रेम्णा तव हृदयमस्मिन्क्षण इव Ut.iii.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवा
द्रव <i>(I) a. (f. वा)</i> 1. Running (as a horse); 2. dropping, oozing, wet, R.vii.7; 3. liquid, K.S.ii.11; 4. melted.(द्रवीभू ‘to melt,’ द्रवीभूतं प्रेम्णा तव हृदयमस्मिन्क्षण इव Ut.iii.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव|द्रवः
द्रव <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Going, motion; 2. dropping, trickling; 3. flight, retreat; 4. play, amusement; 5. speed, velocity; 6. fluidity, liquefaction; 7. juice, decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवाधार|द्रवाधारः
द्रव-आधार <i>m.</i> 1. a small vessel; 2. the hands joined and hollowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवज|द्रवजः
द्रव-ज <i>m.</i> treacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवद्रव्य
द्रव-द्रव्य <i>n.</i> a fluid substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवरसा
द्रव-रसा <i>f.</i> lac, gum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=347-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवंती
द्रवंती <i>f.</i> A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=348-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविड|द्रविडः
द्रविड <i>m.</i> 1. Name of a country on the east coast of the Dekkan; 2. a native of that country, विमुक्तं द्रविडपुंगवेन R.G.; 3. name of a degraded tribe. See M.x.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=348-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविण|द्रविणं
द्रविण <i>n.</i> 1. Property, substance, wealth, Bh.V.iv.29; 2. gold, R.iv.70; 3. thing, matter, material; 4. strength, power; 5. valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=348-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविणाधिपति|द्रविणाधिपतिः
द्रविण-अधिपति, -ईश्वर <i>n.</i> an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=348-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविणेश्वर|द्रविणेश्वरः
द्रविण-अधिपति, -ईश्वर <i>n.</i> an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=348-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्य|द्रव्यं
द्रव्य <i>n.</i> 1. Substance, thing, object; 2. material to be worked upon; 3. elementary substance considered as one of the seven categories (in the Vaiśeṣika philosophy); (dravya is ninefold- पृथिव्यापस्तेजोवाय्वाकाशकालदिगात्ममनांसि T.S.); 4. possession, wealth, goods, money; 5. a fit object (to receive any impression &c. Cf. अद्रव्य); 6. bell-metal; 7. modesty; 8. spirituous liquor; 9. a stake, a wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=348-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यार्जन|द्रव्यार्ज्जन
