द्वैध|द्वैधं
द्वैध <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Duality, duplicity; 2. disunion, diversity, contest, difference, श्रुतिद्वैधं तु यत्र स्यात् M.ii.14; 3. doubt, uncertainty; 4. double-dealing, one of the six modes of foreign policy. See द्वैधीभाव below and आसन (5).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=352-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीभाव|द्वैधीभावः
द्वैधीभाव <i>m.</i> 1. Duplicity, double nature; 2. difference; 3. doubt, uncertainty; 4. one of the six military tactics (गुण q.v.) or courses. According to some, it consists in dividing one’s army and opposing the enemy in parts somewhat after the mode of guerilla warfare, M.vii.160, 173. According to others, it means ‘keeping friendly attitude with all or with two hostile powers,’ ‘a kind of double-dealing or duplicity.’ See Mall. on Sis.ii.56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=352-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

