धातृ
धातृ <i>m.</i> 1. A maker, a creator, an author; 2. a bearer, a supporter; 3. an epithet of Brahman (m.), the creator of the world, सुतेन धातुश्चरणौ भुवस्तले Sis.i.13, R.xiii.6, Sr.T.3, Megh.ii.19; 4. an epithet of Viṣṇu; 5. the soul; 6. a name for the seven sages (सप्तर्षयः), the first creation of Brahman (m.); See K.S.vi.9; 7. a married woman’s paramour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=358-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्र|धात्रं
धात्र <i>n.</i> A vessel for holding any thing, a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=358-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्री
धात्री <i>f.</i> 1. A nurse, a wet-nurse, a foster-mother, उवाच धात्र्या प्रथमोदितं वचः R.iii.25, K.S.vii.25; 2. the earth; 3. mother, Yaj.iii.82; 4. the āmalaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=358-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रीपुत्र|धात्रीपुत्त्रः|धात्रीपुत्रः
