धारिणी
धारिणी <i>f.</i> The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिन्
धारिन् <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> 1. Carrying, bearing, sustaining, holding, R.xii.41; 2. keeping in one’s memory, अज्ञेभ्यो ग्रंथिनः श्रेष्ठा ग्रंथिभ्यो धारिणो वराः M.xii.103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिणी
धारिन् <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> 1. Carrying, bearing, sustaining, holding, R.xii.41; 2. keeping in one’s memory, अज्ञेभ्यो ग्रंथिनः श्रेष्ठा ग्रंथिभ्यो धारिणो वराः M.xii.103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्तराष्ट्र|धार्तराष्ट्रः|धार्त्तराष्ट्र|धार्त्तराष्ट्रः
धार्तराष्ट्र <i>m.</i> 1. A son of Dhṛtarāṣṭra; 2. a sort of goose with black legs and bill, निपतंति धार्तताष्ट्राः कालवशान्मेदिनीपृष्ठे Ve.i. (where the word is used in both the senses as explained in the play itself).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिक|धार्मिकः|धार्म्मिक|धार्म्मिकः
धार्मिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. Righteous, just, virtuous; 2. resting on right, conformable to justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिकी
धार्मिक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. Righteous, just, virtuous; 2. resting on right, conformable to justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिण|धार्मिणं
