धार्ष्ट्य|धार्ष्ट्यं
धार्ष्ट्य <i>n.</i> Violence, arrogance, impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
धाव् <i>(I) vi. 1P (pp. धावित; pres. धावति)</i> 1. To flow, to stream forth, आशुकारी धावत्यंभसि तैलवत् Suśruta; 2. to run, to advance, to run fast or away, धावंत्यमी मृगजवाक्षमयेव रथ्याः Sak.i., धावति पश्चादसंस्तुतं चेतः ibid, Bt.xiv.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
धाव् <i>(II) vt. (pp. धावित or धौत; pres. धावति-ते)</i> To rub, to cleanse, to wash, to purify, to brighten, to polish, दधावाद्भिस्ततश्चक्षुः सुग्रीवस्य Bt.xiv.50, Sis.xvii.8.With निस्-, to wash off, निर्धौतदानामलगंडभित्तिः R.v.43, Sis.viii.51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
धावक <i>m.</i> 1. A washerman; 2. name of a poet, श्रीहर्षादेर्धावकादीनामिव (v.l. for बाणादीनामिव) यशः K.Pr.i., or प्रथितयशसां धावकसौमिल्लकविपुत्रादीनां प्रबंधानतिक्रम्य Mal.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावन|धावनं
धावन <i>n.</i> 1. Running, galloping; 2. flowing; 3. attack, assault; 4. cleansing, purifying; 5. rubbing with anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावल्य|धावल्यं
धावल्य <i>n.</i> Whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि <i>vt. 6P (pres. धियति)</i> To have, to hold, to possess.With सम्-, to make peace with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि <i>m. (at the end of compounds)</i> Any receptacle, e.g. उदधि, इषुधि, तोयधि, वारिधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=359-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक् <i>ind.</i> An interjection of reproach, menace or displeasure (‘fie,’ ‘shame,’ ‘what a pity’). This particle generally governs the acc. धिक्, तां च तं च मदनं च इमां च मां च Bhartr.ii.2, धिक्, सानुजं कुरुपतिं धिगजातशत्रुं धिग्भूपतीन् विफलशस्त्रभृतो धिगस्मान् Ve.iii.; but sometimes the nom. and loc. also, धिगर्थाः कष्टसंश्रयाः Panch.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कार|धिक्कारः
धिक्-कार <i>m.</i> reproach, contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्क्रिया
धिक्-क्रिया <i>f.</i> reproach, contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्दंड|धिग्दण्ड|धिग्दण्डः
धिक्-दंड <i>m.</i> reprimand, censure, M.viii.129.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्पारुष्य
धिक्-पारुष्य <i>n.</i> abuse, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिप्सु
धिप्सु <i>a.</i> Desiring to deceive, Bt.ix.33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिन्व्
धिन्व् <i>vt. 5P (pres. धिनोति)</i> To delight, to please, धिनोति नास्माञ्जलजेन पूजा त्वयान्वहं तन्वि वितन्यमाना Na.viii.97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण|धिषणः
धिषण <i>(I) m.</i> An epithet of Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण|धिषणः
