धीमत्|धीमन्त्
धी-मत् <i>(I) a.</i> wise, learned, intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमत्|धीमन्त्
धी-मत् <i>(II) m.</i> an epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमंत्रिन्|धीमन्त्रिन्
धी-मंत्रिन्, -सचिव <i>m.</i> a minister for counsel, (op. to कर्ममंत्रिन् ‘a member of the executive’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसचिव|धीसचिवः
धी-मंत्रिन्, -सचिव <i>m.</i> a minister for counsel, (op. to कर्ममंत्रिन् ‘a member of the executive’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीशक्ति|धीशक्तिः
धी-शक्ति <i>f.</i> intellectual faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसख|धीसखः
धी-सख <i>m.</i> an adviser, a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
धीत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Drunk, sucked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीता
धीत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Drunk, sucked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीति|धीतिः
धीति <i>f.</i> 1. Drinking; 2. thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर <i>(I) a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Wise, learned, clever, intelligent, धृतेश्च धीरः सदृशीर्व्यधत्त सः R.iii.10; 2. steady, steadfast, durable, R.ii.6; 3. resolute, persevering, of firm mind, विकारहेतौ सति विक्रियंते येषां न चेतांसि त एव धीराः K.S.i.59; 4. energetic, strong; 5. courageous, brave, bold; 6. composed, calm, collected; 7. well-behaved; 8. grave, solemn, R.xviii.4; 9. deep, hollow, loud (as sound), स्वरेण धीरेण निवर्तयन्निव R.iii.43; 10. lazy, dull; 11. gentle, slow; 12. pleasing, beautiful, attractive, धीरसमीरे यमुनातीरे Git.G.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरा
धीर <i>(I) a. (f. रा)</i> 1. Wise, learned, clever, intelligent, धृतेश्च धीरः सदृशीर्व्यधत्त सः R.iii.10; 2. steady, steadfast, durable, R.ii.6; 3. resolute, persevering, of firm mind, विकारहेतौ सति विक्रियंते येषां न चेतांसि त एव धीराः K.S.i.59; 4. energetic, strong; 5. courageous, brave, bold; 6. composed, calm, collected; 7. well-behaved; 8. grave, solemn, R.xviii.4; 9. deep, hollow, loud (as sound), स्वरेण धीरेण निवर्तयन्निव R.iii.43; 10. lazy, dull; 11. gentle, slow; 12. pleasing, beautiful, attractive, धीरसमीरे यमुनातीरे Git.G.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The ocean; 2. an epithet of king Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर <i>(III) n.</i> Saffron.(धीरम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘firmly, steadily, steadfastly,’ Am.S.11.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोदात्त|धीरोदात्तः
धीर-उदात्त <i>m.</i> the hero of a poetic composition who is brave and noble-minded. (He is thus defined- अविकत्थनः क्षमावानतिगंभीरो महासत्वः । स्थेयान्निगूढमानो धीरोदात्तो दृढव्रतः कथितः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोद्धत|धीरोद्धतः
धीर-उद्धत <i>m.</i> the hero of a poetic composition who is brave but haughty and boastful (thus defined- मायापरः प्रचंडश्चपलोऽहंकारदर्पभूयिष्ठः । आत्मश्लाघानिरतो धीरैर्धीरोद्धतः कथितः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरचेतस्
धीर-चेतस् <i>a.</i> strong minded, courageous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरप्रशांत|धीरप्रशान्त|धीरप्रशान्तः
धीर-प्रशांत <i>m.</i> the hero of a poetic composition who is brave and calm (thus defined- सामान्यगुणैर्भूयान् द्विजादिको धीरप्रशांतः स्यात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरललित|धीरललितः
धीर-ललित <i>m.</i> the hero of a poetic composition who is brave but sportive and reckless (thus defined- निश्चिंतो मृदुरनिशं कलापरो धीरललितः स्यात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरस्कंध|धीरस्कन्ध|धीरस्कन्धः
धीर-स्कंध <i>m.</i> a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरता
धीरता <i>f.</i> 1. Fortitude (physical or moral), सहजामप्यपहाय धीरतां (विललाप) R.viii.43; 2. gravity, solemnity (as indicated by silence &c.), प्रत्यादेशान्न (v.l. शं न) खलु भवतो धीरतां कल्पयामि Megh.ii.51. For other meanings, See धैर्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरा
धीरा <i>f.</i> The heroine of a poetic composition, who though jealous of her husband or lover suppresses all outward expression of her resentment in his presence (व्यंग्यकोपप्रकाशिका धीरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीराधीरा
धीरा-अधीरा <i>f.</i> the heroine of a poetic piece who being jealous of her husband or lover, alternately expresses and conceals her jealousy (व्यंग्याव्यंग्यकोपप्रकाशिका धीराधीरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटि|धीलटिः
धीलटि(टी) <i>f.</i> A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटी
धीलटि(टी) <i>f.</i> A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर <i>(I) m.</i> A fisherman, विस्तारितं मकरकेतनधीवरेण Bhartr.i.85, ii.61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर <i>(II) m.</i> Iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरी
धीवरी <i>f.</i> 1. A fisherman’s wife; 2. a fish-basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु <i>vt. or vi. 5U (pp. धुत; pres. धुनोति, धुनुते)</i> See धू below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष्
धुक्ष् <i>vi. 1Ā (pp. धुक्षित; pres. धुक्षते)</i> 1. To be kindled; 2. to be weary.With सम्-, to be kindled, to be excited, संदुधुक्षे तयोः कोपः Bt.xiv.109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष्
धुक्ष् <i>Caus. (धुक्षयति-ते)</i> With सम्-, to kindle, to excite, निर्वाणभूयिष्ठमथास्य वीर्यं संधुक्षयंतीव वपुर्गुणेन K.S.iii.52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=360-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुत|धुतः
धुत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Abandoned; 2. shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुता
धुत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Abandoned; 2. shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनी
धुनी(नि) <i>f.</i> A river, कतमया पुराणां संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G.L.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनि|धुनिः
धुनी(नि) <i>f.</i> A river, कतमया पुराणां संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G.L.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनीनाथ|धुनीनाथः
धुनी(नि)-नाथ <i>m.</i> the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनिनाथ|धुनिनाथः
धुनी(नि)-नाथ <i>m.</i> the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर् <i>f. (nom. sing. धूः)</i> 1. A yoke, अत्रस्नुभिर्युक्तधुरं तुरंगैः R.xiv.47; 2. that part of it which rests on the shoulder; 3. the pin at both ends of an axle for fastening the nave of the wheel; 4. the pole of a carriage; 5. a load, a burden (lit. and fig.), तेन धूर्जगतो गुर्वीं सचिवेषु निचिक्षिपे R.i.34, v.66, K.S.vi.30; 6. the highest place, the front, the top, अपांसुलानां धुरि कीर्तनीया R.ii.2, स्थेयाः पितेव धुरि पुत्रिणाम् i.91, धुरि स्थिता त्वं पतिदेवतानाम् xiv.74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्गत
धूर्गत <i>a.</i> 1. standing on the pole of a chariot; 2. standing at the head, foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्जटि|धूर्जटिः|धूर्ज्जटि
धूर्जटि <i>m.</i> an epithet of Sira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्धर|धूर्धरः
धूर्धर <i>(I) a.</i> 1. bearing the yoke; 2. fit to be harnessed; 3. laden with important duties; 4. chief, foremost, preeminent, e.g. धुरंधरः पुण्यकृदेष तापसः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरंधर|धुरन्धर|धुरन्धरः
धूर्धर <i>(I) a.</i> 1. bearing the yoke; 2. fit to be harnessed; 3. laden with important duties; 4. chief, foremost, preeminent, e.g. धुरंधरः पुण्यकृदेष तापसः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरंधर|धुरन्धर|धुरन्धरः
धुरंधर <i>(II) m.</i> 1. a beast of burden; 2. a man of business; 3. a chief, a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वह|धूर्वहः|धूर्व्वह|धूर्व्वहः
धूर्वह <i>(I) a.</i> 1. carrying a burden; 2. managing affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वह|धूर्वहः|धूर्व्वह|धूर्व्वहः
धूर्वह <i>(II) m.</i> a beast of burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरा
धुरा <i>f.</i> A burden, a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण <i>(f. णा) (I) a.</i> 1. Able to bear a burden; 2. charged with important duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीणा
धुरीण <i>(f. णा) (I) a.</i> 1. Able to bear a burden; 2. charged with important duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A beast of burden; 2. a man of business; 3. a chief, a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य <i>(I) a. (f. र्या)</i> 1. Able to bear a burden; 2. able to discharge important duties; 3. standing at the head, foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्या
धुर्य <i>(I) a. (f. र्या)</i> 1. Able to bear a burden; 2. able to discharge important duties; 3. standing at the head, foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A beast of burden; 2. a horse or bullock yoked to a carriage, अथ यंतारमादिश्य धुर्यान् विश्रामयेति सः R.i.54, M.iv.67, K.S.vi.76; 3. a leader, a chief, न हि सति कुलधुर्ये सूर्यवंश्या गृहाय R.vii.71; 4. one who carries a burden, R.v.66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तुर|धुस्तुरः
धुस्तु(स्तू)र <i>m.</i> Name of a plant, (the same as धत्तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तूर|धुस्तूरः
धुस्तु(स्तू)र <i>m.</i> Name of a plant, (the same as धत्तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
धू <i>vt. 1U, 5U, 6P, 9U, 10U (pp. धूत or धून; pres. धवति-ते; धूनोति, धुनुते; धुवति; धुनाति, धुनीते; धूनयति-ते)</i> 1. To shake, to agitate, to cause to tremble, धुन्वन् मुहुः प्रोतघने विषाणे K.S.vii.49, धुन्वन् कल्पद्रुमकिसलयानि Megh.i.62, Bt.i.101, Am.S.58; 2. to excite, to kindle, भ्रमति पवनधूतः सर्वतोऽग्निर्वनांते Rt.i.26; 3. to shake off, to remove, स्रजमपि शिरस्यंधः क्षिप्तां धुनोत्याहिशंकया Sak.vii.; 4. to treat roughly, to hurt, आरोहितं शनैः पश्चाद्धुन्वंतमपि पार्थिवम् Panch.i.With अव-, 1. to disregard, to treat with contempt or disrespect, अवधूतप्रणिपाताः पश्चात्संतप्यमानमनसोऽपि Vikr.iii., K.S.iii.8; 2. to remove, to shake off, सुरवधूरवधूतभयाः शरैः R.ix.19, or आलिंगन् योऽवधूतस्त्रिपुरयुवतिभिः Am.S.2 (where the word is used in both the senses); 3. to shake, to move, to cause to tremble, लीलावधूतैः … चामरैः Megh.i.35, R.vii.43.With उद्-, 1. to shake up, to throw up, to raise, to move up, रजःकणैः खुरोद्धूतैः R.i.85, ix.50, Kir.v.39; 2. to shake off, to throw off, उद्धूतपापाः Megh.i.55; 3. to disturb, to excite.With निस्-, 1. to shake off, to remove, to expel, ज्ञाननिर्धूतकल्मषाः Bg.v.16, R.xii.57; 2. to disregard, to treat with contempt.With वि-, 1. to shake, to cause to tremble, नलिनीं निधुन्वन् Rt.iii.10, vi.29; 2. to treat with disrespect; 3. to shake off.(The Kavirahasya illustrates the several conjugations of धू (and धु) in the following stanza- धूनोति चंपकवनानि धुनोत्यशोकं चूतं धुनाति धुवति स्फुटितातिमुक्तम् । वायुर्विधूनयति चंपकपुष्परेणून् यत्कानने धवति चंदनमंजरीश्च.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
धू <i>f.</i> Shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूत|धूतः
धूत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Shaken; 2. shaken off, removed; 3. disregarded, treated with contempt; 4. guessed, (pp. of धू q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूता
धूत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Shaken; 2. shaken off, removed; 3. disregarded, treated with contempt; 4. guessed, (pp. of धू q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतपाप
धूत-पाप <i>a.</i> who has shaken off his sins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूति|धूतिः
धूति <i>f.</i> Shaking, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धून|धूनः
धून <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Shaken, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूना
धून <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Shaken, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनि|धूनिः
धूनि <i>f.</i> Shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप्
धूप् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1P (pp. धूपायित; pres. धूपायति)</i> 1. To heat; 2. to be heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप्
धूप् <i>(II) vt. or vi. 10U (pres. धूपयति-ते)</i> 1. To fumigate, to perfume, to make fragrant; 2. to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=361-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
