धृ <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1U, 6Ā (pp. धृत; pres. धरति-ते, ध्रियते; desid. दिधरिषते)</i> To be, to exist, ध्रियते यावदेकोऽपि रिपुस्तावत्कुतः सुखम् Sis.ii.35, सुरतश्रमसंभृतो मुखे ध्रियते स्वेदलवोद्गमोऽपि ते R.viii.51. For other senses, See धृ II.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृ
धृ <i>(II) vt. 10U (pres. धारयति-ते) (The senses of this root are variously modified according to the noun it is connected with.)</i> 1. To hold, to bear, to carry, to hold up, to bear up, वैणवीं धारयेद्यष्टिं सोदकं च कमंडलुम् M.iv.36, Bg.vi.13, Bt.xvii.54; 2. to support, to maintain, प्रातःकुंदप्रसवशिथिलं जीवितं धारयेथाः Megh.ii.50; 3. to restrain, to curb; 4. to fix upon, to direct towards, e.g. युद्धे मतिमधारयम्; 5. to suffer, to bear, to undergo; 6. to wear, to use (as a garment); 7. to assign anything to any person; 8. (cl. 10 only) to owe anything to a person, (with dat. or gen., e.g. कृष्णाय or कृष्णस्य शतं धारयति).(दंडं धृ to chastise, to use force, M.xi.21. जीवितं, प्राणान्, शरीरं, देहं or गात्रं धृ to preserve the vital spirits, to continue to live. मनः, मतिं or चित्तं धृ to fix the mind, to think of, to resolve. व्रतं धृ to observe a vow. तुलया धृ to hold in a balance, to weigh. शिरसा or मूर्ध्नि धृ to bear on the head, to respect highly. मनसा धृ to recollect, to remember, to bear in the mind. समये धृ to cause to make an agreement.)With अव-, 1. to fix, to determine; 2. to understand, to know, न विश्वमूर्तेरवधार्यते वपुः K.S.v.78.With उद्-, 1. to save, lift up; 2. to root up, to draw out.With निस्-, to verify, to determine accurately, प्रचुरीभवन्न निरधारि तमः Sis.ix.20.With वि-, 1. to seize, to take hold of, अंशुकपल्लवेन विधृतः Am.S.79, 85; 2. to wear, to bear; 3. to maintain, to support.With सम्-, 1. to hold, to bear; 2. to restrain, to curb; 3. to retain in the mind.With समुद्-, 1. to pull up by the roots, to take out, e.g. नवसंरोहणशिथिलस्तरुरिव सुकरः समुद्धर्तुम्; 2. to deliver.With संप्र-, 1. to consider, to think of; 2. to determine, to ascertain, Sis.ix.60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत|धृतः
धृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Held, borne, supported; 2. possessed; 3. kept, retained; 4. seized, laid hold of; 5. placed, deposited; 6. weighed, (pp. of धृ q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृता
धृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Held, borne, supported; 2. possessed; 3. kept, retained; 4. seized, laid hold of; 5. placed, deposited; 6. weighed, (pp. of धृ q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतात्मन्
धृत-आत्मन् <i>a.</i> firm-minded, steady, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतपट
धृत-पट <i>a.</i> covered with a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतराजन्
धृत-राजन् <i>m.</i> a country governed by a good king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतवर्मन्|धृतवर्म्मन्
धृत-वर्मन् <i>a.</i> cased in an armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृति|धृतिः
धृति <i>f.</i> 1. Holding, seizing, possessing; 2. firmness, steadiness; 3. fortitude, resolution; 4. satisfaction, contentment; 5. satisfaction considered as one of the 33 subordinate feelings (in rhetoric); (it is thus defined- ज्ञानाभीष्टागमाद्यैस्तु संपुर्णस्पृहता धृतिः); 6. pleasure, joy, चक्षुर्बध्नाति धृतिम् Vikr.ii., R.iii.10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमत्|धृतिमन्त्
धृति-मत् <i>a.</i> 1. firm, resolute, M.vii.210; 2. glad, happy, satisfied, R.xiii.77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=362-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वन्
धृत्वन् <i>m.</i> 1. An epithet of Viṣṇu; 2. virtue, morality; 3. the sky; 4. the ocean; 5. a clever man; 6. a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्
धृष् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1P (pp. धर्षित; pres. धर्षति)</i> 1. To come together, to be compact; 2. to hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्
धृष् <i>(II) vt. 1P, 10U (pres. धर्षति, धर्षयति-ते)</i> 1. To offend, to injure; 2. to insult, to treat with indignity; 3. to assail, to overpower, to conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्
धृष् <i>(III) vi. or vt. 5P (pp. धृष्ट; pres. धृष्णोति)</i> 1. To be bold or courageous; 2. to be confident; 3. to be impudent or impatient; 4. to brave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्
धृष् <i>(IV) vt. 10Ā (pres. धर्षयते)</i> To assail, to attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ट|धृष्टः
धृष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Bold, courageous, confident; 2. impudent, rude, shameless; 3. forward, presumptuous; 4. profligate, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टा
धृष्ट <i>(I) a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Bold, courageous, confident; 2. impudent, rude, shameless; 3. forward, presumptuous; 4. profligate, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ट|धृष्टः
धृष्ट <i>(II) m.</i> A faithless husband or lover not ashamed of his fault; (the S.D. thus describes him- कृतागा अपि निःशंकस्तर्जितोऽपि न लज्जितः । दृष्टदोषोऽपि मिथ्यावाक् कथितो धृष्टनायकः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टमानिन्
धृष्ट-मानिन् <i>a.</i> having a high opinion of oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णज्
धृष्णज् <i>a.</i> 1. Bold, confident; 2. shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णि|धृष्णिः
धृष्णि <i>m.</i> A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णु|धृष्णुः
धृष्णु <i>a.</i> 1. Courageous, bold; 2. impudent, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धे
धे <i>vt. 1P (pp. धीत; pres. धयति; desid. धित्सति)</i> 1. To suck, to drink, to absorb; 2. to seek out, to draw away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेन|धेनः
धेन <i>m.</i> 1. The ocean; 2. a male river (नद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनु|धेनुः
धेनु <i>f.</i> A cow, milch cow, R.i.82, ii.1, 45.(धेनु is sometimes affixed to names of other animals to denote the female of a species, e.g. वडवधेनु; and at the end of a compound word it sometimes forms a dimunitive, e.g. खड्गधेनु, असिधेनु.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुक|धेनुकः
धेनुक <i>m.</i> Name of a demon killed by Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकसूदन|धेनुकसूदनः
धेनुक-सूदन <i>m.</i> an epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुका
धेनुका <i>f.</i> 1. A female elephant; 2. a milch cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्या
धेनुष्या <i>f.</i> A cow that has been pledged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैनुक|धैनुकं
धैनुक <i>n.</i> 1. A herd of cows; 2. a particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्य|धैर्यं|धैर्य्य|धैर्य्यं
धैर्य <i>n.</i> 1. Firmness, durability, strength, constancy, imperturbability, Sis.ix.59, Am.S.92; 2. calmness; 3. gravity patience; 4. fortitude, courage; 5. boldness, forwardness, Megh.i.40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत|धैवतः
धैवत <i>m.</i> The sixth of the seven primary notes of the gamut (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत्य|धैवत्यं
धैवत्य <i>n.</i> Cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोड|धोडः
धोड <i>m.</i> The same as डुंडुभ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोर्
धोर् <i>vt. or vi. 1P (pres. धोरति)</i> 1. To go quickly, to run, to trot; 2. to be skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरण|धोरणं
धोरण <i>n.</i> 1. A vehicle in general; 2. going well or quickly; 3. a horse’s trot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणि|धोरणिः
धोरणि(णी) <i>f.</i> 1. An uninterrupted series, यैर्माकंदवने मनोज्ञपवने सद्यः स्खलन्माधुरीधाराधोरणिधौतधामनि धराधीशत्वमालंब्यते Ud.; 2. tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणी
धोरणि(णी) <i>f.</i> 1. An uninterrupted series, यैर्माकंदवने मनोज्ञपवने सद्यः स्खलन्माधुरीधाराधोरणिधौतधामनि धराधीशत्वमालंब्यते Ud.; 2. tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरित|धोरितं
धोरित <i>n.</i> 1. Injuring, hurting; 2. going, motion; 3. a horse’s trot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
धौत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Washed, cleaned, purified, येन धौता गिरः पुंसां विमलैः Śikshā., K.S.vi.57; 2. polished, brightened; 3. white, bright, shining, हरशिरश्चंद्रिकाधौतहर्म्या Megh.i.7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौता
धौत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Washed, cleaned, purified, येन धौता गिरः पुंसां विमलैः Śikshā., K.S.vi.57; 2. polished, brightened; 3. white, bright, shining, हरशिरश्चंद्रिकाधौतहर्म्या Megh.i.7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=363-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
