नद्
नद् <i>(I) vi. (but often used with a cognate acc., e.g. ननाद, नादान्) 1P (pres. नदति, प्रणदति)</i> 1. To sound, to resound, to thunder, नदत्याकाशगंगायाः स्रोतस्युद्दामदिग्गजे R.i.78, Sis.v.63, Bt.ii.4; 2. to shout, to cry, to speak.With उद्-, to roar, to cry, K.S.i.56.With नि-, to sound, R.v.75.With प्र-, to sound, to resound, Sis.ix.71.With वि-, to sound, to resound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=367-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्
नद् <i>Caus. (नादयति-ते)</i> 1. to fill with noise, to make resonant; 2. to cause to make sound.With वि-, to cause to utter notes, Ghat.10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=367-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्
नद् <i>(II) vi. 1P (pres. नंदति)</i> To be glad, to be satisfied with, to be glad of anything, ननंदरुस्तौ R.ii.22, iii.11, 22, iv.3.With अभि-, 1. to be glad, to be satisfied, नाभिनंदति न द्वेष्टि Bg.ii.57; 2. to desire, to wish for, to like, नाभिनंदेत मरणं नाभिनंदेत जीवितम् M.vi.45; 3. to greet, to congratulate upon, तमभ्यनंदत् प्रथमं प्रबोधितः R.iii.68, vii.69, 71; 4. to praise, to approve of, ताः पितृभिश्चाभिनंदिताः Sak.iii.With आ-, to be glad, आनंदितारस्त्वां दृष्ट्वा Bt.xxii.14.With प्रति-, 1. to bless, K.S.vii.87; 2. to congratulate upon, M.ii.54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=367-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्
नद् <i>Caus. (नंदयति-ते)</i> to gladden, to please, to make happy, सैव कुमुद्वती मे दृष्टिं न नंदयति संस्मरणीयशोभा Sak.iv., Bt.ii.16.With आ-, to gladden, to please, to make joyous, Yaj.i.356.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=367-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

