नम्
नम् <i>vt. or vi. 1U (pp. नत; pres. नमति-ते, प्रणमति-ते; caus. नमयति, नामयति, प्रणमयति; desid. निनंसति)</i> 1. To bow to, to make obeisance to, कस्माच्च ते न नमेरन् महात्मन् Bg.xi.37, K.S.vi.89; 2. to sink, to go down, अनंसीद्भूर्भरेणास्य Bt.xv.25, उन्नमति नमति वर्षति गर्जति मेघः Mrich.v.; 3. to bend; 4. to be bent or curved, e.g. पुष्पभारनता लता; 5. to subject oneself, e.g. अशक्तः संधिमान् नमेत्.With अभुद्-, to rise, to elevate.With अव-, 1. to bend, Sis.ix.74; 2. to bend oneself, to go down, त्वय्यादातुं जलमवनते Megh.i.46.With उद्-, 1. to rise, to spring up, to arise, उन्नमत्यकालदुर्दिनम् Mrich.iv.; 2. to rise, to ascen, to go up (lit. or fig.), उन्नमति नमति वर्षति गर्जति मेघः Mrich.v., उपासितगुरुप्रज्ञाभिमानोन्नताः Bhartr.iii.24; 3. to raise.With उप-, 1. to fall to one’s share, to occur, to happen, कस्यात्यंतं सुखमुपनतं दुःखमेकांततो वा Megh.ii.46, मत्संभोगः कथमुपनमेत् स्वप्नजोऽपि ii.28; 2. to present one with, to present, to offer, परलोकोपनतं जलांजलिम् R.viii.68; 3. to approach.With परि-, to stoop (as an elephant about to strike with his tusks, विष्के नागः पर्यणंसीत् स्व एव Sis.xviii.27); 2. to bend down, लज्जापरिणतैः (वदनकमलैः) Bhartr.i.4; 3. to be changed into, to appear in a different form, यथाहि लोके क्षीरं जलं वा स्वयमेव दधिहिमभावेन परिणमतेऽनपेक्ष्य बाह्यसाधनं तथेहापि भविष्यति S.Bh.; 4. to be developed, to be aged, to grow old, to decay, परिणतशरच्चंद्रिकासु क्षपासु Megh.ii.47; 5. to be digested (as food).With प्र-, 1. to bow to, to make obeisance to, (with an acc. or dat.), Bg.xi.44, R.ii.21. (साष्टांगं प्रणम्. See अष्टांग. दंडवत् प्रणम् to make obeisance by throwing oneself on the ground completely prostrate, like a staff, touching the ground at all parts. See दंडप्रणाम).With वि-, 1. to bend oneself, to be bent, विनमंति चास्य तरवः प्रचये Kir.vi.34, Bhartr.i.67.With विपरि-, to change for worse.With सम्-, 1. to subject oneself to, R.xviii.34; 2. to bend, K.S.i.34, Bt.ii.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=369-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

