नाथ्
नाथ् <i>vt. 1P (but Atm. in the last sense)</i> 1. To ask, to solicit anything, नाथंति के नाम न लोकनाथम् Na.iii.25; 2. to have power, to be master; 3. to harass; 4. to bless, to confer blessings, to wish good to. (See the line त्वामनुनाथते कुचयुगं पत्रावृतं मा कृथाः and Mammata’s remarks on it at, K.Pr.vii.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=374-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ|नाथः
नाथ <i>(I) m.</i> 1. A protector, master, leader, lord, R.ii.73, iii.45, K.S.i.58; 2. a husband; 3. a rope passed through the nose of a draft ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=374-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथवत्|नाथवन्त्
