नाना
नाना <i>ind.</i> 1. In different places, manifoldly, variously; 2. distinctly, separately; 3. without, (with an acc., inst. or abl.), e.g. नाना नारीं निष्फला लोकयात्रा, or न नाना शंभुना रामात्; 4. (when used as an adjective in the beginning of a compound) various, sundry, different, diverse, नानादिगंतवास्तव्यो महाजनसमाजः M.M.i., Bg.i.9, M.ix.148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=374-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

