नाय|नायः
नाय <i>m.</i> 1. A leader, a guide; 2. policy; 3. means, expedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=375-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायक|नायकः
नायक <i>m.</i> 1. A guide, a conductor; 2. a leader, a chief, a lord; 3. preeminent or principal personage, Bg.i.7; 4. a general, a commandant; 5. a hero in a piece of poetic composition (in rhetoric); (he is either a पति, उपपति or वैशिक); 7. the central gem of a necklace; 8. a paradigm, a leading example, e.g. दशैते पुंसि नायकाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=375-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायकाधिप|नायकाधिपः
नायक-अधिप <i>m.</i> a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=375-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायिका
नायिका <i>f.</i> 1. A mistress; 2. a wife; 3. the heroine in a piece of poetic composition (she is either स्वीया, परकीया or साधारणस्त्री). See under अन्यस्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=375-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

