निमग्न <i>a. (f. ग्ना)</i> 1. Plunged, submerged, sunk, निमग्नेन क्लेशैर्मननजलधेरंतरुदकम् R.G.; 2. gone down, set (as the sun); 3. overwhelmed, covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्ना
निमग्न <i>a. (f. ग्ना)</i> 1. Plunged, submerged, sunk, निमग्नेन क्लेशैर्मननजलधेरंतरुदकम् R.G.; 2. gone down, set (as the sun); 3. overwhelmed, covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जथु|निमज्जथुः
निमज्जथु <i>m.</i> 1. The act of diving or entering into; 2. plunging into the bed, sleeping, तल्पे कांतांतरैः सार्धं मन्येऽहं धिङ् निमज्जथुम् Bt.v.20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जन|निमज्जनं
निमज्जन <i>m.</i> Bathing, diving (lit. and fig.), दृङ् निमज्जनमुपैति सुधायाम् Na.v.94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमंत्रण|निमन्त्रण|निमंत्रणं|निमन्त्रणं
निमंत्रण <i>n.</i> 1. Invitation; 2. summoning, calling; 3. a summons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमय|निमयः
निमय <i>m.</i> Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमान|निमानं
निमान <i>n.</i> 1. Measure; 2. price (निमानं मूल्यम् S.K.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमि|निमिः
निमि <i>m.</i> 1. Twinkling; 2. name of a king of Videha, R.xi.49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्त|निमित्तं
निमित्त <i>n.</i> 1. A mark, a sign, a token; 2. a butt, a target, निमित्तादपराद्धेषोर्धानुष्कस्येन वल्गितम् Sis.ii.27; 3. an omen (good or bad), निमित्तानि च पश्यामि विपरीतानि केशव Bg.i.30, R.i.86, M.vi.50; 4. cause, motive; 5. instrumental or efficient cause, (op. to उपादान); 6. apparent cause, pretext, निमित्तमात्रं भव सव्यसाचिन् Bg.xi.33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तार्थ|निमित्तार्थः
निमित्त-अर्थ <i>m.</i> the infinitive mood (in gram.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तकारण|निमित्तकारणं
निमित्त-कारण <i>n.</i> an instrumental or efficient cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=381-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तहेतु
