नियुक्त|नियुक्तः
नियुक्त <i>(I) a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Directed, instructed, commanded, e.g. केनापि देवेन हृदि स्थितेन यथा नियुक्तोऽस्मि तथा करोमि; 2. authorized, appointed. Also See नियोग (7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्ता
नियुक्त <i>(I) a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Directed, instructed, commanded, e.g. केनापि देवेन हृदि स्थितेन यथा नियुक्तोऽस्मि तथा करोमि; 2. authorized, appointed. Also See नियोग (7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्ति|नियुक्तिः
नियुक्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Injunction, order; 2. appointment, commission, office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत|नियुतं
नियुत <i>n.</i> 1. A million; 2. a hundred thousand; 3. ten thousand krores.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुद्ध|नियुद्धं
नियुद्ध <i>n.</i> Fighting on foot, close fight, personal struggle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग|नियोगः
नियोग <i>m.</i> 1. Employment, use; 2. command, commission, charge, appointed task, मनो नियोगक्रिययोत्सुकं R.v.11, M.i.41; 3. any function committed to one’s charge, daily occupation, स्वमपि स्वं नियोगमशून्यं कुरु ‘you, too, may go about your work’ Sak.ii.; (this sentence often occurs in plays being a polite way of asking servants to retire); 4. effort, exertion; 5. certainty, ascertainment; 6. necessity, inevitableness, तत्सिषेवे नियोगेन स विकल्पपराङ्मुखः R.xvii.49; 7. the practice in ancient times by which a childless widow was permitted to have intercourse with the brother or any other near relative of her deceased husband to raise up issue to him, उक्तो नियोगो मनुना निषिद्धः स्वयमेव हि Bṛhaspati.. Also See M.ix.59-68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगिन्
नियोगिन् <i>m.</i> An officer, a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग्य|नियोग्यः
नियोग्य <i>m.</i> A lord, a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजन|नियोजनं
नियोजन <i>n.</i> 1. Fastening; 2. ordering, prescribing; 3. urging impelling; 4. appointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोज्य|नियोज्यः
नियोज्य <i>m.</i> One charged with a commission, a functionary, an officer, an employe, सिध्यंति कर्मसु महत्स्वपि यन्नियोज्याः Sak.vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोद्धृ
नियोद्धृ <i>m.</i> 1. A combatant, a wrestler; 2. a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्
निर् <i>ind.</i> A substitute for निस् (q.v.) before vowels and soft consonants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंश
निर्-अंश <i>a.</i> 1. whole, entire; 2. not entitled to any share of the patrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरक्ष|निरक्षः
निर्-अक्ष <i>m.</i> the place of no latitude (in astronomy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरग्नि
निर्-अग्नि <i>a.</i> having lost or neglected the consecrated fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंकुश|निरङ्कुश|निरङ्कुशः
निर्-अंकुश <i>a.</i> uncontrolled, unruly, unchecked, independent, कुवलयदृश वामः कामो निकामनिरंकुशः Git.G.vii. or निरंकुशाः कवयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंग|निरङ्ग
निर्-अंग <i>a.</i> 1. having no parts; 2. deprived of expedients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरजिन
निर्-अजिन <i>a.</i> skinless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंजन|निरञ्जन|निरञ्जनः
निर्-अंजन <i>(I) a.</i> 1. without collyrium; 2. free from falsehood; 3. simple, artless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंजन|निरञ्जन|निरञ्जनः
निर्-अंजन <i>(II) m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरतिशय|निरतिशयः
निर्-अतिशय <i>a.</i> unsurpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत्यय
निर्-अत्यय <i>a.</i> 1. free from danger, secure, R.xvii.53; 2. free from fault, disinterested, Kir.i.12; 3. completely successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरध्व
निर्-अध्व <i>a.</i> one who has lost his way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुक्रोश|निरनुक्रोशः
निर्-अनुक्रोश <i>(I) a.</i> pitiless, hard-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुक्रोश|निरनुक्रोशः
निर्-अनुक्रोश <i>(II) m.</i> hard-heartedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुग
निर्-अनुग <i>a.</i> without followers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुनासिक
निर्-अनुनासिक <i>a.</i> not nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुरोध
निर्-अनुरोध <i>a.</i> 1. unfavourable, unfriendly; 2. unkind, unamiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंतर|निरन्तर|निरन्तरं
निर्-अंतर <i>a.</i> 1. constant, perpetual, निरंतरास्वंतरवातवृष्टिषु K.S.v.25; 2. having no intervening space, having no interval, close, हृदयं निरंतरबृहत्कठिनस्तनमंडलावरणमप्यभिदन् Sis.ix.66; 3. compact, dense; 4. faithful, true (as a friend); 5. not hidden from view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंतरम्|निरन्तरम्
निर्-अंतरम् <i>ind.</i> 1. without interruption, constantly, continually; 2. closely, tightly, firmly, परिष्वंजते शयने निरंतरम् Rt.ii.11; 3. immediately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंतराभ्यास|निरन्तराभ्यास|निरन्तराभ्यासः
निर्-अंतरम्˚अभ्यास <i>m.</i> constant study, diligent exrcise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंतराल|निरन्तराल
निर्-अंतराल <i>a.</i> without an intervening space, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्वय
निर्-अन्वय <i>a.</i> 1. having no issue, childless; 2. unconnected, unrelated; 3. not agreeing with the context (as a word); 4. without being seen, out of sight, M.viii.332; 5. without retinue, unattended, का स्वमेकाकिनी भीरु निरन्वयजने वने Bt.v.66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपत्रप|निरपत्रपः
निर्-अपत्रप <i>a.</i> 1. shameless, impudent; 2. bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपराध|निरपराधः
निर्-अपराध <i>a.</i> innocent, faultless, blameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपाय
निर्-अपाय <i>a.</i> 1. free from decay, imperishable; 2. infallible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्ष|निरपेक्षः
निर्-अपेक्ष <i>a.</i> 1. having no necessity of, not depending on, (with a loc.), न्यायनिर्णीतसारत्वान्निरपेक्षमिवागमे Kir.xi.39; 2. without desire, indifferent, especially indifferent to worldly pursuits, M.vi.41; 3. not expecting anything from another; 4. without purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिभव
निर्-अभिभव <i>a.</i> not subject to humiliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिमान
निर्-अभिमान <i>a.</i> free from self-conceit, devoid of egotism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभिलाष
निर्-अभिलाष <i>a.</i> not intent upon, indifferent to, स्वसुखनिरभिलाषः ख्हिद्यसे लोकहेतोः Sak.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरभ्र
निर्-अभ्र <i>a.</i> cloudless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरंबु|निरम्बु
निर्-अंबु <i>a.</i> 1. abstaining from water; 2. destitute of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्गल|निरर्गलः
निर्-अर्गल <i>a.</i> unbarred, unobstructed, unimpeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थ|निरर्थः
निर्-अर्थ <i>a.</i> 1. poor, indigent; 2. meaningless (as a word or sentence); 3. nonsensical, vain, purposeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थक|निरर्थकं
निर्-अर्थक <i>(I) a.</i> 1. useless, vain, unprofitable; 2. unmeaning, nonsensical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थक|निरर्थकं
निर्-अर्थक <i>(II) n.</i> an expletive, निरर्थकं तुहीत्यादि पूरणैकप्रयोजनम् Chandrāloka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवकाश
निर्-अवकाश <i>a.</i> 1. without space; 2. without desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवग्रह|निरवग्रहः
निर्-अवग्रह <i>a.</i> 1. unrestrained, unchecked, uncontrolled; 2. free, independent; 3. head-strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवद्य
निर्-अवद्य <i>a.</i> blameless, faultless, unexceptionable, निरवद्यानि पद्यानि यदि नाट्यस्य का क्षतिः Bhavabhūti, as quoted in Sr.P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवधि
निर्-अवधि <i>a.</i> unlimited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवयव
निर्-अवयव <i>a.</i> 1. without parts; 2. without limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवलंब|निरवलम्ब
निर्-अवलंब <i>a.</i> unsupported, without support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवशेष
निर्-अवशेष <i>a.</i> whole, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवशेषेण
निर्-अवशेषेण <i>ind.</i> completely, fully, totally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरशन|निरशनं
निर्-अशन <i>(I) a.</i> abstaining from food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरशन|निरशनं
निर्-अशन <i>(II) n.</i> fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्त्र
निर्-अस्त्र <i>a.</i> weaponless, unarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्थि
निर्-अस्थि <i>a.</i> boneless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहंकार|निरहङ्कार
निर्-अहंकार, -अहंकृति <i>a.</i> free from egotism, humble, lowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहंकृति|निरहङ्कृति
निर्-अहंकार, -अहंकृति <i>a.</i> free from egotism, humble, lowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहम्
निर्-अहम् <i>a.</i> free from self-conceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकांक्ष|निराकाङ्क्ष
निर्-आकांक्ष <i>a.</i> 1. free from desire; 2. wanting nothing to make complete (as the sense of a sentence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकार|निराकारः
निर्-आकार <i>(I) a.</i> 1. formless, without form; 2. deformed; 3. disguised; 4. modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकार|निराकारः
निर्-आकार <i>(II) m.</i> 1. the universal spirit; 2. an epithet of Śiva; 3. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृति|निराकृतिः
निर्-आकृति <i>m.</i> a Brāhmaṇa who has not pursued his studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रोश
निर्-आक्रोश <i>a.</i> unaccused, unreviled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=382-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरागस्
