निर्विष्ट <i>a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Enjoyed; 2. enjoyed out, R.xii.1; 3. obtained as wages, निर्विष्टं वैश्यशूद्रयिःGautama; 4. married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष्टा
निर्विष्ट <i>a. (f. ष्टा)</i> 1. Enjoyed; 2. enjoyed out, R.xii.1; 3. obtained as wages, निर्विष्टं वैश्यशूद्रयिःGautama; 4. married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत
निर्वृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Satisfied, happy; 2. at ease, secure; 3. ended, ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृता
निर्वृत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Satisfied, happy; 2. at ease, secure; 3. ended, ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृति|निर्वृतिः
निर्वृति <i>f.</i> 1. Satisfaction, happiness, Sis.iv.64, R.ix.38; 2. tranquility, rest, repose; 3. final emancipation from worldly existence, द्वारं निर्वृतिसद्मनो विजयते कृष्णेति वर्णद्वयम् Bh.V.iv.14; 4. completion, accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्त|निर्वृत्तः
निर्वृत्त <i>a. (f. त्ता)</i> Accomplished, attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्ता
निर्वृत्त <i>a. (f. त्ता)</i> Accomplished, attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्ति|निर्वृत्तिः
निर्वृत्ति <i>f.</i> Accomplishment, M.xii.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेद|निर्वेदः|निर्व्वेदः
निर्वेद <i>m.</i> 1. Disgust, loathing; 2. despondency, परिभवान्निर्वेदमापद्यते Mrich.i.; 3. humiliation, grief; 4. disregard of worldly objects, Bg.ii.52; 5. indifference to worldly objects, considered as the feeling which gives rise to the sentiment of quietude (शांत) (in rhetoric), (निर्वेदस्थायिभावोऽस्ति शाम्तोऽपि नवमो रसः K.Pr.iv.); 6. self-humiliation, considered as one of the 33 subordinate feelings (in rhetoric).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेश|निर्वेशः|निर्व्वेशः
निर्वेश <i>m.</i> 1. Gaining, obtaining; 2. wages, hire; 3. enjoyment; 4. expiation, atonement; 5. marriage; 6. fainting, swooning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथन|निर्व्यथनं
निर्व्यथन <i>n.</i> 1. Extreme pain; 2. a hole, chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढ|निर्व्यूढं
निर्व्यूढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Finished, completed; 2. grown, developed, निर्व्यूढसौहृदभरे M.M.iv.; 3. proved true, vindicated, निर्व्यूढस्तेपत्यस्नेहः Ut.iii., M.M.iv.; 4. abandoned, deserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढा
निर्व्यूढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Finished, completed; 2. grown, developed, निर्व्यूढसौहृदभरे M.M.iv.; 3. proved true, vindicated, निर्व्यूढस्तेपत्यस्नेहः Ut.iii., M.M.iv.; 4. abandoned, deserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढि|निर्व्यूढिः
निर्व्यूढि <i>f.</i> 1. End, completion; 2. the top, the highest point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूह|निर्व्यूहः
निर्व्यूह <i>m.</i> 1. A turret; 2. a crest; 3. a door; 4. a peg projecting from a wall; 5. decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हरण|निर्हरणं
निर्हरण <i>n.</i> 1. Carrying out dead bodies to be burnt; 2. drawing out, extracting, rooting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हाद|निर्हादः
निर्हाद <i>m.</i> Voiding excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हार|निर्हारः
निर्हार <i>m.</i> 1. Extracting, rooting up; 2. taking away, removal; 3. carrying out a corpse to be burnt; 4. accumulation of a private store of wealth, M.ix.199; 5. evacuation of any of the natural excrements of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारिन्
निर्हारिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Fragrant, sweet-scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारिणी
निर्हारिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Fragrant, sweet-scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृति|निर्हृतिः
निर्हृति <i>f.</i> Taking out of one’s way, removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्राद|निर्ह्रादः
निर्ह्राद <i>m.</i> A sound in general, R.i.41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलय|निलयः
निलय <i>m.</i> 1. A hiding place, a den of animals, a nest; 2. abode, residence, house; 3. disappearance, setting, दिनांते निलयाय गंतुम् R.ii.15 (where the word is used in the last two senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयन|निलयनं
निलयन <i>n.</i> 1. Settling in a place, alighting; 2. a place of refuge, a dwelling, a habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिंप|निलिम्प|निलिंपः|निलिम्पः
निलिंप <i>m.</i> A god, निलिंपैर्निर्मुक्तानपि च निरयांतर्निपतितान् G.L.15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=389-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिंपनिर्झरी|निलिम्पनिर्झरी
