परमेष्ठिन्
परमेष्ठिन् <i>m.</i> 1. an epithet of Brahman (m.); 2. of Śiva; 3. of Viṣṇu; 4. of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमहंस|परमहंसः
परम-हंस <i>m.</i> an ascetic who has subdued all his senses by abstract meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमम्
परमम् <i>ind.</i> A particle expressing- (1) permission; (2) assent or acceptance, ततः परममित्युक्त्वा प्रतस्थे मुनिमंडलम् K.S.vi.35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश|परशं|परशः
परश <i>m.</i> A stone, the touch of which turns iron into gold, the philosopher’s stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशव्य|परशव्यं
परशव्य <i>a. (f. व्या)</i> Fit for a hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशव्या
परशव्य <i>a. (f. व्या)</i> Fit for a hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशु|परशुः
परशु <i>m.</i> 1. A hatchet, a battle-axe, तर्जितः परशुधारया मम R.xi.78; 2. a weapon in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुधर|परशुधरः
परशु-धर <i>m.</i> 1. an epithet of Paraśurāma; 2. of Gaṇeśa; 3. a soldier armed with an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वध|परश्वधः
परश्व(स्व)ध <i>m.</i> A battle-axe, a hatchet, धारां शितां रामपरश्वधस्य संभावयत्युत्पलपत्रसाराम् R.vi.42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वध|परस्वधः
परश्व(स्व)ध <i>m.</i> A battle-axe, a hatchet, धारां शितां रामपरश्वधस्य संभावयत्युत्पलपत्रसाराम् R.vi.42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्
परस् <i>ind.</i> Beyond, further, more than, on the other side of, with the exception of &c. (not used by itself in classical Sanskrit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःकृष्ण
परःकृष्ण <i>a.</i> extremely dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्तात्
परस्-तात् <i>ind.</i> on the other side of, beyond, (with an abl. or gen., e.g. ग्रामात् or ग्रामस्य परस्तात्), आदित्यवर्णं तमसः परस्तात् Bg.viii.9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःपुरुष
परःपुरुष <i>a.</i> higher than a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःशत|परःशतं
परःशत <i>a.</i> more than a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःश्वस्
परःश्वस् <i>ind.</i> the day after tomorrow. Cf. परश्वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःसहस्र|परःसहस्रं
परःसहस्र <i>a.</i> more than a thousand, तप्त्वा परःसहस्रा शरदस्तपांसि Ut.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=413-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परा
परा <i>ind.</i> A prefix to verbs implying- (1) overcoming; (2) liberation; (3) inverted order; (4) pride; (5) encounter; (6) excess; (7) going; (8) killing, injuring &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकरण|पराकरणं
पराकरण <i>n.</i> The act of rejecting or disregarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रम|पराक्रमः
पराक्रम <i>m.</i> 1. Heroism, prowess, valour, M.i.51; 2. attempt, endeavour, enterprise; 3. a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराग|परागः
पराग <i>m.</i> 1. Dust in general; 2. the pollen of a flower, Am.S.54; 3. fragrant powder used after bathing; 4. an eclipse of the sun or moon; 5. sandal; 6. independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परांगव|पराङ्गव|परांगवः|पराङ्गवः
परांगव <i>m.</i> The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराच्
पराच् <i>a. (f. ची)</i> 1. Situated beyond or on the other side; 2. distant; 3. directed outwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराची
पराच् <i>a. (f. ची)</i> 1. Situated beyond or on the other side; 2. distant; 3. directed outwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुख|पराङ्मुखः
पराङ्मुख <i>a.</i> 1. having the face turned away, turning the back upon, विग्रहाच्च शयने पराह्मुखीर्नानुनेतुमबलाः स तत्वरे R.xix.38, Am.S.90; 2. averse from, मातुर्न केवलं स्वस्याः श्रियोऽप्यासीत् पराङ्मुखः R.xii.1; 3. unfavourable, तनुरपि न ते दोषोऽस्माकं विधिस्तु पराङ्मुखः Am.S.27; 4. not caring about, regardless of, मर्त्येऽवास्थापराङ्मुखः R.x.43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीन|पराचीनः
पराचीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Turned in an opposite direction; 2. not minding, not caring about; 3. happening subsequently; 4. situated on the other side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीना
पराचीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Turned in an opposite direction; 2. not minding, not caring about; 3. happening subsequently; 4. situated on the other side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजय|पराजयः
पराजय <i>m.</i> 1. Overpowering, subjugating, defeating, defeat, R.xi.19; 2. the being overcome by, (with an abl., e.g. अध्ययनात्पराजयः); 3. loss, failure (as in a lawsuit), अन्यथावादिनो (साक्षिणः) यस्य ध्रुवस्तस्य पराजयः Yaj.ii.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=414-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

