परिकर|परिकरः
परिकर <i>m.</i> 1. Retinue, train, followers; 2. a multitude, a crowd; 3. beginning, commencement; 4. a sofa; 5. a girth, cloth worn round the loins; (परिकरं बंध् or परिकरं कृ ‘to gird up the loins, i.e. to be ready, to be prepared,’ e.g. बधान द्रागेव द्रढिमरमणीयंपरिकरम् G.L.47, कृतपरिकरस्य भवादृशस्य त्रैलोक्यमपि न क्षमं परिपंथीभवितुम् Ve.iii., Am.S.92); 6. name of a figure of speech consisting in the employment of suggestive epithets (in rhetoric), (विशेषणैर्यत्साकूतैरुक्तिः परिकरस्तु सः K.Pr.x.); 7. covert intimation of coming events in the plot of a drama (in dramaturgy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

