परिखात|परिखातं
परिखात <i>n.</i> 1. A moat, a ditch; 2. digging round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखेद|परिखेदः
परिखेद <i>m.</i> Fatigue, exhaustion, lassitude, K.S.i.60, Rt.i.27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्याति|परिख्यातिः
परिख्याति <i>f.</i> Fame, reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणन|परिगणनं
परिगणन <i>n.</i> Complete enumeration, accurate calculation, श्रेणीभूताः परिगणनया निर्दिशंतो बलाकाः Megh.i. (considered to be spurious by Mall.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणना
परिगणना <i>f.</i> Complete enumeration, accurate calculation, श्रेणीभूताः परिगणनया निर्दिशंतो बलाकाः Megh.i. (considered to be spurious by Mall.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगत|परिगतः
परिगत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Surrounded, encircled; 2. diffused, spread; 3. known, understood; 4. remembered; 5. filled, possessed of, (pp. of गम् with परि q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगता
परिगत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Surrounded, encircled; 2. diffused, spread; 3. known, understood; 4. remembered; 5. filled, possessed of, (pp. of गम् with परि q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगलित
परिगलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Sunk; 2. dropped down, vanished; 3. melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगलिता
परिगलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Sunk; 2. dropped down, vanished; 3. melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-32" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगर्हण|परिगर्हणं
परिगर्हण <i>n.</i> Excessive blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-33" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगूढ
परिगूढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Quite secret, very mysterious; 2. very difficult to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगूढा
परिगूढ <i>a. (f. ढा)</i> 1. Quite secret, very mysterious; 2. very difficult to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-34" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीत
परिगृहीत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Grasped, clutched; 2. embraced, surrounded; 3. accepted, consented to; 4. favoured; 5. obeyed; 6. opposed, (pp. of ग्रह् with परि q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीता
परिगृहीत <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Grasped, clutched; 2. embraced, surrounded; 3. accepted, consented to; 4. favoured; 5. obeyed; 6. opposed, (pp. of ग्रह् with परि q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृह्या
परिगृह्या <i>f.</i> A married woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रह|परिग्रहः
परिग्रह <i>m.</i> 1. Taking, seizing, grasping, R.ix.46; 2. surrounding, encircling; 3. putting on (as a dress); 4. assuming, Am.S.92; 5. accepting, receiving, R.xviii.38, xiii.70, K.S.vi.53; 6. possession, property, belongings, त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः Bg.iv.21; 7. marriage; 8. a wife, प्रयतपरिग्रहद्वितीयः R.i.95, 92, xi.31, ix.14; 9. retinue, train, suite; 10. the seraglio of a prince, Sak.iii.; 11. an eclipse of the sun or the moon; 12. an oath; 13. root, origin; 14. the rear of an army; 15. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=415-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्लान
परिग्लान <i>a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Languid, exhausted; 2. averse from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्लाना
परिग्लान <i>a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Languid, exhausted; 2. averse from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघ|परिघः
परिघ <i>m.</i> 1. An iron or wooden bar used for locking a gate, धरित्रीमेकः कृत्स्नां नगरपरिघप्रांशुबाहुर्भुनक्ति Sak.ii.; 2. a bar, an obstacle, a hindrance, भार्गवस्य सुकृतोऽपि सोऽभवत्स्वर्गमार्गपरिघो दुरत्ययः R.xi.88; 3. a stick mounted with iron, R.xii.73; 4. an iron club; 5. a pitcher, a water-jar; 6. a glass-pitcher; 7. a house; 8. killing, striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघट्टन|परिघट्टनं
परिघट्टन <i>n.</i> Stirring up, stirring round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघात|परिघातः
परिघात <i>m.</i> 1. Killing, striking; 2. a club, an iron bludgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघातन|परिघातनं|परिघातनः
परिघातन <i>n.</i> 1. Killing, striking; 2. a club, an iron bludgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघोष|परिघोषः
परिघोष <i>m.</i> 1. Noise; 2. improper speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचतुर्दशन्
परिचतुर्दशन् <i>a. pl.</i> Fully fourteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचय|परिचयः
परिचय <i>m.</i> 1. Heaping up, accumulation; 2. familiarity, intimacy; 3. acquaintance, Sant.S.ii.7; 4. study, practice, हेतुः परिचयस्थैर्ये वक्तुर्गुणनिकैव सा Sis.ii.75, R.ix.49; 5. recognition, Megh.i.9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर|परिचरः
परिचर <i>m.</i> 1. A servant, an attendant; 2. a body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरण|परिचरणः
परिचरण <i>(I) m.</i> A servant, an assistant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरण|परिचरणः
परिचरण <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Serving, waiting upon; 2. going about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्या|परिचर्य्या
परिचर्या <i>f.</i> 1. Service, attendance, R.i.91, Bg.xviii.44; 2. adoration, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचाय्य|परिचाय्यः
परिचाय्य <i>m.</i> Sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचार|परिचारः
परिचार <i>m.</i> 1. Service, attendance; 2. servant; 3. place for walking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारक|परिचारकः
परिचारक <i>m.</i> A servant, an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारिक|परिचारिकः
परिचारक <i>m.</i> A servant, an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचित|परिचितः
परिचित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Heaped, accumulated; 2. familiar with, intimate with; 3. learnt, practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचिता
परिचित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Heaped, accumulated; 2. familiar with, intimate with; 3. learnt, practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचिति|परिचितिः
परिचिति <i>f.</i> Acquaintance, familiarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद्
परिच्छद् <i>f.</i> 1. Retinue, train; 2. paraphernalia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद|परिच्छदः|परिछद
परिच्छद <i>m.</i> 1. A covering, a cover; 2. dress; 3. train, retinue, R.ix.70; 4. paraphernalia, R.i.19; 5. furniture, chattels, (उपपादयेत्) गृहं वा सपरिच्छदम् M.xi.76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छंद|परिच्छन्द|परिच्छंदः|परिच्छन्दः
परिच्छंद <i>m.</i> Train, retinue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्न|परिच्छन्नः|परिछन्न
परिच्छन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> 1. Enveloped, covered; 2. overlaid; 3. surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्ना
परिच्छन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> 1. Enveloped, covered; 2. overlaid; 3. surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छित्ति|परिच्छित्तिः|परिछित्ति
परिच्छित्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Accurate definition; 2. partition, separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छिन्न|परिच्छिन्नः|परिछिन्न
परिच्छिन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> 1. Cut off, divided; 2. limited, confined, (pp. of छिद् with परि q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छिन्ना
परिच्छिन्न <i>a. (f. न्ना)</i> 1. Cut off, divided; 2. limited, confined, (pp. of छिद् with परि q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेद|परिच्छेदः|परिछेद
परिच्छेद <i>m.</i> 1. Cutting, separating; 2. accurate distinction or definition; 3. exact determination, परिच्छेदव्यक्तिर्भवति न पुरस्थेऽपि विषये M.M.i., इत्यारूढ बहुप्रतर्कमापरिच्छेदाकुलं मे मनः Sak.v.; 4. limit, boundary, परिच्छेदातीतः सकलवचनानामविषयः M.M.i.; 5. a chapter of a book. (For other names for sections or chapters of books, See under अध्याय.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेद्य
परिच्छेद्य <i>a. (f. द्या)</i> 1. Definable, R.x.28; 2. to be estimated, to be weighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेद्या
परिच्छेद्य <i>a. (f. द्या)</i> 1. Definable, R.x.28; 2. to be estimated, to be weighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजन|परिजनः
परिजन <i>m.</i> 1. Attendants, servants (collectively), e.g. परिजने दीर्घां कथां कुर्वति Am.S.75; 2. a single servant; 3. family, dependents; 4. retinue, suite (especially the maids of a lady), R.xix.23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजल्पित|परिजल्पितं
परिजल्पित <i>n.</i> A servant’s indication of his superiority by finding fault with his master, (प्रभोर्निर्दयताव्यचापलाद्युपपादनात् । स्वविचक्षणताव्यक्तिर्भंग्या स्यात् परिजल्पितम् Ujjvaladatta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञप्ति|परिज्ञप्तिः
परिज्ञप्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Conversation, discourse; 2. recognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञान|परिज्ञानं
परिज्ञान <i>n.</i> Thorough knowledge, complete acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिडीन|परिडीनं
परिडीन <i>n.</i> The flight of a bird in circles. See डीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणत|परिणतं|परिणतः
परिणत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Ripe, ripened, matured, Megh.i.23, कवेः परिणतप्रज्ञस्य वाणीं Ut.i.; 2. bent down, old; 3. changed or transformed into; 4. digested; 5. full grown, perfected, advanced, e.g. परिणतशरच्चंद्रिकासु क्षपासु Megh.ii.47; 6. ended, come to a close, e.g. परिणतो दिवसः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणता
परिणत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Ripe, ripened, matured, Megh.i.23, कवेः परिणतप्रज्ञस्य वाणीं Ut.i.; 2. bent down, old; 3. changed or transformed into; 4. digested; 5. full grown, perfected, advanced, e.g. परिणतशरच्चंद्रिकासु क्षपासु Megh.ii.47; 6. ended, come to a close, e.g. परिणतो दिवसः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणत|परिणतं|परिणतः
परिणत <i>(II) m.</i> An elephant that gives a side-blow with the tusks, (तिर्यग्दंतप्रहारश्च गजः परिणतो मतः Halāyudha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-29" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणति|परिणतिः
परिणति <i>f.</i> 1. Bending down, bowing; 2. ripeness, maturity; 3. transformation, transmutation; 4. fulfilment; 5. result, issue, संसारे स्मिन्नसारे परिणतितरले Bhartr.i.20; 6. end, conclusion; 7. old age, अभवद्गतः परिणतिं शिथिलः परिमंदसूर्यनयनो दिचसः Sis.ix.3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणय|परिणयः
परिणय <i>m.</i> Marriage, e.g. नवपरिणया वधूः R.G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=416-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणयन|परिणयनं
