पर्वन्|पर्व्वन्
पर्वन् <i>n. (at the end of compounds पर्वन् is sometimes changed into पर्व, e.g. कर्कशांगुलिपर्वया R.xii.41)</i> 1. A knot, a joint; 2. a limb, a member; 3. a portion, a division; 4. a chapter, a book, (e.g. of the Mahābhārata); 5. a festival, an occasion of joy; 6. an opportunity, an occasion; 7. the days of the four changes of the moon, viz., the eighth and fourteenth day of each half month and the days of the new and full moon; 8. a sacrifice performed on the occasion of a change of the moon; 9. the day of new or full moon, R.vii.33, M.iv.150; 10. eclipse of the sun or moon; 11. step of a staircase, R.xvi.46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=424-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

