पश्चिमरात्र|पश्चिमरात्रः
पश्चिम-रात्र <i>m.</i> the latter part of the night, e.g. उपारताः पश्चिमरात्रगोचरात् Kir.iv.10. (The reading of Mall. however, is पश्चिमरात्रि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=426-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिमा
पश्चिमा <i>f.</i> The west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=426-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिमोत्तरा
पश्चिमा-उत्तरा <i>f.</i> the north-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=426-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यत्
पश्यत् <i>a. (f. न्ती)</i> Seeing, beholding, looking, observing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=426-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यन्ती
पश्यत् <i>a. (f. न्ती)</i> Seeing, beholding, looking, observing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=426-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यतोहर|पश्यतोहरः
