पाटल <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The pale-red colour, e.g. कपोलपाटलादेशि बभूव रघुचेष्टितम् R.iv.68; 2. the trumpet-flower, पाटलसंसर्गिसुरभिवनावाताः Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल <i>(III) n.</i> 1. The blossom of this tree, R.xvi.52, xix.46; 2. rice; 3. saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलोपल|पाटलोपलः
पाटल-उपल <i>m.</i> a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलद्रुम|पाटलद्रुमः
पाटल-द्रुम <i>m.</i> name of a tree. See पाटल II.2 above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटला
पाटला <i>f.</i> 1. The red lodhra; 2. the trumpet-flower (either the tree or its blossom); 3. an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलि|पाटलिः
पाटलि <i>f.</i> The trumpet-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिपुत्र
पाटलि-पुत्र <i>n.</i> name of an ancient city, the capital of Magadha, situated near the confluence of the Śoṇā and the Ganges, identified with the modern Pāṭnā. It is also known by the name of Pushpapura in Sanskrit literature. See R.vi.24, Mud.ii.111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिक|पाटलिकः
पाटलिक <i>m.</i> A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल्या
पाटल्या <i>f.</i> A multitude of pātāla flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटव|पाटवं
पाटव <i>m.</i> 1. Sharpness, acuteness; 2. cleverness, eloquence, पाटवं संस्कृतोक्तिषु Hit.i.; 3. quickness, rashness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटविक|पाटविकः
पाटविक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. Clever, skilful; 2. cunning, fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटविकी
पाटविक <i>a. (f. की)</i> 1. Clever, skilful; 2. cunning, fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटित|पाटितं
पाटित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Torn, split, broken; 2. pierced, R.xi.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटिता
पाटित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Torn, split, broken; 2. pierced, R.xi.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटी
पाटी <i>f.</i> Arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीगणित
पाटी-गणित <i>n.</i> arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीर|पाटीरः
पाटीर <i>m.</i> 1. Sandal, पाटीर तव पटीयान् कः परिपाटीमिमामुरीकर्तुम् Bh.V.i.12; 2. a field; 3. tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ|पाठः
पाठ <i>m.</i> 1. Reciting, recitation, e.g. पाठदोषाश्चतुर्दश; 2. reading, perusal, study; 3. one of the five daily yajnyas, viz., that of reciting the Vedas (ब्रह्मयज्ञ); 4. the text of a book, a reading, a variant, e.g. कपिशकायां तु पंजराजाति क्वाचित्कः पाठः । अपपाठः स इति हरदत्तः. See अपपाठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठांतर|पाठान्तर
पाठ-अंतर <i>n.</i> another reading, a variant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठच्छेद|पाठच्छेदः
पाठ-च्छेद <i>m.</i> a pause, cæsura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठदोष|पाठदोषः
पाठ-दोष <i>m.</i> a false reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठनिश्चय|पाठनिश्चयः
पाठ-निश्चय <i>m.</i> settling the text (of a passage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशाला
पाठ-शाला <i>f.</i> a school, a college.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठक|पाठकः
पाठक <i>m.</i> 1. A teacher, a preceptor; 2. a public reader of religious or mythological books; 3. a scholar, a student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठकमंजरी
पाठक-मंजरी, -शालिनी <i>f.</i> the Śārikā bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठकशालिनी
पाठक-मंजरी, -शालिनी <i>f.</i> the Śārikā bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठन|पाठनं
पाठन <i>n.</i> Teaching, lecturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठित
पाठित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Taught, instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिता
पाठित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Taught, instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठीन|पाठीनः
पाठीन <i>m.</i> 1. A public reader of mythological books; 2. a kind of fish, विवृतपाठीनपराहतं पयः Kir.iv.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण|पाणः
पाण <i>m.</i> 1. Trade, traffic; 2. a trader; 3. an agreement, a contract; 4. praise; 5. the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणि|पाणिः
पाणि <i>(I) m.</i> The hand, R.iii.68, xi.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणि|पाणिः
पाणि <i>(II) f.</i> A market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणौकरण|पाणौकरणं
पाणौकरण <i>n.</i> marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिगृहीती
पाणि-गृहीती <i>f.</i> a wife married according to the ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रह|पाणिग्रहः
पाणि-ग्रह <i>m.</i> marrying, marriage, R.vii.29, viii.7, K.S.vii.4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहण|पाणिग्रहणं
पाणि-ग्रहण <i>n.</i> marrying, marriage, R.vii.29, viii.7, K.S.vii.4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहीतृ
पाणि-ग्रहीतृ, -ग्राह <i>m.</i> a bridegroom, a husband, बाल्ये पितुर्वशे तिष्ठेत् पाणिग्राहस्य यौवने M.v.148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्राह|पाणिग्राहः
पाणि-ग्रहीतृ, -ग्राह <i>m.</i> a bridegroom, a husband, बाल्ये पितुर्वशे तिष्ठेत् पाणिग्राहस्य यौवने M.v.148.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघ|पाणिघः
पाणि-घ <i>m.</i> 1. a drummer; 2. a workman, a handicraftsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघात|पाणिघातः
पाणि-घात <i>m.</i> A blow with the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिज|पाणिजः
पाणि-ज <i>m.</i> a finger-nail, पाणिजैराविद्धः Git.G.xii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणितल|पाणितलं
पाणि-तल <i>n.</i> the palm of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=428-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

