पुरुष|पुरुषः
पुरुष <i>(I) m.</i> 1. Mankind; 2. a male, a man, M.vii.17, ix.2; 3. representative of a generation; 4. an official, a functionary; 5. the height of a man considered as a measure of length; 6. the soul; 7. the supreme being; 8. the pupil of the eye; 9. a person (in gram.); 10. the twenty-fifth principle of creation of the Sāṅkhyas, i.e. the soul which, according to them, is neither a production nor productive. See /Sāṅkhya K./3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=445-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

