प्रत्यनीक|प्रत्यनीकः
प्रति-अनीक <i>(II) m.</i> an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=461-43" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यनीक|प्रत्यनीकः
प्रति-अनीक <i>(III) n.</i> 1. a hostile army, ऋतेऽपि त्वां न भविष्यंति सर्वे येऽवस्थिताः प्रत्यनीकेषु योधाः Bg.xi.32; 2. hostility, enmity; 3. a figure of speech in which someone is represented as injuring a person or thing connected with an enemy who cannot be injured himself (प्रतिपक्षमशक्तेन प्रतिकर्तुं तिरस्क्रिया । या तदीयस्य तत्स्तुत्यै प्रत्यनीकं तदुच्यते K.Pr.x.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=461-43" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

