प्रत्यक्ष|प्रत्यक्षं
प्रत्यक्ष <i>(I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Present, in sight, perceptible, visible, प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः Sak.i.; 2. distinct, evident, clear, Bg.ix.2; 3. direct, immediate; 4. corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=469-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षा
प्रत्यक्ष <i>(I) a. (f. क्षा)</i> 1. Present, in sight, perceptible, visible, प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः Sak.i.; 2. distinct, evident, clear, Bg.ix.2; 3. direct, immediate; 4. corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=469-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्ष|प्रत्यक्षं
प्रत्यक्ष <i>(II) n.</i> Ocular evidence, apprehension by the senses, perception (considered as a mode of proof) (in phil.).(प्रत्यक्षम्, प्रत्यक्षेण and प्रत्यक्षात् are used as indeclinables in the sense of- (1) in the presence of, before; (2) publicly; (3) immediately, directly, personally.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=469-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षज्ञान
प्रत्यक्ष-ज्ञान <i>n.</i> knowledge obtained by perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=469-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षदृष्ट
प्रत्यक्ष-दृष्ट <i>a.</i> seen with the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=469-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

