प्रशम|प्रशमः
प्रशम <i>m.</i> 1. Calmness, tranquility, composure, R.viii.15, Kir.ii.32; 2. assuagement, appeasement; 3. abatement, extinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=480-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमन|प्रशमनं
प्रशमन <i>n.</i> 1. Tranquillizing, pacifying; 2. soothing, assuaging, आपन्नार्तिप्रशमनफलाः संपदो ह्युत्तमानाम् Megh.i.53, 3. curing, healing; 4. extinguishing; 5. bestowing fitly, M.vii.56 (where Medhātithi and Kull. give this meaning to the word; Sarvajnyanārāyaṇa renders it differently); 6. securing, guarding, लब्धप्रशमनस्वस्थमथैनं समुपस्थिता R.iv.14; 7. cessation, abatement; 8. killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=480-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमित
प्रशमित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Appeased, composed; 2. quenched, extinguished; 3. expiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=480-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमिता
प्रशमित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Appeased, composed; 2. quenched, extinguished; 3. expiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=480-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्त|प्रशस्तं
प्रशस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Praised, eulogised, extolled; 2. best, excellent; 3. happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=480-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्ता
प्रशस्त <i>a. (f. स्ता)</i> 1. Praised, eulogised, extolled; 2. best, excellent; 3. happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=480-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

