प्रस्थ <i>(I) a. (f. स्था)</i> 1. Going on a journey; 2. spreading, expanding; 3. firm, stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=484-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थ|प्रस्थः
प्रस्थ <i>(II) m.n.</i> 1. A level expanse (as in इंद्रप्रस्थ); 2. the tableland or peak of a mountain, दशमुखभुजोच्छ्वासितप्रस्थसंधेः कैलासस्य Megh.i.58, or प्रस्थं हिमाद्रेर्मृगनाभिगंधि किंचित् क्वणत् किंनरमध्युवास K.S.x.54; 3. a particular measure of capacity equal to thirty-two palas; 4. anything measuring a prastha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=484-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

