प्राण|प्राणः
प्राण <i>m.</i> 1. Breath of life, vitality, principle of life (generally used in the pl.), प्राणैरुपक्रोशमलिमसैर्वा R.ii.53, or प्राणानामनिलेन वृत्तिरुचिता Sak.vii.; 2. the first of the five bodily airs; (they are प्राण, अपान, समान, व्यान and उदान), Bg.iv.29; (it resides in the heart); 3. wind, air; 4. digestion; 5. muscle, strength, power, गिरिचर इव नागः प्राणसारं बिभर्ति Sak.ii.; 6. the soul; 7. the supreme spirit; 8. an organ of sense, M.iv.143; 9. anything as dear as life; 10. the life of poetry, poetical talent, inspiration; 11. frank-incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=487-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

