प्री
प्री <i>(I) vi. 4Ā (pres. प्रीयते)</i> 1. To feel affection; 2. to be gratified, विश्वे देवाश्च प्रीयंताम् Yaj.i.245; 3. to be satisfied, to assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=493-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्री
प्री <i>(II) vt. or vi. 10U (pp. प्रीत; pres. प्रीणाति, प्रीणीते; caus. प्रीणयति-ते)</i> 1. To please, to delight, to gladden, प्रीणाति यः सुचरितैः पितरं स पुत्रः Bhartr.ii.68, Bt.v.104, iii.38; 2. to take delight in, e.g. कच्चिन्मन्सस्ते प्रीणाति वनवासे; 3. to show kindness to, to act kindly towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=493-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

