प्लु
प्लु <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. प्लुत; pres. प्लवते)</i> 1. To float, to swim, बालाः क्लेशोत्तरं रागवशात्प्लवंते R.xvi.60, मज्जंत्यलाबूनि ग्रावाणः प्लवंत इति Mv.i.; 2. to fly, to soar, to hover; 3. to jump, to leap, to spring, Bt.v.48, xiv.13; 4. to be lengthened (as a vowel).With अभि-, to overflow, to overwhelm.With अव-, to jump, to jump out.With आ-, 1. to bathe; 2. to jump up.With उद्-, 1. to float, to swim; 2. to spring, to leap, M.viii.236.With उप-, 1. to float; 2. to assault, to attack; 3. to trouble, to harass, to torment, तस्मिन्नवसरे देवाः पौलस्त्योपप्लुता हरिम् । अभिजग्मुः R.x.5, xiv.64.With परि-, 1. to swim, to float; 2. to bathe; 3. to overwhelm; 4. to jump, to spring; 5. to flood, to inundate; 6. to curer with.With वि-, 1. to float about, to fluctuate; 2. to be scattered; 3. to become confused; 4. to be ruined.With सम्-, 1. to float about, to fluctuate; 2. to meet, e.g. आपः संप्लवंते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लु
प्लु <i>Caus. (प्लावयति-ते)</i> 1. to cause to swim, to cause to float; 2. to remove, to wash away; 3. to cause to stagger.With वि-, 1. to cause to swim; 2. to spread abroad, to divulge; 3. to confound, to confuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुत|प्लुतं|प्लुतः
प्लुत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Floating, swimming; 2. inundated, overflowed; 3. jumped, leaped; 4. protracted, lengthened (as a vowel), (pp. of प्लु q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुता
प्लुत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Floating, swimming; 2. inundated, overflowed; 3. jumped, leaped; 4. protracted, lengthened (as a vowel), (pp. of प्लु q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुत|प्लुतं|प्लुतः
प्लुत <i>(II) n.</i> 1. A jump, a leap; 2. a particular pace of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुतगति|प्लुतगतिः
प्लुत-गति <i>(I) m.</i> a hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुतगति|प्लुतगतिः
प्लुत-गति <i>(II) f.</i> 1. going by leaps; 2. galloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुति|प्लुतिः
प्लुति <i>f.</i> 1. Overflowing; 2. a. leap, a jump, a skip; 3. a particular pace of a horse; 4. protraction (of a vowel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्
प्लुष् <i>(I) vt. 1P, 4P (pres. प्लेषति, प्लुष्यति)</i> To burn, to scorch, Rt.i.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्
प्लुष् <i>(II) vt. or vi. 9P (pres. प्लुष्णाति)</i> 1. To sprinkle; 2. to fill; 3. to be wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=496-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

