फणमणि|फणमणिः
फण-मणि <i>m.</i> a jewel supposed to be found in the hood of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=497-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणमंडल|फणमण्डल
फण-मंडल <i>n.</i> the rounded hood of a serpent, करालफणमंडलम् R.xii.98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=497-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणा
फणा <i>f.</i> The expanded hood of a serpent, तत्फणामंडलोदंचिर्मणिद्योविग्रहम् R.x.7, or पर्यंकीकृतनागनायकफणाश्रेणीमणीनां गणे Git.G.xii. (For compounds, See under फण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=497-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिन्
फणिन् <i>m.</i> 1. The hooded serpent, फणी मयूरस्य तले निषीदति Rt.i.13, R.xvi.17, K.S.iii.21; 2. an epithet of Rāhu; 3. an epithet of Pantanjali, the author of the Mahābhāshya on Pāṇini’s sūtras, फणिभाषितभाष्यफक्किका Na.ii.95, (whether he is identical with the author of the Yogasūtra is not known).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=497-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणींद्र|फणीन्द्र|फणीन्द्रः
फणिन्-इंद्र, -ईश्वर <i>m.</i> 1. an epithet of the serpent-demon Śeṣa; 2. an epithet of Ananta, a serpent-chief; 3. an epithet of Patanjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=497-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणीश्वर|फणीश्वरः
फणिन्-इंद्र, -ईश्वर <i>m.</i> 1. an epithet of the serpent-demon Śeṣa; 2. an epithet of Ananta, a serpent-chief; 3. an epithet of Patanjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=497-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

