बकजित्
बक-जित्, -निषूदन <i>m.</i> 1. a name of Bhīmasena; 2. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकनिषूदन
बक-जित्, -निषूदन <i>m.</i> 1. a name of Bhīmasena; 2. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकव्रत
बक-व्रत <i>n.</i> crane-like observance, i.e. hypocrisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुल|बकुलः
बकुल <i>(I) m.</i> A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुल|बकुलः
बकुल <i>(II) n.</i> Its flower; (there is a convention among poets that this tree blossoms when young ladies throw on it mouthfuls of wine; thus we have, in the Meghadūta, कांक्षत्यन्यो (i.e. केसरः) वदनमदिरां दोहदच्छद्मनाऽस्याः ii.15; the following stanza puts together all these conventions- स्त्रीणां स्पर्शात्प्रियंगुर्विकसति बकुलः सीधुगंडूषसेकात्पादाघातादशोकस्तिलककुरबकौ वीक्षणालिंगनाभ्याम् । मंदारो नर्मवाक्यात् पटुमृदुहसनाच्चंपको वक्त्रवाताच्चूतो गीतान्नमेरुर्विकसति च पुरो नर्तनात्कर्णिकारः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकेरुका
बकेरुका <i>f.</i> A small crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकोट|बकोटः
बकोट <i>m.</i> A crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बटु|बटुः
बटु <i>m.</i> A boy, a youth, (the same as वटु q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडिश|बडिशं
बडि(लि)श <i>n.</i> A fish-hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिश|बलिशं
बडि(लि)श <i>n.</i> A fish-hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बत
बत <i>ind.</i> A particle expressing- (1) sorrow or regret; (2) compassion, e.g. क्व बत हरिणकानां जीवितं चातिलोलम् Sak.i.; (3) calling, addressing, त्यजत मानमलं बत विग्रहैः R.ix.47; (4) joy; (5) wonderment; (6) satisfaction, e.g. अहो बतासि स्पृहणीयवीर्यः K.S.iii.20.(With a preceding अहो, it is used in the sense of joy, surprise, regret or calling. See under अहो.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदर|बदरं|बदरः
बदर <i>(I) m.</i> The jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदर|बदरं|बदरः
बदर <i>(II) n.</i> The fruit of the jujube, करबदरसदृशमखिलं भुवनतलं यत्प्रसादतः कवयः पश्यंति Vas.D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरपाचन
बदर-पाचन <i>n.</i> name of a sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिका
बदरिका <i>f.</i> 1. The jujube tree and its fruit, e.g. अन्ये बदरिकाकारा बहिरेव मनोहराः Hit.i.; 2. name of one of the sources of the Ganges and of the neighbouring hermitage of Nara and Nārāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=499-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिकाश्रम|बदरिकाश्रमः
