बंदी(दि) <i>f.</i> 1. Confinement; 2. a captive, a prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=500-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्|बंध्
बन्ध् <i>vt. 9P (pp. बद्ध; pres. बध्नाति; pass. बध्यते)</i> 1. To bind, to tie, to fix, to fasten, अबद्धादपरिस्कंदं ब्रह्मपाशेन विस्फुरन् Bt.ix.75, R.vii.9, K.S.vii.25; 2. to attract, to arrest, बध्नाति मे चक्षुः … चित्रकूटः R.xiii.47, Kir.vii.17; 3. to ensnare, to catch, to take captive, to imprison, to chastise, चलिर्बबंधे Bt.ii.39, or बध्यंते निपुणैरगाधसलिलान्मत्स्याः समुद्रादपि Hit.i.; 4. to put on, to wear, Bt.xiv.7; 5. to form, to construct, to build, to compose, छायाबद्धकदंबकं मृगकुलम् Sak.ii., R.xi.35, 78, K.S.ii.47, v.30, R.xvi.5, Bt.vii.77, Megh.ii.13, 16, R.iv.38, vi.66; 6. to construct verses, to compose, e.g. श्लोक एव त्वया बद्धो नात्र कार्यां विचारणा Ram.; 7. to fix on or upon, R.iii.4, Bt.xx.22; 8. to form or bear fruit, R.xii.69.(अंजलिं बंध् ‘to place the two hands hollowed side by side.’ चित्तं, धियं or मनः बंध् ‘to set the heart on.’ प्रीतिं, भावं or रागं बंध् ‘to be enamoured of, to fall in love with.’ परिकरं बंध् ‘to gird up one’s loins.’ भ्रूकुटिं बंध् ‘to knit the eyebrows.’ मुष्टिं बंध् ‘to clench the fist.’ सेतुं बंध् ‘to construct a bridge.’ गोलं बंध् ‘to form a globe.’ सख्यं, सौहृदं or अजर्यं बंध् ‘to contract friendship.’ वैरं बंध् ‘to contract enmity.’)With अनु-, 1. to be affixed or attached to; 2. to follow, को नु खल्वयमनुबध्यमानस्तपस्विनीभ्यामबालसत्वो बालः Sak.vii.; 3. to importune, to press.With आ-, 1. to form, to compose, आबद्धरेखामभितो रविमंजरीभिः Git.G.xi., Megh.i.9, Bt.iii.30; 2. to fix on or upon, R.i.40; 3. to bind, to tie, M.xi.205.With उद्-, to tie up, to raise up and tie, K.S.iii.46, R.xvi.67.With नि-, 1. to bind, to tie, to fasten, to chain, K.S.v.10, Bg.iv.41, ix.9, xiv.7; 2. to fix, to rivet; 3. to form, to build, to construct, to compose, e.g., पाषाणचयनिबद्धे कूपे, or निबद्धं पुण्यमाख्यानं रामायणम्; 4. to compose verses.With निस्-, to press, to insist upon, to urge.With परि-, 1. to bind; 2. to put on, to encircle; 3. to stop, to interrupt.With प्रति-, 1. to tie, to bind, पीतप्रतिबद्धवत्साम् R.ii.1; 2. to set, to encase, बहलानुरागकुरुविंददलप्रतिबद्धमध्यमिव दिग्वलयम् Sis.ix.8; 3. to fix, to direct; 4. to obstruct, to keep off, to shut out, to exclude, to cut off, प्रतिबध्नाति हि श्रेयः पूज्यपूजाव्यतिक्रमः R.i.79.With सम्-, 1. to bind together, to tie together, to unite; 2. to attach, to connect; 3. to form, to construct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=500-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंध|बन्ध|बंधः|बन्धः
बंध <i>m.</i> 1. Fettering, confining, imprisoning, M.v.49; 2. a bond, a tie, a fetter; 3. capturing, catching; 4. joining, uniting; 5. forming, constructing; 6. a legature, a bandage; 7. connection, intercourse; 8. agreement, union; 9. result, consequence; 10. a sinew; 11. border, framework; 12. the body; 13. manifestation, display, R.xviii.52; 14. bondage, (op. to मुक्ति in which the soul is freed from all connection with the world) (in phil.), बंधोन्मुक्त्यै खलु मल्हमुखान् कुर्वते कर्मपाशान् Bh.V.iv.21, R.xviii.7, xiii.58, Bg.xviii.30; 15. a posture, a position, K.S.iii.45, 59; 16. a form of sexual intercourse; (the Ratimanjarī mentions sixteen forms, other treatises give different numbers); 17. conceiving, fooling, R.vi.81; 18. laying snares, R.xvi.2; 19. a stanza which can be arranged in a particular shape (in rhetoric). e.g., पद्मबंध, खड्गबंध, मुरजबंध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=500-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधतंत्र|बन्धतन्त्र
बंध-तंत्र <i>n.</i> a complete army containing chariots, elephants, horse and foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=500-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधपारुष्य|बन्धपारुष्य
बंध-पारुष्य <i>n.</i> forced construction of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=500-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधस्तंभ|बन्धस्तम्भ|बन्धस्तम्भः
बंध-स्तंभ <i>m.</i> the post to which an elephant is tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=500-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधक|बन्धक|बन्धकं|बंधकः|बन्धकः
बंधक <i>(I) m.</i> 1. A binder; 2. a catcher; 3. a ravisher; 4. a tie, a rope; 5. a bank, a dike; 6. a deposit; 7. exchange, barter; 8. a promise; 9. a city; 10. a part, a portion, ऋणं सदशबंधकम् Yaj.ii.76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=501-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधक|बन्धक|बन्धकं|बंधकः|बन्धकः
बंधक <i>(II) n.</i> Confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=501-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधकी|बन्धकी
बंधकी <i>f.</i> 1. An unchaste woman, दुर्योधनस्तु मोहादविज्ञातबंधकीहृदयसारः क्वापि परिभ्रांतः Ve.ii.; 2. a harlot, a courtezan; 3. a female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=501-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधन|बन्धन|बन्धनं
बंधन <i>n.</i> 1. Fastening, binding, tying, fettering, R.xii.70; 2. capturing, catching; 3. a bond, a chain, a fetter; 4. confinement, captivity, imprisonment; 5. a gaol, a prison, त्वां कारयामि कमलोदरबंधास्थम् Sak.vi., M.ix.288; 6. a sinew, a muscle; 7. hurting, injuring; 8. connecting, uniting, joining; 9. forming, constructing, K.S.iv.6; 10. clasping, clutching, binding round, घटय भुजबंधनं जनय रदखंडनं येन वा भवति सुखजातम् Git.G.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=501-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंधनागार|बन्धनागार|बन्धनागारः
