बाध्
बाध् <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. बाधित; pres. बाधते)</i> 1. To oppress, to harass, to torment, to trouble, to disturb, to vex, ऊनं न सत्वेष्वधिको बबाधे R.ii.14, M.x.129, Bt.xiv.45, Megh.i.53; 2. to oppose, to resist, to check, to obstruct; 3. to assault, to attack; 4. to drive away, to remove; 5. to invalidate, to abolish, to annul, न धर्ममर्थकामाभ्यां बबाधे च तेन तौ R.xvii.57.With अभ्-, 1. to injure; 2. to vex, to torment.With आ-, to injure, to vex.With प्र-, 1. to avert, to get the better of, कथं नु दैवं शक्येत पौरुषेण प्रबाधितम् Bh.; 2. to torment, to tease, to trouble, प्रबाधमानस्य जगंति Bt.xii.2.With सम्-, to trouble, to torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=506-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध|बाधः
बाध <i>m.</i> 1. Pain, suffering, affliction; 2. annoyance; 3. hurt, damage, Yaj.ii.156; 4. danger, peril; 5. resistance, opposition; 6. objection; 7. contradiction, absurdity; 8. a particular flaw in a syllogism, a form of fallacious middle term (in logic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=506-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

