बीजक <i>(I) m.</i> 1. The common citron; 2. the position of the arms of a child at birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजक|बीजकः
बीजक <i>(II) n.</i> Seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजल
बीजल <i>a. (f. ला)</i> Furnished with seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजला
बीजल <i>a. (f. ला)</i> Furnished with seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजिक
बीजिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Abounding in seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजिका
बीजिक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Abounding in seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजिन्
बीजिन् <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> Possessed of seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजिनी
बीजिन् <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> Possessed of seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीजिन्
बीजिन् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A father in general; 2. a real progenitor, (op. to क्षेत्रिन्, ‘the husband (owner) of a woman’); See M.ix.51; 3. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीज्य
बीज्य <i>a. (f. ज्या)</i> Well-born, of respectable family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीज्या
बीज्य <i>a. (f. ज्या)</i> Well-born, of respectable family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्स|बीभत्सः
बीभत्स <i>(I) a. (f. त्सा)</i> 1. Nauseous, revolting, hideous, loathsome; 2. envious, mischievous; 3. estranged in mind; 4. savage, ferocious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्सा
बीभत्स <i>(I) a. (f. त्सा)</i> 1. Nauseous, revolting, hideous, loathsome; 2. envious, mischievous; 3. estranged in mind; 4. savage, ferocious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्स|बीभत्सः
बीभत्स <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Disgust, detestation; 2. the disgusting considered as one of the eight or nine sentiments in poetry, (जुगुप्सास्थायिभावस्तु बीभत्सः कथ्यते रसः S.D.iii.236); 3. a name of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्सु|बीभत्सुः
बीभत्सु <i>m.</i> An epithet of Arjuna, (न कुर्यां कर्मं बीभत्सं युध्यमानः कथंचन । तेन देवमनुष्येषु बीभत्सुरिति विश्रुतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्
बुक् <i>ind.</i> An imitative word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्कार|बुक्कारः
बुक्-कार <i>m.</i> the roaring of a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क्
बुक्क् <i>vt. 1P, 10U (pres. बुक्कति, बुक्कयति-ते)</i> 1. To bark; 2. to speak, to talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क|बुक्कं|बुक्कः
बुक्क <i>(I) m.n.</i> 1. The heart; 2. the chest, बुक्काघातैर्युवातिनिकटे प्रौढवाक्येन राधा Ud.; 3. blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क|बुक्कं|बुक्कः
बुक्क <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A goat; 2. time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्कन्
बुक्कन् <i>m.</i> The heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्कन|बुक्कनं
बुक्कन <i>n.</i> Barking, yelping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्कस|बुक्कसः
बुक्कस <i>m.</i> A Chaṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्का
बुक्का <i>f.</i> The heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्की
बुक्का <i>f.</i> The heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्
बुद् <i>vt. 1U (pres. बोदति-ते)</i> 1. To perceive, to see, to discern; 2. to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध|बुद्धः
बुद्ध <i>(I) a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Known, understood; 2. observed; 3. awake, awakened; 4. wise, enlightened, (pp. of बुध् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धा
बुद्ध <i>(I) a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Known, understood; 2. observed; 3. awake, awakened; 4. wise, enlightened, (pp. of बुध् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध|बुद्धः
बुद्ध <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A wise man, a learned man; 2. a saint, who by perfect knowledge of the truth has attained liberation from all existence and reveals to the world the secret of obtaining it before his final emancipation (in Buddhistic works); 3. an epithet of Śākyasinha, the founder of the Bauddha religion; his native place was Kapilavastu, somewhere near Nepal; he is regarded as the ninth incarnation of Viṣṇu, निंदसि यज्ञविधेरहह श्रुतिजातम् । सदयहृदय दर्शितपशुघातम् । केशव धृतबुद्धशरीर जय जगदीश हरे Git.G.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धागम|बुद्धागमः
बुद्ध-आगम <i>m.</i> Buddha’s doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धोपासक|बुद्धोपासकः
बुद्ध-उपासक <i>m.</i> a worshipper of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धगया
बुद्ध-गया <i>f.</i> name of a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धमार्ग|बुद्धमार्गः
बुद्ध-मार्ग <i>m.</i> the doctrines of Buddha, Buddhism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धि|बुद्धिः
बुद्धि <i>f.</i> 1. Perception; 2. intelligence, understanding, intellect, discernment, शास्त्रेष्वकुंठिता बुद्धिः R.i.19, मूढः परप्रत्ययनेयबुद्धिः Mal.i., M.i.97, 106; 3. knowledge, e.g. बुद्धिर्यस्य बलं तस्य निर्बुद्धेस्तु कुतो बलम् (Cf. ‘knowledge is power’); 4. presence of mind; 5. impression, idea, notion, feeling, सौहार्दाद्वा विधुर इति वा मय्यनुक्रोशबुद्ध्या Megh.ii.52; 7. mind (as in कृपणबुद्धि q.v.); 8. purpose, plan, design; (बुद्ध्या ‘deliberately, purposely’); 9. intellect considered as the second of the twenty-five principles of creation (in Sāṅkhya phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध्यतीत
बुद्धि-अतीत <i>a.</i> beyond the reach of the understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध्यवज्ञान
बुद्धि-अवज्ञान <i>n.</i> disregard for one’s understanding, e.g., अप्राप्तकालं वचनं बृहस्पतिरपि ब्रुवन् । प्राप्नोति बुद्ध्यवज्ञानमपमानं च शाश्वतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धींद्रिय|बुद्धीन्द्रिय|बुद्धीन्द्रियं
बुद्धि-इंद्रिय <i>n.</i> a perceptive organ of sense (of which there are five, viz., the eye, ear, nose, tongue and skin, to these sometimes the mind is added. See ज्ञानेंद्रिय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिगम्य
बुद्धि-गम्य, ग्राह्य <i>a.</i> attainable by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिग्राह्य
बुद्धि-गम्य, ग्राह्य <i>a.</i> attainable by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिजीविन्
बुद्धि-जीविन् <i>a.</i> rationale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपुरःसर
बुद्धि-पुरःसर, -पूर्व, -पूर्वक <i>a.</i> intentional, designed, purposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपूर्व
बुद्धि-पुरःसर, -पूर्व, -पूर्वक <i>a.</i> intentional, designed, purposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपूर्वक
बुद्धि-पुरःसर, -पूर्व, -पूर्वक <i>a.</i> intentional, designed, purposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपूर्वम्
बुद्धि-पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम्, -पुरःसरम् <i>ind.</i> intentionally, purposely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपूर्वकम्
बुद्धि-पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम्, -पुरःसरम् <i>ind.</i> intentionally, purposely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपुरःसरम्
बुद्धि-पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम्, -पुरःसरम् <i>ind.</i> intentionally, purposely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिभ्रम|बुद्धिभ्रमः
बुद्धि-भ्रम <i>m.</i> aberration of the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिमत्|बुद्धिमन्त्
बुद्धि-मत् <i>a.</i> 1. sharp, acute, sensible; 2. rational, intelligent; 3. wise, learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धियोग|बुद्धियोगः
बुद्धि-योग <i>m.</i> mental union with the supreme being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिलक्षण
बुद्धि-लक्षण <i>n.</i> a sign of talent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिवैभव
बुद्धि-वैभव <i>n.</i> force of understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिशस्त्र
बुद्धि-शस्त्र <i>a.</i> armed with understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिसहाय|बुद्धिसहायः
बुद्धि-सहाय <i>m.</i> a counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिहीन
बुद्धि-हीन <i>a.</i> destitute of intelligence, silly, foolish, ignorant, e.g. अग्निहोत्रं त्रयो वेदास्त्रिदंडं भस्मगुंठनम् । बुद्धिपौरुषहीनानां जीविकेति बृहस्पतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=510-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्बुद|बुद्बुदः
बुद्बुद <i>m.</i> A bubble, (मानुष्ये) जलबुद्बुदसंनिभे Yaj.iii.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=511-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्
बुध् <i>vt. or vi. 1U, 4Ā (pp. बुद्ध; pres. बोधति-ते, बुध्यते)</i> 1. To know, to understand, to comprehend, नाबुद्ध कल्पद्रुमतां विहाय जातं तमात्यन्यसिपत्रवृक्षम् R.xiv.48, M.vii.68, Bh.V.i.53; 2. to mark, to attend to, to notice, to recognize, अपि लंघितमध्वानं बुबुधे न बुधोपमः R.i.47, xii.39; 3. to regard as, to esteem as, to consider; 4. to think, to reflect; 5. to awake, to wake up, ते च प्रापुरुदन्वंतं बुबुधे चादिपूरुषः R.x.6; 6. to be restored to one’s senses, शनैरबोधि सुग्रीवः Bt.xiv.57.With अनु-, 1. to know, to learn, to understand; 2. to be aware of.With अव-, to know, to learn, Bt.xv.101.With उद्-, 1. to awake; 2. to expand.With नि-, to know, to learn, to understand, K.S.iii.14, v.52; 2. to regard as, to consider as.With प्र-, 1. to awake, to wake up, Sis.ix.30; 2. to blow, to expand, साभ्रेऽह्रीव स्थलकमलिनीं न प्रबुद्धां न सुप्ताम् Megh.ii.27.With प्रति-, to wake, to wake up, M.i.74.With सम्-, to know, to understand, to learn, संभुत्सीष्ठाः स्वनयनैर्विद्विषामीहितानि Bt.xix.30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=511-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्
बुध् <i>Caus. (बोधयति-ते)</i> 1. to make known, to inform; 2. to revive, to restore to life; 3. to advise, to admonish, बोधयंतः परस्परम् Bg.x.9; 4. to remind anyone of anything; 5. to renew the scent (of a perfume); 6. to wake up, to rouse, प्राबोधयन्नुषसि वाग्मिरुदारवाचः R.v.65, 75; 7. to cause to expand (as a flower).With अनु-, to advise, to admonish, R.viii.75.With अव-, 1. to make known, to inform, to draw the attention of, चलवलयक्वणितैरवबोधय हरिमपि निजगतिशीलम् Git.G.xi.; 2. to awaken to rouse, R.xii.23.With उद्-, 1. to awaken, to excite; 2. to cause to expand.With प्र-, 1. to awaken, to rouse, R.v.65, vi.56; 2. to inform, to make known, R.iii.68.With प्रति-, 1. to inform, to communicate, अथैनं प्रत्यबोधयत् R.i.74; 2. to rouse, to awaken.With वि-, 1. to awaken, to rouse; 2. to restore to life, विवशा कामवधूर्विबोधिता K.S.iv.1.With सम्-, to inform, to give information, तवागतिज्ञं समबोधयन्माम् R.xiii.25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=511-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

