ब्रह्मण्या <i>f.</i> An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
ब्रह्मन् <i>(I) m.</i> 1. The first deity of the Hindu triad on whom falls the duty of creating the world, तस्मिञ् जज्ञे स्वयं ब्रह्मा सर्वलोकपितामहः M.i.9; 2. a Brnhmana; 3. one of the four principal priests at a Soma sacrifice; 4. an epithet of Bṛhaspati; 5. an epithet of Śiva; 6. the sun; 7. intellect; 8. an epithet of the seven sages (मरीच, अत्रि, अंगिरस्, पुलस्त्य, पुलह, क्रतु and वसिष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
ब्रह्मन् <i>(II) n.</i> 1. The supreme being regarded as impersonal, the soul of the universe from which all created things emanate and to which they return; 2. the mystic syllable Om, एकाक्षरं परं ब्रह्म M.ii.83; 3. the Vedas (collectively); See M.i.23, ii.172; 4. a Mantra used as a spell; 5. penance, austerity; 6. chastity, celibacy; 7. final beatitude or emancipation; 8. the Brāhmaṇīcal caste (collectively), ब्रह्मैव संनियंतृ स्यात्क्षतं हि ब्रह्मसंभवम् M.ix.320; 9. wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माक्षर
ब्रह्मन्-अक्षर <i>n.</i> the sacred syllable Om.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माग्रभू
ब्रह्मन्-अग्रभू <i>m.</i> a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

