ब्रह्मचारिन्
ब्रह्मन्-चारिन् <i>m.</i> 1. a Brāhmaṇa in the first period of his life, which commences from the time of his investiture with the sacred thread, he remains at the house of his spiritual teacher studying the Veda and observing the duties of his Āśrama; he is either नैष्ठिक or उपकुर्वाण qq.vv., M.ii.41, iii.50; 2. one who has taken a vow to lead a celibate life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मचारिणी
ब्रह्मन्-चारिणी <i>f.</i> 1. an epithet of Durgā; 2. a woman who observes the vow of chastity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

