ब्रह्महन्
ब्रह्मन्-हन् <i>a.</i> murdering Brāhmaṇa, M.xi.101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महुत|ब्रह्महुतं
ब्रह्मन्-हुत <i>n.</i> one of the five daily yajnyas consisting in the performance of the rights of hospitality. See M.iii.74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महृदय|ब्रह्महृदयः
ब्रह्मन्-हृदय <i>m.n.</i> name of a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=512-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माणी
ब्रह्माणी <i>f.</i> 1. The wife of Brahman (m.); 2. an epithet of Durgā; 3. a kind of brass; 4. a kind of perfume, (रेणुका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मिन्
ब्रह्मिन् <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> Relating to Brahman (n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

