ब्राह्म|ब्राह्मं|ब्राह्मः
ब्राह्म <i>(I) a. (f. ह्मी)</i> 1. Relating to Brahman (m.), R.xiii.60; 2. relating to Brahman (n.), Bg.ii.72; 3. relating to the Brāhmaṇas; 4. holy, sacred; 5. relating to sacred knowledge; 6. relating to or prescribed by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मी
ब्राह्म <i>(I) a. (f. ह्मी)</i> 1. Relating to Brahman (m.), R.xiii.60; 2. relating to Brahman (n.), Bg.ii.72; 3. relating to the Brāhmaṇas; 4. holy, sacred; 5. relating to sacred knowledge; 6. relating to or prescribed by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म|ब्राह्मं|ब्राह्मः
ब्राह्म <i>(II) m.</i> 1. One of the eight forms of marriage; in it, the bride is bestowed on the bridegroom decorated and without any gift from the bridegroom, (ब्राह्मो विवाह आहूय दीयते शक्त्यलंकृता Yaj.i.58), M.iii.27; 2. an epithet of Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म|ब्राह्मं|ब्राह्मः
ब्राह्म <i>(III) n.</i> 1. The part of the hand under the root of the thumb; 2. study of the Veda; 3. a missile presided oyer by Brahman (m.), R.xii.97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्माहोरात्र|ब्राह्माहोरात्रः
ब्राह्म-अहोरात्र <i>m.</i> a day and night of Brahman (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मदेया
ब्राह्म-देया <i>f.</i> a girl to be given in accordance with the Brahma form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्ममुहूर्त|ब्राह्ममुहूर्तः|ब्राह्ममुहूर्त्त|ब्राह्ममुहूर्त्तः
ब्राह्म-मुहूर्त <i>m.n.</i> a particular period of the early part of the day, ब्राह्मे मुहूर्ते किल तस्य देवी कुमारकल्पं सुषुवे कुमारम् R.v.36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं|ब्राह्मणः
ब्राह्मण <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> 1. Relating to or becoming a Brāhmaṇa; 2. given by a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणी
ब्राह्मण <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> 1. Relating to or becoming a Brāhmaṇa; 2. given by a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं|ब्राह्मणः
ब्राह्मण <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A member of the first of the four primary castes of the Hindus, a Brāhmaṇa (जन्मना जायते शूद्रः सम्स्कारैर्द्विज उच्यते । कर्मणा याति विप्रत्वं ब्रह्म जानाति ब्राह्मणः) M.i.31, v.95; 2. an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं|ब्राह्मणः
ब्राह्मण <i>(III) n.</i> 1. A society of Brāhmaṇas; 2. that portion of the Veda which contains rules for the employment of the Mantras, explanations of sacrifices and illustrations in the way of old stories; (the Veda consists of Mantra and Brāhmaṇa); 3. name of that class of Vedic works which contain the Brāhmaṇa portion of the Veda; (there are extant several Brāhmaṇas: to the Ṛgveda are attached the ऐतरेय and कौशीतकि; to the Yajurveda belongs the शतपथ; पंचविंश and षड्विंश Brāhmaṇas belong to the Sāmaveda and the गोपथ to the Atharvaveda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणातिक्रम|ब्राह्मणातिक्रमः
ब्राह्मण-अतिक्रम <i>m.</i> insulting behaviour towards a Brāhmaṇa, ब्राह्मणातिक्रमत्यागो भवतामेव भुतये Mv.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=515-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्ति|ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तिः
