भवच्छिद्
भव-च्छिद् <i>a.</i> preventing birth or transmigration, भवच्छिदस्त्रयंबकपादपांशवः Kad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदारु
भव-दारु <i>m.n.</i> the devadāru tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभूति|भवभूतिः
भव-भूति <i>m.</i> the celebrated author of the three plays that pass under his name; he flourished at the end of the seventh century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवरुत्
भव-रुत् <i>m.</i> a drum played at a funeral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवत्|भवन्त्
भवत् <i>(I) a. (f. न्ती)</i> 1. Being, becoming, happening, R.viii.78; 2. prcscnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्ती
भवत् <i>(I) a. (f. न्ती)</i> 1. Being, becoming, happening, R.viii.78; 2. prcscnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवत्|भवन्त्
भवत् <i>(II) pron. (f. ती)</i> The respectable pronoun translatable by ‘your worship, your honour, you’ (used for the second personal pronoun but with the third person of the verb), R.iii.48, ii.40, Sis.i.68, Bg.i.8; (it is often used with अत्र or तत्र prefixed; See अत्रभवत् and तत्रभवत्; ‘स’ is sometimes prefixed to it when the person referred to is absent, e.g. यन्मां विधेयविषये सभवान् नियुंक्ते M.M.i.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवती
भवत् <i>(II) pron. (f. ती)</i> The respectable pronoun translatable by ‘your worship, your honour, you’ (used for the second personal pronoun but with the third person of the verb), R.iii.48, ii.40, Sis.i.68, Bg.i.8; (it is often used with अत्र or तत्र prefixed; See अत्रभवत् and तत्रभवत्; ‘स’ is sometimes prefixed to it when the person referred to is absent, e.g. यन्मां विधेयविषये सभवान् नियुंक्ते M.M.i.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदीय|भवदीयं
भवदीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Your honour’s your, thine, शरीरभाजां भवदीयदर्शनम् Sis.i.26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदीया
भवदीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Your honour’s your, thine, शरीरभाजां भवदीयदर्शनम् Sis.i.26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=521-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

