भारत|भारतं|भारतः
भारत <i>(II) n.</i> 1. India, the country of Bharata; 2. name of the most popular itihāsa in Sanskrit detailing the history of the descendants of Bharata. Vyāsa is its reputed author, श्रवणांजलिपुटपेयं विरचितवान् भारताख्यममृतं यः । तमहमरागमकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं वंदे Ve.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=524-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारती
भारती <i>f.</i> 1. The goddess of speech; 2. speech, eloquence, literary art, जयति पद्मावतीरमणकविभारती Git.G.x., भारती कवेर्जयति K.Pr.i.; 3. a particular kind of style, (भारती संस्कृतप्रायो वाग्व्यापारो नटाश्रयः D.R.iii.5); 4. a quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=524-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

