भावसंधि|भावसन्धि|भावसंधिः
भाव-संधि <i>m.</i> coexistence of two emotions; for an illustration, See Bh.V.ii.37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=524-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसमाहित
भाव-समाहित <i>a.</i> collected in mind, abstracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=524-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसर्ग|भावसर्गः
भाव-सर्ग <i>m.</i> the intellectual creation, the creation of the faculties and affections of the human mind (as op. to material creation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=524-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावस्निग्ध
भाव-स्निग्ध <i>a.</i> affectionately disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=524-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावक|भावकः
