भावितात्मन्
भावित-आत्मन्, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> 1. one whose soul is purified by meditating on the universal soul; 2. thoughtful, meditative; 3. engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=525-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितबुद्धि
भावित-आत्मन्, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> 1. one whose soul is purified by meditating on the universal soul; 2. thoughtful, meditative; 3. engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=525-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितक|भावितकं
भावितक <i>n.</i> The product of a multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितृ
भावितृ <i>n.</i> The worlds collectively (heaven, earth and the lower regions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविन्
भाविन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> 1. To be or to happen in future, प्रस्थानं ते कथमपि सखे लंबमानस्य भावि Megh.i.41, R.xviii.38; 2. future, about to be, पुरुषस्य पदेष्वजन्मनः समतीतं च भवच्च भावि च R.viii.78; 3. becoming, being; 4. predestined, यद्भावि तद्भवति नात्र विचारहेतुः Panch.i.; 5. possessed of; 6. beautiful, illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविनी
भाविन् <i>a. (f. नी)</i> 1. To be or to happen in future, प्रस्थानं ते कथमपि सखे लंबमानस्य भावि Megh.i.41, R.xviii.38; 2. future, about to be, पुरुषस्य पदेष्वजन्मनः समतीतं च भवच्च भावि च R.viii.78; 3. becoming, being; 4. predestined, यद्भावि तद्भवति नात्र विचारहेतुः Panch.i.; 5. possessed of; 6. beautiful, illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविनी
भाविनी <i>f.</i> 1. A handsome woman; 2. a wanton woman; 3. a noble woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> 1. About to be, about to happen; 2. prosperous, happy; 3. appreciative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुका
भावुक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> 1. About to be, about to happen; 2. prosperous, happy; 3. appreciative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक <i>(II) m.</i> A sister’s husband (in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक <i>(III) n.</i> 1. Welfare, happiness, स रातु वो दुश्च्यवनो भावुकानां परंपराम् K.Pr.vii.; 2. language full of passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्य|भाव्यं
भाव्य <i>(I) a. (f. व्या)</i> 1. About to happen; 2. to be performed; 3. to be conceived; 4. to be demonstrated; 5. to be investigated. (For the impersonal use of भाव्य, See under भवितव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्या
भाव्य <i>(I) a. (f. व्या)</i> 1. About to happen; 2. to be performed; 3. to be conceived; 4. to be demonstrated; 5. to be investigated. (For the impersonal use of भाव्य, See under भवितव्य.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्य|भाव्यं
भाव्य <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Anything which is sure to happen in the future; 2. futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्
भाष् <i>vt. 1Ā (pp. भाषित; pres. भाषते)</i> 1. To say, to speak, to speak to, तद्भाषंते किमपि भजते यज्जुगुप्सास्पदत्वम् Vikr.Ch.xviii.97, मुख्मस्तीत्यभाषिष्ठाः का मे साशंकता त्वयि Bt.ix.122, R.vii.66; 2. to announce, क्षितिपालमुच्चैः प्रीत्या तमेवार्थमभाषतेव R.ii.51; 3. to speak about, त्वयैकमांशं प्रति साधु भाषितम् K.S.v.81; 4. to name, to call; 5. to describe.With अनु-, 1. to speak, to say; 2. to announce, M.xi.228.With अप-, to abuse, to find fault with, न केवलं यो महतोऽपभाषते शृणोति तस्मादपि यः स पापभाक् K.S.v.83.With अभि-, 1. to address, to speak to, M.ii.128; 2. to tell, to communicate; 3. to use or employ (a word).With आ-, to speak to, to address, आभाषि रामेण वचः कनीयान् Bt.iii.51.With परि-, to make a convolition, to speak conventionally.With प्र-, to speak, to speak to, स्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत Bg.ii.54.With प्रति-, to speak in return, to reply; 2. to speak what one has heard; 3. to name, to call, कामिनि तामुपगीतिं प्रतिभाषंते महाकवयः Sr.B.6.With वि-, to lay down optionally.With सम्-, to converse, to speak together, to hold conversation with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषण|भाषणं
भाषण <i>n.</i> 1. Speaking, M.xi.69; 2. speech; 3. kind words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषा
भाषा <i>f.</i> 1. Speech, स्थितप्रज्ञस्य का भाषा Bg.ii.54; 2. a language; 3. a vernacular dialect, (op. to संस्कृत), M.ix.332; 4. an epithet of the goddess of speech; 5. a charge, an accusation (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषांतर|भाषान्तर
भाषा-अंतर <i>n.</i> 1. another language; 2. a translation (modern and incorrect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषापाद|भाषापादः
भाषा-पाद <i>m.</i> the first of the four stages of a law-suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषासम|भाषासमः
भाषा-सम <i>m.</i> a sentence so arranged that it may be read as being written either in Sanskrit or in one or more of the Prākṛts, e.g. सरले साहसरागं परिहर रंभोरु मुंच संरंभम् । विरसं विरहायासं सोढुं तव चित्तमसहं मे M.M.vi., or मंजुलमणिमंजीरे कलगंभीरे विहारसरसीतीरे । विरसासि केलिकीरे किमालि धीरे च गंधसारसमीरे S.D.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिका
भाषिका <i>f.</i> Speech, language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषित|भाषितं
भाषित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Spoken, uttered, said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिता
भाषित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Spoken, uttered, said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषित|भाषितं
भाषित <i>(II) n.</i> Speech, language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषितपुंस्क
भाषित-पुंस्क <i>m.</i> the same as उक्तपुंस्क q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्य|भाष्यं
भाष्य <i>n.</i> 1. Speaking; 2. work written in any vernacular; 3. a commentary which explains sūtras word by word, adding its own comments, (सूत्रार्थो वर्ण्यते यत्र पदैः सूत्रानुसारिभिः । स्वपदानि च वर्ण्यते भाष्यं भाष्यविदो विदुः), फणिभाषितभाष्यफक्किका Na.ii.95, संक्षिप्तस्याप्यतोऽस्यैव वाक्यस्यार्थगरीयसः सुविस्तरतरा वाचो भाष्यभूता भवंतु मे Sis.ii.24. (The word is preeminently applied to Patanjali’s commentary on the sūtras of Pāṇini).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकर|भाष्यकरः
भाष्य-कर, -कार, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the writer of a Bhāshya (especially applied to Patanjali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकार|भाष्यकारः
भाष्य-कर, -कार, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the writer of a Bhāshya (especially applied to Patanjali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकृत्
भाष्य-कर, -कार, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the writer of a Bhāshya (especially applied to Patanjali).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास् <i>vi. 1Ā (pres. भासते)</i> 1. To shine, to be bright, विश्वद्रीच्या भुवनमखिलं भासते यस्य भासा Bh.V.iv.18; 2. to become evident, to become clear, to come into the mind, e.g. त्वदंगमार्दवं द्रष्टुः कस्य चित्ते न भासते । मालतीशशभृल्लेखाकदलीनां कठोरता; 3. to appear.With अव-, 1. to shine; 2. to appear, to appear like.With आ-, to appear like, स्थानांतरं स्वर्ग इवाबभांस K.S.vii.3.With उद्-, 1. to shine; 2. to appear like.With प्रति-, 1. to present the appearance of, to appear like; 2. to shine.With वि-, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास् <i>Caus. (भासयति-ते)</i> 1. to illuminate, to brighten, न तद्भासयते सूर्यो न शशांको न पावकः Bg.xv.6; 2. to make clear, to make evident, Bt.xv.42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=526-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास् <i>f.</i> 1. Light, lustre, brightness, भासते यस्य भासा Bh.V.iv.18; 2. a ray of light; 3. a reflection, an image; 4. glory, splendour; 5. wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्कर|भास्करं|भास्करः
भास्-कर <i>(I) m.</i> 1. the sun, R.xi.7, xii.25, K.S.vi.49; 2. a hero; 3. fire; 4. an epithet of Śiva; 5. name of a celebrated Hindu astronomer who flourished in the eleventh century of the Christian era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्कर|भास्करं|भास्करः
भास्-कर <i>(II) n.</i> gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करप्रिय|भास्करप्रियः
भास्-कर˚प्रिय <i>m.</i> a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करसप्तमी
भास्-कर˚सप्तमी <i>f.</i> the seventh day in the light half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करि|भास्करिः
भास्-करि <i>m.</i> the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वत्|भास्वन्त्
भास्-वत् <i>(I) a.</i> luminous, splendid, K.S.vi.60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वत्|भास्वन्त्
भास्-वत् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. light, lustre; 2. the sun, दिगुत्तरा भास्वति संनिवृत्ते R.xvi.44; 3. a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

