भिक्ष्
भिक्ष् <i>vt. or vi. 1Ā (pres. भिक्षते) (This is one of those roots which take two accusatives, e.g. भिक्षमाणो वनं प्रियाम् Bt.vi.9.)</i> 1. To ask, to ask for, to beg for; 2. to beg alms, यज्ञार्थमर्थं भिक्षित्वा यो न सर्वं प्रयच्छति M.xi.25; 3. to ask for without obtaining; 4. to be weary, to be distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=527-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षण|भिक्षणं
