भ्रम्
भ्रम् <i>vt. or vi. 1P, 4P (pp. भ्रांत; pres. भ्रमति, भ्रम्यति, भ्राम्यति)</i> 1. To roam about, to wander about, to go about, देशे देशे विपणिषु तथा चत्वरे पानगोष्ठ्यामुन्मत्तेव भ्रमति भवतो वल्लभा हंत कीर्तिः R.G., भ्रमति गवययूथः सर्वतस्तोयमिच्छन् Rt.i.24, Bt.xii.72; (भिक्षां भ्रम् ‘to go about begging’); 2. to circulate, to turn round, to move in a circle, e.g. कुलालचक्रवन्नातस्तदा तूर्णमथाश्रमन्; 3. to totter, to waver; 4. to err, to go astray, to fall in error, to be ignorant, आभरणकारस्तु तालव्यांत इति बभ्राम S.K.; 5. to move unsteadily, to flicker, to quiver; 6. to surround; 7. to fly about humming, शोणपद्ममिवोपरि भ्रमताकुलं भ्रमरेण Git.G.iii.With उद्-, 1. to be confused, to be wild, to be mad, ध्यायत्युद्भ्रमति प्रमीलति पतत्युद्याति मूर्छत्यापे Git.G.iv.; 2. to err, to fall in error; 3. to wander about, मारीचोद्भ्रांतहारीता मलयाद्रेरुपत्यकाः R.v.46.With परि-, 1. to wander about, to rove, to ramble; 2. to hover, परिभ्रमन्मूर्धजषट्पदाकुलैः Kir.iv.14; 3. to whirl round, to revolve; 4. to describe a circle round.With वि-, 1. to wander about; 2. to hover; 3. to scatter, to frighten away; 4. to be disarranged, to be confused, to be bewildered, Bg.xvi.16.With सम्-, 1. to wander about; 2. to err, to be confused, to be perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=538-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम्
भ्रम् <i>Caus. (भ्रमयति-ते, भ्रामयति-ते)</i> 1. to cause to wander, to cause to move about, भ्रमय जलदानंभोगर्भान् M.M.ix.; 2. to cause to err, to delude, to confuse, to embarass, भ्रामयन्म्सर्वभूतानि यंत्रारूढानि मायया Bg.xviii.61; 3. to wave, to brandish, लीलारविंदं भ्रमयांचकार R.vi.13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=538-30" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

