मत|मतं|मतः
मत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Thought, supposed; 2. considered, deemed, regarded; 3. conjectured; 4. honoured, respected; 5. commended, valued; 6. meditated upon, perceived, recognized; 7. assented to, approved, consented to, (pp. of मन् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=545-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मता
मत <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Thought, supposed; 2. considered, deemed, regarded; 3. conjectured; 4. honoured, respected; 5. commended, valued; 6. meditated upon, perceived, recognized; 7. assented to, approved, consented to, (pp. of मन् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=545-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत|मतं|मतः
मत <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Opinion, view, belief, Bt.xviii.6; 2. doctrine, creed, tenet, ये ते मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठति मानवाः Bg.iii.31; 3. counsel, advice; 4. design, aim, purpose; 5. approbation, commendation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=545-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

