मनु|मनुः
मनु <i>(I) m.</i> 1. Name of a divine sage supposed to be the father of the human race; 2. a term applied to fourteen successive progenitors or sovereigns of the earth; (they are- (1) स्वायंभुव, (2) स्वारोचिष, (3) औत्तमि, (4) तामस, (5) रैवत, (6) चाक्षुष, (7) वैवस्वत, (8) सावर्णि, (9) दक्षसावर्णि, (10) ब्रह्मसावर्णि, (11) धर्मसावर्णि, (12) देवसावर्णि, (13) इंद्रसावर्णि; of these the seventh Manu called वैवस्वत is supposed to be the progenitor of the present race of living beings; the first Manu called Mārīchi is supposed (erroneously) to be the author of the Manusanhitā; the seventh or present Manu is regarded to be the founder of the Solar race of kings; See R.i.11 and Bg.iv.1); 3. the number ‘fourteen.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=552-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनु|मनुः
मनु <i>(II) f.</i> The wife of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=552-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्वंतर|मन्वन्तर|मन्वन्तरं
मनु-अंतर <i>n.</i> the period of a Manu; (this period comprises 43,20,000 human years, See M.i.79; every such period is presided over by a Manu; six of these have already elapsed and the seventh is now going on; according to Hindu mythology seven more are to come).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=552-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

