मंद|मन्द|मन्दः
मंद <i>(I) a. (f. दा)</i> 1. Slow, tardy, inactive, idle, loitering, भिंदंति मंदां गतिमश्वमुख्यः K.S.i.11; 2. apathetic, cold; 3. silly, foolish, stupid, dull, मंदः कवियशःप्रार्थी गमिष्याम्युपहास्यताम् R.i.3, द्विषंति मंदाश्चरितं महात्मनाम् K.S.v.75; 4. feeble, blunt, miserable; 5. wicked, vile; 6. addicted to drinking; 7. unhappy, unlucky; 8. little, small, (e.g. मंदोदरी); 9. withered (as flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=554-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंदा|मन्दा
मंद <i>(I) a. (f. दा)</i> 1. Slow, tardy, inactive, idle, loitering, भिंदंति मंदां गतिमश्वमुख्यः K.S.i.11; 2. apathetic, cold; 3. silly, foolish, stupid, dull, मंदः कवियशःप्रार्थी गमिष्याम्युपहास्यताम् R.i.3, द्विषंति मंदाश्चरितं महात्मनाम् K.S.v.75; 4. feeble, blunt, miserable; 5. wicked, vile; 6. addicted to drinking; 7. unhappy, unlucky; 8. little, small, (e.g. मंदोदरी); 9. withered (as flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=554-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मंद|मन्द|मन्दः
मंद <i>(II) m.</i> 1. the planet Saturn; 2. an epithet of Yama; 3. the end of the world; 4. a kind of elephant.(मंदम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of- (1) slowly, gradually, by degrees, स्तनभरपरिखेदान्मंदमंदं व्रजंत्यः Rt.v.15; (2) gently, softly, मंदं मंदं नुदति पवनश्चानुकूलो यथा त्वाम् Megh.i.9; (3) weakly, feebly, faintly; (4) in a low voice. मंदीक्रू ‘to slacken,’ Sak.i.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=554-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

