मह्
मह् <i>(I) vi. 1Ā (pres. मंहते)</i> To grow, to increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह्
मह् <i>(II) vt. 10U (pp. महित; pres. महयति-ते)</i> To value greatly, to honour, to revere, to worship, e.g. गोप्तारं न निधीनां महयंति महेश्वरं विबुधाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह|महं|महः
मह <i>m.</i> 1. A festival, न खलु दूरगतोप्यतिवर्तते महमसाविति बंधुतयोदितैः Sis.vi.19; 2. a buffalo; 3. light lustre; 4. a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महक|महकः
महक <i>m.</i> 1. A distinguished man; 2. an epithet of Viṣṇu; 3. a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-37" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्|महन्त्
महत् <i>(I) a. (f. ती; compar. महीयस्; super. महिष्ठ) (nom. महान्-हान्तौ-हान्तः; acc. pl. महतः)</i> 1. Large, great, extensive, ample, huge, e.g. महान्; 2. loud, e.g. महान् घोषः; 3. late, far advanced, e.g. महत्यपराह्णे; 4. long, e.g. महानध्वा, महती कथा; 5. intense, excessive, e.g. महती तृषा; 6. important, e.g. महान् कार्यभारः; 7. eminent, high, e.g. महत्कुलम्; 8. distinguished, e.g. महाञ् जनः; 9. dense, thick, e.g. महत्तमः; 10. numerous, abundant, e.g. महतो जनस्य मध्ये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महती
महत् <i>(I) a. (f. ती; compar. महीयस्; super. महिष्ठ) (nom. महान्-हान्तौ-हान्तः; acc. pl. महतः)</i> 1. Large, great, extensive, ample, huge, e.g. महान्; 2. loud, e.g. महान् घोषः; 3. late, far advanced, e.g. महत्यपराह्णे; 4. long, e.g. महानध्वा, महती कथा; 5. intense, excessive, e.g. महती तृषा; 6. important, e.g. महान् कार्यभारः; 7. eminent, high, e.g. महत्कुलम्; 8. distinguished, e.g. महाञ् जनः; 9. dense, thick, e.g. महत्तमः; 10. numerous, abundant, e.g. महतो जनस्य मध्ये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्|महन्त्
महत् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. The second of the twenty five principles of creation according to the Sāṅkhyas. See Sank.K.3; 2. a camel; 3. an epithet of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्|महन्त्
महत् <i>(III) n.</i> 1. Kingdom, dominion; 2. sacred knowledge; 3. infinity, greatness.(महत् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of ‘much, exceedingly.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=559-38" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महदावास|महदावासः
