महा-महोपाध्याय <i>m.</i> 1. a very great teacher; 2. a title of honour conferred upon scholars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=560-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामात्र|महामात्रः
महा-मात्र <i>m.</i> 1. an elephant-driver; 2. a superintendent of elephants; 3. a prime minister, a minister (मंत्रे कर्मणि भूषायां वित्ते माने परिच्छदे । मात्रा च महती येषां महामात्र्तास्तु ते स्मृताः) M.ix.259.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=560-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामात्री
महा-मात्री <i>f.</i> 1. the wife of a prime minister; 2. the wife of a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=560-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामाय|महामायः
