माधवी
माधव <i>(I) a. (f. वी)</i> 1. Made of honey; 2. vernal; 3. belonging to the descendants of Madhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=568-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधव|माधवः
माधव <i>(II) m.</i> 1. An epithet of Kṛṣṇa, यावदर्थपदां वाचमेवमादाय माधवः Sis.ii.13, Bg.i.14; 2. the spring season, स माधवेनाभिमतेन सख्या रत्या च साशंकमनुप्रयातः K.S.iii.23; 3. the month of Vaiśākha, भास्करस्य मधुमाधवाविव R.xi.7; 4. an epithet of Paraśurāma; 5. of Indra; 6. name of a celebrated scholar, supposed by some to be identical with Śāyaṇa; but he tells us that his father’s name was Māyaṇa and that he had two brothers Śāyaṇa and Bhoganātha; he flourished in the middle of the fourteenth century, and has left works on almost every branch of Sanskrit literature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=568-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवश्री
