मृग्
मृग् <i>vt. 4P, 10Ā (pp. मृगित; pres. मृग्यति, मृगयते)</i> 1. To seek, to search for, न रत्नमन्विष्यति मृग्यते हि तत् K.S.v.45; 2. to investigate, to examine, अंतर्यश्च मुमुक्षुभिर्नियमितप्राणादिभिर्मृग्यते Vikr.i., अविचलितमनोभिः साधकैर्मृग्यमाणः M.M.v.; 3. to beg anything from anybody, e.g. तत्सकाशादृणं किंचिदेह्यद्य मृगयामहे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=581-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग|मृगः
मृग <i>m.</i> 1. A quadruped, an animal in general, मूकांडजं शांतमृगप्रचारम् K.S.iii.42; 2. a deer, an antelope, a stag, मृगद्वंद्वेषु पश्यंतौ स्यंदनाबद्धदृष्टिषु R.i.40, अभिन्नगतयः शब्दं सहंते मृगाः Sak.i., R.i.50; 3. a species of elephant; 4. musk; 5. seeking, search; 6. chase, hunting; 7. asking, soliciting; 8. the constellation मृगशिरस्; 9. the sign Capricornus of the zodiac; 10. the month Mārgaśīrṣa; 11. the spots of the moon represented as an antelope; 12. a particular class of men (in erotic literature), e.g. मृगे तुष्टा च चित्रिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=581-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

