म्लै
म्लै <i>vi. 1P (pp. म्लान; pres. म्लायति)</i> 1. To grow weary, to be fatigued, मम्लुतुर्न मणिकुट्टिमोचितौ R.xi.9; 2. to be sad, to be dispirited, मम्लौ साथ विषादेन पद्मिनीव हिमांभसा K.Pr.x.; 3. to wither, to fade; 4. to become thin, to be emaciated.With परि- 1. to be dejected, to be dispirited, R.xiv.50, K.S.ii.2; 2. to fade, to wither.With प्र-, 1. to fade, to wither; 2. to be dejected; 3. to be dirty, to be soiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=588-31" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य <i>m.</i> 1. A goer, a mover; 2. union; 3. air, wind; 4. fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्
यकृत् <i>n.</i> 1. The liver; 2. a disease of the liver.(यकन् is optionally substituted for this word in some of the declensions.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृदात्मिका
यकृत्-आत्मिका <i>f.</i> a kind of cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृदुदर
यकृत्-उदर <i>n.</i> enlargment of the liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्कोष|यकृत्कोषः
यकृत्-कोष <i>m.</i> the membrane enveloping the liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष|यक्षः
यक्ष <i>m.</i> 1. A class of demigods, attendant on Kubera and employed in guarding his treasures, यस्यां यक्षाः सितमणिमयान्येत्य हर्म्यस्थलानि Megh.ii.3, Bg.x.23, xi.22; 2. a ghost, an evil spirit; 3. the palace of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षाधिप|यक्षाधिपः
यक्ष-अधिप, -अधिपति <i>m.</i> Kubera, the lord of Yakshas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षाधिपति|यक्षाधिपतिः
यक्ष-अधिप, -अधिपति <i>m.</i> Kubera, the lord of Yakshas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षावास|यक्षावासः
यक्ष-आवास <i>m.</i> the Indian fig tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षकर्दम|यक्षकर्दमः|यक्षकर्द्दम|यक्षकर्द्दमः
यक्ष-कर्दम <i>m.</i> an ointment consisting of camphor, agallochum, musk, kakkola and saffron mixed in equal proportions, (कर्पूरागुरुकस्तूरीकल्लोलैर्यक्षकर्दमः Am.ii.6.133).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षग्रह|यक्षग्रहः
यक्ष-ग्रह <i>m.</i> the being possessed by an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षतरु|यक्षतरुः
यक्ष-तरु <i>m.</i> the Indian fig tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षधूप|यक्षधूपः
यक्ष-धूप <i>m.</i> resin, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरस|यक्षरसः
यक्ष-रस <i>m.</i> a kind of intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज्
यक्ष-राज्, -राज <i>m.</i> a name of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज|यक्षराजः
यक्ष-राज्, -राज <i>m.</i> a name of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरात्रि|यक्षरात्रिः
यक्ष-रात्रि <i>f.</i> the festival of Dīpāvalī on the full-moon-day in the month of Kārtīka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षवित्त|यक्षवित्तः
यक्ष-वित्त <i>a.</i> one who stores up wealth but never uses it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षिणी
यक्षिणी <i>f.</i> 1. A female Yaksha; 2. a female fiend attendant on Durgā; 3. a fairy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षी
यक्षी <i>f.</i> A female Yaksha, स्वक्षी यक्षी साप्यदृश्यतामयासीत् D.K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्म|यक्ष्मः
यक्ष्म <i>m.</i> Pulmonary disease, consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मन्
यक्ष्म <i>m.</i> Pulmonary disease, consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मग्रह|यक्ष्मग्रहः
यक्ष्म-ग्रह <i>m.</i> an attack of consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मग्रह|यक्ष्मग्रहः
यक्ष्म-ग्रह <i>m.</i> an attack of consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मघ्नी
यक्ष्म-घ्नी <i>f.</i> a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मघ्नी
यक्ष्म-घ्नी <i>f.</i> a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मिन्
यक्ष्मिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> One who suffers from consumption, M.iii.154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मिणी
यक्ष्मिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> One who suffers from consumption, M.iii.154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्
यज् <i>vi. or vt. 1U (pp. इष्ट; pres. यजति-ते; pass. इज्यते; desid. यियक्षति-ते)</i> 1. To sacrifice, M.xi.40; (often used with the instrumental of the word signifying ‘rite, sacrifice,’ इष्ट्वा च शक्तितो यज्ञैः M.vi.36); 2. to make an oblation to a particular deity, (with acc. of the deity and inst. of the oblation, वाग्दैवत्यैश्च चरुभिर्यजेरंस्ते सरस्वतीम् M.viii.105); 3. to worship.With सम्-, to worship, समयष्टास्रमंडलम् Bt.xv.96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजति|यजतिः
यजति <i>m.</i> A term for those sacrifices to which the verb यजति is applied, as distinguished from those rites to which the verb जुहोति applies. (See M.ii.84 and Medhātithi thereon; Sarvajnyanārāyaṇa renders जुहोति by उपविष्टहोम and यजति by तिष्ठद्धोम.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्र|यजत्रः
यजत्र <i>(I) m.</i> A Brāhmaṇa maintaining consecrated fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्र|यजत्रः
यजत्र <i>(II) n.</i> The maintenance of such fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन|यजनं
यजन <i>n.</i> 1. The act of sacrificing; 2. a sacrifice; 3. a place of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमान|यजमानः
यजमान <i>m.</i> 1. A person who institutes a regular sacrifice and pays its expenses; 2. one who employs priests to perform a sacrifice for his behoof; 3. a patron, a rich man, a host.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमानशिष्य|यजमानशिष्यः
यजमान-शिष्य <i>m.</i> a pupil of a Brāhmaṇa who performs a sacrifice, ततः प्रविशति कुशानुनादाय यजमानशिष्यः Sak.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजि|यजिः
यजि <i>m.</i> 1. A sacrificer; 2. a sacrifice, दानमध्ययनं यजिः M.x.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुस्
यजुस् <i>n.</i> A sacred mantra in prose, a text of the Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुर्वेद|यजुर्वेदः|यजुर्व्वेदः
यजुर्वेद <i>m.</i> the second of the three principal Vedas consisting of sacred texts in prose and relating to sacrifices. It is two-fold, viz., तैत्तिरीय or शुक्लयजुर्वेद and वाजसनेय or कृष्णयजुर्वेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञ|यज्ञः
यज्ञ <i>m.</i> 1. A sacrifice, R.i.26, Bg.ix.20; 2. any devotional act generally; (the five daily acts of devotion enjoined to a Brāhmaṇa are- भूतयज्ञ, मनुष्ययज्ञ, पितृयज्ञ, देवयज्ञ and ब्रह्मयज्ञ; they are collectively called the five ‘great sacrifices’; See महायज्ञ); 3. a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञांश|यज्ञांशः
यज्ञ-अंश <i>m.</i> a share of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञांशभुज्
यज्ञ-अंश˚भुज् <i>m.</i> a deity, यज्ञांशभुजामिदानीम् K.S.iii.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञागार|यज्ञागारः
यज्ञ-अगार, -आगार <i>m.n.</i> a sacrificial hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञागार|यज्ञागारः
यज्ञ-अगार, -आगार <i>m.n.</i> a sacrificial hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञांग|यज्ञाङ्ग|यज्ञाङ्गः
यज्ञ-अंग <i>(I) m.</i> the Udumbara tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञांग|यज्ञाङ्ग|यज्ञाङ्गः
यज्ञ-अंग <i>(II) n.</i> 1. a part of a sacrifice; 2. a means or instrument of a sacrifice, यज्ञांगयोनित्वमवेक्ष्य यस्य K.S.i.17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञात्मन्
यज्ञ-आत्मन्, -ईश्वर <i>m.</i> a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञेश्वर|यज्ञेश्वरः
यज्ञ-आत्मन्, -ईश्वर <i>m.</i> a name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपकरण
यज्ञ-उपकरण <i>n.</i> any utensil or implement necessary for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपवीत|यज्ञोपवीतं
यज्ञ-उपवीत <i>n.</i> the sacred thread usually worn by the twice-born over the left shoulder and under the right arm (See M.ii.63), वामांसावलंबिना यज्ञोपवीतेनोद्भासमानः Kad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकर्मन्|यज्ञकर्म्मन्
यज्ञ-कर्मन् <i>(I) a.</i> engaged in a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकर्मन्|यज्ञकर्म्मन्
यज्ञ-कर्मन् <i>(II) n.</i> a sacrificial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकल्प
यज्ञ-कल्प <i>a.</i> of the nature of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकीलक|यज्ञकीलकः
यज्ञ-कीलक <i>m.</i> the post to which the victim is fastened at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकुंड|यज्ञकुण्ड
यज्ञ-कुंड <i>n.</i> a hole in the ground built for receiving the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञक्रतु|यज्ञक्रतुः
यज्ञ-क्रतु <i>m.</i> 1. a complete rite, a chief ceremony; 2. on epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञघ्न|यज्ञघ्नः
यज्ञ-घ्न <i>m.</i> a demon interrupting sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञदक्षिणा
यज्ञ-दक्षिणा <i>f.</i> the fee given to a priest engaged in a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञदीक्षा
यज्ञ-दीक्षा <i>f.</i> 1. admission to a sacrificial rite; 2. performance of a sacrifice, M.ii.169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=589-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञद्रव्य
