यज्ञिय|यज्ञियं|यज्ञियः
यज्ञिय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> 1. Sacred, holy; 2. relating to or suitable for a sacrifice, sacrificial; 3. pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=590-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिया
यज्ञिय <i>(I) a. (f. या)</i> 1. Sacred, holy; 2. relating to or suitable for a sacrifice, sacrificial; 3. pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=590-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिय|यज्ञियं|यज्ञियः
यज्ञिय <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A god, a deity; 2. the third or Dvāpara age of the Hindus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=590-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञियदेश|यज्ञियदेशः
यज्ञिय-देश <i>m.</i> region fit for sacrifices, a particular part of India thus defined by Manu- कृष्णसारस्तु चरति मृगो यत्र स्वभावतः । स ज्ञेयो यज्ञियो देशः ii.23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=590-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

