यशस्-विन् <i>a.</i> renowned, glorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=595-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशःशेष|यशःशेषः
यशस्-शेष <i>(I) a.</i> having left nothing but glory, i.e. dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=595-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशःशेष|यशःशेषः
यशस्-शेष <i>(II) m.</i> death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=595-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्य
यशस्य <i>a. (f. स्या)</i> 1. Famous, glorious; 2. bestowing, glory or distinction, M.i.106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=595-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्या
यशस्य <i>a. (f. स्या)</i> 1. Famous, glorious; 2. bestowing, glory or distinction, M.i.106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=595-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टि|यष्टिः
यष्टि <i>f.</i> 1. A staff, a stick; 2. a column, a pillar; 3. a stem, a support; 4. a stalk; 5. a branch, चूतयष्टिरिवाभाशे मधौ परभृतोन्मुखी K.S.vi.2; 6. a string of pearls, a necklace, क्वचित्प्रभालेपिभिरिंद्रनीलैर्मुक्तामयी यष्टिरिवानुविद्धा R.xiii.54, K.S.v.8; 7. any creeping plant; (at the end of compounds the word is used to imply ‘thinness, slenderness,’ असंभृतं मंडनमंगयष्टेः K.S.i.31).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=595-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिग्रह|यष्टिग्रहः
