युक्त-अर्थ <i>a.</i> sensible, significant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=597-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तदंड|युक्तदण्ड
युक्त-दंड <i>a.</i> punishing justly, R.iv.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=597-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तरूप
युक्त-रूप <i>a.</i> suit, able, proper, fit for, (with a gen. or loc.), जन्म यस्य पुरोर्वंशे युक्तरूपमिदं Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=597-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्ति|युक्तिः
युक्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Junction, combination; 2. use, practice; 3. means, expedient; 4. device, contrivance; 5. propriety, fitness; 6. skill, art; 7. inference, argument; 8. probability, enumeration of circumstances (as specification of time, place &c.), असाक्षिकहते चिह्नैर्युक्तिभिश्चागमेन च Yaj.ii.212; 9. connection of incidents in a drama, S.D.343; 10. emblematic expression of a purpose; 11. arrangement (of words), यत्र खल्वियं वाचोयुक्तिः M.M.i.; 12. sum, total; 13. alloying of metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=597-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तिकर
युक्ति-कर <i>a.</i> 1. suitable; 2. proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=597-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तियुक्त
युक्ति-युक्त <i>a.</i> 1. expert, skillful; 2. suitable, fit; 3. proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=597-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग <i>(I) m.n.</i> A yoke, छिन्ननस्येन यानेन तथा भग्नयुगादिना Yaj.ii.299, R.iii.34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग <i>(II) n.</i> 1. A pair, a couple, स्तनयुगपरिणाहाच्छादिना कल्कलेन Sak.i., Sis.ix.72; 2. a long mundane period of years, an age; (there are four such periods, viz., कृत, त्रेता, द्वापर and कलि, which together comprise 43,20,000 years of men and are called a Mahāyuga, M.i.69-73; the regularly descending length of them is accompanied by a corresponding physical and moral deterioration), धर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय संभवामि युगे युगे Bg.iv.8; 3. a measure of four cubits; 4. an expression for the numbers ‘four’ and ‘twelve’; 5. life, birth, अश्रेयाञ् श्रेयसीं जातिं गच्छत्यासप्तमाद्युयात् M.x.64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगांत|युगान्त|युगान्तः
युग-अंत <i>m.</i> 1. the end of the yoke; 2. midday, noon; 3. the end of an age, destruction of the world, अमुं युगांतोचितयोगनिद्रः संहृत्य लोकान् पुरुषोऽविशेते R.xiii.6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगकीलक|युगकीलकः
युग-कीलक <i>m.</i> the pin of a yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगंधर|युगन्धर|युगंधरं|युगंधरः|युगन्धरः
युगंधर <i>m.n.</i> the pole of a carriage to which the yoke is fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपार्श्वग|युगपार्श्वगः
युग-पार्श्वग <i>m.</i> an ox in training.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपद्
युगपद् <i>ind.</i> At the same time, simultaneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगल|युगलं
युगल <i>n.</i> A pair, a couple, संपीड्य बाहुयुगलेन पिबामि वक्त्रम् Ch.P.3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगलक|युगलकं
युगलक <i>n.</i> 1. A pair; 2. two verses forming one sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्म|युग्मं
युग्म <i>(I) a. (f. ग्मा)</i> Even, षोडशर्तुनिशाः स्त्रीणां तस्मिन्युग्मासु संविशेत् Yaj.i.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मा
युग्म <i>(I) a. (f. ग्मा)</i> Even, षोडशर्तुनिशाः स्त्रीणां तस्मिन्युग्मासु संविशेत् Yaj.i.79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्म|युग्मं
युग्म <i>(II) n.</i> 1. A pair, a couple; 2. a couple of verses forming one sentence, (द्वाभ्यां युग्ममिति प्रोक्तं त्रिभिः श्लोकैर्विशेषकम् । कलापकं चतुर्भिः स्यात्तदूर्ध्वं कुलकं स्मृतम् Mall. on Kir.iii.1); 3. twin; 4. junction, union; 5. the sign Gemini of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्य|युग्यं|युग्यः
युग्य <i>(I) a. (f. ग्या)</i> 1. Yoked; 2. drawn by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्या
युग्य <i>(I) a. (f. ग्या)</i> 1. Yoked; 2. drawn by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्य|युग्यं|युग्यः
युग्य <i>(II) n.</i> A carriage, a vehicle, M.viii.293.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्य|युग्यं|युग्यः
युग्य <i>(III) m.</i> An animal yoked, a carriage horse, हरियुग्यं रथं तस्मै प्रजिघाय पुरंदरः R.xii.34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् <i>(I) vt. 1P, 10P (pres. योजति, योजयति)</i> To unite, to yoke.With नि-, to appoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् <i>(II) vi. 4Ā (pres. युज्यते)</i> To curb or concentrate the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् <i>(III) vt. 7U (pp. युक्त; pres. युनक्ति, युंक्ते; desid. युयुक्षति-ते)</i> 1. To unite, to join, रविपीतजला पतात्यये पुनरोधेन हि युज्यते नदी K.S.iv.44; 2. to apply, to use, प्रशस्ते कर्मणि तथा सच्छब्दः पार्थ युज्यते Bg.xvii.26; 3. to prepare, to make ready; 4. to concentrate the mind, to meditate, युंजन्नेवं सदात्मानं योगी नियतमानसः Bg.vi.15; 5. to grant, to endow; 6. to design, to intend.With अनु-, (Atm.) 1. to ask, किं वस्तु विद्वन्गुरवे प्रदेयं त्वया कियद्वेति तमन्वयुंक्त R.v.18, Sis.xiii.68; 2. to examine.With अभि-, (Atm) 1. to accuse, to attack, M.viii.193; 2. to sue for, to claim, विभावितैकदेशेन देयं यदभियुज्यते Vikr.iv.With उद्-, 1. to make effort, to endeavour; 2. (Atm.) to prepare.With उप-, (Atm.) 1. to take, to experience, R.xviii.46; 2. to use, to employ, पणबंधमुखान्गुणानजः षड्गुणयुंक्त समीक्ष्य तत्फलम् R.viii.21; 3. to enjoy, to eat, Bt.viii.39.With नि-, (Atm.) 1. to order, to appoint, (with a loc.), अवैमि ते सारमतः खलु त्वां कार्ये गुरुण्यात्मसमं नियोक्ष्ये K.S.iii.13; 2. to join.With प्र-, (Atm.) 1. to employ, to order, अरण्ययाने सुकरे पिता मां प्रायुंक्त राज्ये बत दुष्करे त्वाम् Bt.iii.51, K.S.vii.35; 2. to lend money, M.viii.146; 3. to give, to bestow, to confer, इत्थं प्रयुज्याशिषमग्रजन्मा R.v.35; 4. to move, to set in motion, मरुत्प्रयुक्ताश्च मरुत्सखाभम् R.ii.10; 5. to employ, to use, सद्भावे साधुभावे च सदित्येतत्प्रयुज्यते Bg.xvii.26; 6. to perform, to represent on the stage, यदिदं वयं मृच्छकटिकं नाम प्रकरणं प्रयोक्तुं व्यवसिताः Mrich.i.; 7. to make effort.With वि-, (Atm.) 1. to separate, K.S.v.26; 2. to leave, to abandon, R.xiii.63; 3. to send.With विनि-, 1. to appoint or employ; 2. to expend, to use; 3. to involve in, to apportion, प्रत्येकं विनियुक्तात्मा कथं न ज्ञास्यसि प्रभो K.S.ii.31.With सम्-, to unite, संयोक्ष्यसे स्वेन वपुर्महिम्ना तदेत्यवोचत्स तपोनिधिर्माम् R.v.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् <i>Pass. (युज्यते)</i> 1. to be fit or suitable, या यस्य युज्यते भूमिका तां भावेन सर्वे वर्ग्याः पाठिताः M.M.i.; 2. to be right, to be explicable; 3. to be ready, ततो युद्धाय युज्यस्व नैवं पापमवाप्स्यसि Bg.ii.38; 4. to be striving or intent upon, M.i.108.With वि-, to be separated from.With संप्र-, to be engaged in any business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् <i>Caus. (योजयति-ते)</i> 1. to join; 2. to achieve, to perform, M.viii.354; 3. to instigate; 4. (Atm.) to oblige; 5. to put to, पापान्निवारयति योजयते हिताय Bhartr.ii.17.With नि-, to yoke, to harness.With सम्-, to unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् <i>(I) m.</i> 1. (nom. sing. युज् or युग्) A sage devoted to abstract contemplation; 2. (nom. sing. युङ्) joiner, one who unites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् <i>(II) n.</i> A pair, a couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=598-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युंजान|युञ्जान|युञ्जानः
युंजान <i>m.</i> 1. A driver, a charioteer; 2. a Brāhmaṇa engaged in the exercise of Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=599-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

