रसनालिह्
रसना-लिह् <i>m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसा
रसा <i>f.</i> 1. The hell, the lower world; 2. the earth, ground, soil, रसासाररसा साररायताक्षक्षताय सा K.Pr.ix.; 3. the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसातल|रसातलं
रसा-तल <i>n.</i> 1. one of the seven hells or regions below the earth; 2. the lower world or hell in general, जातिर्यातु रसातलं गुणगणस्तस्याप्यधो गच्छतु Bhartr.ii.39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाल|रसालं|रसालः
रसाल <i>(I) m.</i> 1. The mango tree, यावन्मिलदलिमालः कोपि रसालः Bh.V.i.7; 2. the sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाल|रसालं|रसालः
रसाल <i>(II) n.</i> Frankincense, gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाला
रसाला <i>f.</i> 1. The tongue; 2. a vine or grape; 3. curds mixed with sugar and spices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिक|रसिकः
रसिक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> 1. Savoury, tasteful, flavoured; 2. impassioned, elegant; 3. witty, humorous; 4. apprehending flavour or beauty, appreciative, रसिकजनं तमुतामतिमुदितम् Git.G.vi.; 5. taking pleasure in, delighting in, अन्तर्धानव्यसनरसिका रात्रिकापालिकीयम् K.Pr.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिका
रसिक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> 1. Savoury, tasteful, flavoured; 2. impassioned, elegant; 3. witty, humorous; 4. apprehending flavour or beauty, appreciative, रसिकजनं तमुतामतिमुदितम् Git.G.vi.; 5. taking pleasure in, delighting in, अन्तर्धानव्यसनरसिका रात्रिकापालिकीयम् K.Pr.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिक|रसिकः
रसिक <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A man full of feeling or passion, a libertine; 2. a horse; 3. an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=607-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिका
रसिका <i>f.</i> 1. The juice of sugarcane, molasses; 2. tongue; 3. a woman’s girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
रसित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Having flavour or sentiment; 2. gilded, plated with gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिता
रसित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Having flavour or sentiment; 2. gilded, plated with gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
रसित <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Wine, liquor; 2. a cry, a thunder, a sound, a noise, गम्भीरमेघरसितव्यथिता कदाहम् Ghat.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोन|रसोनः
रसोन <i>m.</i> A kind of garlic. Cf. लसोन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्य|रस्यं
रस्य <i>a. (f. स्या)</i> Juicy, savoury, palatable, रस्याः स्निग्धाः स्थिरा हृद्या आहाराः सात्विकप्रियाः Bg.xvii.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्या
रस्य <i>a. (f. स्या)</i> Juicy, savoury, palatable, रस्याः स्निग्धाः स्थिरा हृद्या आहाराः सात्विकप्रियाः Bg.xvii.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह्
रह् <i>vt. 1P, 10U (pres. रहति, रहयति-ते)</i> To quit, to abandon, to desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहण|रहणं
