रहित|रहितं
रहित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Abandoned, deserted; 2. deprived of, without, सत्वोत्साहरहितः स्वाहारमप्युत्पादयितुमक्षमः Hit.i.; 3. lonely, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहिता
रहित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Abandoned, deserted; 2. deprived of, without, सत्वोत्साहरहितः स्वाहारमप्युत्पादयितुमक्षमः Hit.i.; 3. lonely, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहित|रहितं
रहित <i>(II) n.</i> Secrecy, privacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रा
रा <i>vt. 2P (pp. रात; pres. राति)</i> To give, to bestow, स रातु वो दुश्च्यवनो भावुकानां परंपराम् K.Pr.vii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राका
राका <i>f.</i> 1. The full-moon day or night, राकायामकलंकं चेदमृतांशोर्भवेद्वपुः K.Pr.x.; 2. a irl in whom menstruation has just commenced; 3. itch, scab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस <i>(I) a. (f. सी)</i> Demoniacal, of the nature of a demon, Bg.ix.12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसी
राक्षस <i>(I) a. (f. सी)</i> Demoniacal, of the nature of a demon, Bg.ix.12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस <i>(II) m.</i> 1. An evil spirit, a demon, an imp; 2. one of the eight forms of marriage; in it, the girl is forcibly carried away by capture, राक्षसो युद्धहरणात् Yaj.i.61; 3. name of the minister of Nandas, who figures as a prominent character in the Mudrārākshasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसी
राक्षसी <i>f.</i> A female demon, R.xii.61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षा
राक्षा <i>f.</i> incorrect form of लाक्षा q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राग|रागः
राग <i>m.</i> 1. Dying, colour, hue; 2. red colour, रागेण बालारुणकोमलेन चूतप्रवालोष्ठमलंचकार K.S.iii.30; 3. an affection, passion, feeling, चित्तं मुनेरपि हरन्ति निवृत्तरागम् Rt.ii.25; 4. musical harmony, a musical mode; (six primary Rāgas are enumerated, भैरवः कोशिकश्चैव हिंदोलो दीपकस्तथा । श्रीरागो मेघरागश्च रागाः षडिति कीर्तिताः; from these are derived innumerable modes mixed and simple), अहो रागपारवाहिणी गीतिः Sak.v., K.S.vii.91; 5. sympathy, pleasure, पुरा चक्षूरागस्तदनु मनसोऽनन्यपरता M.M.vi.; 6. anger, wrath; 7. regret, sorrow; 8. greediness, envy; 9. beauty, charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागचूर्ण|रागचूर्णः
राग-चूर्ण <i>m.</i> 1. the Khadira tree; 2. red lead; 3. a red powder thrown by people on one another at the Holī festival; 4. the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागद्रव्य
राग-द्रव्य <i>n.</i> a paint, a dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागबन्ध|रागबन्धः
राग-बन्ध <i>m.</i> the expression of Rāgas in due order, the manifestation of musical harmony, भावो भावं नुंदति विषयाद्रागबन्धः स एव Mal.ii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागयुज्
राग-युज् <i>m.</i> a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागसूत्र|रागसूत्रं
राग-सूत्र <i>n.</i> 1. any coloured thread, a silk-thread; 2. the string of a balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिन्
रागिन् <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> 1. Coloured, dyed; 2. red; 3. full of feeling, impassioned, affectionate; 4. devotedly attached to, delighted in, desirous of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिणी
रागिन् <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> 1. Coloured, dyed; 2. red; 3. full of feeling, impassioned, affectionate; 4. devotedly attached to, delighted in, desirous of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिन्
रागिन् <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A painter; 2. a lover, a libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिणी
रागिणी <i>f.</i> 1. A modification of a musical mode of which thirty or thirty-six are enumerated; 2. a wanton and intriguing woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रांकव|राङ्कव|राङ्कवं
रांकव <i>(I) a. (f. वी)</i> Belonging to the ranku deer or made from its hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=608-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

