राद्ध|राद्धं
राद्ध <i>a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Propitiated, conciliated; 2. accomplished, completed, performed; 3. cooked; 4. perfect in magical power, initiated; 5. successful, fortunate; 6. obtained, attained, (pp. of राध् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धा
राद्ध <i>a. (f. द्धा)</i> 1. Propitiated, conciliated; 2. accomplished, completed, performed; 3. cooked; 4. perfect in magical power, initiated; 5. successful, fortunate; 6. obtained, attained, (pp. of राध् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धांत|राद्धान्त|राद्धान्तः
राद्ध-अंत <i>m.</i> a demonstrated conclusion, a dogma, a doctrine, वैशेषिकराध्हांतो दुर्युक्तियोगान्नपेक्षितव्य इत्युक्तम् S.Bh.ii.2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धांतित|राद्धान्तित
राद्ध-अंतित <i>a.</i> demonstrated, proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धि|राद्धिः
राद्धि <i>f.</i> 1. Accomplishment, perfection; 2. success, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्
राध् <i>(I) vt. 5P (pp. राद्ध; pres. राध्नाति)</i> 1. To propitiate, to conciliate; 2. to effect, to complete, to accomplish; 3. to kill, to destroy, वानरा भूधरान् रेधुः Bt.xiv.19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्
राध् <i>(II) vt. or vi. 4P (pres. राध्यति)</i> 1. To be favourable or merciful; 2. to be accomplished, to be successful, to be ready; 3. to kill, to destroy.With अनु- or आ-, to propitiate, to adore.With अप-, (used with a loc. but sometimes with a gen.) 1. to offend, to err, to miss, अथवा यौवनमत्रापराध्यति न चारित्र्यम् Mrich.ix., Sis.ii.27; 2. to injure, न तु ग्रीष्मस्यैवं सुभगमपराद्धं युवतिषु Sak.iii.With वि-, to injure, to hurt, to offend, विराद्ध एवं भवता विराद्धा बहुधा च नः Sis.ii.41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्
राध् <i>Caus. (राधयति-ते)</i> With आ-, 1. to propitiate, to please, to conciliate, न तु प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्खजनचित्तमाराधयेत् Bhartr.ii.4; 2. to serve, to worship, आराध्यैनं शरवणभवं देवमुल्लंघिताध्वा Megh.i.45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध|राधः
राध <i>m.</i> The month Vaiśākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधा
राधा <i>f.</i> 1. Prosperity, success; 2. lightning; 3. name of the foster-mother of Karṇa; 4. name of the famous cowherdess loved by Kṛṣṇa, राधामाधवयोर्जयंति यमुनाकूले रहःकेलयः Git.G.i.; 5. the lunar asterism called Visākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=610-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधिका
राधिका <i>f.</i> See राधा (4).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधेय|राधेयः
राधेय <i>m.</i> An epithet of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम|रामं|रामः
राम <i>(I) a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Delighting, rejoicing; 2. beautiful, charming; 3. obscure, dark-coloured, black; 4. white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामा
राम <i>(I) a. (f. मा)</i> 1. Delighting, rejoicing; 2. beautiful, charming; 3. obscure, dark-coloured, black; 4. white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम|रामं|रामः
राम <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Name of several ancient heroes, especially of Paraśurāma, Balarāma and Rāmachandra, the son of Daśaratha; (See App. II.); 2. a species of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामानुज|रामानुजः
राम-अनुज <i>m.</i> name of the founder of a Vedāntic sect; he has written a Bhāshya on the Vedānta sūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामगिरि|रामगिरिः
राम-गिरि <i>m.</i> name of a mountain, स्निग्धच्छायातरुषु वसतिं रामगिर्याश्रमेषु Megh.i.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामचंद्र|रामचन्द्र|रामचन्द्रः
राम-चंद्र, -भद्र <i>m.</i> name of Rāma, son of Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामभद्र|रामभद्रः
राम-चंद्र, -भद्र <i>m.</i> name of Rāma, son of Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामनवमी
राम-नवमी <i>f.</i> the ninth day in the light half of Chaitra, the anniversary of the birth of Rāmachandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसेतु|रामसेतुः
राम-सेतु <i>m.</i> a bridge of sand, now a chain of islands, between the Indian peninsula and Ceylon (called ‘Adam’s bridge’ by the Europeans).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=611-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

