लज्जा-शून्य, -हीन <i>a.</i> shameless, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाहीन
लज्जा-शून्य, -हीन <i>a.</i> shameless, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जालु|लज्जालुः
लज्जालु <i>(I) a.</i> Modest, bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जालु|लज्जालुः
लज्जालु <i>(II) m.f.</i> Name of a sensitive plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जित|लज्जितः
लज्जित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Modest, bashful; 2. ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जिता
लज्जित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Modest, bashful; 2. ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लंज|लञ्ज|लंजः|लञ्जः
लंज <i>m.</i> 1. A foot; 2. a tail; 3. the end of a lower garment tucked behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लंजा
लंजा <i>f.</i> 1. A current; 2. sleep; 3. an adulteress; 4. an epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लंजिका|लञ्जिका
लंजिका <i>f.</i> A whore, a prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्
लट् <i>vt. or vi. 1P (pres. लटति)</i> 1. To be young, to be a child; 2. to talk like a child, to prattle; 3. to cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट|लटः
लट <i>m.</i> 1. A fool, a blockhead; 2. a fault; 3. a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटक|लटकः
लटक <i>m.</i> A rogue, a rascal, a contemptible person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=619-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटभ
लटभ <i>a. (f. भा)</i> This word is found no where in the existing dictionaries, but is used thrice or four times by Bilhaṇa in his Vikramānkadevacharita and once by Bhartṛhari. We are inclined to believe that it is the original Sanskrit word from which the Prākṛt लडह is derived. Of course, it is possible that the Sanskrit लटभ may have been consciously derived from the Prākṛt by the ordinary rules. It means ‘pretty, handsome, attractive,’ तस्याः पादनखश्रेणिः शोभते लटभभ्रुवः Vikr.Ch.viii.6, अतिक्रांतः कालो लटभललनाभोगसुलभः Bhartr.iii.32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=620-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटभा
लटभ <i>a. (f. भा)</i> This word is found no where in the existing dictionaries, but is used thrice or four times by Bilhaṇa in his Vikramānkadevacharita and once by Bhartṛhari. We are inclined to believe that it is the original Sanskrit word from which the Prākṛt लडह is derived. Of course, it is possible that the Sanskrit लटभ may have been consciously derived from the Prākṛt by the ordinary rules. It means ‘pretty, handsome, attractive,’ तस्याः पादनखश्रेणिः शोभते लटभभ्रुवः Vikr.Ch.viii.6, अतिक्रांतः कालो लटभललनाभोगसुलभः Bhartr.iii.32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=620-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

