लेलिह|लेलिहः
लेलिह <i>m.</i> A snake, a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=629-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिहान|लेलिहानः
लेलिहान <i>m.</i> 1. A snake, a serpent; 2. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=629-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश|लेशः
लेश <i>m.</i> 1. A particle, an atom, a bit, a small quantity, गीतांतरेषु श्रमवारिलेशैः K.S.iii.38, M.viii.51; 2. a particular measure of time equal to two kalās; 3. name of a figure of speech in rhetoric; in it, what is generally regarded as an advantage is represented as a disadvantage and vice versa (गुणस्यानिष्टसाधनतया दोषत्वेन दोषस्येष्टसाधनतया गुणत्वेन च वर्णनं लेशः R.G.). For instances, See Bh.V.i.88, 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=629-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

