वत्स <i>(I) m. (fem. ˚त्सा)</i> 1. A calf, the young of any animal, R.i.84, ii.1; 2. a son, a boy; 3. a term of endearment translatable by ‘my darling, my dear child,’ उत्तिष्ठ वत्सेत्यमृतायमानं वचो निशम्योत्थितमुत्थितः सन् R.ii.61; 4. a year; 5. name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=636-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्स|वत्सं|वत्सः
वत्स <i>(II) m. pl.</i> The people of the Vatsa country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=636-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्स|वत्सं|वत्सः
वत्स <i>(III) n.</i> The breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=636-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्साक्षी
वत्स-अक्षी <i>f.</i> a kind of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=636-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सादन|वत्सादनः
वत्स-अदन <i>m.</i> a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=636-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सेश|वत्सेशः
वत्स-ईश, -राज <i>m.</i> a king of the Vatsas, लोके हारि च वत्सराजचरितं नाट्ये च दक्षा वयम् Rat.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=636-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सराज|वत्सराजः
