वप्तृ
वप्तृ <i>m.</i> 1. A sower, a husbandman, न शालेः स्तंबकरिता वप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mud.i.; 2. a father, a progenitor; 3. a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=639-35" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्र|वप्रं|वप्रः
वप्र <i>(I) m.n.</i> 1. A rampart, a mud-wall; 2. the slope of a hill, वप्रक्रीडापरिणतगजप्रेक्षणीयं ददर्श Megh.i.2, R.v.44; 3. a summit, a peak, वप्रेण पर्यंतचरोडुचक्रः Sis.iii.37; 4. the foundation of a building; 5. the gate of a fortified city; 6. the bank of a river, वप्रांतःस्खलितविवर्तनं Kir.vii.11, vi.4; 7. a ditch; 8. a field; 9. the butting of an elephant or bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=639-36" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

