वम्
वम् <i>vt. 1P (pp. वांत; pres. वमति; caus. वमयति or वामयति)</i> 1. To vomit, to eject from the mouth, Bt.xiv.30, xv.62; 2. to put into, to drop, अविदितगुणापि सत्कविभणितिः कर्णेषु वमति मधुधाराम् Vas.D.; 3. to emit, to send forth, to give out, Megh.i.20.With उद्-, 1. to give out, to emit, to disgorge, उद्ववामेंद्रसिक्ता भूर्बिलमग्नाविवोरगौ R.xii.5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=640-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम|वमः
वम <i>m.</i> Ejecting, vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=640-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमथु|वमथुः
वमथु <i>m.</i> 1. Ejecting, vomiting; 2. water thrown by an elephant from his trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=640-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

