विज् <i>vi. 6Ā, 7P (pp. विग्न; pres. विजते, विनक्ति)</i> 1. To shake, to tremble; 2. to tremble with fear; 3. to be afraid; 4. to be distressed.With उद्-, 1. to be afraid of, to fear, (with an abl. or gen.), यस्मानोद्विकते लोको लोकान्नेद्विजते च यः Bg.xii.15; 2. to be disgusted, (with an abl.), e.g. उद्विनक्ति तु संसारादसारात् (मनः); 3. to be distressed, to be sorry, न प्रहृष्येत्प्रियं प्राफ्य नोद्विजेत्प्राप्य चाप्रियम् Bg.v.19; 4. to afflict, to frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=661-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

