वितान <i>(I) a. (f. ना)</i> 1. Empty, vacant; 2. dull, stupid; 3. wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=663-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितान|वितानं|वितानः
वितान <i>(II) m.n.</i> 1. Expansion, Sis.xi.28; 2. a canopy, an awning, बृहत्तुलैरप्यतुलैर्वितानमालापिनद्धैरपि चावितानैः Sis.iii.50; 3. a cushion; 4. a sacrifice, an oblation, सोमपायिनि भविष्यते मया वांच्छितोत्तमवितानयाजिना Sis.xiv.10, Ve.iii.; 5. a sacrificial hearth; 6. season, opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=663-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

