वेवी
वेवी <i>vt. or vi. 2Ā (pres. वेवीते)</i> 1. To go, to move; 2. to pervade; 3. to throw; 4. to eat; 5. to wish, to desire; 6. to be pregnant. (This root is not used in classics.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=692-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश|वेशः
वेश <i>m.</i> 1. Dress, apparel, गतवति कृतवेशे केशवे कुंजशय्याम् Git.G.xi.; 2. entrance, ingress; 3. a house, a dwelling; 4. a house of prostitutes, तरुगणनसहायश्चिंत्यतां वेशवासः Mrich.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=692-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशदान|वेशदानः
