व्यवहारदर्शन|व्यवहारदर्शनं
व्यवहार-दर्शन <i>n.</i> judicial investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=698-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारपद|व्यवहारपदं
व्यवहार-पद <i>n.</i> an occasion of litigation, a head of legal procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=698-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारपाद|व्यवहारपादः
व्यवहार-पाद <i>m.</i> the fourth stage in the conduct of a law-suit, that which concerns the decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=698-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारमातृका
व्यवहार-मातृका <i>f.</i> any subject relating to the administration of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=698-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारविधि|व्यवहारविधिः
व्यवहार-विधि <i>m.</i> rule of law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=698-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारविषय|व्यवहारविषयः
व्यवहार-विषय <i>m.</i> a head of legal procedure, a matter which can be made a subject of legal proceedings; (these are eighteen, for an enumeration of which, See M.viii.4-7).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=698-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारक|व्यवहारकः
व्यवहारक <i>m.</i> A dealer, a trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=699-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिक|व्यवहारिकः
व्यवहारिक <i>a. (f. का or की)</i> 1. Relating to business; 2. relating to legal process; 3. customary, usual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=699-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

