व्रातीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Hired for labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातीना
व्रातीन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Hired for labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्य|व्रात्यः
व्रात्य <i>m.</i> 1. A man of any of the first three castes over whom the purificatory ceremonies are not performed, भव्त्या हि व्रात्याधमपतितपाषंडपरिषत्परित्राणस्नेहः श्लथयितुमशक्यः खलि यदा G.L.37; 2. a low person in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यब्रुव|व्रात्यब्रुवः
व्रात्य-ब्रुव <i>m.</i> one who calls himself a Vrātya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यस्तोम|व्रात्यस्तोमः
व्रात्य-स्तोम <i>m.</i> name of a particular sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री <i>(I) vt. 4Ā (pp. व्रीण; pres. व्रीयते)</i> To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री <i>(II) vt. 9P (pres. व्रिणाति, व्रीणाति)</i> To choose, to select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड्
व्रीड् <i>vt. or vi. 4P (pres. व्रीडयति)</i> 1. To throw, to cast; 2. to feel shame, to be ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड|व्रीडः
व्रीड <i>m.</i> 1. Shame, व्रीडामावहति मे स संप्रति व्यस्तवृत्तिरुदयोन्मुखे त्वयि R.xi.78; 2. modesty, bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडा
व्रीडा <i>f.</i> 1. Shame, व्रीडामावहति मे स संप्रति व्यस्तवृत्तिरुदयोन्मुखे त्वयि R.xi.78; 2. modesty, bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडित
व्रीडित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Ashamed, abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडिता
व्रीडित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Ashamed, abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस्
व्रीस् <i>vt. 1P, 10U (pres. व्रीसति, व्रीसयति-ते)</i> The same as व्रस् q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहि|व्रीहिः
व्रीहि <i>m.</i> 1. Rice; 2. a grain of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीह्यगार|व्रीह्यगारं
व्रीहि-अगार <i>m.</i> a granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिराजिक
व्रीहि-राजिक <i>m.</i> a kind of grain (कंगू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड्
व्रुड् <i>vt. or vi. 6P (pres. व्रुडति)</i> 1. To cover; 2. to be gathered, to be piled up; 3. to sink, to plunge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस्
व्रूस् <i>vt. 1P, 10U (pres. व्रूसति, व्रूसयति-ते)</i> To injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय <i>n.</i> A field fit for growing rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली <i>vt. 9P (pres. व्लिनाति, व्लीनाति; caus. व्लेपयति-ते)</i> 1. To go, to move; 2. to hold, to maintain; 3. to choose, to select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श <i>(I) m.</i> 1. A cutter, a destroyer, Kir.xv.45; 2. a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श <i>(II) n.</i> Happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु <i>a.</i> Happy, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंव <i>m.</i> 1. The thunderbolt of Indra; 2. the iron head of a pestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्
शंस् <i>vt. 1U (pp. शस्त; pres. शंसति; pass. शस्यते)</i> 1. To relate, to tell, to report, to announce, to communicate to, (with dat. or gen. of the person communicated to), न मे ह्रिया शंसति किंचिदीप्सितं स्पृहावती वस्तुषु केषु मागधी R.iii.5, xi.84, M.iii.109, vii.116, K.S.v.51, iii.60; 2. to indicate, to suggest, पीडाभाजः कुसुमचिताः साशंसं शंसंत्यस्मिन् सुरतविशेषं शय्याः Kir.v.23; 3. to praise, to approve, संन्यासं कर्मणां कृष्ण पुनर्योगं च शंससि Bg.v.1; 4. to hurt, to injure.With अभि-, to curse, M.viii.116.With आ-, (in the Atm., शंसतेरपेक्षायामात्मनेपदमिष्यते Mall. on R.xiv.50) 1. to hope, to expect, जितेंद्रिये शूलिनि पुष्पचापः स्वकार्यसिद्धिं पुनराशशंसे K.S.iii.57, आशंसंते समितिषु सुराः सक्तवैरा हि दैत्यैरस्याधिज्ये धनुषिविजयं पौरुहूते च वज्रे Sak.ii.; 2. to desire, to wish, राज्ञः शिवं सावरजस्य भूयादित्याशशंसे करणैरबाह्यैः R.xiv.50, संग्रामं चाशशंसिरे Bt.xiv.70; 3. (Par.) to tell, to relate, to speak of, आशंसता बाणगतिं वृषांके कार्यं त्वया नः प्रतिपन्नकल्पम् K.S.iii.14.With प्र-, to praise, to extol, to approve, to speak highly of, प्राशंसीत्तं निशाचरः Bt.xii.65, हरिणा युवतिः प्रशशंसे Git.G.i., M.x.33, vii.64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसन|शंसनं
शंसन <i>n.</i> 1. the act of reciting or repeating; 2. praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसा
शंसा <i>f.</i> 1. Repeating, narrating; 2. wish, desire; 3. praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसित|शंसितः
शंसित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Said, told; 2. praised, celebrated; 3. wished, desired; 4. falsely accused; 5. ascertained, established, (pp. of शंस् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिता
शंसित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Said, told; 2. praised, celebrated; 3. wished, desired; 4. falsely accused; 5. ascertained, established, (pp. of शंस् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिन्
शंसिन् <i>a. (f. नी) (often at the end of a compound)</i> 1. Saying, announcing, indicating, प्रार्थनासिद्धिशंसिनः R.i.42, iii.14, Sis.ix.77; 2. praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिनी
शंसिन् <i>a. (f. नी) (often at the end of a compound)</i> 1. Saying, announcing, indicating, प्रार्थनासिद्धिशंसिनः R.i.42, iii.14, Sis.ix.77; 2. praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् <i>(I) vi. 5P (pp. शक्त; pres. शक्नोति; desid. शिक्षति)</i> 1. To be able, to be able to effect, to be competent for, (generally with an inf.), अंतःसारं घन तुलयितुं नानिलः शक्ष्यति त्वाम् Megh.i.20, Bt.iii.6; 2. to bear, to endure; 3. to be powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् <i>(II) vt. 4U (pp. शक्त; pres. शक्यति-ते)</i> 1. To be able, to be competent for; 2. to endure, to bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=703-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक <i>(I) m. pl.</i> The name of a country and its people, M.x.44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Name of a king, (commonly applied to Śālivāhana); (the whole question about the word and its real import is yet unsettled); 2. an epoch, an era, (especially that of Śālivāhana which began 78 years after Christ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकांतक|शकान्तक|शकान्तकः
शक-अंतक, -अरि <i>m.</i> an epithet of king Vikramāditya who is supposed to have subdued the Śakas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकारि|शकारिः
शक-अंतक, -अरि <i>m.</i> an epithet of king Vikramāditya who is supposed to have subdued the Śakas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकाब्द|शकाब्दः
शक-अब्द <i>m.</i> a year of the Śaka era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शककर्तृ
शक-कर्तृ <i>m.</i> the founder of an era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकट|शकटं|शकटः
शकट <i>(I) m.n.</i> A carriage, a waggon, M.v.117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकट|शकटं|शकटः
शकट <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A form of military array resembling a wedge, M.vii.187; 2. a measure of capacity equal to two thousand Paṇas; 3. a demon slain by Kṛṣṇa in his infancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटारि|शकटारिः
शकट-अरि, -हन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटहन्
शकट-अरि, -हन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाह्वा
शकट-आह्वा <i>f.</i> the asterism Rohiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका <i>f.</i> 1. A small cart (as in मृच्छकटिका); 2. a toy-cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकन्
शकन् <i>n.</i> Animal-dung.(This word has no forms for the first five cases; according to some, this is not a separate word but a substitute for शकृत्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल|शकलं|शकलः
शकल <i>(I) m.n.</i> A part, a portion, a fragment, a piece, अथांधकारं गिरिगह्वराणां दंष्ट्रामयूखैः शकलानि कुर्वन् R.ii.46, v.73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल|शकलं|शकलः
शकल <i>(II) m.</i> 1. Bark; 2. the scales of a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलित
शकलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Reduced to fragments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिता
शकलित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> Reduced to fragments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन् <i>m.</i> A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकार|शकारः
शकार <i>m.</i> The brother of a king’s concubine, the brother-in-law of a king by a wife not regularly married; (the S.D. thus describes him- मदमूर्खताभिमानी दुष्कुलतैश्वर्यसंयुक्तः । सोऽयमनूढाभ्राता राज्ञः श्यालः शकार उद्दिष्टः). In the Mricchakaṭikā, where a principal part is assigned to this character, he is represented as a foolish, blundering, frivolous, proud, and cruel man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन|शकुनं|शकुनः
शकुन <i>(I) n.</i> A prognostic or omen foreboding good or evil, Sis.ix.83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन|शकुनं|शकुनः
शकुन <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A bird in general, गोघ्रातं शकुनोच्छिष्टम् Yaj.i.168; 2. a vulture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञ
शकुन-ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञान
शकुन-ज्ञान <i>n.</i> knowledge of omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनशास्त्र
शकुन-शास्त्र <i>n.</i> science of omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनि|शकुनिः
