शक्त|शक्तः
शक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Able, capable, competent, तस्योपकारे शक्तस्त्वं किं जीवन् किमुतान्यथा Ve.iii.; 2. strong, powerful; 3. opulent, rich, M.xi.9; 4. significant, expressive (as a word); 5. speaking agreeably; 6. clever, diligent, (pp. of शक् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ता
शक्त <i>a. (f. क्ता)</i> 1. Able, capable, competent, तस्योपकारे शक्तस्त्वं किं जीवन् किमुतान्यथा Ve.iii.; 2. strong, powerful; 3. opulent, rich, M.xi.9; 4. significant, expressive (as a word); 5. speaking agreeably; 6. clever, diligent, (pp. of शक् q.v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ति|शक्तिः
शक्ति <i>f.</i> 1. Ability, power, strength, energy, prowess, ज्ञाने मौनं क्षमा शक्तौ R.ii.22, ii.34, xi.42; 2. regal power (in politics); [it is of three kinds, viz., (1) प्रभावशक्ति or प्रभुशक्ति (the eminent position of the king); (2) मंत्रशक्ति (the power of good counsel); (3) उत्साहशक्ति (energy)], त्रिसाधना शक्तिरिवार्थमक्षयम् R.iii.13, Sis.ii.26; 3. a female deity; (these are variously enumerated); 4. a kind of missile, ततो बिभेद पौलस्त्यः शक्त्या वक्षसि लक्ष्मणम् R.xii.77; 5. the expressive power of a word, (op. to लक्षणा and व्यंजना) (in rhetoric), the relation of a word to the thing designated by it (in Nyāya); 6. the poetic faculty, poetic genius, शक्तिर्निपुणता लोकशास्त्रकाव्याद्यवेक्षणात् K.Pr.i.; 7. the inherent power of a cause to produce its effects (in Nyāya phil.); 8. the female organ worshipped by the Śāktas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=704-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

