शंखिनी
शंखिनी <i>f.</i> 1. A woman of one of the four classes into which they are divided by writers on erotical science; (शंखिनी is thus described- दीर्घा सुदीर्घनयना वरसुंदरी या कामोपभोगरसिका गुणशीलयुक्ता । रेखात्रयेण च विभूषितकंठदेशा संभोगकेलिरसिका किल शंखिनी सा); See चित्रिणी, पद्मिनी, हस्तिनी; 2. a particular female spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शच्
शच् <i>vt. 1Ā (pres. शंचते in the first sense; शचते in the second)</i> 1. To go, to move; 2. to speak, to say, to tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शची
शची(चि) <i>f.</i> Name of the wife of Indra, R.iii.13, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचि|शचिः
शची(चि) <i>f.</i> Name of the wife of Indra, R.iii.13, 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचीपति|शचीपतिः
