शठ्
शठ् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1P (pres. शठति)</i> 1. To deceive, to defraud; 2. to hurt, to kill; 3. to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
शठ् <i>(II) vt. 10P pres. शठयति)</i> To deceive, to defraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ <i>(I) a. (f. ठा)</i> Dishonest, perfidious, crafty, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठा
शठ <i>(I) a. (f. ठा)</i> Dishonest, perfidious, crafty, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A rogue, a knave, Bg.xviii.28; 2. a false lover (thus described in the S.D.- एकत्र बद्धभावो यः … दर्शितबहिरनुरागो विप्रियमन्यत्र गूढमाचरति), ध्रुवमस्मि शठः शुचिस्मिते विदितः कैतववत्सलस्त्व R.viii.49; 3. a fool, a blockhead; 4. a mediator, an umpire; 5. the Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ <i>(III) n.</i> 1. Saffron; 2. iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=706-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण|शणं|शणः
