शास्
शास् <i>vt. 2P (pp. शिष्ट; pres. शास्ति; caus. शासयति-ते) (This is one of those roots which take two accusatives, e.g. माणवकं धर्मं शास्ति.)</i> 1. To teach, to instruct, to train, शिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नम् Bg.ii.7, Bt.vi.10; 2. to inform, to communicate, to report, तस्मिन्नायोधनं वृत्तं लक्ष्मणायाशिन्महत् Bt.vi.27; 3. to rule, to govern, to command, to direct, अनन्यशासमामुर्वीं शशासैकपुरीमिव R.i.30, x.1; 4. to punish, to correct, M.iv.175; 5. to advise, K.S.vi.24.With अनु-, 1. to rule, to govern; 2. to advise, to teach, K.S.v.5; 3. to punish, to chastise.With आ-, 1. to order, to command, Bt.vi.4; 2. (Atm.) to confer blessings on, ऋक्छंदसा आशास्ते Sak.iv.; 3. (Atm.) to desire, to see, श्रियमाशासते लोलां तां हस्तेकृत्य मा श्वसीः Bt.v.16; 4. to praise.With प्र-, 1. to rule, to govern, R.vi.76; 2. to command; 3. to teach, to instruct, Bt.xix.19; 4. to chastise; 5. (Atm.) to pray for, to solicit, इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो नमोवाकं प्रशास्महे Ut.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=716-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासन|शासनं
शासन <i>n.</i> 1. Governing, ruling, government, R.i.30; 2. instructing, instruction; 3. a precept; 4. an order, a decree, a command, कुसुमशरासनशासनवंदिनि पिकनिकरे भज भावम् Git.G.xi., R.iii.69; 5. a charter, a royal grant, Yaj.ii.240; 6. a written agreement, a deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=716-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनपत्र
शासन-पत्र <i>n.</i> 1. a plate on which a grant is inscribed; 2. a paper on which an older is written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=716-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनहर|शासनहरः
शासन-हर <i>m.</i> a royal measenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=716-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनहारिन्
शासन-हारिन् <i>m.</i> a messenger, an envoy, R.iii.68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=716-28" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासित|शासितः
शासित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Governed, ruled; 2. punished, chastised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासिता
शासित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Governed, ruled; 2. punished, chastised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ <i>m.</i> 1. A king, a ruler; 2. a father; 3. a teacher, an instructor; 4. a Buddha, a deified teacher of the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्र|शास्त्रं
शास्त्र <i>n.</i> 1. A rule, a precept, an institute; 2. a science, (e.g. काव्यशास्त्र, वेदांतशास्त्र &c.), शास्त्रेष्वकुंठिता बुद्धिः R.i.9; 3. a scientific treatise, तंत्रैः पंचभिरेतच्चकार सुमनोहरं शास्त्रम् Panch.i., M.i.58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानतिक्रम
शास्त्र-अनतिक्रम <i>m.</i> non-violation of sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुष्ठान
शास्त्र-अनुष्ठान <i>n.</i> observance of the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुसार|शास्त्रानुसारः
शास्त्र-अनुसार <i>m.</i> conformity to sacred ordinances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राभिज्ञ
शास्त्र-अभिज्ञ <i>a.</i> learned in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रार्थ|शास्त्रार्थः
शास्त्र-अर्थ <i>m.</i> a scriptural statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रोक्त
शास्त्र-उक्त <i>a.</i> enjoined or allowed by the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकृत्
शास्त्र-कृत् <i>m.</i> the author of a Śāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकोविद
शास्त्र-कोविद <i>a.</i> learned in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रगंड|शास्त्रगण्ड|शास्त्रगण्डः
शास्त्र-गंड <i>m.</i> a superficial scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रचक्षुस्
शास्त्र-चक्षुस् <i>n.</i> grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञान
शास्त्र-ज्ञान <i>n.</i> acquaintance with sacred works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतत्व
शास्त्र-तत्व <i>n.</i> the truth of the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रदृष्ट
शास्त्र-दृष्ट <i>a.</i> stated in sacred works, M.viii.3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रयोनि|शास्त्रयोनिः
शास्त्र-योनि <i>m.</i> the source of the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविद्
शास्त्र-विद् <i>a.</i> conversant with the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविधि|शास्त्रविधिः
शास्त्र-विधि <i>m.</i> a ceremonial injunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविप्रतिषेध|शास्त्रविप्रतिषेधः
शास्त्र-विप्रतिषेध, -विरोध <i>m.</i> 1. an act contrary to the Śāstras; 2. mutual contradiction of sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविरोध|शास्त्रविरोधः
शास्त्र-विप्रतिषेध, -विरोध <i>m.</i> 1. an act contrary to the Śāstras; 2. mutual contradiction of sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रव्युत्पत्ति|शास्त्रव्युत्पत्तिः
शास्त्र-व्युत्पत्ति <i>f.</i> proficiency in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रशिल्पिन्
शास्त्र-शिल्पिन् <i>m.</i> the country of Kashmere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रसिद्ध
शास्त्र-सिद्ध <i>a.</i> established by the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिन्
शास्त्रिन् <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> Skilled in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिणी
शास्त्रिन् <i>(I) a. (f. णी)</i> Skilled in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिन्
शास्त्रिन् <i>(II) m.</i> One who has studied the Śāstras a learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रीय
शास्त्रीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Scriptural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रीया
शास्त्रीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Scriptural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्य|शास्यः
शास्य <i>a. (f. स्या)</i> 1. To be governed; 2. to be advised; 3. deserving punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्या
शास्य <i>a. (f. स्या)</i> 1. To be governed; 2. to be advised; 3. deserving punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि <i>vt. or vi. 5U (pres. शिनोति, शिनुते)</i> 1. To whet, to sharpen; 2. to attenuate; 3. to excite; 4. to be attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि <i>m.</i> 1. Auspiciousnes, good fortune; 2. calm, composure; 3. an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशपा
शिंशपा <i>f.</i> 1. Name of a tree called शिशु; 2. the Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्कु|शिक्कुः
शिक्कु <i>a.</i> Idle, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्थ|शिक्थं
शिक्थ <i>n.</i> Bees’-wax. Cf. सिक्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्य|शिक्यं
शिक्य <i>n.</i> The same as सिक्थ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्या
शिक्या <i>f.</i> The same as सिक्थ q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्
शिक्ष् <i>vt. 1Ā (pres. शिक्षते)</i> To learn, to acquire knowledge, स्वं स्वं चरित्रं शिक्षेरन् M.ii.20, R.iii.31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षक|शिक्षकः
शिक्षक <i>a. (f. क्षका or क्षिका)</i> 1. A learner; 2. a teacher, an instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षका
शिक्षक <i>a. (f. क्षका or क्षिका)</i> 1. A learner; 2. a teacher, an instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षिका
शिक्षक <i>a. (f. क्षका or क्षिका)</i> 1. A learner; 2. a teacher, an instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षण|शिक्षणं
शिक्षण <i>n.</i> 1. Learning, acquiring knowledge; 2. teaching, instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा <i>f.</i> 1. Study, acquisition of knowledge, R.ix.63; 2. desire of being able to effect anything, Kir.xv.37; 3. teaching, training, instruction, अभूच्च नम्रः प्रणिपातशिक्षया R.iii.25; 4. modesty, humility; 5. a science which teaches proper pronunciation, especially of the Veda (one of the six Vedāṅgas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाकर|शिक्षाकरः
शिक्षा-कर <i>m.</i> 1. a teacher, an instructor; 2. an epithet of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षानर|शिक्षानरः
शिक्षा-नर <i>m.</i> an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाशक्ति|शिक्षाशक्तिः
शिक्षा-शक्ति <i>f.</i> dexterity, skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Learned, studied; 2. trained, disciplined; 3. taught, instructed; 4. skilful, conversant; 5. modest, diffident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षिता
शिक्षित <i>a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Learned, studied; 2. trained, disciplined; 3. taught, instructed; 4. skilful, conversant; 5. modest, diffident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षिताक्षर|शिक्षिताक्षरः
शिक्षित-अक्षर <i>m.</i> a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षितायुध
शिक्षित-आयुध <i>a.</i> skilled in the use of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्यमाण
शिक्ष्यमाण <i>m.</i> A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिख्
शिख् <i>vt. 1P (pres. शिंखति)</i> To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=717-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

