शील|शीलः
शील <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Character, disposition, tendency, inclination, पात्रे निधायार्घ्यमनर्घशीलः R.v.2, मधुरिपुरहमिति भावनशीला Git.G.vi.; (hence in compounds, शील means ‘habituated to, prone to, apt,’ e.g. दुःखशील, दयाशील); 2. conduct, behaviour; 3. good conduct, amiability, प्राप्तेयं शीलवंचना Mrich.i.; 4. virtue, morality, right conduct, कोऽपवादः स्तुतिपदे यदशीलेषु चंचलाः । साधुवृत्तानपि क्षुद्रा विक्षिपंत्येव संपदः Kir.xi.25, Bhartr.ii.39; 5. beauty, form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=722-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

