श्रम्
श्रम् <i>vi. 4P (pp. श्रांत; pres. श्राम्यति)</i> 1. To make effort, to exert oneself; 2. to perform acts of penance; 3. to be wearied, to be fatigued, प्रदुद्रवतुरन्योन्यं वीरौ शशमतुर्न च Bt.xiv.110; 4. to be distressed, यो बृंदानि त्वरयति पथि श्राम्यतां प्रोषितानाम् Megh.ii.36.With परि-, to be fatigued.With वि-, 1. to take rest, to repose; 2. to cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=731-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्
श्रम् <i>Caus. (श्रामयति-ते)</i> With वि-, 1. to take rest, to repose; 2. to cause to alight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=731-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम|श्रमः
श्रम <i>m.</i> 1. Labour, exertion, toil, अलं महीपाल तव श्रमेण R.ii.34, वंध्यश्रमास्ते सरयूं विगाह्य R.xvi.75, विरम विरम व्यर्थ एष श्रमस्ते Bhartr.iii.66; 2. penance, mortification of the body; 3. military exercise; 4. hard study; 5. weariness, fatigue, विनीताध्वश्रमास्तस्य सिंधुतीरविचेष्टनैः R.iv.67, Megh.i.17, 52; 6. distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=731-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

