श्री
श्री <i>(I) vt. 9U (pres. श्रीणाति, श्रीणीते)</i> To cook, to dress, to boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=732-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री <i>(II) vt. 1U, 10U (pres. श्रयति-ते, श्राययति-ते)</i> To please, to propitiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=732-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री <i>f.</i> 1. Wealth, prosperity, riches, plenty, R.iii.46, Megh.i.30; 2. royalty, majesty, royal glory; 3. the insignia of royalty, K.S.vii.46; 4. beauty, grace, loveliness, splendour, Megh.i.47, K.S.vii.32, R.iii.8, Sis.iv.68, i.75; 5. appearance, K.S.ii.2; 6. Lakṣmī, the goddess of wealth, श्रियः पतिः श्रीमति शासितुंजगत् Sis.i.1, ii.118; 7. intellect, understanding; 8. any virtue or excellence; 9. the three objects of life collectively (viz., धर्म, अर्थ and काम); 10. superhuman power; 11. a lotus; 12. cloves; 13. the sarala tree; 14. the Bilva tree; (this word will be found used in the concluding stanza of each canto of the Śiśupālavadha; it is used as an honorific prefix to the names of deities, e.g. श्रीराम, श्रीकृष्ण, as a prefix to the names or eminent persons, e.g. श्रीवाल्मीकि and celebrated works, e.g. श्रीरामायण and is found used at the beginning of manuscripts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=732-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

