षट्कर्मन्|षट्कर्म्मन्
षट्कर्मन् <i>n.</i> 1. the six duties enjoined to a Brāhmaṇa, (they are- अध्यापनमध्ययनं यजनं याजनं तथा । दानं प्रतिग्रहश्चैव षट् कर्नाण्यग्रजन्मनः M.x.75); 2. the six acts allowable to a Brāhmaṇa for livelihood; 3. the six acts belonging to the practice of Yoga (viz., धौति, वस्ती, नेती, त्राटक, नौलिक and कपालभाती); 4. the six acts that may be performed by magic; (they are- शांति, वश्य, स्तंभन, द्वेष, उच्चाटन and मारण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=737-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कोण|षट्कोणं
षट्कोण <i>n.</i> 1. a hexagon; 2. the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=737-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गव|षड्गवं
षड्गव <i>n.</i> a yoke of six oxen, (the word is sometimes used after the names of other animals to denote ‘a group of six,’ e.g. अश्वषड्गव ‘six horses’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=737-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गुण
षड्गुण <i>(I) a.</i> 1. six-fold; 2. having six qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=737-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गुण
षड्गुण <i>(II) n.</i> 1. an assemblage of six qualities; 2. the six acts to be practised by a king in foreign politics. (See under गुण.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=737-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

