सात्वत <i>(I) m.</i> 1. An epithet of Viṣṇu; 2. of Balarāma; 3. a son of an outcast Vaiśya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत|सात्वतः
सात्वत <i>(II) m. pl.</i> The name of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वती
सात्वती <i>f.</i> 1. One of the four dramatic styles; 2. name of the mother of Śiśupāla, न दूये सात्वतीसूनुर्यन्मह्यमपराध्यति Sis.ii.11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद|सादः
साद <i>m.</i> 1. Perishing, decay, Nal.ii.26, iii.24; 2. leanness, thinness, emaciation, शरीरदादादसमग्रभूषणा R.iii.2; 3. weariness, exhaustion, उदितोरुसादमतिवेपथुमत् Sis.v.77; 4. cessation, stoppage, गतिविभ्रमसादनीरवा R.viii.56; 5. pain; 6. purity, clearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादन|सादनं
सादन <i>n.</i> 1. Dispelling; 2. destroying; 3. wearing; 4. exhaustion; 5. a house, a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन् <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिनी
सादिन् <i>(I) a. (f. नी)</i> Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन् <i>(II) m.</i> One who rides on a horse or elephant, or is mounted in a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादृश्य|सादृश्यं
सादृश्य <i>n.</i> 1. Resemblance, similarity, जनता प्रेक्ष्य सादृश्यम् नाक्षिकंपं व्यतिष्ठत R.xv.67, i.40; 2. a likeness, an image, a portrait, मत्सादृश्यं विरहतनु वा भावगम्यं लिखंती Megh.ii.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क|साद्यस्कः
साद्यस्क <i>a. (f. स्की)</i> Quick, instantaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्की
साद्यस्क <i>a. (f. स्की)</i> Quick, instantaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् <i>(I) vt. 5P (pres. साध्नोति)</i> 1. To finish, to accomplish; 2. to conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् <i>(II) vi. 4P (pres. साध्यति)</i> To be completed or accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् <i>(III) vi. 10P (pres. साधयति)</i> To go, to depart, साधयाम्यहमविघ्नमस्तु ते R.xi.91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् <i>Caus. (साधयति-ते)</i> 1. to accomplish, to effect, to perform; 2. to secure, to settle, R.v.25, xvii.38; 3. to substantiate, to prove; 4. to enforce settlement, to recover a debt; 5. to obtain, K.S.ii.33; 6. to subdue, to overcome, to make peace with, e.g. न हि साम्ना न दानेन न भेदेन च पांडवाः । शक्याः साधयितुम्; 7. to destroy, to kill,सुग्रीवांतिकमासेदुः साधयिष्याम इत्यारिम् Bt.vii.31; 8. to learn, to understand, तपसश्चरणैश्चोग्रैः साधयंतीह तत्पदम् M.vi.75; 9. to prepare oneself for heaven; 10. to set out, to depart.With प्र-, 1. to further; 2. to accomplish; 3. to dress; 4. to acquire; 5. to subdue.With सम्-, 1. to be successful; 2. to endow with; 3. to destroy; 4. to distinguish; 5. to obtain; 6. to cause to be paid, यदि संसाधयेत्तत्तु दर्पाल्लोभेन वा पुनः M.viii.213; 7. to regain, M.viii.50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधक|साधकः
साधक <i>a. (f. धका or धिका)</i> 1. Effecting, accomplishing, fulfilling; 2. effecting by magic, magical; 3. efficient, skilful, adept; 4. aiding, helping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधका
साधक <i>a. (f. धका or धिका)</i> 1. Effecting, accomplishing, fulfilling; 2. effecting by magic, magical; 3. efficient, skilful, adept; 4. aiding, helping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=771-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

