सिंह|सिंहः
सिंह <i>m.</i> 1. A lion; (it is thus derived- भवेद्वर्णागमाद्धंसः सिंहो वर्णविपर्ययात्), ददर्श राजा जननीमिव स्वां गामग्रतः प्रस्राविणीं न सिंहम् R.ii.61; 2. the sign Leo of the zodiac.(As the last member of a compound, it means ‘preeminent.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=778-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहावलोकनन्याय
सिंह-अवलोकनन्याय <i>m.</i> the maxim of the lion’s glance. It is used to denote the connection of a thing with the preceding and the following, just as the lion constantly pauses and casts his glance backward and forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=778-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

