सुख <i>(I) a. (f. खा)</i> 1. Happy, joyful, delighted; 2. agreeable, sweet, comfortable, दिशः प्रसेदुर्मरुतो ववुः सुखाः R.iii.14; 3. virtuous, pious; 4. easy, practicable; 5. meet, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=783-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख|सुखं
सुख <i>(II) n.</i> 1. Happiness, pleasure, delight, joy, comfort, सुखं हि दुःखान्यनुभूय शोभते Mrich.i.; 2. prosperity, सुखे वा दुःखे वा क्व नु खलु तदैक्यं हृदययोः Ut.vi.; 3. ease, alleviation; 4. easiness; 5. heaven, paradise; 6. water.(सुखा f. ‘the city of Varuṇa.’)(सुखम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of- (1) happily, joyfully, well, e.g. सुखमास्तं भवान् ‘may your honour be well’; (2) willingly, rather; (3) comfortably, सुखं शेते मातस्तव खलु कृपातः पुनरयं जगन्नाथः G.L.30; (4) easily, अज्ञः सुखमाराध्यः सुखतरमाराध्यते विषेषज्ञः Bhartr.ii.3, Bg.v.3.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=783-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

