सेना
सेन <i>a. (f. ना)</i> Having a lord, possessing a master or leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेना
सेना <i>f.</i> 1. Army, स सेनां महतीं कर्षन् पूर्वसागरगामिनीम् R.iv.32; 2. the wife of Kārtikeya, the god of war (?). (See देवसेना and the reference given there).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाग्र
सेना-अग्र <i>n.</i> the front of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाग्रग
सेना-अग्र˚ग <i>m.</i> the leader of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनांग|सेनाङ्ग|सेनाङ्गं
सेना-अंग <i>n.</i> a component part of an army; (they are four- हस्त्यश्वरथपादातं सेनांगं स्याच्चतुष्टयम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाचर|सेनाचरः
सेना-चर <i>m.</i> 1. a soldier; 2. a sutler, a camp-follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानिवेश|सेनानिवेशः
सेना-निवेश <i>m.</i> the camp of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानी
सेना-नी <i>m.</i> 1. a leader of an army, a commander, a general, सेनानीनामहं स्कंदः Bg.x.24; 2. an epithet of Kārtikeya, अथैनमद्रेस्तनया शुशोच सेनान्यमालीढमिवासुरास्त्रैः R.ii.37, Kir.xv.7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापति|सेनापतिः
सेना-पति <i>m.</i> 1. a general; 2. a name of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापरिच्छद्
सेना-परिच्छद् <i>a.</i> surrounded by an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापृष्ठ
सेना-पृष्ठ <i>n.</i> the rear of an rmy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाभंग|सेनाभङ्ग|सेनाभङ्गः
सेना-भंग <i>m.</i> the breaking of an army, rout, disorderly flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनामुख|सेनामुखं
सेना-मुख <i>n.</i> 1. a division of an army; 2. a mound in front of a city gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनायोग|सेनायोगः
सेना-योग <i>m.</i> the equipment of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनारक्ष|सेनारक्षः
सेना-रक्ष <i>m.</i> a guard, a sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेफ|सेफः
सेफ <i>m.</i> The penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेमंती|सेमन्ती
सेमंती <i>f.</i> The Indian white rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेर|सेरः
सेर <i>m.</i> A kind of measure; (it is thus defined- पादोनगद्यानकतुल्यटंकैर्द्विसप्ततुल्यैः कथितोऽत्र सेरः Līlāvatī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरराह
सेरराह <i>m.</i> A horse of a milk-white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेराह|सेराहः
सेरराह <i>m.</i> A horse of a milk-white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरु|सेरुः
सेरु <i>a.</i> Binding, tying, fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-25" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल्
सेल् <i>vt. 1P (pres. सेलति)</i> To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल्
सेल् <i>Caus. (सेलयति-ते)</i> to cause to go or move.With अति-, to oblige to make excessive march.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-26" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्
सेव् <i>vt. 1Ā (the initial स् of this root is changed into ष् after परि, नि, or वि) (pp. सेवित; pres. सेवते; desid. सिसेविषति)</i> 1. To serve, to wait upon, to honour, to obey, ऐश्वर्यादनपेतमीश्वरमयं लोकोर्थतः सेवते Mud.i.; 2. to follow, to go after, to pursue; 3. to use, to enjoy, तप्तं वारि विहाय तीरनलिनीं कारंडवः सेवते Vikr.ii.; 4. to attend to, to devote oneself to, to cultivate, to practise, to perform; 5. to enjoy (sexually); 6. to frequent, to dwell in, to inhebit, e.g. अगस्त्यसेवितामाशाम्; 7. to watch over, to guard, to protect.With आ-, 1. to enjoy, दीर्घिकावलोकनगवाक्षगता प्रवातमासेवमाना तिष्ठति Mal.i.; 2. to practise.With उप-, 1. to apply oneself to, to practise; 2. to perform; 3. to enjoy; 4. to serve, वैरिणं नोपसेवेत सहायं चैव वैरिणः M.iv.133.With नि-, 1. to pursue, to attach oneself to; 2. to practise; 3. to employ, विषतां निषेवितमपक्रियया Sis.ix.69; 4. to enjoy, निषेवते श्रांतमना विविक्तम् Sak.v.; 5. to inhabit; 6. to observe; 7. to attend.With परि-, to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=795-27" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव|सेवं
सेव <i>m.</i> See सेवन (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
सेवक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> 1. Serving, worshipping; 2. practising; 3. servile, dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवका
सेवक <i>(I) a. (f. का)</i> 1. Serving, worshipping; 2. practising; 3. servile, dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
सेवक <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A servant, भयं तावत्सेव्यादभिनिविशते सेवकजनम् Mud.v.; 2. a votary; 3. a sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवधि|सेवधिः
सेवधि <i>m.</i> The same as शेवधि q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन|सेवनं
सेवन <i>n.</i> 1. Sewing, stitching; 2. a sack; 3. following, practising, using; 4. enjoying, enjoying sexually, यत्करोत्येकरात्रेण वृषलीसेवनाद् द्विजः M.xi.178; 5. service, worship, पात्रीकृतात्मा गुरुसेवनेन स्पष्टाकृतिः पत्ररथेंद्रकेतोः R.xviii.30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवनी
सेवनी <i>f.</i> 1. A needle; 2. a seam; 3. a suture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवा
सेवा <i>f.</i> 1. Service, attendance, servitude, सेवां लाघवकारिणीं कृतधियः स्थाने श्ववृत्तिं विदुः Mud.iii.; 2. devotion, worship, homage; 3. addition to; 4. use, practice, employment; 5. resorting to, frequenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाकाकु|सेवाकाकुः
सेवा-काकु <i>f.</i> change of voice in service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाधर्म|सेवाधर्मः
सेवा-धर्म <i>m.</i> 1. the functions of service, सेवाधर्मः परमगहनो योगिनामप्यगम्यः Hit.ii.; 2. the duty or rule of service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=796-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाव्यवहार|सेवाव्यवहारः
