स्खल् <i>vi. 1P (pres. स्खलति)</i> 1. To stumble, to fall down, to slip, to trip, स्खलंती स्वर्लोकादवनितलशोकापहृतये G.L.14, K.S.v.25; 2. to totter, to waver; 3. to fall or deviate from the right course; 4. to make mistakes, to blunder, to err, स्मरसि स्मर मेखलागुणैरुत गोत्रस्खलितेषु बंधनम् K.S.iv.8; 5. to stammer, to falter, to lisp, वदनकमलकं शिशोः स्मरामि स्खलदसमंजसमंजुजल्पितं ते Ut.iv., K.S.v.56; 6. to drop, to drip, to trickle; 7. to go, to move; 8. to disappear; 9. to gather, to collect.With प्र-, to jolt, to jostle, रथ्याः प्रचस्खलुः साश्वाः Bt.xiv.94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=802-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खल्
स्खल् <i>Caus. (स्खलयति-ते)</i> 1. to cause to stumble, to trip up; 2. to cause to make mistakes, to cause to blunder, to fail, skhalayati vacanaM te saMSrayatyaMgamaMgam M.M.iii., वचनानि स्खलनम् पदे पदे K.S.iv.12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=802-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलन|स्खलनं
स्खलन <i>n.</i> 1. The act of stumbling, slipping, tripping; 2. falling or deviating from the right course; 3. blundering, error, mistake; 4. blundering in speech or pronunciation, faltering; 5. dropping, dripping; 6. dashing, clashing; 7. mutual striking or rubbing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=802-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलित|स्खलितं
स्खलित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Stumbled, slipped; 2. dropped down; 3. shaking, fluctuating, hesitating; 4. intoxicated, drunk; 5. agitated, disturbed; 6. dropped, effused, emitted; 7. trickling down; 8. interrupted, stopped; 9. confounded; 10. gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=802-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

