स्तंबेरम <i>m.</i> an elephant, स्तंबेरमा मुखरशृंखलकर्षिणस्ते R.v.82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभ्|स्तम्भ्
स्तंभ् <i>vt. or vi. 1Ā, 5P, 9P (the initial स् of this root is changed into ष् after अव or any preposition ending in इ or उ) (pp. स्तंभित or स्तब्ध; pres. स्तंभते, स्तभ्नोति, स्तभ्नाति)</i> 1. To fix firmly, to make stiff or immovable; 2. to paralyze, to stupefy, प्राणा दध्वंसिरे गात्रं तस्तम्भे च प्रिये हते Bt.xvi.55; 3. to prop, to support, to sustain; 4. to stop, to arrest, to suppress, to hinder, कंठः स्तंभितबाष्पवृत्तिकलुषः Sak.iv.; 5. to become stiff or haughty, e.g. स्तंभते पुरुषः प्रायो यौवनेन धनेन च.With अव-, 1. to bind; 2. to rest on, to rely on; 3. to restrain, to overpower, प्रकृतिं स्वामवष्टभ्य विसृजामि औनः पुनः Bg.ix.8.With उद्-, 1. to uphold, to prop; 2. to stop, to arrest.With नि-, to stop.With पर्यव-, 1. to surround; 2. to surround and oppose.With वि-, to fix, to plant immovably, अत्युच्छ्रिते मंत्रिणि पार्थिवे च विष्टभ्य पादावुपतिष्ठते Mud.iv.With सम्-, 1. to support; 2. to stop, प्रयत्नसंस्तंभितविक्रियाणां कथंचिदीशा मनसां बभूवुः K.S.iii.34; 3. to corroborate, to make firm or immovable, एवं बुद्धेः परं बुद्ध्या संस्तभ्यात्मानमात्मना Bg.iii.43.With समव-, to encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभ|स्तम्भ|स्तंभः|स्तम्भः
स्तंभ <i>m.</i> 1. Fixedness, stiffness, rigidity, गात्रस्तंभः स्तनमुकुलयोरुत्प्रबंधः प्रकंपः M.M.ii.; 2. prop, support, fulcrum; 3. insensibility, stupor, paralysis; 4. stupidity; 5. want of feeling or excitability; 6. stoppage, obstruction, hindrance, सोऽपश्यत्प्रणिधानेन संततेः स्तंभकारणम् R.i.74; 7. a pillar, a column, a post, e.g. तैः स्तंभैरिव सुस्थिरैश्चिरभरक्लांतां धरा धार्यते; 8. immobility, motionlessnes, तत्संकल्पोऽपहितजडिम स्तंभमभ्येति गात्रम् M.M.i.; 9. suppression or arresting of any force or feeling by magical means; 10. suppressing, curbing, restraining, कृतश्चित्तस्तंभः प्रतिहतधियामंजलिरपि Bhartr.iii.6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभोत्कीर्ण|स्तम्भोत्कीर्ण
स्तंभ-उत्कीर्ण <i>a.</i> carved out of a post of wood (as a statue).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभकर|स्तम्भकर|स्तम्भकरः
स्तंभ-कर <i>(I) a.</i> 1. paralyzing; 2. obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभकर|स्तम्भकर|स्तम्भकरः
स्तंभ-कर <i>(II) m.</i> a fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभकरण|स्तम्भकरण
स्तंभ-करण <i>n.</i> cause of obstruction or impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभपूजा|स्तम्भपूजा
स्तंभ-पूजा <i>f.</i> worship of the posts of the temporary pavilions erected for marriages or other festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभकिन्|स्तम्भकिन्
स्तंभकिन् <i>m.</i> A kind of musical instrument covered with leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभन|स्तम्भन|स्तंभनं|स्तम्भनं|स्तम्भनः
स्तंभन <i>(I) n.</i> 1. The act of fixing firmly or making stiff; 2. paralyzing, stunning, benumbing; 3. propping, supporting; 4. stopping, hindering, arresting, suppressing, checking, लोलोल्लोलक्षुभितकरुणोज्जृंभणस्तंभनार्थम् Ut.iii.; 5. stopping the flow of blood; 6. anything employed as an astringent; 7. a particular magical act or faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=803-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभन|स्तम्भन|स्तंभनं|स्तम्भनं|स्तम्भनः
