स्रु <i>vt. or vi. 1P (pp. स्रुत; pres. स्रवति)</i> 1. To flow, to stream, to ooze, to drop, to exude, शोणितं चाप्यसुस्रुवत् Bt.xv.56; 2. to move, to go; 3. to let flow, to shed; 4. to trickle away, to slip away, to perish, धैर्यं नस्तव हेतोरसुस्रुवन् Bt.vi.18; 5. to spread about, to transpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=818-40" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रु|स्रुः
स्रु <i>Caus. (स्रावयति-ते)</i> to cause to flow, to pour out, to shed, to spill, न गात्रात्स्रावयेदसृक् M.iv.169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=818-40" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्न|स्रुघ्नः
स्रुघ्न <i>m.</i> Name of a district, न हि देवदत्तः स्रुध्रे संनिधीयमानस्तदहरेव पाटलिपुत्रे सन्निधीयते S.Bh.ii.1.7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्नी
स्रुघ्नी <i>f.</i> Natron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्
स्रुच् <i>f.</i> A sort of wooden ladle, used for pouring clarified butter on sacrificial fire; (it ought to be made of certain trees only), ऋत्विजां च्युतविकंकतस्रुचाम् R.xi.25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुक्प्रणालिका
स्रुक्प्रणालिका <i>f.</i> the spout of a ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत|स्रुतं
स्रुत <i>a. (generally at the end of a compound)</i> Flowing, distilling, अमृतस्रुतोऽपि विरहाद्भवतः Sis.ix.68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुति|स्रुतिः
स्रुति <i>f.</i> 1. Oozing, distilling, अमृतलवस्रुतिशालिभिर्मयूखैः Kir.v.44; 2. exudation, resin, ये तत्क्षीरस्रुतिसुरभयो दक्षिणेन प्रवृत्ताः Megh.ii.44; 3. a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुव|स्रुवः
स्रुव <i>m.</i> A sacrificial ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवा
स्रुवा <i>f.</i> A sacrificial ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रू
स्रू <i>f.</i> 1. A sacrificial ladle; 2. a cascade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेक्
स्रेक् <i>vt. 1Ā (pres. स्रेकते)</i> To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रै
स्रै <i>vi. 1P (pres. स्रायति)</i> 1. To boil, to be hot; 2. to sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोत|स्रोतं|स्रोतः
स्रोत <i>n.</i> A rapid stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्
स्रोतस् <i>n.</i> 1. A current, a stream, a course of water, पुरा यत्र स्रोतः पुलिनमधुना तत्र सरिताम् Ut.ii.; 2. a torrent, a rapid stream, स्रोतसेवोह्यमानस्य प्रतीपतरणं महत् Vikr.ii.; 3. a wave; 4. a spring; 5. water; 6. an organ of sense; 7. the trunk of an elephant, स्रोतोरंध्रध्वनितसुभगं दंतिभिः पीयमानः Megh.i.42 (where Mall. observes- स्रोतः शब्देनेंद्रियवाचिना तद्विशेषो घ्राणं लक्ष्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोञ्जन|स्रोतोञ्जनं
स्रोतोऽञ्जन <i>n.</i> antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोरंध्र|स्रोतोरन्ध्र
स्रोतोरंध्र <i>n.</i> the aperture of the trunk of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोवहा
स्रोतोवहा <i>f.</i> a river in general, स्रोतोवहां पथि निकामजलामतीत्य, or कार्यां सैकतलीनहंसमिथुना स्रोतोवहा मालिनी Sak.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्य|स्रोतस्यः
स्रोतस्य <i>m.</i> 1. An epithet of Śiva; 2. a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्वती
स्रोतस्वती <i>f.</i> A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्विनी
स्रोतस्वती <i>f.</i> A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व <i>(I) pron. a. (f. स्वा)</i> 1. Own, belonging to oneself, सा निंदंती स्वानि भाग्यानि बाला Sak.v.; 2. of one’s own tribe or family, न विप्रं स्वेषु तिष्ठत्सु मृतं शूद्रेण नाययेत् M.v.104; 3. natural, original, वपुरभिनवमस्याः पुष्यति स्वां न शोभाम् Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वा
स्व <i>(I) pron. a. (f. स्वा)</i> 1. Own, belonging to oneself, सा निंदंती स्वानि भाग्यानि बाला Sak.v.; 2. of one’s own tribe or family, न विप्रं स्वेषु तिष्ठत्सु मृतं शूद्रेण नाययेत् M.v.104; 3. natural, original, वपुरभिनवमस्याः पुष्यति स्वां न शोभाम् Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व <i>(II) m.</i> 1. A relative, a kinsman; 2. soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व <i>(III) m.n.</i> Wealth, riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाक्षपाद|स्वाक्षपादः
स्व-अक्षपाद <i>m.</i> a follower of the Nyāya system of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिकार|स्वाधिकारः
स्व-अधिकार <i>m.</i> one’s own function or office, स्वाधिकारात् प्रमत्तः Megh.i.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिष्ठान|स्वाधिष्ठानं
स्व-अधिष्ठान <i>n.</i> one of the six chakras or mystical circles of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीन|स्वाधीनः
स्व-अधीन <i>a.</i> self-dependent, in one’s own power, e.g. स्वाधीना वचनीयताऽपि हि वरं बद्धो न सेवांजलिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनकुशल
स्व-अधीन˚कुशल <i>a.</i> having prosperity in one’s own power, स्वाधीनकुशलाः सिद्धिमंतः Sak.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनपतिका
स्व-अधीन˚पतिका <i>f.</i> a woman who has control over her husband, प्रभावप्रभवं कांतं स्वाधीनपतिका यथा K.Pr.x.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्याय|स्वाध्यायः
स्व-अध्याय <i>m.</i> study of the Vedas, a sacred study, perusal of sacred books.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुभूति|स्वानुभूतिः
स्व-अनुभूति <i>f.</i> one’s own experience, self-enjoyment, स्वानुभूत्येकसाराय नमः शांताय तेजसे Bhartr.ii.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वांत|स्वान्त|स्वान्तं
स्व-अंत <i>n.</i> 1. the mind; 2. a cavern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थ|स्वार्थः
स्व-अर्थ <i>m.</i> 1. self interest; 2. own meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थपंडित|स्वार्थपण्डित
स्व-अर्थ˚पंडित <i>a.</i> clever in one’s own affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थविघात
स्व-अर्थ˚विघात <i>m.</i> the frustration of one’s own object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थानुमान
स्व-अर्थ˚अनुमान <i>n.</i> a particular process of induction, (as op. to परार्थानुमान) (in logic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायत्त
स्व-आयत्त <i>a.</i> depending upon oneself, स्वायत्तमेकांतगुणं विधात्रा Bhartr.ii.7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छा
स्व-इच्छा <i>f.</i> self-will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छामृत्यु|स्वेच्छामृत्युः
स्व-इच्छा˚मृत्यु <i>m.</i> an epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोदय|स्वोदयः
स्व-उदय <i>m.</i> the rising of a sign or heavenly body at any particular place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोपधि|स्वोपधिः
स्व-उपधि <i>m.</i> a fixed star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकंपन|स्वकम्पन|स्वकम्पनः
स्व-कंपन <i>m.</i> air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगतम्
स्व-गतम् <i>ind.</i> to oneself, aside, (in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छंद|स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छन्दः|स्वछन्द
स्व-च्छंद <i>(I) a.</i> self-willed, wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छंद|स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छन्दः|स्वछन्द
स्व-च्छंद <i>(II) m.</i> own fancy, own choice, independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छंदम्|स्वच्छन्दम्
स्व-च्छंदम् <i>ind.</i> voluntarily, wantonly, स्वच्छंदोच्छलदच्छकच्छकुहरच्छातेतरांबुच्छटा K.Pr.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज|स्वजं|स्वजः
स्व-ज <i>(I) a.</i> selfborn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज|स्वजं|स्वजः
स्व-ज <i>(II) m.</i> 1. a child; 2. sweat, perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज|स्वजं|स्वजः
स्व-ज <i>(III) n.</i> blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजन|स्वजनः
स्व-जन <i>m.</i> a kinsman, a relative, इतः प्रत्यादेशात् स्वजनमनुगतंतुं व्यवसिता Sak.vi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतंत्र|स्वतन्त्र|स्वतन्त्रः
स्व-तंत्र <i>a.</i> self-willed, independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्र|स्वत्रः
स्व-त्र <i>m.</i> a blind-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्व|स्वत्वं
स्व-त्व <i>n.</i> 1. self-existence; 2. ownership (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म|स्वधर्मः|स्वधर्म्म|स्वधर्म्मः
स्व-धर्म <i>m.n.</i> 1. own right, own duty; (See M.i.88-91); 2. one’s own religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधा
स्व-धा <i>(I) f.</i> 1. spontaneity; 2. self-will; 3. worldly illusion; 4. the food offered to deceased ancestors, व्यपैति ददतः स्वधा M.ix.127; 5. the food of the Manes personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधा
स्व-धा <i>(II) ind.</i> an exclamation used on presenting an oblation to the Manes, e.g. स्वाहास्वधाकाराविवर्जितानि श्मशानतुल्यानि गृहाणि तानि; (it governs a dat., e.g. पितृभ्यः स्वधा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाभुज्
स्व-धा˚भुज् <i>m.</i> 1. a deified ancestor; 2. a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपरमंडल|स्वपरमण्डल
स्व-परमंडल <i>n.</i> one’s own and an enemy’s country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रकाश
स्व-प्रकाश <i>a.</i> self-evident, self-luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रयोगात्
स्व-प्रयोगात् <i>ind.</i> by means of one’s own exertions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभट|स्वभटः
स्व-भट <i>m.</i> one’s own warrior, body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाव|स्वभावः
स्व-भाव <i>m.</i> (own state) an essential or inherent property, natural constitution, nature, e.g. किमप्यस्ति स्वभावेन सुंदरं वाप्यसुंदरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावोक्ति
स्व-भाव˚उक्ति <i>f.</i> 1. spontaneous declaration; 2. a figure of speech (in rhetoric) consisting in a life-like description of any thing. It is thus defined by Danḍin- नानावस्थं पदार्थानां रूपं साक्षाद्विवृण्वती K.D.ii.8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावज
स्व-भाव˚ज, ˚सिद्ध <i>a.</i> inborn, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावसिद्ध
स्व-भाव˚ज, ˚सिद्ध <i>a.</i> inborn, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाववाद
स्व-भाव˚वाद <i>m.</i> the doctrine that the universe was produced and is sustained by the natural and necessary action of substances according to their inherent properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभू
स्व-भू <i>m.</i> 1. epithet of Brahman (n.); 2. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयोनि
स्व-योनि <i>(I) a.</i> nearly related on the mother’s side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयोनि
स्व-योनि <i>(II) m.f.</i> own womb, one’s own place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयोनि
स्व-योनि <i>(III) f.</i> a sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरस|स्वरसः
स्व-रस <i>m.</i> proper taste or sentiment in composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराज्
स्व-राज् <i>m.</i> the supreme being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूप|स्वरूपं|स्वरूपः
स्व-रूप <i>(I) a.</i> 1. handsome, posing, agreeable; 2. learned, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूप|स्वरूपं|स्वरूपः
स्व-रूप <i>(II) n.</i> 1. one’s own form or shape; 2. true constitution, natural character; 3. peculiar aim; 4. nature; 5. species, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपासिद्धि
स्व-रूप˚असिद्धि <i>f.</i> a form of fallacious proof (in Nyāya phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववासिनी
स्व-वासिनी <i>f.</i> a woman whether married or unmarried who continues to dwell after maturity in her father’s house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंवृत
स्व-संवृत <i>a.</i> self-guarded, self-covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंस्था
स्व-संस्था <i>f.</i> self-possession, absorption in one’s own self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थ|स्वस्थः
स्व-स्थ <i>a.</i> 1. relying upon oneself, confident, firm; 2. contented, Sis.ii.46; 3. well, healthy, at ease, comfortable, अस्वस्थशरीरा शकुंतला Sak.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थम्
स्व-स्थम् <i>ind.</i> composedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थान
स्व-स्थान <i>n.</i> one’s own place, own home, e.g. नक्रः स्वस्थानमासाद्य गजेंद्रमपि कर्षति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहस्तिका
स्व-हस्तिका <i>f.</i> an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहित
स्व-हित <i>(I) a.</i> good for oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहित
स्व-हित <i>(II) n.</i> one’s own advantage, one’s own welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=819-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक|स्वकं|स्वकः
स्वक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Own, one’s own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वका
स्वक <i>a. (f. का)</i> Own, one’s own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीय|स्वकीयः
स्वकीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. Own; 2. of one’s own family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीया
स्वकीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> 1. Own; 2. of one’s own family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वग्
स्वग् <i>vt. 1P (pres. स्वंगति)</i> To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंग|स्वङ्ग|स्वंगः|स्वङ्गः
स्वंग <i>m.</i> An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं|स्वच्छः
स्वच्छ <i>a. (f. च्छा)</i> 1. White, beautiful; 2. pure, transparent, bright, विकचनवकुसुंभस्वच्छसिंदूरभासा Rt.i.24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छा
स्वच्छ <i>a. (f. च्छा)</i> 1. White, beautiful; 2. pure, transparent, bright, विकचनवकुसुंभस्वच्छसिंदूरभासा Rt.i.24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छपत्र|स्वच्छपत्रं
स्वच्छ-पत्र <i>n.</i> talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छमणि|स्वच्छमणिः
स्वच्छ-मणि <i>m.</i> crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंज्|स्वञ्ज्
स्वंज् <i>vt. 1Ā (the initial स् of this root is changed into ष् after a preposition ending in इ or उ) (pres. स्वजते; caus. स्वंजयति-ते)</i> 1. To embrace, to clasp, पर्यश्रुरस्वजत मूर्धनि चोपजघ्रौ R.xiii.70; 2. to encircle, to twist round.With परि-, to embrace, हला एत पीडितं मां परिष्वजध्वम् Vikr.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वठ्
स्वठ् <i>vt. 10U (pres. स्वठयति-ते)</i> 1. To finish; 2. to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद्
स्वद् <i>(I) vt. or vi. 1Ā (pres. स्वदते or स्वादते)</i> 1. To be pleasant to the taste, to be liked, (with a dat.), सस्वदे मुखसुरं प्रमदाभ्यः Sis.x.23; 2. to taste, to eat, to relish; 3. to please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद्
स्वद् <i>(II) vt. 10U (pres. स्वादयति-ते)</i> To sweeten, to make sweet.With आ-, to taste, to eat, आस्वादितद्विरदशोणितशोणशोभाम् Mud.i.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदन|स्वदनं
स्वदन <i>n.</i> Eating, tasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
स्वदित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Eaten, tasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदिता
स्वदित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Eaten, tasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
स्वदित <i>(II) n.</i> An exclamation meaning ‘may it be well-tasted’ uttered at a Śrāddha after presenting the oblation of food to the Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिति|स्वधितिः
स्वधिति <i>m.f.</i> An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिती
स्वधिती <i>f.</i> An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन्
स्वन् <i>vi. 1P (pres. स्वनिति)</i> 1. To sound, to make a noise, वेणवः कीचकास्ते स्युर्ये स्वनंत्यनिलोद्धताः Am.ii.4, 161; 2. to sing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन्
स्वन् <i>Caus. (स्वनयति-ते)</i> 1. to make to resound; 2. to sound; 3. to adorn; (in this sense स्वानयति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन|स्वनः
स्वन <i>m.</i> Sound, noise, मनोभिरामाः शृण्वंतौ रथनेमिस्वनोन्मुखैः R.i.39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनोत्साह|स्वनोत्साहः
स्वन-उत्साह <i>m.</i> a rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनि|स्वनिः
स्वनि <i>m.</i> Sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनित|स्वनितं
स्वनित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Sounded, sounding, making a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिता
स्वनित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> Sounded, sounding, making a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनित|स्वनितं
स्वनित <i>(II) n.</i> The noise of thunder, thunder-clap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिक
स्वनिक <i>m.</i> One who clasps his hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्
स्वप् <i>vi. 2P (pp. सुप्त; pres. स्वपिति; pass. सुप्यते; desid. सुषुप्सति) (sometimes also 1U (pres. स्वपति-ते)</i> 1. To sleep, to fall asleep, to go to bed, तां कस्यांचिद्भवनवलभौ सुप्तपारवितायाम् Megh.i.38, R.xii.50; 2. to lie down, to recline, to repose.With अव-, प्र- or सम्-, to sleep, तत्प्रसुप्तभुजगेंद्रभीषणं वीक्ष्य R.xi.44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्न|स्वप्नः
स्वप्न <i>m.</i> 1. Sleep, sleeping, रसातलादिवोन्मग्नं शेषं स्वप्नाय शार्ङ्गिणः R.xii.70; 2. dream, dreaming, स्वप्नो नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो नु Sak.vi., दृष्टः स्वप्ने कितव रमयन् कामपि त्वं मयेति Megh.ii.48; 3. indolence, sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नावस्था
स्वप्न-अवस्था <i>f.</i> state of dreaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नोपम
स्वप्न-उपम <i>a.</i> 1. resembling a dream; 2. transitory, evanescent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नदोष|स्वप्नदोषः
स्वप्न-दोष <i>m.</i> pollutio nocturna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नधीगम्य
स्वप्न-धीगम्य <i>a.</i> perceptible by the intellect (only) in a state of sleep like abstraction, M.xii.122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्ननिकेतन
स्वप्न-निकेतन <i>n.</i> a sleeping room, bed-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नप्रपंच|स्वप्नप्रपञ्च|स्वप्नप्रपञ्चः
स्वप्न-प्रपंच <i>m.</i> the illusions of sleep, the world as represented in a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नविचार|स्वप्नविचारः
स्वप्न-विचार <i>m.</i> interpretation of dreams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नशील
स्वप्न-शील <i>a.</i> sleepy, drowsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नसृष्टि|स्वप्नसृष्टिः
स्वप्न-सृष्टि <i>f.</i> the creation of dreams or illusions in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=820-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज्
स्वप्नज् <i>xxx</i> Sleepy, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम् <i>ind.</i> 1. Self; (this word is applicable to all persons, such as myself, thyself, itself, herself, and is sometimes used emphatically with other pronouns), स्थातुं नियोक्तुर्न हि शक्यमग्रे विनाश्य रक्ष्यं स्वयमक्षतेन R.i.56, iii.45; 2. by oneself, spontaneously, of one’s own accord, स्वयमेवोत्पद्यंते एवंविदाः शरारसंभवाः महाकृमयः Kad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमुक्ति|स्वयमुक्तिः
स्वयम्-उक्ति <i>f.</i> 1. voluntary declaration; 2. information, deposition (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंग्रह
स्वयम्-ग्रह <i>m.</i> the taking for one’s self (without leave).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंग्राह
स्वयम्-ग्राह <i>a.</i> voluntary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंजात
स्वयम्-जात <i>a.</i> self-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंदत्त|स्वयन्दत्त|स्वयन्दत्तः|स्वयंदत्तः
स्वयम्-दत्त <i>(I) a.</i> self-given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंदत्त|स्वयन्दत्त|स्वयन्दत्तः|स्वयंदत्तः
स्वयम्-दत्त <i>(II) m.</i> a boy who has given himself to be adopted; (one of the twelve kinds of sons recognized by Hindu law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंभु|स्वयम्भु|स्वयम्भुः
स्वयम्-भु <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman (m.), शंभुस्वयंभुहरयो हरिणेक्षणानाम् Bhartr.i.1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंभुव|स्वयम्भुव|स्वयम्भुवः
स्वयम्-भुव <i>m.</i> 1. name of the first Manu; 2. an epithet of Brahman (m.); 3. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंभू|स्वयम्भू
स्वयम्-भू <i>(I) a.</i> self-existent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंभू|स्वयम्भू
स्वयम्-भू <i>(II) m.</i> 1. an epithet of Brahman (m.); 2. of Viṣṇu; 3. of Śiva; 4. of Kāla, the deity presiding over time; 5. of Kāmadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवर|स्वयंवरः
स्वयम्-वर <i>m.</i> a choice-marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवरा
स्वयम्-वरा <i>f.</i> a virgin who chooses a husband for herself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् <i>vt. 10U (pres. स्वरयति-ते)</i> To find fault, to blame, to censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् <i>ind.</i> 1. Heaven, paradise, छायेव या स्वर्जलधेर्जलेषु Sis.iii.35, Nal.iii.1; 2. the heaven of Indra and the temporary abode of the virtuous after death; 3. the sky, ether; 4. the space between the sun and the polar star; 5. a mystical word pronounced in daily prayers. See under व्याहृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरापगा
स्वर्-आपगा, -गंगा, -सिंधु <i>f.</i> 1. the celestial Ganges; 2. the milky way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गंगा|स्वर्गङ्गा
स्वर्-आपगा, -गंगा, -सिंधु <i>f.</i> 1. the celestial Ganges; 2. the milky way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वःसिंधु|स्वःसिन्धु
स्वर्-आपगा, -गंगा, -सिंधु <i>f.</i> 1. the celestial Ganges; 2. the milky way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गमन
स्वर्-गमन <i>n.</i> 1. future felicity; 2. death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णदी
स्वर्णदी <i>f.</i> the celestial Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तरु|स्वस्तरुः
स्वस्तरु <i>m.</i> a tree of paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्दृश्
स्वर्-दृश् <i>m.</i> 1. an epithet of Indra; 2. of Agni; 3. of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानव|स्वर्भानवः
स्वर्-भानव <i>m.</i> a kind of precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानु|स्वर्भानुः
स्वर्-भानु <i>m.</i> an epithet of Rāhu, तुल्येऽपराधे स्वर्भानुर्भानुमंतं चिरेण यत् । हिमांशुमाशु ग्रसते तन्म्रदिम्नः स्फुटं फलम् Sis.ii.49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानुसूदन|स्वर्भानुसूदनः
स्वर्-भानु˚सूदन <i>m.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्मध्य
स्वर्-मध्य <i>n.</i> the central point of the sky, the zenith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्लोक|स्वर्लोकः
स्वर्-लोक <i>m.</i> the celestial region, the heaven, स्खलंती स्वर्लोकादवनितलशोकापहृतये G.L.14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वधू
स्वर्-वधू <i>f.</i> an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वापी|स्वर्व्वापी
स्वर्-वापी <i>f.</i> the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वेश्या|स्वर्व्वेश्या
स्वर्-वेश्या <i>f.</i> a courtezan of heaven, a nymph of heaven, an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वैद्य|स्वर्वैद्यः
स्वर्-वैद्य <i>m. du.</i> an epithet of the two Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्षा
स्वर्-षा <i>m.</i> 1. an epithet of soma; 2. of the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर|स्वरः
स्वर <i>m.</i> 1. Sound, noise; 2. voice, अवोचदेनं गगनस्पृशा रघुः स्वरेण धीरेण R.iii.43; 3. tone, tune, a note of the musical scale or gamut, (which are thus enumerated- निषादर्षभगांधारषड्रजमध्यमधैवताः । पंचमश्चेत्यमी सप्त तंत्रीकंठोत्थिताः स्वराः); 4. a symbolical expression for the number ‘seven’; 5. a vowel; 6. a Vedic accent, (of which there are three, viz., उदात्त, अनुदात्त and स्वरित); 7. air breathed through the nostrils; 8. snoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरांश|स्वरांशः
स्वर-अंश <i>m.</i> a half or quarter tone in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरांतर|स्वरान्तर
स्वर-अंतर <i>n.</i> the interval between two vowels, hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरोपध
स्वर-उपध <i>a.</i> preceded by a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरग्राम|स्वरग्रामः
स्वर-ग्राम <i>m.</i> the musical scale, gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरबद्ध
स्वर-बद्ध <i>a.</i> composed in musical measure, adapted to musical time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभक्ति|स्वरभक्तिः
स्वर-भक्ति <i>f.</i> a vowel-sound phonetically inserted in the pronunciation of र् or ल्, when these letters are followed by a sibilant, e.g. वर्ष pronounced as वरिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभंग|स्वरभङ्ग|स्वरभङ्गः
स्वर-भंग <i>m.</i> indistinctness of utterance, broken articulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरमंडलिका|स्वरमण्डलिका
स्वर-मंडलिका <i>f.</i> kind of vīṇā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरलासिका
स्वर-लासिका <i>f.</i> a flute, a pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरवत्|स्वरवन्त्
स्वर-वत् <i>a.</i> 1. having sound, sonorous; 2. having a voice, vocal; 3. having an accent, accentuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरशून्य
स्वर-शून्य <i>a.</i> without musical notes, unmelodious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंयोग|स्वरसंयोगः
स्वर-संयोग <i>m.</i> 1. the junction of vowels; 2. intonation, voice, आर्यायाः पंडितकौशिक्या इव स्वरसंयोगः श्रूयते Mal.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंक्रम
स्वर-संक्रम <i>m.</i> a transition or succession of notes, तं तस्य स्वरसंक्रमं मृदुगिरः श्लिष्टं च तंत्रीस्वनम् Mrich.iii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंधि
स्वर-संधि <i>m.</i> the junction or coalition of vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसामन्
स्वर-सामन् <i>m. pl.</i> an epithet of particular days in a sacrificial session.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरित|स्वरितः
स्वरित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Sounded; 2. sounded as a note, pitched; 8. articulated; 4. accented; 5. circumflexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरिता
स्वरित <i>(I) a. (f. ता)</i> 1. Sounded; 2. sounded as a note, pitched; 8. articulated; 4. accented; 5. circumflexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरित|स्वरितः
स्वरित <i>(II) m.</i> The third or mixed tone between high and low; (it is thus defined- समाहारः स्वरितः Pan.i.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=821-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरु|स्वरुः
स्वरु <i>m.</i> 1. Sunshine; 2. a part of a sacrificial post; 3. a thunderbolt; 4. an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=822-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुस्
स्वरुस् <i>m.</i> A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=822-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग|स्वर्गः
