स्वारोचिस्
स्वारोचिष <i>m.</i> Name of the second Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वालक्षण्य|स्वालक्षण्यं
स्वालक्षण्य <i>m.</i> Peculiar characteristic, natural disposition, M.ix.19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्प
स्वाल्प <i>(I) a. (f. ल्पी)</i> 1. Little, small; 2. few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्पी
स्वाल्प <i>(I) a. (f. ल्पी)</i> 1. Little, small; 2. few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्प
स्वाल्प <i>(II) n.</i> Littleness, smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्थ्य|स्वास्थ्यं
स्वास्थ्य <i>n.</i> 1. Self-reliance, self-dependence, fortitude, courage, firmness; 2. sound state, health; 3. prosperity, comfortableness, competence; 4. complacency, satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-22" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहा
स्वाहा <i>(I) f.</i> 1. The wife of fire, अन्वासितमरुंधत्या स्वाहयेव हविर्भुजम् R.i.56; 2. an oblation made to gods indiscriminately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहा
स्वाहा <i>(II) ind.</i> An exclamation uttered at the time of making an offering to the gods (used with a noun in the dat., e.g. अग्नये स्वाहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाकार|स्वाहाकारः
स्वाहा-कार <i>m.</i> utterance of the term svāhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहापति|स्वाहापतिः
स्वाहा-पति, -प्रिय <i>m.</i> an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाप्रिय|स्वाहाप्रियः
स्वाहा-पति, -प्रिय <i>m.</i> an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाभुज्
स्वाहा-भुज् <i>m.</i> a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-23" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वित्
स्वित् <i>ind.</i> A particle of interrogation or inquiry (often implying doubt or surprise and translatable by ‘hey!’ ‘what!’ ‘can it be that’), अद्रेः शृंगं हरति पवनः किंस्विदित्युन्मुखीभिः Megh.i.14. It is added to interrogative pronouns and adverbs to impart to them the sense of indefiniteness. For the use of स्वित् after आहो, See under आहो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=823-24" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
स्विद् <i>(I) vi. 4P (pp. स्विदित or स्विन्न; pres. स्विद्यति)</i> To sweat, to perspire, सद्यः स्विद्यन्नयमविरतोत्कंपलोलांगुलीकः M.M.i., K.S.vii.77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
स्विद् <i>(II) vi. 1Ā (pp. स्विन्न or स्वेदित; pres. स्वेदते)</i> 1. To be anointed; 2. to be greasy or unctuous; 3. to be disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरण|स्वीकरणं
स्वीकरण <i>n.</i> 1. Assenting, accepting; 2. promising; 3. marriage, wedding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकार|स्वीकारः
स्वीकार <i>m.</i> 1. Assent, acceptance; 2. promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृति|स्वीकृतिः
स्वीकृति <i>f.</i> 1. Assent, acceptance; 2. promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीय|स्वीयः
स्वीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Own, e.g. मां कांतिं वहसि परां प्रदीप भद्र स्वीयाऽस्माविति हृदि मास्म मन्यथास्त्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीया
स्वीय <i>a. (f. या)</i> Own, e.g. मां कांतिं वहसि परां प्रदीप भद्र स्वीयाऽस्माविति हृदि मास्म मन्यथास्त्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वृ
स्वृ <i>vt. or vi. 1P (pres. स्वरति; desid. सिस्वरिषति, सुस्वूर्षति)</i> 1. To sound; 2. to praise; 3. to be pained; 4. to go.With सम्-, (Atm.) to pain, द्रुतं संस्वरिषीष्ठास्त्वम् Bt.ix.28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वॄ
स्वॄ <i>vt. 9P (pres. स्वृणाति)</i> To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेक्
स्वेक् <i>vt. 1P (pres. स्वेकते)</i> To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेद|स्वेदः
स्वेद <i>m.</i> Perspiration, sweat, गंडस्वेदापनयनरुजा क्लांतकर्णोत्पलानाम् Megh.i.26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदोद
स्वेद-उद, -उदक <i>n.</i> perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदोदक
स्वेद-उद, -उदक <i>n.</i> perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदचूषक|स्वेदचूषकः
स्वेद-चूषक <i>m.</i> a cooling breeze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदज|स्वेदजः
स्वेद-ज <i>a.</i> engendered by heat and moisture (said of insects).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर <i>(I) a. (f. री)</i> 1. Going; 2. following one’s own fancy, wanton, unrestrained, अव्याहतैः स्वैरगतैः स तस्याः सम्राट् समाराधनतत्परोऽभूत् R.ii.5; 3. slow, lazy; 4. dependent on will, voluntary, optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरी
स्वैर <i>(I) a. (f. री)</i> 1. Going; 2. following one’s own fancy, wanton, unrestrained, अव्याहतैः स्वैरगतैः स तस्याः सम्राट् समाराधनतत्परोऽभूत् R.ii.5; 3. slow, lazy; 4. dependent on will, voluntary, optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर <i>(II) n.</i> Wilfulneas.(स्वैरम् is used as an indeclinable in the sense of- (1) with one’s on will or assent, of one’s an accord, सार्थाः स्वैरं स्वकीयेषु चेरुर्वेश्मस्विवाद्रिषु R.xvii.64; (2) lowly, inaudibly, indistinctly, स्वैरं शेषे गज इति किल व्याहृतं सत्यवाचा Ve.iii.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरता
स्वैर-ता <i>f.</i> wilfulness, independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिणी
स्वैरिणी <i>f.</i> A loose or unchaste woman, an adulteress, a wanton woman, स्वैरिणी या पतिं हित्वा सवर्णं कामतः श्रयेत् Yaj.i.67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिन्
स्वैरिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Self-willed, wanton, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिणी
स्वैरिन् <i>a. (f. णी)</i> Self-willed, wanton, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिंध्री|स्वैरिन्ध्री
स्वैरिंध्री <i>f.</i> See सैरंध्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-12" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोरस|स्वोरसः
स्वोरस <i>m.</i> The sediment of oily substances ground with a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-13" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोवश्वीय
स्वोवश्वीय <i>n.</i> Happiness, prosperity. Cf. श्वोवसीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-14" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
ह <i>ind.</i> An emphatic particle laying stress on the preceding word and equlvalent to ‘verily,’ ‘indeed,’ ‘manifestly,’ ‘evidently.’ Often it is used without any distinct signification, merely as an expletive, e.g. दाराधीनस्तथास्वर्गः पितॄणामात्मनश्च ह. It is sometimes used as a vocative particle also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंस|हंसः
हंस <i>m. (this word is curiously derived by native philologists; भवेद् वर्णागमाद् हंसः, i.e. it is derived from हस् by the insertion of a nasal.)</i> 1. A goose, a swan, a flamingo, हिरण्मयं हंसमबोधि नैषधः Na.i.117, Megh.i.23, 57, R.xvii.25, iii.10, v.12, xii.62; (the description of this bird as found in Sanskrit poetry is rather poetical than real; swans are considered to fly to the Mānasa lake when monsoon sets in; they are also represented as being the vehicle of Brahman (m.); there is a convention among poets that this bird is gifted with the power of separating milk from water; thus Bhartṛhari says- अम्भोजिनीवननिवासविलासमेव हंसस्य हंति नितरां कुपितो विधाता । नत्वस्य दुग्धजलभेदविधौ प्रसिद्धां वैदग्ध्यकीर्तिमपहर्तुमसौ समर्थः, See also Bh.V.i.13; 2. the supreme soul, Brahman (n.); 3. the jīvātman or individual soul; 4. the sun; 5. an unambitious monarch; 6. Viṣṇu; 7. Śiva; 8. an ascetic of a particular order; 9. a preceptor; 10. free from envy or malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाधिरूढा
हंस-अधिरूढा <i>f.</i> an epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाभिख्य|हंसाभिख्यं
हंस-अभिख्य <i>n.</i> silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकांता|हंसकान्ता
हंस-कांता <i>f.</i> a female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकीलक|हंसकीलकः
हंस-कीलक <i>m.</i> a particular form of sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगति
हंस-गति <i>a.</i> having a swan’s gait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगद्गदा
हंस-गद्गदा <i>f.</i> sweetly speaking woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगामिनी
हंस-गामिनी <i>f.</i> 1. a woman having a graceful gait, M.iii.10; 2. an epithet of Brāhmaṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसतूल|हंसतूलः
हंस-तूल <i>m.</i> the soft feathers of a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसदाहन|हंसदाहनं
हंस-दाहन <i>n.</i> aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनाद|हंसनादः
हंस-नाद <i>m.</i> the cackling of a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनादिनी
हंस-नादिनी <i>f.</i> woman having a slender waist, large hips, the gait of an elephant and the voice of a cuckoo, (गजेंद्रगमना तन्वी कोकिलालापसंयुता । नितंबे गुर्विणी या स्यात् सा स्मृता हंसनादिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसमाला
हंस-माला <i>f.</i> 1. a flight of wild geese, K.S.i.30; 2. a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसयुवन्
हंस-युवन् <i>m.</i> a young goose or swan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसरथ|हंसरथः
हंस-रथ, -वाहन <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसवाहन|हंसवाहनः
हंस-रथ, -वाहन <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसराज|हंसराजः
हंस-राज <i>m.</i> a king of geese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलोहक|हंसलोहकं
हंस-लोहक <i>n.</i> brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसश्रेणी
हंस-श्रेणी <i>f.</i> a row of geese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=824-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसक|हंसकः
हंसक <i>m.</i> 1. A goose, a flamingo; 2. an ornament for the ankles, सरित इव सविभ्रमश्रयातप्रणदितहंसकभूषणा विरेजुः Sis.vii.23 (where the word is used in both the senses).(हंसक may be used in all the senses of हंस.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-01" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसिका
हंसिका <i>f.</i> A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसी
हंसिका <i>f.</i> A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-02" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंहो
हंहो <i>(I) ind.</i> 1. A vocative particle corresponding to ‘ho,’ ‘hollo,’ हंहो चिन्मयचित्तचंद्रमणयः Ch.L.i.2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंहो
हंहो <i>(II) ind.</i> A particle expressing haughtiness, contempt or interrogation.(In drama, it is found used as a form of address in speeches assigned to characters of the middling class, e.g. हंहो ब्बह्मण कस्य एदं गेहम् Mud.i.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हक्क|हक्कः
हक्क <i>m.</i> The calling of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंजा|हञ्जा
हंजा <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle used in addressing a female attendant or maidservant, हंजे तरलिए उवणेहि मे अग्घभाअणम् Ve.ii., (हंडे हंजे हलाह्वाने नीचां चेटीं सखीं प्रति Am.i.7.15).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंजे|हञ्जे
हंजा <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle used in addressing a female attendant or maidservant, हंजे तरलिए उवणेहि मे अग्घभाअणम् Ve.ii., (हंडे हंजे हलाह्वाने नीचां चेटीं सखीं प्रति Am.i.7.15).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्
हट् <i>vi. 1P (pp. हटित; pres. हटति)</i> To shine, to be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्ट|हट्टः
हट्ट <i>m.</i> A market, a fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टचौरक|हट्टचौरकः
हट्ट-चौरक <i>m.</i> a thief who steals from fairs and markets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टविलासिनी
हट्ट-विलासिनी <i>f.</i> 1. a wanton woman, a prostitute; 2. a sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ|हठः
हठ <i>m.</i> 1. Violence, force, e.g. वानरान् वारयामास हठेन मधुरेण च; 2. oppression, rapine.(The inst. and abl. singulars, viz., हठेन and हठात् are used as indeclinables in the sense of ‘forcibly, violently, suddenly.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठयोग|हठयोगः
हठ-योग <i>m.</i> a particular mode of yoga or abstract contemplation difficult to practise, and as such distinguished from राजयोग q.v. (It is performed in various ways, such as standing on one leg, holding up the arms, inhaling smoke with the head inverted &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठविद्या
हठ-विद्या <i>f.</i> the science of forced meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडिक|हडिकः
हडि(ड्डि)क <i>m.</i> A man of the lowest cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डिक|हड्डिकः
हडि(ड्डि)क <i>m.</i> A man of the lowest cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्ड|हड्डं
हड्ड <i>n.</i> A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=825-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डज|हड्डजं
