हस्
हस् <i>vt. or vi. 1P (pp. हसित; pres. हसति)</i> 1. To laugh, to smile, परिघोरुभुजानाह हसन्ती स्वागतं कपीन् Bt.vii.63, xiv.93; 2. to open, to blow, e.g. हसिष्यति पद्मजालम्; 3. to joke, Kir.xiii.47; 4. to resemble, e.g. श्रिया हसद्भिः कमलानि सस्मितैः Kir.viii.44; 5. to brighten up; 6. to laugh at, to ridicule.With अप-, to deride, to ridicule.With अव-, to laugh at, to deride, स्थितावहस्येव पुरं मघोनः Bt.i.6.With उप-, to laugh at, to deride, कुटज किं कुसुमैरुपहस्यते Ghat.17.With परि-, 1. to laugh at, to deride, जनानामानंदः परिहसति निर्वाणपदवीम् G.L.5; 2. to joke.With प्र-, 1. to laugh, to smile, ततः प्रहस्यापभयः पुरंदरम् R.iii.51; 2. to mock, to deride, to ridicule, e.g. हसंतं प्रहसंत्येताः.With वि-, 1. to laugh gently, to smile, किंचिद्विहस्यार्थपतिं बभाषे R.ii.46; 2. to laugh at, to ridicule, गौरीवक्त्रभृकुटिरचनां या विहस्येव फेनैः Megh.i.50, किमिति विषादसि रोदिषि विकला विहसति युवतिसभा तव सकला Git.G.ix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=829-15" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस|हसः
हस <i>m.</i> 1. Laughter; 2. mirth, merriment, joy; 3. derision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=829-16" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन|हसनं
हसन <i>n.</i> the act of laughing, laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=829-17" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसनी
हसनी <i>f.</i> A portable fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=829-18" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसंती|हसन्ती
हसंती <i>f.</i> 1. A portable fireplace; 2. a kind of mallikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=829-19" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसित|हसितं|हसितः
हसित <i>n.</i> 1. Laughter; 2. jesting; 3. the bow of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=829-20" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त|हस्तं|हस्तः
हस्त <i>m.</i> 1. The hand, M.iii.214, 216, Megh.ii.12, 33; 2. possession (fig.), M.viii.340; 3. signature, handwriting, स्वहस्तकालसंपन्नं शासनं कारयेत् स्थिरः Yaj.i.320, or धार्यतामयं प्रियायाः स्वहस्तः Vikr.ii.; 4. a measure of length from the elbow to the tip of the middle finger (equal to about 18 inches); 5. an elephant’s trunk, नागेंद्रहस्तास्त्वचि कर्कशत्वात् K.S.i.36; 6. the thirteenth lunar asterism consisting of five stars; 7. abundance, mass; (in this sense it is used only at the end of compounds and implies excellence), e.g. रतिविगलितबंधे केशवहस्ते सुकेश्याः सतिकुसुमसनाथे किं करात्येषे बर्हः Vikr.iv.(हस्तेकृ ‘to take in hand, to take possession of, to make one’s own, to take by the hand’; in this phrase, हस्ते is considered as a prefix or not; hence हस्तेकृत्य or हस्ते कृत्वा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=829-21" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

