हस्तिन्-मल्ल <i>m.</i> 1. a name of Airāvata; 2. of Gaṇeśa; 3. a heap of ashes; 4. a shower of dust; 5. frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तियूथ|हस्तियूथः
हस्तिन्-यूथ <i>m.</i> a herd of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिवर्चस
हस्तिन्-वर्चस <i>n.</i> the magnificence of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिवाह|हस्तिवाहः
हस्तिन्-वाह <i>m.</i> 1. an elephant-driver; 2. a hook for driving elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिस्नान
हस्तिन्-स्नान <i>n.</i> the bathing of an elephant; (it is figuratively used to indicate any useless occupation, from the elephant’s throwing dirt over his body in the very act of bathing, अवशेंद्रियचित्तानां हस्तिस्नानमिव क्रिया Hit.i.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिहस्त|हस्तिहस्तः
हस्तिन्-हस्त <i>m.</i> an elephant’s trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-03" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनपुर|हस्तिनपुरं
हस्तिन(ना)पुर <i>n.</i> Name of a city founded by king Hastina. It forms the central scene of action in the Mahābhārata. (It is also called गजाह्वय, नागसाह्वय, नागह्व, हस्तिन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनापुर|हस्तिनापुरं
हस्तिन(ना)पुर <i>n.</i> Name of a city founded by king Hastina. It forms the central scene of action in the Mahābhārata. (It is also called गजाह्वय, नागसाह्वय, नागह्व, हस्तिन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-04" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनी
हस्तिनी <i>f.</i> 1. A female elephant; 2. a kind of perfume; 3. a woman of a particular class; (she is described as having thick lips, thick hips, thick fingers, large breasts, and libidinous appetite, स्थूलाधरा स्थूलनितंबबिंबा स्थूलांगुलिझ् स्थूलकुचा सुशीला । कामोत्सुका गाढरतिप्रिया च नितंबखर्वा खलु हस्तिनी स्यात् Ratimanjarī). See चित्रिणी, पद्मिनी and शंखिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-05" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्य|हस्त्यः
हस्त्य <i>a. (f. स्त्या)</i> 1. Given with the hand; 2. done with the hand, manual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्या
हस्त्य <i>a. (f. स्त्या)</i> 1. Given with the hand; 2. done with the hand, manual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-06" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहल|हहलं
हहल <i>n.</i> A sort of deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-07" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहा
हहा <i>m.</i> Name of a Gandharva. (See हाहा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-08" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा <i>ind.</i> A particle expressing- (1) pain, grief, or weariness (ah! alas! woe me!), हा प्रिये जानकि Ut.iii., हा हा हतोऽहमिति रोदिति विष्णुशर्मा K.Pr.iv.5, हा हा देवि स्फुटति हृदयम् Ut.iii.; (2) joy or surprise (oh! ha!), हा कथं महाराजदशरथस्य धर्मदाराः प्रियसखी मे कौसल्या Ut.iv.; (3) anger or reproach, हा पितः क्वासि हे सुभ्रु Bt.vi.11, (in the sense of ‘woe be to,’ हा is used with the acc. of the object of reproach, e.g. हा लोकं केशवद्विषम् Vopadeva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-09" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा <i>(I) vt. 3Ā (pp. हान; pres. जिहीते; pass. हायते)</i> 1. To go, to move, मुकुलं सुरप्रवेकेऽहास्त Nal.i.38, Kir.xiii.23; 2. to attain.With उद्-, 1. to go up, to rise, यतो रजः पार्थिवमुज्जिहीते R.xiii.64; 2. to, revive, to come to life, उज्जिहीषे महाराज त्वं प्रशांतो न किं पुनः Bt.xviii.27; 3. to spring up, to arise, कोलाहलो लोकस्योदजिहीति D.K.; 4. to come up, to rise, (as the sun or moon), तेनारुणश्रीरयमुज्जिहीते Na.xxii.45, 55; 5. to leave, to depart, उज्जिहानजीविता M.M.ix.; 6. to raise, to throw up, सौमित्रिरक्षिभ्रुवमुज्जिहानः Bt.iii.47.With उप-, to come down to, to descend, निजौजसोज्जासयितुं जगद्द्रुहामुपाजिहीथा न महीतलं यदि Sis.i.31.With सम्-, to attain, नगरे जनता समहास्त मुदम् Nal.i.54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा <i>(II) vt. 3P (pp. हीन; pres. जहाति; desid. जिहासति)</i> 1. To abandon, to leave, to quit, to desert, to forsake, to relinquish, to dismiss, जहाति सोऽयं न पुत्रकृतकः पदवीं मृगस्ते Sak.iv., R.xii.24, xv.59, v.72, viii.52, xiv.61, 87, Bt.v.91, Megh.i.49, 60, Bt.iii.53, Bg.ii.33; 2. to let fall; 3. to resign; 4. to omit, to neglect.With अप-, to abandon, सहजामप्यपहाय धीरताम् R.viii.43.With अपा-, to abandon.With परि-, 1. to relinquish, to abandon; 2. to neglect, to omit, यथोक्तान्यपि कर्माणि परिहाय M.xii.92.With प्र-, 1. to abandon, to give up, कर्मबंधं प्रहास्यसि Bg.ii.39, प्रजहाति यदा कामान् 55, iii.41; 2. to throw, to let go, प्रजहुः शूलपट्टिशान् Bt.xiv.With वि-, to abandon, to give up, ज्ञातास्वादो विवृतजघनां को विहातुं समर्थः Megh.i.41, R.xii.102, Rt.i.27, R.ii.40, v.67, Bg.ii.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा <i>Pass. (हीयते) (generally with परि)</i> 1. to be wanting in, to be deficient in, सुवुहितप्रयोगतया आर्यस्य न किमपि परिहास्यते Sak.i.; 2. to diminish, to decrease, तथा धर्मो न हीयते M.xi.188; 3. to fail (in a law-suit), हीयते व्यवहारतः Yaj.ii.19; 4. to be deprived of, (with the inst. or abl., विरूपाक्षो जहे प्राणैः Bt.xiv.35, येषां ज्येष्ठः कनिष्ठो वा हीयेताशप्रदानतः M.ix.211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा <i>Caus. (हापयति-ते)</i> to cause to abandon, Yaj.i.115, M.iii.71.With वि-, to give away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=830-10" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

