हृष्
हृष् <i>vi. 1P, 4P (pp. हृष्ट or हृषित; pres. हर्षति, हर्षयति)</i> 1. To rejoice, to exult, to be pleased, तौ चाप्यहृषतां ततः Bt.xvii.164; 2. to stand erect (as the hair of the body), e.g. रोमाणि मेऽहृष्यन्; 3. to become erect, (said of other things also).With प्र-, 1. to be glad, to rejoice, न प्रहृष्येत्प्रियं प्राप्य Bg.v.19, xvii.36; 2. to stand erect (as the hair of the body).With सम्-, to be glad, to rejoice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=LRV&page=836-11" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=lrv" target="_blank">Correction</a>

